window.NOUHA_CONTENT = {"built":"2026-11-01T14:00:24","lessons":[{"id":"l01","order":1,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"👋","title_en":"Hello! Greetings & introductions","title_da":"Salam! Tte7iyat w tta3arof","goals_da":["Tsellmi 3la nnas b lingliziya f sbah, f l3chiya w f lil","T9eddmi rassek: smiytek w mnin nti","Tfehmi `How are you?` w tjawbi 3liha","T9oli `Thank you`, `Please` w `Goodbye`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kifach nsellmo","body_da":"F lingliziya, melli kanchoufo chi wa7ed kan9oulo `Hello` wla `Hi`. `Hi` m3a s7ab w nnas li kan3erfouhom, `Hello` kadkhol f kolchi (f lkhedma, f l'idara, m3a nnas li makan3erfouhomch).\n\nF sbah kan9oulo `Good morning`, men ba3d 12h kan9oulo `Good afternoon`, w f l3chiya wla f lil `Good evening`. Melli kanmchiw kan9oulo `Goodbye` wla `Bye`.\n\n- `Hello` / `Hi` = Salam / Ahlan\n- `Good morning` = Sbah lkhir (7ta l 12h)\n- `Good afternoon` = Msa lkhir (men 12h 7ta l 18h)\n- `Good evening` = Msa lkhir (f l3chiya w f lil)\n- `Good night` = Layla sa3ida (ghir melli ghadi tn3si wla tmchi f lil)\n- `Goodbye` / `Bye` = Bslama\n\n**Nasi7a:** `Good night` machi bhal `Good evening`! `Good night` kat9al ghir f l'akhir, melli ghadi tmchi tn3si.","examples":[{"en":"Hello! Good morning.","da":"Salam! Sbah lkhir.","pron":"hé-lo! goud mor-ning"},{"en":"Hi, Sarah!","da":"Ahlan, Sarah!","pron":"haï, sé-ra"},{"en":"Good evening, everyone.","da":"Msa lkhir 3la ljami3.","pron":"goud iv-ning, év-ri-wan"},{"en":"Goodbye! See you tomorrow.","da":"Bslama! Nchoufouk ghedda.","pron":"goud-baï! si you tou-mo-ro"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Smiyti… — kifach t9eddmi rassek","body_da":"Bach t9oli smiytek, kayn jouj tari9at, bjouj s7a7:\n\n- `My name is Nouha.` = Smiyti Nouha.\n- `I am Nouha.` = Ana Nouha.\n\n`I am` kat9der tt9esser w twelli `I'm` — nefs lma3na, walakin kat9al bzzaf f lhadra: `I'm Nouha.`\n\nBach tsewli chi wa7ed 3la smiyto: `What is your name?` wla m9essra: `What's your name?`\n\nMelli kat3erfi chi wa7ed l'awwal merra, kan9oulo `Nice to meet you` (= metcherfa b m3erftek). Howa ghadi yjawbek `Nice to meet you too` (= ana 7ta ana). Lkelma `too` hna kat3ni \"7ta ana / b7alek\".","examples":[{"en":"What's your name?","da":"Chno smiytek?","pron":"wats your néym"},{"en":"My name is Nouha.","da":"Smiyti Nouha.","pron":"maï néym iz nou-ha"},{"en":"I'm Nouha.","da":"Ana Nouha.","pron":"aïm nou-ha"},{"en":"Nice to meet you!","da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek!","pron":"naïs tou mit you"},{"en":"Nice to meet you too.","da":"Ana 7ta ana.","pron":"naïs tou mit you tou"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"How are you? — Kidayra?","body_da":"`How are you?` = Kidayra? / Labas 3lik? Had so2al kaytsewwel dima men ba3d ssalam.\n\nLjawab:\n\n- `I'm fine, thank you.` = Labas, lhamdollah. (7arfiyan: ana mzyana, choukran)\n- `I'm good.` / `I'm great!` = Ana mzyana / Bikhir bzzaf!\n- `I'm OK.` = Labas, 3adi.\n- `Not bad.` = Machi khayb.\n\nMen ba3d kanzido `And you?` (= w nti? / w nta?) bach nsewlo l'akhor 7ta howa. Bhal f darija: \"Labas, lhamdollah, w nta?\"\n\n`Thank you` w `Thanks` bjouj kay3niw \"choukran\". `Thanks` khfifa chwiya, m3a s7ab.","examples":[{"en":"How are you?","da":"Kidayra? / Labas?","pron":"haw ar you"},{"en":"I'm fine, thank you. And you?","da":"Labas, choukran. W nta?","pron":"aïm faïn, thank you. and you"},{"en":"I'm great, thanks!","da":"Bikhir bzzaf, choukran!","pron":"aïm gréyt, thanks"},{"en":"Not bad, thanks.","da":"Machi khayb, choukran.","pron":"not bad, thanks"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"hello","da":"salam","emoji":"👋","pron":"hé-lo","example_en":"Hello, Sarah!","example_da":"Salam, Sarah!"},{"en":"hi","da":"ahlan (m3a s7ab)","emoji":"🙂","pron":"haï","example_en":"Hi! How are you?","example_da":"Ahlan! Kidayra?"},{"en":"good morning","da":"sbah lkhir","emoji":"🌅","pron":"goud mor-ning","example_en":"Good morning, everyone!","example_da":"Sbah lkhir 3la ljami3!"},{"en":"good afternoon","da":"msa lkhir (men 12h 7ta l 18h)","emoji":"☀️","pron":"goud af-teur-noun","example_en":"Good afternoon, Mr. Brown.","example_da":"Msa lkhir, a ssi Brown."},{"en":"good evening","da":"msa lkhir (f l3chiya)","emoji":"🌆","pron":"goud iv-ning","example_en":"Good evening! Welcome.","example_da":"Msa lkhir! Mer7ba."},{"en":"good night","da":"layla sa3ida","emoji":"🌙","pron":"goud naït","example_en":"Good night, see you tomorrow.","example_da":"Layla sa3ida, nchoufouk ghedda."},{"en":"goodbye","da":"bslama","emoji":"🚶‍♀️","pron":"goud-baï","example_en":"Goodbye, Omar!","example_da":"Bslama, Omar!"},{"en":"thank you","da":"choukran","emoji":"🙏","pron":"thank you","example_en":"Thank you very much!","example_da":"Choukran bzzaf!"},{"en":"please","da":"3afak","emoji":"🤲","pron":"pliz","example_en":"Repeat, please.","example_da":"3awed, 3afak."},{"en":"yes","da":"ah / iyeh","emoji":"✅","pron":"yès","example_en":"Yes, I'm Nouha.","example_da":"Ah, ana Nouha."},{"en":"no","da":"la","emoji":"❌","pron":"no","example_en":"No, I'm not Sarah.","example_da":"La, ana machi Sarah."},{"en":"sorry","da":"sme7 liya / sma7 liya","emoji":"😔","pron":"so-ri","example_en":"Sorry, I'm late.","example_da":"Sme7 liya, t3ettelt."},{"en":"excuse me","da":"sme7 liya (bach tsewli wla tdouz)","emoji":"🙋‍♀️","pron":"ik-skiouz mi","example_en":"Excuse me, what's your name?","example_da":"Sme7 liya, chno smiytek?"},{"en":"name","da":"smiya / l'ism","emoji":"🏷️","pron":"néym","example_en":"My name is Nouha.","example_da":"Smiyti Nouha."},{"en":"nice to meet you","da":"metcherfa b m3erftek","emoji":"🤝","pron":"naïs tou mit you","example_en":"Nice to meet you, Tom.","example_da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek, Tom."},{"en":"you're welcome","da":"bla jmil / la choukr 3la wajib","emoji":"😊","pron":"your wél-keum","example_en":"Thank you! — You're welcome.","example_da":"Choukran! — Bla jmil."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Awwal li9a2 f dawra dyal lingliziya","context_da":"Nouha dkhlat l dawra jdida dyal lingliziya f Casa. Tla9at m3a Sarah, wa7ed lkanadiya kat9ra m3aha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hello! I'm Sarah. What's your name?","da":"Salam! Ana Sarah. Chno smiytek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Hi, Sarah. My name is Nouha.","da":"Ahlan, Sarah. Smiyti Nouha."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nice to meet you, Nouha!","da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek, Nouha!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Nice to meet you too. How are you?","da":"Ana 7ta ana. Kidayra?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I'm fine, thank you. And you?","da":"Labas, choukran. W nti?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm good, thanks.","da":"Ana mzyana, choukran."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Where are you from?","da":"Mnin nti?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm from Morocco. I live in Casablanca.","da":"Ana men lmeghrib. Kanskon f Casa."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Oh, nice! I'm from Canada.","da":"Wah, zwin! Ana men Canada."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Welcome to Morocco, Sarah!","da":"Mer7ba bik f lmeghrib, Sarah!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`Hi` w `Hello` bjouj mzyanin. M3a chi wa7ed makat3rfihch (f lkhedma, f l'idara) khtari `Hello` wla `Good morning`. M3a s7abek, `Hi` kafya. W dima zidi `please` w `thank you` — l'ingliz kaysta3mlouhom bzzaf, kter men 7na!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"salam\" b lingliziya?","options":["Hello","Goodbye","Thank you","Please"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Hello` = salam. `Goodbye` = bslama. `Thank you` = choukran. `Please` = 3afak."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Good morning!","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Sbah lkhir","Msa lkhir","Bslama","Choukran"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Good morning` = sbah lkhir. Kat9al f sbah 7ta l 12h."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lkelma b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"Thank you","da":"Choukran","emoji":"🙏"},{"en":"Goodbye","da":"Bslama","emoji":"👋"},{"en":"Please","da":"3afak","emoji":"🤲"},{"en":"Sorry","da":"Sme7 liya","emoji":"😔"},{"en":"Yes","da":"Ah / Iyeh","emoji":"✅"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"My ___ is Nouha.","options":["name","is","hello"],"answer":"name","hint_da":"Smiyti = My name","explain_da":"`My name is Nouha.` = Smiyti Nouha."},{"type":"order","words":["name","My","is","Sarah."],"answer":"My name is Sarah.","da":"Smiyti Sarah."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"How are you?","question_da":"Achmen jawab mzyan 3la had so2al?","options":["I'm fine, thank you.","My name is Ali.","Goodbye!","I'm from Morocco."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`How are you?` = kidayra? Ljawab: `I'm fine, thank you.` = labas, choukran."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Nice to ___ you.","options":["meet","name","fine"],"answer":"meet","hint_da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek.","explain_da":"`Nice to meet you.` = metcherfa b m3erftek. `meet` = tla9a / t3erref."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"What's your name?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["3la smiytek","3la ss7a dyalek","mnin nti","3la l3mer dyalek"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What's your name?` = chno smiytek?"},{"type":"translate","da":"Ana men lmeghrib.","answers":["I am from Morocco.","I'm from Morocco."],"hint_en":"I ... from ...","explain_da":"`I'm from Morocco.` — `from` = men."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Nice to meet you.","da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek.","explain_da":"Sem3i mzyan: `Nice` – `to` – `meet` – `you`."},{"type":"order","words":["are","How","you?"],"answer":"How are you?","da":"Kidayra?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"F lil, 9bel ma tn3si, kat9oli:","options":["Good night","Good morning","Good afternoon","Hello"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Good night` kat9al ghir melli ghadi tn3si wla tmchi f lil."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Hi\" is more formal than \"Hello\".","statement_da":"`Hi` rasmiya kter men `Hello`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! `Hello` hiya li rasmiya kter. `Hi` m3a s7ab."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Hello, my name is Nouha. Nice to meet you.","da":"Salam, smiyti Nouha. Metcherfa b m3erftek.","pron":"hé-lo, maï néym iz nou-ha. naïs tou mit you"},{"type":"translate","da":"Choukran bzzaf!","answers":["Thank you very much!","Thanks a lot!","Thank you so much!","Thanks very much!"],"hint_en":"Thank you ... ...","explain_da":"`Thank you very much!` = choukran bzzaf. `very much` = bzzaf."}],"reading":{"title_en":"A new friend","title_da":"Sa7ba jdida","emoji":"👭","text_en":"Hello! My name is Nouha. I am from Morocco. I live in Casablanca. This is my friend Sarah. She is from Canada. She is a nurse. Sarah is very nice. We are students in an English class. Our teacher is Mr. Brown. He is from London. Nice to meet you!","text_da":"Salam! Smiyti Nouha. Ana men lmeghrib. Kanskon f Casa. Hadi sa7bti Sarah. Hiya men Canada. Hiya fermliya. Sarah zwina bzzaf (dérifa). 7na tlamed f 9ism dyal lingliziya. L'oustad dyalna howa ssi Brown. Howa men London. Metcherfa b m3erftkom!","glossary":[{"en":"friend","da":"sa7eb / sa7ba"},{"en":"live","da":"kanskon"},{"en":"nurse","da":"fermliya"},{"en":"very","da":"bzzaf"},{"en":"nice","da":"zwin / dérif"},{"en":"students","da":"tlamed"},{"en":"class","da":"9ism / dawra"},{"en":"teacher","da":"oustad / oustada"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Mnin Nouha?","options":["Men lmeghrib","Men Canada","Men London","Men Fransa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I am from Morocco\" = ana men lmeghrib."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Sarah is from Canada.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"She is from Canada.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khedmet Sarah?","options":["Nurse (fermliya)","Teacher (oustada)","Doctor (tbiba)","Student (taliba)"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"She is a nurse.\" = hiya fermliya."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Mnin l'oustad Mr. Brown?","options":["Men London","Men Casablanca","Men Canada","Men Rabat"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"He is from London.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F l9ism dyal lingliziya","emoji":"🏫","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: chno smiyt ttalib? w mnin howa?","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Good morning, everyone! I'm Mr. Brown. What's your name?","da":"Sbah lkhir 3la ljami3! Ana ssi Brown. Chno smiytek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good morning. My name is Omar.","da":"Sbah lkhir. Smiyti Omar."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Nice to meet you, Omar. Where are you from?","da":"Metcherref b m3erftek, Omar. Mnin nta?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I'm from Rabat, in Morocco.","da":"Ana men Rabat, f lmeghrib."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Great! And how are you today?","da":"Mzyan! W kidayer lyouma?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I'm fine, thank you. And you?","da":"Labas, choukran. W nta?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"I'm very well, thanks. Welcome to the class!","da":"Ana bikhir bzzaf, choukran. Mer7ba bik f l9ism!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno smiyt l'oustad?","options":["Mr. Brown","Mr. Omar","Mr. Smith","Mr. Green"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm Mr. Brown.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Mnin Omar?","options":["Men Rabat","Men Casa","Men Fes","Men Tanja"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm from Rabat, in Morocco.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar is not fine today.","statement_da":"Omar machi labas lyouma.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: Omar 9al \"I'm fine, thank you.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Welcome to the class!","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni had ljomla?","options":["Mer7ba bik f l9ism","Bslama","Smiyti Omar","Kidayrin"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Welcome` = mer7ba. `class` = l9ism."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Hello! How are you?","da":"Salam! Kidayra?","pron":"hé-lo! haw ar you"},{"target_en":"I'm fine, thank you.","da":"Labas, choukran.","pron":"aïm faïn, thank you"},{"target_en":"My name is Nouha.","da":"Smiyti Nouha.","pron":"maï néym iz nou-ha"},{"target_en":"Nice to meet you.","da":"Metcherfa b m3erftek.","pron":"naïs tou mit you"},{"target_en":"Good morning! Have a nice day.","da":"Sbah lkhir! Nhar zwin.","pron":"goud mor-ning! hav a naïs déy"},{"target_en":"Goodbye! See you tomorrow.","da":"Bslama! Nchoufouk ghedda.","pron":"goud-baï! si you tou-mo-ro"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Awwal li9a2 m3a l'oustad","context_da":"Nti f dawra dyal lingliziya. L'oustad ghadi yhder m3ak. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hello! Good morning. What's your name?","bot_da":"Salam! Sbah lkhir. Chno smiytek?","expect_keywords":["my name is","i am","i'm","name"],"sample_en":"My name is Nouha."},{"bot_en":"Nice to meet you! How are you today?","bot_da":"Metcherref! Kidayra lyouma?","expect_keywords":["fine","good","great","ok","okay","well","not bad"],"sample_en":"I'm fine, thank you. And you?"},{"bot_en":"I'm very well, thanks. Where are you from?","bot_da":"Ana bikhir, choukran. Mnin nti?","expect_keywords":["from","morocco","casablanca","rabat","moroccan"],"sample_en":"I'm from Morocco."},{"bot_en":"Wonderful! Welcome to the class. Goodbye for now!","bot_da":"Ra2i3! Mer7ba bik f l9ism. Bslama daba!","expect_keywords":["bye","goodbye","see you","thank"],"sample_en":"Thank you! Goodbye!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"9eddmi rassek","prompt_da":"Ktbi 3 wla 4 jomal 3la rassek b lingliziya: smiytek, mnin nti, fin kattskni, w sellmi 3la l9ari. Sta3mli ljomal li t3ellemti f had dars.","helper_en":["Hello! My name is ...","I am from ...","I live in ...","Nice to meet you!"],"min_words":15,"keywords":["name","from"],"model_en":"Hello! My name is Nouha. I am from Morocco. I live in Casablanca. Nice to meet you!"}},{"id":"l02","order":2,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"🔤","title_en":"The alphabet, spelling & numbers 0–20","title_da":"L7orouf, ttehjiya w l'ar9am 0–20","goals_da":["T3erfi l7orouf dyal lingliziya w kifach kayt9raw","Tsewli `How do you spell…?` w tthejjay smiytek 7erf b 7erf","T7esbi men 0 7ta l 20","Tsta3mli ljomal dyal l9ism: `Can you repeat, please?`, `I don't understand`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L7orouf dyal lingliziya (the alphabet)","body_da":"`The alphabet` = l7orouf. F lingliziya kaynin **26 7erf**. Houma nefs l7orouf li katktbi bihom darija f lportable (A, B, C…), walakin **smiyathom b lingliziya mkhtalfa**. Khassek t7efdihom mzyan, 7it ghadi t7tajihom bach tthejjay smiytek f lbanka, f lmatar, f ttilifoun…\n\nHa l7orouf w kifach kayt9raw (mktoubin b l7orouf dyal darija):\n\n- `A` = éy\n- `B` = bi\n- `C` = si\n- `D` = di\n- `E` = i\n- `F` = éf\n- `G` = dji\n- `H` = éytch\n- `I` = aï\n- `J` = djéy\n- `K` = kéy\n- `L` = él\n- `M` = ém\n- `N` = én\n- `O` = o\n- `P` = pi\n- `Q` = kiou\n- `R` = ar\n- `S` = és\n- `T` = ti\n- `U` = you\n- `V` = vi\n- `W` = da-beul-you\n- `X` = éks\n- `Y` = waï\n- `Z` = zéd (f Amérika kay9oulo: zi)\n\n**7ila bach t7efdihom:** jem3i l7orouf li kaysaliw b nefs ssot:\n\n- \"éy\": `A` `H` `J` `K`\n- \"i\": `B` `C` `D` `E` `G` `P` `T` `V`\n- \"é\": `F` `L` `M` `N` `S` `X`\n- \"aï\": `I` `Y`\n- \"ou\": `Q` `U` `W`\n\n**Redi lbal:** `E` kat9ra \"i\", w `I` kat9ra \"aï\" — hadi lghalta li kaydirouha bzzaf dyal nnas! W `G` (dji) machi bhal `J` (djéy). Jarrbi t9rayhom b sot 3ali.","examples":[{"en":"A, B, C, D, E, F, G.","da":"L7orouf lewwlin.","pron":"éy, bi, si, di, i, éf, dji"},{"en":"N-O-U-H-A.","da":"Nouha, 7erf b 7erf.","pron":"én-o-you-éytch-éy"},{"en":"C-A-S-A.","da":"Casa, 7erf b 7erf.","pron":"si-éy-és-éy"},{"en":"W, X, Y, Z.","da":"L7orouf l'akhira.","pron":"da-beul-you, éks, waï, zéd"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"How do you spell…? — kifach katktbiha?","body_da":"Melli chi wa7ed ma 3refch kifach katkteb smiytek, kaysewlek: `How do you spell your name?` = kifach katktbi smiytek? (7erf b 7erf). Bhal melli lmowaddaf f l'idara kay9oul lik: \"ktebha liya 7erf b 7erf\".\n\nLjawab: kat9oli l7orouf wa7ed b wa7ed: `It's N-O-U-H-A.`\n\nJomal mohimma:\n\n- `How do you spell it?` = kifach katktbiha?\n- `Can you spell that, please?` = wach t9der tthejja liya hadik, 3afak?\n- `It's N-O-U-H-A.` = hiya N-O-U-H-A.\n- `Double L` = jouj L mtab3in (bhal f `Ella`: E, double L, A)\n- `Capital N` = N kbira (7erf kbir)\n\n`First name` = smiya (l'ism lewwel). `Last name` wla `family name` = lknya (l'ism l3a2ili). `Your full name` = smiytek kamla. F lmeghrib kanktbo lknya lewwla f lwra9, walakin f lingliziya `first name` dima lewwel!","examples":[{"en":"How do you spell your name?","da":"Kifach katktbi smiytek?","pron":"haw dou you spél your néym"},{"en":"It's N-O-U-H-A.","da":"Hiya N-O-U-H-A.","pron":"its én-o-you-éytch-éy"},{"en":"Can you spell that, please?","da":"Wach t9der tthejja liya hadik, 3afak?","pron":"kan you spél that, pliz"},{"en":"My last name is Alami: A-L-A-M-I.","da":"Lknya dyali Alami: A-L-A-M-I.","pron":"maï last néym iz a-la-mi: éy-él-éy-ém-aï"},{"en":"Sorry, is it one L or double L?","da":"Sme7 liya, wach L we7da wla jouj?","pron":"so-ri, iz it wan él or da-beul él"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'ar9am men 0 7ta l 20","body_da":"Ha l'ar9am men 0 7ta l 20. 9rayhom b sot 3ali bzzaf dyal lmerrat:\n\n- 0 `zero` = zi-ro\n- 1 `one` = wan\n- 2 `two` = tou\n- 3 `three` = thri\n- 4 `four` = for\n- 5 `five` = faïv\n- 6 `six` = siks\n- 7 `seven` = sé-ven\n- 8 `eight` = éyt\n- 9 `nine` = naïn\n- 10 `ten` = tén\n- 11 `eleven` = i-lé-ven\n- 12 `twelve` = twélv\n- 13 `thirteen` = theur-tin\n- 14 `fourteen` = for-tin\n- 15 `fifteen` = fif-tin\n- 16 `sixteen` = siks-tin\n- 17 `seventeen` = sé-ven-tin\n- 18 `eighteen` = éy-tin\n- 19 `nineteen` = naïn-tin\n- 20 `twenty` = twén-ti\n\n**Lmola7ada:** men 13 7ta 19 kolhom kaysaliw b `-teen` — bhal f darija melli kan9oulo tlettach, rb3tach, khemstach… kolhom kaysaliw b \"-tach\"! Walakin redi lbal: `thirteen` (machi \"threeteen\") w `fifteen` (machi \"fiveteen\"). W `eleven` w `twelve` khassin, bhal 7dach w tnach f darija.\n\n**Ssot \"th\":** f `three` w `thirteen`, 7etti lsanek bin ssnan w nef7i — ssot bin \"t\" w \"s\". Jarrbi: `three`, `thirteen`, `thank you`.","examples":[{"en":"Page ten, please.","da":"Ssef7a 3achra, 3afak.","pron":"péydj tén, pliz"},{"en":"One, two, three, go!","da":"Wa7ed, jouj, tlata, yallah!","pron":"wan, tou, thri, go"},{"en":"Number fifteen.","da":"Nnemra khemstach.","pron":"nam-beur fif-tin"},{"en":"Twelve dirhams, please.","da":"Tnach derhem, 3afak.","pron":"twélv di-ramz, pliz"},{"en":"I'm in room twenty.","da":"Ana f lbit 3echrin.","pron":"aïm in roum twén-ti"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ljomal dyal l9ism (classroom language)","body_da":"F l9ism, ila ma fhemtich wla ma sme3tich mzyan, **ma t7echmich!** Hadi hiya ljomal li ghadi tn9dek:\n\n- `Can you repeat, please?` = wach t9der t3awed, 3afak?\n- `Slowly, please.` = bchwiya, 3afak.\n- `I don't understand.` = ma fhemtch.\n- `What does \"open\" mean?` = chno kat3ni `open`?\n- `How do you say \"khobz\" in English?` = kifach kan9oulo \"khobz\" b lingliziya?\n- `How do you write it?` = kifach katktbiha?\n- `Sorry?` / `Pardon?` = chno? (3awed, ma sme3tch)\n- `I have a question.` = 3ndi so2al.\n- `I know!` / `I don't know.` = 3reft! / ma 3reftch.\n\n`Can you…?` = wach t9der / t9edri…? — tari9a mo2addaba (b l'adab) bach ttelbi chi 7aja. W `please` dima f l'akhir!\n\nL'oustad ghadi y9oul likom: `Open your books.` (7ellou lktouba), `Listen.` (sem3ou), `Repeat.` (3awdou), `Read.` (9raw), `Write.` (ktbou), `Good job!` (mzyan!).","examples":[{"en":"Can you repeat, please?","da":"Wach t9der t3awed, 3afak?","pron":"kan you ri-pit, pliz"},{"en":"Sorry, I don't understand.","da":"Sme7 liya, ma fhemtch.","pron":"so-ri, aï dont an-deur-stand"},{"en":"What does \"page\" mean?","da":"Chno kat3ni `page`?","pron":"wat daz péydj min"},{"en":"How do you say \"khobz\" in English?","da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"khobz\" b lingliziya?","pron":"haw dou you séy khobz in in-glich"},{"en":"Slowly, please. I have a question.","da":"Bchwiya, 3afak. 3ndi so2al.","pron":"slo-li, pliz. aï hav a kwés-tcheun"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"letter","da":"7erf","emoji":"🔤","pron":"lé-teur","example_en":"The letter A.","example_da":"L7erf A."},{"en":"number","da":"ra9m / nemra","emoji":"🔢","pron":"nam-beur","example_en":"Number seven, please.","example_da":"Nnemra sb3a, 3afak."},{"en":"spell","da":"thejja (9oli l7orouf wa7ed b wa7ed)","emoji":"🔡","pron":"spél","example_en":"Spell your name, please.","example_da":"Thejjay smiytek, 3afak."},{"en":"repeat","da":"3awed","emoji":"🔁","pron":"ri-pit","example_en":"Can you repeat the number?","example_da":"Wach t9der t3awed nnemra?"},{"en":"understand","da":"fhem","emoji":"💡","pron":"an-deur-stand","example_en":"I understand now, thank you.","example_da":"Fhemt daba, choukran."},{"en":"mean","da":"3na (kat3ni)","emoji":"🤔","pron":"min","example_en":"What does \"letter\" mean?","example_da":"Chno kat3ni `letter`?"},{"en":"say","da":"9al / goul","emoji":"🗣️","pron":"séy","example_en":"How do you say \"atay\" in English?","example_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"atay\" b lingliziya?"},{"en":"slowly","da":"bchwiya","emoji":"🐢","pron":"slo-li","example_en":"Speak slowly, please.","example_da":"Hder bchwiya, 3afak."},{"en":"question","da":"so2al","emoji":"❓","pron":"kwés-tcheun","example_en":"I have a question.","example_da":"3ndi so2al."},{"en":"answer","da":"jawab","emoji":"💬","pron":"an-seur","example_en":"Good answer, Nouha!","example_da":"Jawab mzyan, Nouha!"},{"en":"word","da":"kelma","emoji":"📝","pron":"weurd","example_en":"\"Hello\" is an English word.","example_da":"`Hello` kelma ngliziya."},{"en":"page","da":"ssef7a","emoji":"📄","pron":"péydj","example_en":"Open your book, page five.","example_da":"7elli lktab dyalek, ssef7a khemsa."},{"en":"book","da":"ktab","emoji":"📘","pron":"bouk","example_en":"This is my English book.","example_da":"Hada lktab dyali dyal lingliziya."},{"en":"first name","da":"smiya (l'ism lewwel)","emoji":"🪪","pron":"feurst néym","example_en":"My first name is Nouha.","example_da":"Smiyti Nouha."},{"en":"last name","da":"knya (l'ism l3a2ili)","emoji":"👪","pron":"last néym","example_en":"What's your last name?","example_da":"Chno lknya dyalek?"},{"en":"teacher","da":"oustad / oustada","emoji":"👩‍🏫","pron":"ti-tcheur","example_en":"Our teacher is Mr. Brown.","example_da":"L'oustad dyalna howa ssi Brown."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Kifach katktbi smiytek?","context_da":"F l9ism, l'oustad Mr. Brown kaykteb smiyat ttlamed. Kaysewwel Nouha 3la smiytha, w Nouha kattleb menno y3awed.","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Good morning, Nouha. How do you spell your name?","da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha. Kifach katktbi smiytek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Sorry, can you repeat, please? Slowly.","da":"Sme7 liya, wach t9der t3awed, 3afak? Bchwiya."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Of course. How do you spell \"Nouha\"?","da":"Wakha. Kifach katktbi \"Nouha\"?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Ah, OK! It's N-O-U-H-A.","da":"Ah, wakha! Hiya N-O-U-H-A."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Thank you. And your last name?","da":"Choukran. W lknya dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Alami. A-L-A-M-I.","da":"Alami. A-L-A-M-I."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Great. Now open your books, page twelve.","da":"Mzyan. Daba 7ellou lktouba dyalkom, ssef7a tnach."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Sorry, what does \"open\" mean?","da":"Sme7 liya, chno kat3ni `open`?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"\"Open\" means… like this. Open the book!","da":"`Open` kat3ni… hakka. 7elli lktab!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Ah, I understand. Thank you!","da":"Ah, fhemt. Choukran!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Melli chi wa7ed kayhder bzer3a w ma fhemtich, ma tskotich w ma t7echmich! 9oli `Sorry, can you repeat, please?` wla `Slowly, please.` — l'ingliz kayfer7o melli kat7awli. W 7fedi smiytek 7erf b 7erf b lingliziya (`N-O-U-H-A`) 7ta twelli kat9oliha bla ma tfekkri: ghadi t7tajiha f lbanka, f lmatar, w f ttilifoun."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kayt9ra l7erf `H` b lingliziya?","options":["éytch","ach","aï","éy"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`H` = éytch. `I` = aï. `A` = éy. Redi lbal: machi \"ach\" bhal f ttilifoun!"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Seven.","question_da":"Sem3i. Achmen ra9m?","options":["7","17","6","11"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`seven` = sb3a (7). `seventeen` = sb3tach (17). `six` = setta (6). `eleven` = 7dach (11)."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli rra9m b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"three","da":"tlata","emoji":"3️⃣"},{"en":"five","da":"khemsa","emoji":"5️⃣"},{"en":"eight","da":"tmenya","emoji":"8️⃣"},{"en":"ten","da":"3achra","emoji":"🔟"},{"en":"twelve","da":"tnach","emoji":"1️⃣2️⃣"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"How do you ___ your name?","options":["spell","say","repeat"],"answer":"spell","hint_da":"7erf b 7erf…","explain_da":"`spell` = thejja (9oli l7orouf wa7ed b wa7ed). `How do you spell your name?` = kifach katktbi smiytek?"},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Ten, eleven, ___, thirteen.","options":["twelve","twenty","two"],"answer":"twelve","hint_da":"10, 11, …, 13","explain_da":"`twelve` = tnach (12). `twenty` = 3echrin (20). `two` = jouj (2)."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"B-R-O-W-N.","question_da":"Sem3i l7orouf. Achmen smiya?","options":["Brown","Bruno","Brian","Boran"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`B-R-O-W-N` = Brown. `O` kat9ra \"o\" w `W` kat9ra \"da-beul-you\"."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"What does \"book\" mean?","question_da":"Chno kat3ni `book`?","options":["ktab","ssef7a","kelma","so2al"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`book` = ktab. `page` = ssef7a. `word` = kelma. `question` = so2al."},{"type":"order","words":["you","Can","repeat,","please?"],"answer":"Can you repeat, please?","da":"Wach t9der t3awed, 3afak?"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Fifteen\" is 50.","statement_da":"`Fifteen` = khemsin (50).","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! `fifteen` = khemstach (15). Khemsin (50) hiya `fifty` — ghadi nchoufouha f dars 5."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Slowly, please.","da":"Bchwiya, 3afak.","explain_da":"`Slowly` = bchwiya. Redi lbal l `-ly` f l'akhir: slo-li."},{"type":"translate","da":"Chno kat3ni `teacher`?","answers":["What does teacher mean?","What does \"teacher\" mean?","What does 'teacher' mean?"],"hint_en":"What does ... mean?","explain_da":"`What does … mean?` = chno kat3ni…? Lkelma kadkhol f lwest, bin `does` w `mean`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Open your books, page eighteen.","question_da":"Sem3i. Achmen ssef7a?","options":["18","8","80","13"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`eighteen` = tmentach (18). `eight` = tmenya (8). `thirteen` = tlettach (13)."},{"type":"order","words":["do","How","you","say","\"choukran\"","in","English?"],"answer":"How do you say \"choukran\" in English?","da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"choukran\" b lingliziya?"},{"type":"translate","da":"Sme7 liya, ma fhemtch.","answers":["Sorry, I don't understand.","Sorry, I do not understand.","Excuse me, I don't understand."],"hint_en":"Sorry, I ... ...","explain_da":"`I don't understand.` = ma fhemtch. `don't` = ma…ch (nnafi)."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"L'oustad kayhder bzer3a bzzaf. Chno kat9oli lih?","options":["Slowly, please.","Good night.","Nice to meet you.","Page ten, please."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Slowly, please.` = bchwiya, 3afak. Kat9oliha melli chi wa7ed kayhder bzer3a."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"My name is Nouha: N-O-U-H-A.","da":"Smiyti Nouha: N-O-U-H-A.","pron":"maï néym iz nou-ha: én-o-you-éytch-éy"}],"reading":{"title_en":"My English class","title_da":"L9ism dyali dyal lingliziya","emoji":"🏫","text_en":"Hello! My name is Nouha. I am a student in an English class in Casablanca. My teacher is Mr. Brown. He is from London. In the class, we are twelve students: seven women and five men. Our book is \"English for Life\". Every day, Mr. Brown says: \"Open your books, please.\" Sometimes I don't understand, so I say: \"Can you repeat, please? Slowly, please.\" Mr. Brown is very nice. He repeats, and I understand. In the class, I spell my name: N-O-U-H-A. English is not easy, but it is fun!","text_da":"Salam! Smiyti Nouha. Ana taliba f 9ism dyal lingliziya f Casa. L'oustad dyali howa ssi Brown. Howa men London. F l9ism, 7na tnach dyal ttlamed: sb3a dyal l3yalat w khemsa dyal rrjal. Lktab dyalna smiyto `English for Life`. Kol nhar, ssi Brown kay9oul: \"7ellou lktouba dyalkom, 3afak.\" Chi merrat makanfhemch, 3ad kan9oul: \"Wach t9der t3awed, 3afak? Bchwiya, 3afak.\" Ssi Brown dérif bzzaf. Kay3awed, w kanfhem. F l9ism, kanthejja smiyti: N-O-U-H-A. Lingliziya machi sahla, walakin momti3a (kat3jeb)!","glossary":[{"en":"student","da":"talib / taliba"},{"en":"women","da":"3yalat (we7da: `woman` = mra)"},{"en":"men","da":"rjal (wa7ed: `man` = rajel)"},{"en":"every day","da":"kol nhar"},{"en":"sometimes","da":"chi merrat / b3d lmerrat"},{"en":"so","da":"3ad / dakchi 3lach"},{"en":"easy","da":"sahl / sahla"},{"en":"fun","da":"momti3 / kay3jeb"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men talib kayn f l9ism?","options":["12","7","5","20"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"We are twelve students.\" = 7na tnach dyal ttlamed."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Mr. Brown is from London.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"He is from London.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kat9oul Nouha melli makatfhemch?","options":["Can you repeat, please?","Good night!","Nice to meet you.","My name is Nouha."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Sometimes I don't understand, so I say: Can you repeat, please?\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"English is easy for Nouha.","statement_da":"Lingliziya sahla 3la Nouha.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"English is not easy, but it is fun!\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Ttasjil f lmadrasa dyal lingliziya","emoji":"📝","pre_da":"Omar kaytsejjel f lmadrasa dyal lingliziya. Sem3i mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: kifach katkteb lknya dyal Omar, w achmen nemra dyal lbit (l9ism) ghadi ymchi liha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Good afternoon! What's your name, please?","da":"Msa lkhir! Chno smiytek, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Hello. My name is Omar Tazi.","da":"Salam. Smiyti Omar Tazi."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"How do you spell your last name?","da":"Kifach katkteb lknya dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"T-A-Z-I.","da":"T-A-Z-I."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Sorry, can you repeat, please? Slowly.","da":"Sme7 liya, wach t9der t3awed, 3afak? Bchwiya."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Of course: T-A-Z-I. Tazi.","da":"Wakha: T-A-Z-I. Tazi."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Thank you, Omar. Your class is room eleven, with Mr. Brown.","da":"Choukran, Omar. L9ism dyalek f lbit nemra 7dach, m3a ssi Brown."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Room eleven. What does \"room\" mean?","da":"Lbit 7dach. Chno kat3ni `room`?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"\"Room\" means the place, the class. Number eleven.","da":"`Room` kat3ni lbit, lblasa fin kayn l9ism. Nnemra 7dach."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Ah, I understand. Thank you very much!","da":"Ah, fhemt. Choukran bzzaf!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno lknya dyal Omar (`last name`)?","options":["Tazi","Tali","Fazi","Taza"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"T-A-Z-I. Tazi.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Your class is room eleven.","question_da":"Sem3i. Achmen nemra dyal lbit?","options":["11","7","17","1"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`eleven` = 7dach (11). `seven` = 7, `seventeen` = 17, `one` = 1."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The teacher is Mr. Brown.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"Your class is room eleven, with Mr. Brown.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno sewwel Omar f l'akhir?","options":["Chno kat3ni `room`","Chno smiytek","Kidayra","Mnin nti"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"What does room mean?\" = chno kat3ni `room`?"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"A, B, C, D, E, F, G.","da":"L7orouf men A 7ta G.","pron":"éy, bi, si, di, i, éf, dji"},{"target_en":"How do you spell your name?","da":"Kifach katktbi smiytek?","pron":"haw dou you spél your néym"},{"target_en":"Can you repeat, please?","da":"Wach t9der t3awed, 3afak?","pron":"kan you ri-pit, pliz"},{"target_en":"I don't understand.","da":"Ma fhemtch.","pron":"aï dont an-deur-stand"},{"target_en":"One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten.","da":"Men wa7ed 7ta l 3achra.","pron":"wan, tou, thri, for, faïv, siks, sé-ven, éyt, naïn, tén"},{"target_en":"Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen, twenty.","da":"Tlettach, rb3tach, khemstach, 3echrin.","pron":"theur-tin, for-tin, fif-tin, twén-ti"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Ttasjil f lmadrasa","context_da":"Nti f lbiro dyal madrasa dyal lingliziya. Lkatiba ghadi tsewlek 3la smiytek w kifach katktbiha. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning! What's your name, please?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir! Chno smiytek, 3afak?","expect_keywords":["my name is","i am","i'm","nouha","name"],"sample_en":"My name is Nouha."},{"bot_en":"How do you spell your name?","bot_da":"Kifach katktbi smiytek?","expect_keywords":["n o u h a","n-o-u-h-a","nouha","en oh","n o","it's","it is"],"sample_en":"It's N-O-U-H-A."},{"bot_en":"Sorry, can you repeat that, please? Slowly.","bot_da":"Sme7 liya, wach t9edri t3awdi, 3afak? Bchwiya.","expect_keywords":["n o u h a","n-o-u-h-a","nouha","n o","yes","of course","ok","okay"],"sample_en":"Of course. N-O-U-H-A."},{"bot_en":"Thank you. Your class is room fifteen. Do you understand?","bot_da":"Choukran. L9ism dyalek f lbit khemstach. Fhemti?","expect_keywords":["yes","understand","fifteen","15","ok","okay","thank"],"sample_en":"Yes, I understand. Room fifteen. Thank you!"},{"bot_en":"Perfect! See you tomorrow at nine. Goodbye!","bot_da":"Mzyan! Nchoufouk ghedda f tts3oud. Bslama!","expect_keywords":["bye","goodbye","see you","thank","nine","ok","okay"],"sample_en":"Thank you! See you tomorrow. Goodbye!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Smiytek 7erf b 7erf","prompt_da":"Ktbi 3 wla 4 jomal b lingliziya: smiytek w lknya dyalek, kifach katktbi smiytek 7erf b 7erf, mnin nti, w jomla we7da dyal l9ism (bhal `I don't understand` wla `Can you repeat, please?`).","helper_en":["My first name is ...","My last name is ...","I spell my name: ...","I am from ...","Can you repeat, please?"],"min_words":15,"keywords":["name","spell","from"],"model_en":"Hello! My first name is Nouha. My last name is Alami. I spell my name: N-O-U-H-A. I am from Morocco. In class, I say: \"Can you repeat, please?\""}},{"id":"l03","order":3,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"🌍","title_en":"Where are you from? The verb \"to be\"","title_da":"Mnin nti? L fi3l \"to be\"","goals_da":["Tsta3mli `am`, `is`, `are` m3a `I`, `you`, `he`, `she`, `it`, `we`, `they`","Tnfi: `I'm not`, `isn't`, `aren't`","Tsewli w tjawbi b jawab 9sir: `Are you…?` — `Yes, I am.` / `No, I'm not.`","T9oli mnin nti, chno jinsiytek w achmen logha kathedri"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ddamayer: I, you, he, she, it, we, they","body_da":"Ddamir (`pronoun`) = lkelma li kan9oulouha f blast l'ism: ana, nti, howa… Ha ddamayer dyal lingliziya:\n\n- `I` = ana (dima b 7erf kbir, 7ta f west ljomla!)\n- `you` = nti / nta / ntouma — kelma we7da l kolchi: l lmra w rrajel, l lwa7ed w l bzzaf\n- `he` = howa (rajel wla weld)\n- `she` = hiya (mra wla bent)\n- `it` = howa / hiya l l7wayj w l7ayawanat (tomobil, ktab, mdina…) — machi l nnas\n- `we` = 7na\n- `they` = houma (nnas, w 7ta l7wayj)\n\n**Lfar9 m3a darija:** f darija kan9oulo \"nti\" l lmra w \"nta\" l rrajel. F lingliziya `you` l bjouj — sahla! Walakin f lingliziya kaynin `he` w `she` l nnas, w `it` l l7wayj: \"tomobil\" = `it`, machi `she`.","examples":[{"en":"I am Nouha. I am from Morocco.","da":"Ana Nouha. Ana men lmeghrib.","pron":"aï am nou-ha. aï am from mo-ro-ko"},{"en":"You are my friend.","da":"Nti sa7bti.","pron":"you ar maï frénd"},{"en":"He is Omar and she is Sarah.","da":"Howa Omar w hiya Sarah.","pron":"hi iz o-mar and chi iz sé-ra"},{"en":"Casablanca? It is a big city.","da":"Casa? Hiya mdina kbira.","pron":"ka-sa-blan-ka? it iz a big si-ti"},{"en":"We are students and they are teachers.","da":"7na tlamed w houma asatida.","pron":"wi ar stiou-dents and théy ar ti-tcheurz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"L fi3l \"to be\": am / is / are","body_da":"F darija melli kan9oulo \"ana men Casa\" wla \"hiya oustada\", ma kaynch fi3l (`verb`) bin lkelmat. F lingliziya **khass dima fi3l**: `I am from Casablanca.` — had l fi3l howa `to be` (bhal \"kan / howa / hiya / kayn\").\n\nL fi3l `to be` kaytbeddel 3la 7sab ddamir — 3ndo ghir tlata dyal l'achkal: `am`, `is`, `are`:\n\n- `I am` → m9essra: `I'm`\n- `you are` → `you're`\n- `he is` → `he's`\n- `she is` → `she's`\n- `it is` → `it's`\n- `we are` → `we're`\n- `they are` → `they're`\n\n**Lmokhtassar (m9essra):** f lhadra, l'ingliz kay9oulo dima `I'm`, `she's`, `we're`… Chkel ttwil (`I am`) kaytkteb f lwra9 rrasmiya wla melli bghina n2ekkdo.\n\n**Kifach t7efdiha:** `am` ghir m3a `I`. `is` m3a wa7ed (`he`, `she`, `it`, Sarah, lktab…). `are` m3a `you` w m3a bzzaf (`we`, `they`, Omar w Ali…).","examples":[{"en":"I am from Morocco.","da":"Ana men lmeghrib.","pron":"aï am from mo-ro-ko"},{"en":"She's from Agadir.","da":"Hiya men Agadir.","pron":"chiz from a-ga-dir"},{"en":"We're students.","da":"7na tlamed.","pron":"wir stiou-dents"},{"en":"They're Moroccan.","da":"Houma mgharba.","pron":"thér mo-ro-kan"},{"en":"Rabat is a city in Morocco.","da":"Rabat mdina f lmeghrib.","pron":"ra-bat iz a si-ti in mo-ro-ko"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Nnafi: I'm not, isn't, aren't","body_da":"Bach tnfi (t9oli \"machi\"), zidi `not` **men ba3d** l fi3l — bhal \"machi\" f darija: \"ana machi men Rabat\" = `I am not from Rabat.`\n\n- `I am not` → `I'm not`\n- `you are not` → `you aren't` wla `you're not`\n- `he is not` → `he isn't` wla `he's not`\n- `she is not` → `she isn't`\n- `it is not` → `it isn't`\n- `we are not` → `we aren't`\n- `they are not` → `they aren't`\n\n**Redi lbal:** m3a `I` ma kaynach \"amn't\"! Kan9oulo ghir `I'm not`.\n\nNnot9: `isn't` kat9ra \"i-zent\", `aren't` kat9ra \"arnt\".","examples":[{"en":"I'm not from Rabat, I'm from Casablanca.","da":"Ana machi men Rabat, ana men Casa.","pron":"aïm not from ra-bat, aïm from ka-sa-blan-ka"},{"en":"She isn't Spanish, she's Moroccan.","da":"Hiya machi sbenyouliya, hiya meghribiya.","pron":"chi i-zent spa-nich, chiz mo-ro-kan"},{"en":"We aren't teachers, we're students.","da":"7na machi asatida, 7na tlamed.","pron":"wi arnt ti-tcheurz, wir stiou-dents"},{"en":"Omar isn't here today.","da":"Omar machi hna lyouma.","pron":"o-mar i-zent hir tou-déy"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"So2al w jawab 9sir: Are you…? Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.","body_da":"Bach tsewli, **9elbi**: l fi3l kayji 9bel ddamir. F darija kanzido ghir \"wach\" f lewwel; f lingliziya kan9elbo:\n\n- `You are from Fes.` → `Are you from Fes?` = wach nti men Fes?\n- `She is a teacher.` → `Is she a teacher?` = wach hiya oustada?\n- `They are here.` → `Are they here?` = wach houma hna?\n\n**Ljawab l9sir** (`short answer`): ma kan3awdouch ljomla kamla, kan9oulo ghir:\n\n- `Yes, I am.` / `No, I'm not.`\n- `Yes, she is.` / `No, she isn't.`\n- `Yes, they are.` / `No, they aren't.`\n\n**Redi lbal:** f ljawab b `Yes`, ma kan9essrouch l fi3l: `Yes, I am.` (machi \"Yes, I'm.\") w `Yes, she is.` (machi \"Yes, she's.\").\n\n**So2al b `Where`** (= fin / mnin): `Where are you from?` = mnin nti? `Where is she from?` = mnin hiya? Ljawab: `I'm from Tangier.` / `She's from Fes.`","examples":[{"en":"Are you from Morocco? — Yes, I am.","da":"Wach nti men lmeghrib? — Ah.","pron":"ar you from mo-ro-ko? yès, aï am"},{"en":"Is he from Spain? — No, he isn't. He's from Italy.","da":"Wach howa men Sbanya? — La. Howa men Italya.","pron":"iz hi from spéyn? no, hi i-zent. hiz from i-ta-li"},{"en":"Where are you from? — I'm from Tangier.","da":"Mnin nti? — Ana men Tanja.","pron":"wér ar you from? aïm from tan-djir"},{"en":"Where is Sarah from? — She's from Canada.","da":"Mnin Sarah? — Hiya men Canada.","pron":"wér iz sé-ra from? chiz from ka-na-da"},{"en":"Are they students? — Yes, they are.","da":"Wach houma tlamed? — Ah, tlamed.","pron":"ar théy stiou-dents? yès, théy ar"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lbouldan, ljinsiyat w llughat","body_da":"Smiyt lblad (`country`) w ljinsiya (`nationality`) mkhtalfin — bhal \"lmeghrib\" w \"meghribi\". F lingliziya, **ljinsiya ma katbeddelch** bin rrajel w lmra: `Moroccan` l bjouj! W lblad, ljinsiya w llugha (`language`) kolhom kaytketbo b **7erf kbir**.\n\nLblad → ljinsiya → llugha:\n\n- `Morocco` → `Moroccan` → `Arabic`\n- `Egypt` → `Egyptian` → `Arabic`\n- `Spain` → `Spanish` → `Spanish`\n- `France` → `French` → `French`\n- `England` → `English` → `English`\n- `the USA` (Amérika) → `American` → `English`\n- `Canada` → `Canadian` → `English` w `French`\n- `Italy` → `Italian` → `Italian`\n- `Germany` → `German` → `German`\n- `Turkey` → `Turkish` → `Turkish`\n- `China` → `Chinese` → `Chinese`\n\nBach t9oli achmen logha kathedri: `I speak Arabic.` = kanhder l3arbiya (ddarija). `I speak a little English.` = kanhder chwiya dyal lingliziya. (`speak` = hder / tkellem.)\n\nLmdina (`city`): `I'm from Casablanca.` = ana men Casa. `I live in Rabat.` = kanskon f Rabat (`live` = skon).","examples":[{"en":"I'm Moroccan. I speak Arabic.","da":"Ana meghribiya. Kanhder l3arbiya.","pron":"aïm mo-ro-kan. aï spik a-ra-bik"},{"en":"Mr. Brown is English. He's from London.","da":"Ssi Brown ngliz. Howa men London.","pron":"mis-teur brawn iz in-glich. hiz from lan-deun"},{"en":"Are you French? — No, I'm not. I'm Moroccan.","da":"Wach nti fransawiya? — La. Ana meghribiya.","pron":"ar you fréntch? no, aïm not. aïm mo-ro-kan"},{"en":"Carlos is from Spain. He's Spanish.","da":"Carlos men Sbanya. Howa sbenyouli.","pron":"kar-los iz from spéyn. hiz spa-nich"},{"en":"I speak a little English.","da":"Kanhder chwiya dyal lingliziya.","pron":"aï spik a li-teul in-glich"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"country","da":"blad","emoji":"🌍","pron":"kan-tri","example_en":"Morocco is my country.","example_da":"Lmeghrib howa bladi."},{"en":"city","da":"mdina","emoji":"🏙️","pron":"si-ti","example_en":"Marrakech is a city in Morocco.","example_da":"Marrakech mdina f lmeghrib."},{"en":"language","da":"logha","emoji":"🗣️","pron":"lan-gwidj","example_en":"Arabic is my language.","example_da":"L3arbiya hiya loghti."},{"en":"speak","da":"hder / tkellem","emoji":"💬","pron":"spik","example_en":"I speak Arabic and a little English.","example_da":"Kanhder l3arbiya w chwiya dyal lingliziya."},{"en":"from","da":"men","emoji":"📍","pron":"from","example_en":"Where are you from?","example_da":"Mnin nti?"},{"en":"here","da":"hna","emoji":"👇","pron":"hir","example_en":"Sarah is here today.","example_da":"Sarah hna lyouma."},{"en":"Morocco","da":"lmeghrib","emoji":"🇲🇦","pron":"mo-ro-ko","example_en":"I live in Morocco.","example_da":"Kanskon f lmeghrib."},{"en":"Moroccan","da":"meghribi / meghribiya","emoji":"🇲🇦","pron":"mo-ro-kan","example_en":"We are Moroccan.","example_da":"7na mgharba."},{"en":"Arabic","da":"l3arbiya","emoji":"📖","pron":"a-ra-bik","example_en":"Arabic is not easy!","example_da":"L3arbiya machi sahla!"},{"en":"England","da":"Ingeltera (blad l'ingliz)","emoji":"🇬🇧","pron":"in-gland","example_en":"London is in England.","example_da":"London f Ingeltera."},{"en":"English","da":"lingliziya / ngliz, ngliziya","emoji":"🇬🇧","pron":"in-glich","example_en":"My English teacher is from London.","example_da":"L'oustad dyali dyal lingliziya men London."},{"en":"Spain","da":"Sbanya","emoji":"🇪🇸","pron":"spéyn","example_en":"Madrid is in Spain.","example_da":"Madrid f Sbanya."},{"en":"Spanish","da":"sbenyouli / sbenyouliya","emoji":"🇪🇸","pron":"spa-nich","example_en":"Carlos and Ana are Spanish.","example_da":"Carlos w Ana sbenyouliyin."},{"en":"France","da":"Fransa","emoji":"🇫🇷","pron":"frans","example_en":"Paris is in France.","example_da":"Paris f Fransa."},{"en":"French","da":"fransawi / fransawiya","emoji":"🇫🇷","pron":"fréntch","example_en":"Marie is French. She's from Lyon.","example_da":"Marie fransawiya. Hiya men Lyon."},{"en":"American","da":"amiriki / amirikiya","emoji":"🇺🇸","pron":"a-mé-ri-kan","example_en":"Tom is American. He's from Chicago.","example_da":"Tom amiriki. Howa men Chicago."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Mnin nti?","context_da":"F l'istira7a (lpause), Nouha kathder m3a Tom, talib jdid f l9ism.","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Hi! I'm Tom. Are you a new student?","da":"Ahlan! Ana Tom. Wach nti taliba jdida?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Hi, Tom. Yes, I am. I'm Nouha.","da":"Ahlan, Tom. Ah, ana jdida. Ana Nouha."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Nice to meet you. Where are you from, Nouha?","da":"Metcherref. Mnin nti, Nouha?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm from Morocco. I'm Moroccan. And you? Are you English?","da":"Ana men lmeghrib. Ana meghribiya. W nta? Wach nta ngliz?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"No, I'm not. I'm American. I'm from Chicago.","da":"La. Ana amiriki. Ana men Chicago."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Oh, nice! Is Chicago a big city?","da":"Wah, zwin! Wach Chicago mdina kbira?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Yes, it is. It's very big. And you, are you from Casablanca?","da":"Ah. Kbira bzzaf. W nti, wach nti men Casa?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I am. Casablanca is a big city too!","da":"Ah. Casa 7ta hiya mdina kbira!"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Great. Sorry, my Arabic isn't good.","da":"Mzyan. Sme7 liya, l3arbiya dyali machi mzyana."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No problem! My English isn't very good, but I'm a good student!","da":"Machi mochkil! Lingliziya dyali machi mzyana bzzaf, walakin ana taliba mzyana!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`I` dima kaytkteb b 7erf kbir, 7ta f west ljomla: `Sarah and I are students.` W ljinsiyat w llughat 7ta houma b 7erf kbir: `Moroccan`, `Arabic`, `English`. W tfekri: f lingliziya ma kaynch jomla bla fi3l — \"ana men Casa\" = `I am from Casablanca`, dima b `am`!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"\"Hiya\" b lingliziya = ?","options":["she","he","we","they"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`she` = hiya. `he` = howa. `we` = 7na. `they` = houma."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ from Morocco.","options":["am","is","are"],"answer":"am","hint_da":"M3a `I` dima…","explain_da":"`I am from Morocco.` (wla `I'm`). M3a `I` dima `am`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"She is from Spain.","question_da":"Sem3i. Mnin hiya?","options":["Men Sbanya","Men Fransa","Men Masr","Men Ingeltera"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Spain` = Sbanya. `France` = Fransa. `Egypt` = Masr. `England` = Ingeltera."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lblad b lingliziya m3a smiytha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"Spain","da":"Sbanya","emoji":"🇪🇸"},{"en":"France","da":"Fransa","emoji":"🇫🇷"},{"en":"England","da":"Ingeltera","emoji":"🇬🇧"},{"en":"Egypt","da":"Masr","emoji":"🇪🇬"},{"en":"Morocco","da":"Lmeghrib","emoji":"🇲🇦"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Omar and Ali ___ students.","options":["are","is","am"],"answer":"are","hint_da":"Omar w Ali = houma (`they`).","explain_da":"Jouj dyal nnas = `they` → `are`. `Omar and Ali are students.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Where ___ you from?","question_da":"Kemmli so2al.","options":["are","is","am","be"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Where are you from?` = mnin nti? M3a `you` dima `are`."},{"type":"order","words":["is","Where","she","from?"],"answer":"Where is she from?","da":"Mnin hiya?"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"We aren't from Rabat. We're from Fes.","question_da":"Sem3i. Mnin houma?","options":["Men Fes","Men Rabat","Men Casa","Men Marrakech"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`We aren't from Rabat` = 7na machi men Rabat. `We're from Fes` = 7na men Fes."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Yes, I'm.\" is a correct short answer.","statement_da":"`Yes, I'm.` jawab 9sir s7i7.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! F ljawab b `Yes` ma kan9essrouch l fi3l: `Yes, I am.`"},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Are you Moroccan?","da":"Wach nti meghribiya?","explain_da":"So2al: l fi3l `Are` f lewwel, men ba3d `you`. `Moroccan` kaytkteb b 7erf kbir."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Tom isn't English. He ___ American.","answers":["is"],"hint_da":"Howa = `he` → achmen fi3l?","explain_da":"`He is American.` M3a `he`, `she`, `it` → `is`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Howa machi men Fransa.","answers":["He isn't from France.","He is not from France.","He's not from France."],"hint_en":"He ... from ...","explain_da":"`He isn't from France.` — `isn't` = `is not` = machi."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Is Sarah from Canada?","question_da":"Sarah men Canada. Khtari ljawab l9sir ss7i7.","options":["Yes, she is.","Yes, she are.","Yes, I am.","Yes, she's."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Sarah = `she` → `Yes, she is.` Ma kan9essrouch f ljawab b `Yes`."},{"type":"order","words":["not","I'm","Moroccan.","Spanish,","I'm"],"answer":"I'm not Spanish, I'm Moroccan.","da":"Ana machi sbenyouliya, ana meghribiya."},{"type":"translate","da":"7na machi men Marrakech.","answers":["We aren't from Marrakech.","We are not from Marrakech.","We're not from Marrakech."],"hint_en":"We ... from ...","explain_da":"`We aren't` = `we are not` = 7na machi."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"I'm Moroccan. I'm from Casablanca and I speak Arabic.","da":"Ana meghribiya. Ana men Casa w kanhder l3arbiya.","pron":"aïm mo-ro-kan. aïm from ka-sa-blan-ka and aï spik a-ra-bik"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Students from many countries","title_da":"Tlamed men bzzaf dyal lbouldan","emoji":"🌍","text_en":"Hello! My name is Nouha and I'm from Morocco. I'm a student in an English class in Casablanca. The students in my class are from many countries. Sarah is from Canada. She's Canadian and she speaks English and French. Tom is American. He's from Chicago. Carlos and Ana are from Spain. They're Spanish. Our teacher, Mr. Brown, is English. He's from London. We are not from the same country, but we are friends. I'm Moroccan and I speak Arabic. My English is not very good, but I am a good student!","text_da":"Salam! Smiyti Nouha w ana men lmeghrib. Ana taliba f 9ism dyal lingliziya f Casa. Ttlamed f l9ism dyali men bzzaf dyal lbouldan. Sarah men Canada. Hiya kanadiya w kathder lingliziya w lfransawiya. Tom amiriki. Howa men Chicago. Carlos w Ana men Sbanya. Houma sbenyouliyin. L'oustad dyalna, ssi Brown, ngliz. Howa men London. 7na machi men nefs lblad, walakin 7na s7ab. Ana meghribiya w kanhder l3arbiya. Lingliziya dyali machi mzyana bzzaf, walakin ana taliba mzyana!","glossary":[{"en":"many","da":"bzzaf dyal"},{"en":"countries","da":"bouldan (we7da: `country` = blad)"},{"en":"Canadian","da":"kanadi / kanadiya"},{"en":"speaks","da":"kathder / kayhder"},{"en":"the same","da":"nefs"},{"en":"friends","da":"s7ab"},{"en":"very","da":"bzzaf"},{"en":"good","da":"mzyan / mzyana"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Mnin Tom?","options":["Men Amérika (Chicago)","Men Canada","Men Sbanya","Men London"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Tom is American. He's from Chicago.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Carlos and Ana are Spanish.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"Carlos and Ana are from Spain. They're Spanish.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chkoun kayhder lfransawiya?","options":["Sarah","Tom","Carlos","Mr. Brown"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"She's Canadian and she speaks English and French.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Mr. Brown is American.","statement_da":"Ssi Brown amiriki.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"Our teacher, Mr. Brown, is English. He's from London.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F lotil f Marrakech","emoji":"🏨","pre_da":"Amina khddama f lotil f Marrakech. Wa7ed ssiyed jdid wsel. Sem3i mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: mnin ssi Rossi? W mnin Amina?","lines":[{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Good evening, sir. Welcome to Hotel Atlas. What's your name, please?","da":"Msa lkhir, a ssi. Mer7ba bik f lotil Atlas. Chno smiytek, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Rossi","en":"Good evening. I'm Marco Rossi.","da":"Msa lkhir. Ana Marco Rossi."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Thank you. Are you Spanish, Mr. Rossi?","da":"Choukran. Wach nta sbenyouli, a ssi Rossi?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Rossi","en":"No, I'm not. I'm Italian. I'm from Rome.","da":"La. Ana talyani. Ana men Roma."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Oh, Rome is a beautiful city! Is this your first time in Morocco?","da":"Wah, Roma mdina zwina! Wach hadi awwel merra lik f lmeghrib?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Rossi","en":"No, it isn't. I'm here every year.","da":"La. Ana kanji hna kol 3am."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Wonderful! Your English is very good.","da":"Ra2i3! Lingliziya dyalek mzyana bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Mr. Rossi","en":"Thank you. And you? Are you from Marrakech?","da":"Choukran. W nti? Wach nti men Marrakech?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"No, I'm not. I'm from Agadir, but I'm here for work.","da":"La. Ana men Agadir, walakin ana hna 3la 9bel lkhedma."},{"speaker":"Mr. Rossi","en":"Nice! Thank you, Amina. Good night.","da":"Zwin! Choukran, Amina. Layla sa3ida."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno jinsiyat ssi Rossi?","options":["Talyani","Sbenyouli","Fransawi","Meghribi"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"No, I'm not. I'm Italian. I'm from Rome.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I'm from Agadir, but I'm here for work.","question_da":"Sem3i. Mnin Amina?","options":["Men Agadir","Men Marrakech","Men Roma","Men Casa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm from Agadir` = ana men Agadir. Hiya f Marrakech ghir 3la 9bel lkhedma (`for work`)."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"This is the first time in Morocco for Mr. Rossi.","statement_da":"Hadi awwel merra l ssi Rossi f lmeghrib.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"No, it isn't. I'm here every year.\" = kanji kol 3am."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach Amina f Marrakech?","options":["3la 9bel lkhedma","3la 9bel l9raya","3la 9bel l3otla","3la 9bel l3a2ila"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm here for work.\" — `work` = lkhedma."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Where are you from?","da":"Mnin nti?","pron":"wér ar you from"},{"target_en":"I'm from Morocco. I'm Moroccan.","da":"Ana men lmeghrib. Ana meghribiya.","pron":"aïm from mo-ro-ko. aïm mo-ro-kan"},{"target_en":"She's from Spain. She isn't French.","da":"Hiya men Sbanya. Machi fransawiya.","pron":"chiz from spéyn. chi i-zent fréntch"},{"target_en":"Are you a student? Yes, I am.","da":"Wach nti taliba? Ah.","pron":"ar you a stiou-dent? yès, aï am"},{"target_en":"We aren't from Rabat.","da":"7na machi men Rabat.","pron":"wi arnt from ra-bat"},{"target_en":"I speak Arabic and a little English.","da":"Kanhder l3arbiya w chwiya dyal lingliziya.","pron":"aï spik a-ra-bik and a li-teul in-glich"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"F lmatar","context_da":"Nti f lmatar f London. Lboulisi dyal l7odoud ghadi ysewlek chi as2ila. Jawbi b jomal 9sira w wad7a. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning. Passport, please. What's your name?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir. Lpaspor, 3afak. Chno smiytek?","expect_keywords":["my name is","i am","i'm","nouha"],"sample_en":"My name is Nouha Alami."},{"bot_en":"Where are you from?","bot_da":"Mnin nti?","expect_keywords":["from","morocco","moroccan","casablanca","rabat"],"sample_en":"I'm from Morocco. I'm Moroccan."},{"bot_en":"Are you a student or a tourist?","bot_da":"Wach nti taliba wla sayi7a (`tourist`)?","expect_keywords":["student","tourist","i am","i'm"],"sample_en":"I'm a tourist."},{"bot_en":"Is this your first time in England?","bot_da":"Wach hadi awwel merra lik f Ingeltera?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","it is","it isn't","first time"],"sample_en":"Yes, it is. It's my first time."},{"bot_en":"OK. Welcome to England! Have a nice day.","bot_da":"Wakha. Mer7ba bik f Ingeltera! Nhar zwin.","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","bye","goodbye","you too"],"sample_en":"Thank you very much! Goodbye."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ana w sa7bti","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal b lingliziya: mnin nti, chno jinsiytek, achmen logha kathedri. Men ba3d ktbi 3la sa7ba wla sa7eb (wla chi wa7ed men l3a2ila): mnin howa wla hiya, w achmen logha kayhder. Sta3mli `am`, `is`, `are` w `isn't`.","helper_en":["I am from ...","I'm Moroccan.","I speak ...","My friend ... is from ...","He/She is ..."],"min_words":20,"keywords":["from","moroccan","speak"],"model_en":"My name is Nouha. I'm from Casablanca, in Morocco. I'm Moroccan and I speak Arabic and a little English. My friend Sarah is from Canada. She's Canadian. She isn't a student, she is a nurse. We are friends."}},{"id":"l04","order":4,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"👨‍👩‍👧","title_en":"My family","title_da":"L3a2ila dyali","goals_da":["Tsemmi l'afrad dyal l3a2ila: `mother`, `father`, `brother`, `sister`…","Tsta3mli `my`, `your`, `his`, `her`, `our`, `their` w `'s` (`Sara's brother`)","T9eddmi nnas: `This is my brother.` / `These are my parents.` w tsewli `Who is this?`","Tsewli w tjawbi: `How many brothers do you have?` — `I have two.`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'afrad dyal l3a2ila (family members)","body_da":"`Family` = l3a2ila. Ha l'afrad dyal l3a2ila b lingliziya:\n\n- `mother` (`mom`) = lwalida / mmi\n- `father` (`dad`) = lwalid / bba\n- `parents` = lwalidin (mmi w bba bjouj)\n- `brother` = khou (khouya)\n- `sister` = khet (khti)\n- `son` = lweld (dyali)\n- `daughter` = lbent (dyali)\n- `children` = lwlad / ddrari (wa7ed: `child`)\n- `husband` = rrajel (dyal lmra)\n- `wife` = lmra (dyal rrajel)\n- `grandmother` = jedda / l7enna\n- `grandfather` = jedd\n- `uncle` = 3emm wla khal\n- `aunt` = 3emma wla khala\n- `cousin` = weld / bent 3emm wla khal\n\n**Lfar9 m3a darija:** 7na kanfer9o bin 3emmi w khali, w bin 3emmti w khalti. F lingliziya kelma we7da: `uncle` l rrajel, `aunt` l lmra — sahla! W `cousin` kadkhol l lweld w lbent bjouj.\n\n`Brothers and sisters` = lkhout (lwlad w lbnat). `My family is big.` = l3a2ila dyali kbira.\n\n**Nnot9:** `th` f `mother`, `father`, `brother` kat9ra b lsan bin ssnan, bhal `the` — ma kaynch \"z\" w ma kaynch \"d\".","examples":[{"en":"This is my mother.","da":"Hadi mmi.","pron":"this iz maï ma-theur"},{"en":"My father is from Fes.","da":"Bba men Fes.","pron":"maï fa-theur iz from fés"},{"en":"I have two brothers and one sister.","da":"3ndi jouj khout w khet we7da.","pron":"aï hav tou bra-theurz and wan sis-teur"},{"en":"My grandmother is in Marrakech.","da":"Jeddti f Marrakech.","pron":"maï grand-ma-theur iz in ma-ra-kéch"},{"en":"Our children are students.","da":"Wladna tlamed.","pron":"awr tchil-dren ar stiou-dents"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"my, your, his, her, our, their — dyali, dyalek, dyalo…","body_da":"F darija kan9oulo \"khouya\" wla \"lkhou dyali\", \"ddar dyalek\", \"lwlad dyalhom\". F lingliziya, lkelma dyal lmilkiya (dyali, dyalek…) **kadji 9bel l'ism**, w ma katbeddelch m3a lwa7ed w lbzzaf:\n\n- `my` = dyali → `my brother` = khouya\n- `your` = dyalek / dyalkom → `your sister` = khtek\n- `his` = dyalo (dyal rajel) → `his wife` = mrato\n- `her` = dyalha (dyal mra) → `her husband` = rajelha\n- `its` = dyalo / dyalha (dyal 7aja) → `its name` = smiyto\n- `our` = dyalna → `our house` = darna\n- `their` = dyalhom → `their children` = wladhom\n\n**Redi lbal l `his` / `her`:** khtari 3la 7sab **lmalik** (li 3ndo l7aja), machi 3la 7sab l7aja. Khou Omar → Omar rajel → `his brother`. Khou Sara → Sara mra → `her brother`. (F darija 7ta 7na: khouh / khouha!)\n\n**Ma tkheltich:** `your` (dyalek) w `you're` (= `you are`) kaytsem3o b7al b7al, walakin lma3na mkhtalef. W `his` (dyalo) machi `he's` (= `he is`).","examples":[{"en":"My mother is a teacher.","da":"Mmi oustada.","pron":"maï ma-theur iz a ti-tcheur"},{"en":"Her name is Fatima.","da":"Smiytha Fatima.","pron":"heur néym iz fa-ti-ma"},{"en":"His brother is in Rabat.","da":"Khouh f Rabat.","pron":"hiz bra-theur iz in ra-bat"},{"en":"Our house is in Casablanca.","da":"Darna f Casa.","pron":"awr haws iz in ka-sa-blan-ka"},{"en":"Their children are young.","da":"Wladhom sghar.","pron":"thér tchil-dren ar yang"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lmilkiya b 's: Sara's brother","body_da":"Bach n9oulo \"khou Sara\" (lkhou dyal Sara), kanzido **`'s`** l smiyt lmalik: `Sara's brother`.\n\nRedi lbal l **ttartib**: f darija kan9oulo \"khou **Sara**\" (l7aja lewwla, lmalik men ba3d). F lingliziya l3eks: \"**Sara's** brother\" (lmalik lewwel, l7aja men ba3d).\n\n- `Omar's wife` = mrat Omar\n- `my mother's name` = smiyt mmi\n- `Nouha's family` = 3a2ilt Nouha\n- `my sister's children` = wlad khti\n\nHad `'s` kaytkteb b7al `is` m9essra (`She's`), walakin lma3na mkhtalef: `Sara's brother` = khou Sara (dyal) / `Sara's a teacher` = `Sara is a teacher`. Lkelma li men ba3d hiya li katbyen: ila men ba3d `'s` kayn ism (`brother`, `wife`, `name`…) → ma3naha \"dyal\".","examples":[{"en":"This is Sara's brother.","da":"Hada khou Sara.","pron":"this iz sa-raz bra-theur"},{"en":"My mother's name is Khadija.","da":"Smiyt mmi Khadija.","pron":"maï ma-theurz néym iz kha-di-ja"},{"en":"Omar's wife is from Tangier.","da":"Mrat Omar men Tanja.","pron":"o-marz waïf iz from tan-djir"},{"en":"Where is Nouha's family from?","da":"Mnin l3a2ila dyal Nouha?","pron":"wér iz nou-haz fa-mi-li from"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"This is… / These are… — Who is this? — How many…?","body_da":"Bach t9eddmi chi wa7ed l nnas: `This is my sister Meryem.` = hadi khti Meryem. `This` l wa7ed (hada / hadi), `these` l bzzaf (hadou): `These are my parents.` = hadou lwalidin dyali.\n\nBach tsewli 3la chi wa7ed (f tswira matalan): `Who is this?` = chkoun hada / hadi? (`who` = chkoun). Ljawab: `This is my uncle.` wla `It's my uncle.`\n\nBach tsewli ch7al: `How many brothers do you have?` = ch7al 3ndek men khout? (`how many` = ch7al, `have` = 3nd). Ljawab:\n\n- `I have two brothers.` = 3ndi jouj khout.\n- `I have one sister.` = 3ndi khet we7da.\n- `I don't have any brothers.` = ma 3ndich khout. (`any` hna ma katterjemch)\n\n7efdi had ljomal b7al ma homa — l fi3l `have` ghadi nfehmouh mzyan f ddrous jayin.","examples":[{"en":"This is my father, Hassan.","da":"Hada bba, Hassan.","pron":"this iz maï fa-theur, ha-san"},{"en":"These are my children, Adam and Lina.","da":"Hadou wladi, Adam w Lina.","pron":"thiz ar maï tchil-dren, a-dam and li-na"},{"en":"Who is this? — It's my aunt.","da":"Chkoun hadi? — Hadi khalti.","pron":"hou iz this? its maï ant"},{"en":"How many sisters do you have? — I have one sister.","da":"Ch7al 3ndek men khwatat? — 3ndi khet we7da.","pron":"haw mé-ni sis-teurz dou you hav? aï hav wan sis-teur"},{"en":"This is Sara's husband, Karim.","da":"Hada rajel Sara, Karim.","pron":"this iz sa-raz haz-band, ka-rim"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Wasfi nnas chwiya: tall, young, old, married, single","body_da":"Bach twesfi nnas chwiya, kansta3mlo `to be` + ssifa (`adjective` = lkelma li katwsef):\n\n- `tall` = twil / twila — `short` = 9sir / 9sira\n- `young` = sghir / sghira f l3mer — `old` = kbir / kbira f l3mer\n- `married` = mzewwej / mzewwja — `single` = 3azeb / 3azba (machi mzewwj)\n- `nice` = dérif / dérifa\n\nMatalan: `My brother is tall.` = khouya twil. `My grandmother is old.` = jeddti kbira f l3mer.\n\n**Lfar9 m3a darija:** ssifa f lingliziya **ma katbeddelch** m3a rrajel w lmra, wla m3a lwa7ed w lbzzaf: `tall` l khouya, l khti, w l khouti kamlin! (F darija: twil, twila, twal.)\n\nSo2al: `Are you married?` = wach nti mzewwja? → `Yes, I am.` / `No, I'm not. I'm single.`","examples":[{"en":"My sister is young. She's a student.","da":"Khti sghira. Hiya taliba.","pron":"maï sis-teur iz yang. chiz a stiou-dent"},{"en":"My grandfather is old.","da":"Jeddi kbir f l3mer.","pron":"maï grand-fa-theur iz old"},{"en":"Is your brother married? — No, he's single.","da":"Wach khouk mzewwej? — La, howa 3azeb.","pron":"iz your bra-theur ma-rid? no, hiz sin-geul"},{"en":"Omar's father is tall.","da":"Bba Omar twil.","pron":"o-marz fa-theur iz tol"},{"en":"Her parents are very nice.","da":"Lwalidin dyalha drraf bzzaf.","pron":"heur pé-rents ar vé-ri naïs"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"mother","da":"lwalida / mmi","emoji":"👩","pron":"ma-theur","example_en":"My mother is from Fes.","example_da":"Mmi men Fes."},{"en":"father","da":"lwalid / bba","emoji":"👨","pron":"fa-theur","example_en":"My father is tall.","example_da":"Bba twil."},{"en":"parents","da":"lwalidin","emoji":"👫","pron":"pé-rents","example_en":"My parents are in Marrakech.","example_da":"Lwalidin dyali f Marrakech."},{"en":"brother","da":"khou (khouya)","emoji":"👦","pron":"bra-theur","example_en":"This is my brother Adam.","example_da":"Hada khouya Adam."},{"en":"sister","da":"khet (khti)","emoji":"👧","pron":"sis-teur","example_en":"Her sister is a nurse.","example_da":"Khetha fermliya."},{"en":"husband","da":"rrajel (dyal lmra)","emoji":"🤵","pron":"haz-band","example_en":"Sara's husband is a doctor.","example_da":"Rajel Sara tbib."},{"en":"wife","da":"lmra (dyal rrajel)","emoji":"👰","pron":"waïf","example_en":"His wife is Moroccan.","example_da":"Mrato meghribiya."},{"en":"son","da":"lweld (dyali)","emoji":"🧒","pron":"san","example_en":"Their son is a student.","example_da":"Weldhom talib."},{"en":"daughter","da":"lbent (dyali)","emoji":"👧🏻","pron":"do-teur","example_en":"Our daughter is young.","example_da":"Bentna sghira."},{"en":"children","da":"lwlad / ddrari","emoji":"👶","pron":"tchil-dren","example_en":"How many children do you have?","example_da":"Ch7al 3ndek men wlad?"},{"en":"grandmother","da":"jedda / l7enna","emoji":"👵","pron":"grand-ma-theur","example_en":"My grandmother is old.","example_da":"Jeddti kbira f l3mer."},{"en":"grandfather","da":"jedd","emoji":"👴","pron":"grand-fa-theur","example_en":"Omar's grandfather is from Tangier.","example_da":"Jedd Omar men Tanja."},{"en":"uncle","da":"3emm / khal","emoji":"🧔","pron":"an-keul","example_en":"My uncle is in Spain.","example_da":"3emmi f Sbanya."},{"en":"aunt","da":"3emma / khala","emoji":"👩‍🦱","pron":"ant","example_en":"Her aunt is a teacher.","example_da":"Khaltha oustada."},{"en":"cousin","da":"weld / bent 3emm wla khal","emoji":"🧑","pron":"ka-zin","example_en":"This is my cousin Yassine.","example_da":"Hada weld 3emmi Yassine."},{"en":"married","da":"mzewwej / mzewwja","emoji":"💍","pron":"ma-rid","example_en":"Is your sister married? — Yes, she is.","example_da":"Wach khtek mzewwja? — Ah."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Tswira dyal l3a2ila","context_da":"Nouha kaywerri l Sarah tswira dyal l3a2ila dyalha f lportable.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Oh, is this a photo of your family?","da":"Wah, wach hadi tswira dyal l3a2ila dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, it is. This is my mother, Khadija, and this is my father, Hassan.","da":"Ah. Hadi mmi, Khadija, w hada bba, Hassan."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Your mother is very nice! And who is this?","da":"Mmek dérifa bzzaf! W chkoun hada?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"This is my brother Youssef. He's a student in Rabat.","da":"Hada khouya Youssef. Howa talib f Rabat."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"How many brothers do you have?","da":"Ch7al 3ndek men khout?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I have two brothers and one sister. This is my sister Meryem.","da":"3ndi jouj khout w khet we7da. Hadi khti Meryem."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Is she married?","da":"Wach hiya mzewwja?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, she is. This is her husband, Karim, and these are their children, Adam and Lina.","da":"Ah. Hada rajelha, Karim, w hadou wladhom, Adam w Lina."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"What a nice family! I have one sister. Her name is Emma. She's in Canada with our parents.","da":"Ya 3a2ila zwina! Ana 3ndi khet we7da. Smiytha Emma. Hiya f Canada m3a lwalidin dyalna."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Oh, nice! Your parents are in Canada, and you are here in Morocco!","da":"Wah, zwin! Lwalidin dyalek f Canada, w nti hna f lmeghrib!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`his` wla `her`? Choufi chkoun **lmalik** (li 3ndo l7aja): ila rajel → `his`, ila mra → `her`. \"Mrat Omar\" = `Omar's wife` = `his wife`. \"Rajel Sara\" = `Sara's husband` = `her husband`. W ma tkheltich `your` (dyalek) m3a `you're` (`you are`): `Your sister is nice.` / `You're nice.`"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"\"Khti\" b lingliziya = ?","options":["my sister","my brother","my mother","my aunt"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`sister` = khet → `my sister` = khti. `brother` = khou, `mother` = lwalida, `aunt` = 3emma / khala."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lkelma b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"mother","da":"lwalida","emoji":"👩"},{"en":"father","da":"lwalid","emoji":"👨"},{"en":"brother","da":"khou","emoji":"👦"},{"en":"grandmother","da":"jedda","emoji":"👵"},{"en":"uncle","da":"3emm / khal","emoji":"🧔"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"This is my father.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chkoun hada?","options":["Bba (lwalid)","Mmi (lwalida)","Khouya","3emmi"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`father` = lwalid / bba. `mother` = lwalida. `brother` = khou. `uncle` = 3emm."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"This is my sister. ___ name is Meryem.","options":["Her","His","Their"],"answer":"Her","hint_da":"Khti = mra → ?","explain_da":"Khti mra → `her` (dyalha). `his` l rajel, `their` l bzzaf dyal nnas."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Omar and Ali are brothers. ___ father is a doctor.","options":["Their","His","Our"],"answer":"Their","hint_da":"Omar w Ali = houma → dyalhom.","explain_da":"Omar w Ali = `they` → `their` (dyalhom). `Their father` = bbahom."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Who is this? — ___ my uncle.","question_da":"Kemmli ljawab.","options":["This is","These are","This are","These is"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Wa7ed → `This is`. Bzzaf → `These are`."},{"type":"order","words":["are","These","my","parents."],"answer":"These are my parents.","da":"Hadou lwalidin dyali."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I have two brothers and one sister.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al 3ndo men khout (wlad)?","options":["2","1","3","4"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`two brothers` = jouj khout (wlad). `one sister` = khet we7da."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Sara's brother\" means: Sara is a brother.","statement_da":"`Sara's brother` kat3ni: Sara hiya lkhou.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `Sara's brother` = khou Sara (lkhou dyal Sara). `'s` hna = dyal."},{"type":"translate","da":"Hada rajel Meryem.","answers":["This is Meryem's husband.","It's Meryem's husband.","This is the husband of Meryem."],"hint_en":"This is ...'s ...","explain_da":"`Meryem's husband` = rajel Meryem. Lmalik (Meryem) lewwel, men ba3d `'s`, men ba3d l7aja (`husband`)."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"How many sisters do you have?","da":"Ch7al 3ndek men khwatat?","explain_da":"Sem3i: `How` – `many` – `sisters` – `do` – `you` – `have`. `How many` = ch7al."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khadija mzewwja w 3ndha tlata dyal lwlad. Achmen jomla s7i7a?","options":["She is married.","She is single.","He is married.","She are married."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Khadija mra → `she`. Mzewwja = `married`. `single` = 3azba. M3a `she` → `is`."},{"type":"order","words":["brother","Her","is","tall","and","young."],"answer":"Her brother is tall and young.","da":"Khouha twil w sghir f l3mer."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Omar is married. ___ wife is from Fes.","answers":["His","his"],"hint_da":"Omar rajel → dyalo = ?","explain_da":"Omar rajel → `his` (dyalo). `His wife` = mrato. Redi lbal: machi `he's`!"},{"type":"translate","da":"Lwalidin dyali men Fes.","answers":["My parents are from Fes.","My parents are from Fez."],"hint_en":"My ... are from ...","explain_da":"`parents` = lwalidin (bzzaf) → `are`. `My parents are from Fes.`"},{"type":"speak","target_en":"This is my family. These are my parents and this is my brother.","da":"Hadi l3a2ila dyali. Hadou lwalidin dyali w hada khouya.","pron":"this iz maï fa-mi-li. thiz ar maï pé-rents and this iz maï bra-theur"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Sarah's family","title_da":"L3a2ila dyal Sarah","emoji":"👨‍👩‍👧‍👦","text_en":"My friend Sarah is from Canada. This is her family. Her father's name is David. He's from Toronto and he's a teacher. Her mother, Anna, is a doctor. She isn't Canadian, she's Italian! Sarah's sister is Emma. Emma is young: she is nineteen. She is tall and very nice. Emma isn't married, she's single. Sarah's grandmother and grandfather are in Italy. They're old, but they're strong. Sarah's family is small, but they are very happy!","text_da":"Sa7bti Sarah men Canada. Hadi l3a2ila dyalha. Smiyt bbaha David. Howa men Toronto w howa oustad. Mmha, Anna, tbiba. Hiya machi kanadiya, hiya talyaniya! Khet Sarah hiya Emma. Emma sghira: 3ndha ts3tach l3am. Hiya twila w dérifa bzzaf. Emma machi mzewwja, hiya 3azba. Jedda w jedd Sarah f Italya. Houma kbar f l3mer, walakin houma 9wiyin. L3a2ila dyal Sarah sghira, walakin houma fer7anin bzzaf!","glossary":[{"en":"friend","da":"sa7eb / sa7ba"},{"en":"doctor","da":"tbib / tbiba"},{"en":"Italian","da":"talyani / talyaniya"},{"en":"nineteen","da":"ts3tach (19)"},{"en":"Italy","da":"Italya"},{"en":"strong","da":"9wi / 9wiya"},{"en":"small","da":"sghir / sghira"},{"en":"happy","da":"fer7an / fer7ana"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khedmet mmi Sarah (Anna)?","options":["Tbiba","Oustada","Fermliya","Taliba"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Her mother, Anna, is a doctor.\" = mmha tbiba."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Anna is Italian.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"She isn't Canadian, she's Italian!\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chkoun Emma?","options":["Khet Sarah","Mmi Sarah","Bent Sarah","Khalt Sarah"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Sarah's sister is Emma.\" = khet Sarah hiya Emma."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Emma is married.","statement_da":"Emma mzewwja.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"Emma isn't married, she's single.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F l3ers","emoji":"💒","pre_da":"Omar 3red Tom l l3ers dyal khto. Sem3i mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: chkoun kay9eddem Omar l Tom? W ch7al 3nd Omar men khout?","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Tom, welcome! This is my father, Ahmed, and this is my mother, Fatima.","da":"Tom, mer7ba! Hada bba, Ahmed, w hadi mmi, Fatima."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Nice to meet you! Omar, who is this?","da":"Metcherref b m3erftkom! Omar, chkoun hadi?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"This is my sister Salma. It's her wedding today!","da":"Hadi khti Salma. Lyouma l3ers dyalha!"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"She's beautiful! And is this her husband?","da":"Zwina! W wach hada rajelha?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, it is. His name is Hamza. He's from Agadir.","da":"Ah. Smiyto Hamza. Howa men Agadir."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"How many brothers and sisters do you have, Omar?","da":"Ch7al 3ndek men khout, Omar?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I have one sister, Salma, and three brothers. Look, these are my brothers: Ali, Mehdi and Sami.","da":"3ndi khet we7da, Salma, w tlata dyal lkhout. Chof, hadou khouti: Ali, Mehdi w Sami."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Wow, a big family! Are they married?","da":"Wow, 3a2ila kbira! Wach houma mzewwjin?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Ali is married. His wife is the tall woman with the children. Mehdi and Sami are single.","da":"Ali mzewwej. Mrato hiya dik lmra ttwila li m3a ddrari. Mehdi w Sami 3azbin."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Thank you for the invitation, Omar. Your family is very nice!","da":"Choukran 3la l3rada, Omar. L3a2ila dyalek dérifa bzzaf!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chkoun Salma?","options":["Khet Omar","Mrat Omar","Mmi Omar","Bent Omar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"This is my sister Salma.\" = hadi khti Salma."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I have one sister and three brothers.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al 3nd Omar men khout (wlad)?","options":["3","1","2","4"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`three brothers` = tlata dyal lkhout. `one sister` = khet we7da."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Hamza is from Agadir.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"His name is Hamza. He's from Agadir.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chkoun mzewwej men khout Omar?","options":["Ali","Mehdi","Sami","Tom"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Ali is married. Mehdi and Sami are single.\""}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"This is my mother and this is my father.","da":"Hadi mmi w hada bba.","pron":"this iz maï ma-theur and this iz maï fa-theur"},{"target_en":"These are my parents.","da":"Hadou lwalidin dyali.","pron":"thiz ar maï pé-rents"},{"target_en":"I have two brothers and one sister.","da":"3ndi jouj khout w khet we7da.","pron":"aï hav tou bra-theurz and wan sis-teur"},{"target_en":"Her husband is a doctor.","da":"Rajelha tbib.","pron":"heur haz-band iz a dok-teur"},{"target_en":"Who is this? It's my uncle.","da":"Chkoun hada? Hada 3emmi.","pron":"hou iz this? its maï an-keul"},{"target_en":"Is your sister married? Yes, she is.","da":"Wach khtek mzewwja? Ah.","pron":"iz your sis-teur ma-rid? yès, chi iz"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Sarah kattsewwel 3la l3a2ila dyalek","context_da":"Sa7btek Sarah bghat t3ref l3a2ila dyalek. Jawbi 3la l'as2ila dyalha b jomal 9sira. 9oli l7a9i9a wla khtar3i — lmohim thedri b lingliziya!","turns":[{"bot_en":"Nouha, tell me about your family. How many brothers do you have?","bot_da":"Nouha, hedri liya 3la l3a2ila dyalek. Ch7al 3ndek men khout?","expect_keywords":["i have","brother","brothers","one","two","three","don't have","no brothers"],"sample_en":"I have two brothers."},{"bot_en":"And how many sisters do you have?","bot_da":"W ch7al 3ndek men khwatat?","expect_keywords":["i have","sister","sisters","one","two","three","don't have","no sisters"],"sample_en":"I have one sister."},{"bot_en":"What's your mother's name?","bot_da":"Chno smiyt mmek?","expect_keywords":["her name is","my mother's name","name","she is","she's","my mother is"],"sample_en":"Her name is Khadija."},{"bot_en":"Where is your father from?","bot_da":"Mnin bbak?","expect_keywords":["he is from","he's from","from","my father is"],"sample_en":"He's from Fes."},{"bot_en":"Is your family in Casablanca?","bot_da":"Wach l3a2ila dyalek f Casa?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","it is","it isn't","they are","in"],"sample_en":"Yes, it is. My parents are in Casablanca."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"L3a2ila dyali","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal 3la l3a2ila dyalek b lingliziya: ch7al 3ndek men khout w khwatat, smiyt mmek w bbak, mnin houma, w wesfi wa7ed menhom (`tall`, `young`, `married`…). Sta3mli `my`, `his`, `her` w `their`.","helper_en":["I have ... brothers and ... sisters.","My mother's name is ...","My father is from ...","My brother is ...","This is my family!"],"min_words":25,"keywords":["my","mother","father"],"model_en":"This is my family. I have two brothers and one sister. My mother's name is Khadija. She is from Casablanca. My father, Hassan, is from Fes. He is a teacher. My brother Youssef is tall and young. My sister Meryem is married. Her husband is a doctor."}},{"id":"l05","order":5,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"🔢","title_en":"Numbers 20–100, age & prices","title_da":"L'ar9am 20–100, l3mer w taman","goals_da":["T3eddi men 20 7ta l 100 b lingliziya","Tsewli 3la l3mer b `How old are you?` w tjawbi `I'm 25 years old`","Tsewli 3la taman b `How much is it?` w tfehmi ljawab b derhem, euro wla dollar","T9oli w tfehmi ra9m ttilifoun, ra9m b ra9m"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'ar9am men 20 7ta l 100","body_da":"F dars 2 t3ellemti l'ar9am men 0 7ta l 20. Daba ghadi nkemmlo 7ta l 100.\n\nL3charat (20, 30, 40…) kolhom kaysaliw b `-ty`:\n\n- `twenty` = 20 (3echrin)\n- `thirty` = 30 (tlatin)\n- `forty` = 40 (reb3in) — chofi: makaynach `u` bhal f `four`!\n- `fifty` = 50 (khemsin)\n- `sixty` = 60 (settin)\n- `seventy` = 70 (seb3in)\n- `eighty` = 80 (tmanin)\n- `ninety` = 90 (tes3in)\n- `a hundred` wla `one hundred` = 100 (mya)\n\nBach ndiro l'ar9am li binathom, kanzido lwa7dat men ba3d l3chara, m3a khatt sghir (-) binathom: `twenty-one` (21), `twenty-two` (22), `thirty-five` (35), `ninety-nine` (99).\n\n**Rdi lbal:** f darija kan9oulo lwa7da 9bel: \"wa7ed w 3echrin\" (1 + 20). F lingliziya l3eks: `twenty-one` (20 + 1). L3chara l'awwla, men ba3d lwa7da.\n\n**Mochkil machhour:** `thirteen` (13) w `thirty` (30) kaytchabho! F 13 kandeghto 3la l'akhir: thir-TIN. F 30 kandeghto 3la l'awwel: THEUR-ti. Nefs chi m3a `fourteen` / `forty`, `fifteen` / `fifty`, `sixteen` / `sixty`.","examples":[{"en":"twenty-one, twenty-two, twenty-three","da":"wa7ed w 3echrin, tnayn w 3echrin, tlata w 3echrin","pron":"twèn-ti-wan, twèn-ti-tou, twèn-ti-thri"},{"en":"forty-five","da":"khemsa w reb3in","pron":"for-ti-faïv"},{"en":"ninety-nine","da":"tes3a w tes3in","pron":"naïn-ti-naïn"},{"en":"My father is sixty.","da":"Bba 3ndo settin 3am.","pron":"maï fa-theur iz siks-ti"},{"en":"a hundred dirhams","da":"myat derhem","pron":"a han-dred di-ramz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"L3mer: How old are you?","body_da":"Bach tsewli 3la l3mer: `How old are you?` = ch7al f 3merek? (7arfiyan: ch7al nti 9dima — walakin machi 3ib, hakka kay9oulouha l'ingliz!)\n\nLjawab b lfi3l `to be` (`am` / `is` / `are`), **machi** b `have`:\n\n- `I am 25.` wla `I'm 25 years old.` = 3ndi 25 3am.\n- `He is 30.` / `She's 42 years old.`\n- `My brother is 19.`\n\n**Rdi lbal:** f darija kan9oulo \"3ndi 25 3am\" b \"3ndi\" (= `have`). F lingliziya **la**! Kan9oulo `I am 25` — b `to be`. `I have 25 years` ✗ ghalet.\n\n`years old` = \"3am f l3mer\". T9edri tzidiha wla t7eydiha: `I'm 25.` w `I'm 25 years old.` bjouj s7a7.\n\nBach tsewli 3la chi wa7ed akhor: `How old is he?` / `How old is she?` / `How old is your mother?`","examples":[{"en":"How old are you?","da":"Ch7al f 3merek?","pron":"haw old ar you"},{"en":"I'm twenty-five years old.","da":"3ndi khemsa w 3echrin 3am.","pron":"aïm twèn-ti-faïv yirz old"},{"en":"How old is your mother?","da":"Ch7al f 3mer mmek?","pron":"haw old iz your ma-theur"},{"en":"She's fifty-three.","da":"3ndha tlata w khemsin 3am.","pron":"chiz fif-ti-thri"},{"en":"My brother is nineteen.","da":"Khouya 3ndo tse3tach 3am.","pron":"maï bra-theur iz naïn-tin"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Taman: How much is it?","body_da":"F ssou9, f l7anout, f l9ehwa… khassek tsewli 3la taman:\n\n- `How much is it?` = bch7al? / ch7al taman?\n- `How much is the tea?` = bch7al atay?\n- `How much are the oranges?` = bch7al llimoun? (`are` 7it bzzaf dyal l7wayj)\n\nLjawab: `It's` + ra9m + lflous:\n\n- `It's thirty dirhams.` = b tlatin derhem.\n- `It's twenty euros.` = b 3echrin euro.\n- `It's five dollars.` = b khemsa dyal ddolar.\n- `It's fifty cents.` = b khemsin santim.\n\nChofi: melli kayn kter men wa7ed kanzido `-s`: `one dirham`, `two dirhams`, `ten euros`. Ghadi nchoufo had l9a3ida mzyan f dars jay.\n\nMelli katkhellsi kat9oli `Here you are.` (= hak). W sserf b lingliziya = `change`: `Your change is ten dirhams.`","examples":[{"en":"How much is it?","da":"Bch7al hada?","pron":"haw match iz it"},{"en":"It's thirty dirhams.","da":"B tlatin derhem.","pron":"its theur-ti di-ramz"},{"en":"How much are the oranges?","da":"Bch7al llimoun?","pron":"haw match ar the o-rin-djiz"},{"en":"They're eight dirhams a kilo.","da":"B tmenya dyal ddrahem lkilo.","pron":"thér éyt di-ramz a ki-lo"},{"en":"Twenty euros, please. Here you are.","da":"3echrin euro, 3afak. Hak.","pron":"twèn-ti you-roz, pliz. hir you ar"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ra9m ttilifoun w How many…?","body_da":"Ra9m ttilifoun f lingliziya kay9al **ra9m b ra9m**, machi jouj b jouj bhal f darija:\n\n- 06 12 34 56 78 → `zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight`\n- Zero t9edri t9oliha `zero` wla `oh` (bhal l7erf O).\n- Melli kayn jouj ar9am kif kif (66), l'ingliz kay9oulo `double six`.\n\nSso2al: `What's your phone number?` = chno ra9m ttilifoun dyalek? Ljawab: `It's 06…` wla `My number is 06…`\n\n`How many…?` = ch7al men…? Kansta3mlouha m3a l7wayj li kan7esbouhom:\n\n- `How many brothers do you have?` = ch7al men khou 3ndek? (t3ellemtiha f dars 4)\n- `How many students are in the class?` = ch7al men talib f l9ism?\n- `How many kilos?` = ch7al men kilo?\n\nW `How much…?` = bch7al? (taman). Matkhelltich binathom: `How much` l taman, `How many` l l3adad.","examples":[{"en":"What's your phone number?","da":"Chno ra9m ttilifoun dyalek?","pron":"wats your fon nam-beur"},{"en":"It's zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight.","da":"Howa 06 12 34 56 78.","pron":"its zi-ro siks, wan tou, thri for, faïv siks, sé-ven éyt"},{"en":"How many students are in the class?","da":"Ch7al men talib f l9ism?","pron":"haw mé-ni stiou-dents ar in the klas"},{"en":"Thirty students.","da":"Tlatin talib.","pron":"theur-ti stiou-dents"},{"en":"How many kilos? — Two kilos, please.","da":"Ch7al men kilo? — Jouj kilo, 3afak.","pron":"haw mé-ni ki-loz — tou ki-loz, pliz"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"twenty","da":"3echrin","emoji":"2️⃣","pron":"twèn-ti","example_en":"I'm twenty years old.","example_da":"3ndi 3echrin 3am."},{"en":"thirty","da":"tlatin","emoji":"3️⃣","pron":"theur-ti","example_en":"My sister is thirty.","example_da":"Khti 3ndha tlatin 3am."},{"en":"forty","da":"reb3in","emoji":"4️⃣","pron":"for-ti","example_en":"Forty dirhams, please.","example_da":"Reb3in derhem, 3afak."},{"en":"fifty","da":"khemsin","emoji":"5️⃣","pron":"fif-ti","example_en":"The bag is fifty dirhams.","example_da":"Ssak b khemsin derhem."},{"en":"sixty","da":"settin","emoji":"6️⃣","pron":"siks-ti","example_en":"My father is sixty-one.","example_da":"Bba 3ndo wa7ed w settin 3am."},{"en":"seventy","da":"seb3in","emoji":"7️⃣","pron":"sé-ven-ti","example_en":"My grandmother is seventy.","example_da":"Jeddati 3ndha seb3in 3am."},{"en":"eighty","da":"tmanin","emoji":"8️⃣","pron":"éy-ti","example_en":"It's eighty euros.","example_da":"B tmanin euro."},{"en":"ninety","da":"tes3in","emoji":"9️⃣","pron":"naïn-ti","example_en":"Ninety, ninety-one, ninety-two.","example_da":"Tes3in, wa7ed w tes3in, tnayn w tes3in."},{"en":"a hundred","da":"mya","emoji":"💯","pron":"a han-dred","example_en":"It's a hundred dirhams.","example_da":"B myat derhem."},{"en":"dirham","da":"derhem","emoji":"💵","pron":"di-ram","example_en":"It's ten dirhams.","example_da":"B 3echra dyal ddrahem."},{"en":"euro","da":"euro (lflous dyal Oroppa)","emoji":"💶","pron":"you-ro","example_en":"The book is fifteen euros.","example_da":"Lktab b khemstach euro."},{"en":"dollar","da":"dollar (lflous dyal Amrika)","emoji":"💲","pron":"do-leur","example_en":"It's five dollars.","example_da":"B khemsa dyal ddolar."},{"en":"cent","da":"santim","emoji":"🪙","pron":"sènt","example_en":"It's fifty cents.","example_da":"B khemsin santim."},{"en":"phone number","da":"ra9m ttilifoun","emoji":"📱","pron":"fon nam-beur","example_en":"My phone number is 06 61 22 33 44.","example_da":"Ra9m ttilifoun dyali howa 06 61 22 33 44."},{"en":"years old","da":"3am (f l3mer)","emoji":"🎂","pron":"yirz old","example_en":"She's forty years old.","example_da":"3ndha reb3in 3am."},{"en":"price","da":"taman","emoji":"🏷️","pron":"praïs","example_en":"It's a good price.","example_da":"Taman mzyan."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"F ssou9: llimoun w lbanan","context_da":"Nouha f ssou9 dyal l7ay dyalha. Katchri llimoun w lbanan men 3nd Hamid, lkhedar.","lines":[{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good morning! How much are the oranges?","da":"Sbah lkhir! Bch7al llimoun?"},{"speaker":"Hamid","en":"Good morning. They're eight dirhams a kilo.","da":"Sbah lkhir. B tmenya dyal ddrahem lkilo."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"And the bananas?","da":"W lbanan?"},{"speaker":"Hamid","en":"Twelve dirhams a kilo.","da":"Tnach derhem lkilo."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"OK. Two kilos of oranges and one kilo of bananas, please.","da":"Wakha. Jouj kilo dyal llimoun w kilo dyal lbanan, 3afak."},{"speaker":"Hamid","en":"That's twenty-eight dirhams.","da":"Hadchi b tmenya w 3echrin derhem."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Here you are. Fifty dirhams.","da":"Hak. Khemsin derhem."},{"speaker":"Hamid","en":"Thank you. Your change: twenty-two dirhams.","da":"Choukran. Sserf dyalek: tnayn w 3echrin derhem."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thanks! Goodbye.","da":"Choukran! Bslama."},{"speaker":"Hamid","en":"Goodbye! Have a nice day.","da":"Bslama! Nhar zwin."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`thirteen` wla `thirty`? Melli kat9oli 13, 14, 15… deghti 3la l'akhir w teddi lwa9t: `thirteen` = thir-TIN (twila). Melli kat9oli 30, 40, 50… deghti 3la lbdaya w khffi l'akhir: `thirty` = THEUR-ti (9sira). W ila ma kontich mti2kkida f ssou9, 9oli ra9m b ra9m: `three zero` = 30. Sahla w madmouna!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo 40 b lingliziya?","options":["forty","fourteen","fifty","four"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`forty` = 40. `fourteen` = 14. `fifty` = 50. `four` = 4. Rdi lbal: `forty` bla `u`!"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"thirty","question_da":"Sem3i mzyan. Achmen ra9m sme3ti?","options":["30","13","33","3"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`thirty` = 30. `thirteen` = 13 — fiha ddeght 3la l'akhir (thir-TIN)."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli ra9m b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"twenty","da":"3echrin (20)","emoji":"2️⃣"},{"en":"fifty","da":"khemsin (50)","emoji":"5️⃣"},{"en":"seventy","da":"seb3in (70)","emoji":"7️⃣"},{"en":"ninety","da":"tes3in (90)","emoji":"9️⃣"},{"en":"a hundred","da":"mya (100)","emoji":"💯"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"How ___ are you? — I'm twenty-five.","options":["old","much","many"],"answer":"old","hint_da":"Ch7al f 3merek?","explain_da":"`How old are you?` = ch7al f 3merek? `How much` = bch7al (taman). `How many` = ch7al men (l3adad)."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's forty-five dirhams.","question_da":"Sem3i. Bch7al?","options":["45 derhem","54 derhem","40 derhem","55 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`forty-five` = 45: `forty` (40) + `five` (5)."},{"type":"order","words":["old","How","is","your","mother?"],"answer":"How old is your mother?","da":"Ch7al f 3mer mmek?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen jomla s7i7a bach t9oli \"3ndi tlatin 3am\"?","options":["I have thirty years.","I'm thirty years old.","I'm thirty year."],"answer":1,"explain_da":"L3mer b `to be`: `I'm thirty years old.` `I have thirty years` ✗ ghalet — f lingliziya makan9oulouch `have` m3a l3mer."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"How ___ is it? — It's twenty dirhams.","answers":["much"],"hint_da":"Bch7al? — sso2al 3la taman","explain_da":"`How much is it?` = bch7al? Kansewlo biha 3la taman."},{"type":"translate","da":"Bba 3ndo settin 3am.","answers":["My father is sixty.","My father is sixty years old.","My father is 60.","My father is 60 years old."],"hint_en":"My father ... sixty ...","explain_da":"`My father is sixty (years old).` — l3mer b `is`, machi b `has`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"She is twenty-one years old.","da":"3ndha wa7ed w 3echrin 3am.","explain_da":"Sem3i mzyan: `twenty-one` = 20 + 1. `years old` = 3am f l3mer."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The word 'fifteen' means 50.","statement_da":"Lkelma `fifteen` kat3ni 50.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `fifteen` = 15. 50 = `fifty`."},{"type":"order","words":["much","How","is","the","tea?"],"answer":"How much is the tea?","da":"Bch7al atay?"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"What's your phone number?","question_da":"Achmen jawab monasib?","options":["I'm twenty-five years old.","It's thirty dirhams.","It's zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight.","I'm from Rabat."],"answer":2,"explain_da":"`What's your phone number?` = chno ra9m ttilifoun dyalek? Ljawab: `It's` + l'ar9am, ra9m b ra9m."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"How much is it? It's ninety dirhams.","da":"Bch7al? B tes3in derhem.","pron":"haw match iz it? its naïn-ti di-ramz"},{"type":"translate","da":"Ch7al f 3mer khouk?","answers":["How old is your brother?","How old's your brother?"],"hint_en":"How ... is your ...?","explain_da":"`How old is your brother?` — `old` l l3mer, `brother` = khou."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Twenty, thirty, ___, fifty.","options":["forty","fourteen","four"],"answer":"forty","hint_da":"20, 30, ?, 50","explain_da":"20, 30, **40**, 50: `twenty`, `thirty`, `forty`, `fifty`."}],"reading":{"title_en":"At the market","title_da":"F ssou9","emoji":"🍊","text_en":"Hello! My name is Nouha. I am twenty-six years old. I live in Rabat with my family. My father is sixty-two and my mother is fifty-eight. I have two brothers: Karim is thirty and Yassine is nineteen. Today I am at the market. The oranges are eight dirhams a kilo and the tomatoes are six dirhams a kilo. I have a hundred dirhams in my bag. My phone number is zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight. Call me!","text_da":"Salam! Smiyti Nouha. 3ndi setta w 3echrin 3am. Kanskon f Rabat m3a l3a2ila dyali. Bba 3ndo tnayn w settin 3am w mmi 3ndha tmenya w khemsin 3am. 3ndi jouj khout: Karim 3ndo tlatin 3am w Yassine 3ndo tse3tach 3am. Lyouma ana f ssou9. Llimoun b tmenya dyal ddrahem lkilo w matecha b setta dyal ddrahem lkilo. 3ndi myat derhem f ssak dyali. Ra9m ttilifoun dyali howa 06 12 34 56 78. 3eyti liya!","glossary":[{"en":"market","da":"ssou9"},{"en":"today","da":"lyouma"},{"en":"oranges","da":"llimoun"},{"en":"tomatoes","da":"matecha"},{"en":"a kilo","da":"lkilo (wa7ed lkilo)"},{"en":"bag","da":"ssak"},{"en":"with","da":"m3a"},{"en":"call me","da":"3eyti liya (b ttilifoun)"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al f 3mer Nouha?","options":["26","62","16","36"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I am twenty-six years old.` = 3ndi 26 3am."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha's father is fifty-eight.","statement_da":"Bba Nouha 3ndo 58 3am.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: bbaha 3ndo 62 (`sixty-two`). Mmha hiya li 3ndha 58."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Bch7al llimoun?","options":["6 derhem lkilo","8 derhem lkilo","18 derhem lkilo","80 derhem lkilo"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`The oranges are eight dirhams a kilo.` = llimoun b 8 derhem lkilo."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al dyal lflous 3nd Nouha f ssak?","options":["100 derhem","50 derhem","10 derhem","20 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I have a hundred dirhams in my bag.` = 3ndi myat derhem."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F lmaktaba: lktab w sstilo","emoji":"📚","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: bch7al lktab? bch7al sstilo? w ch7al sserf li rje3 l Tom f l'akhir?","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Excuse me, how much is the English book?","da":"Sme7 liya, bch7al lktab dyal lingliziya?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"It's seventy-five dirhams.","da":"B khemsa w seb3in derhem."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"And the pen?","da":"W sstilo?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"The pen is twelve dirhams.","da":"Sstilo b tnach derhem."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"OK. The book and two pens, please.","da":"Wakha. Lktab w jouj stilouwat, 3afak."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"That's ninety-nine dirhams.","da":"Hadchi b tes3a w tes3in derhem."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Here you are. A hundred dirhams.","da":"Hak. Myat derhem."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Thank you. Your change is one dirham. Goodbye!","da":"Choukran. Sserf dyalek derhem wa7ed. Bslama!"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Thanks! Goodbye.","da":"Choukran! Bslama."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Bch7al lktab?","options":["57 derhem","75 derhem","70 derhem","95 derhem"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`seventy-five` = 75: `seventy` (70) + `five` (5)."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men stilo chra Tom?","options":["jouj","wa7ed","tlata","3echra"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`The book and two pens, please.` = jouj stilouwat."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The pen is twenty dirhams.","statement_da":"Sstilo b 3echrin derhem.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `The pen is twelve dirhams.` = 12, machi 20."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Your change is one dirham.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni had ljomla?","options":["Sserf dyalek derhem wa7ed","Sserf dyalek 3echra dyal ddrahem","Lktab b derhem wa7ed","Choukran bzzaf"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`change` = sserf. `one dirham` = derhem wa7ed."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"How old are you?","da":"Ch7al f 3merek?","pron":"haw old ar you"},{"target_en":"I'm twenty-five years old.","da":"3ndi khemsa w 3echrin 3am.","pron":"aïm twèn-ti-faïv yirz old"},{"target_en":"How much is it?","da":"Bch7al?","pron":"haw match iz it"},{"target_en":"It's thirty-five dirhams.","da":"B khemsa w tlatin derhem.","pron":"its theur-ti-faïv di-ramz"},{"target_en":"Thirteen, thirty. Fourteen, forty.","da":"Tlettach, tlatin. Rba3tach, reb3in.","pron":"theur-tin, theur-ti. for-tin, for-ti"},{"target_en":"My phone number is zero six, two two, four five, six seven, eight nine.","da":"Ra9m ttilifoun dyali howa 06 22 45 67 89.","pron":"maï fon nam-beur iz zi-ro siks, tou tou, for faïv, siks sé-ven, éyt naïn"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Sarah bghat t3erfek kter","context_da":"Nti f l9ism m3a Sarah. Katsewlek 3la l3mer, ra9m ttilifoun w taman dyal lktab. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! How old are you?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Ch7al f 3merek?","expect_keywords":["i'm","i am","years","twenty","thirty","forty","fifty"],"sample_en":"I'm twenty-five years old."},{"bot_en":"Nice! And how old is your mother?","bot_da":"Zwin! W ch7al f 3mer mmek?","expect_keywords":["she's","she is","years","forty","fifty","sixty","seventy","eighty"],"sample_en":"She's fifty-five."},{"bot_en":"What's your phone number?","bot_da":"Chno ra9m ttilifoun dyalek?","expect_keywords":["zero","oh","six","seven","one","two","three","four","five","eight","nine","number"],"sample_en":"It's zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight."},{"bot_en":"Thanks! How much is the English book?","bot_da":"Choukran! Bch7al lktab dyal lingliziya?","expect_keywords":["it's","it is","dirham","hundred","fifty","sixty","seventy","eighty","ninety"],"sample_en":"It's eighty dirhams."},{"bot_en":"OK, thank you. See you tomorrow!","bot_da":"Wakha, choukran. Nchoufouk ghedda!","expect_keywords":["see you","bye","goodbye","thank","tomorrow"],"sample_en":"See you tomorrow, Sarah!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ana w l3a2ila dyali: l3mer w l'ar9am","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal b lingliziya: ch7al f 3merek, ch7al f 3mer jouj men l3a2ila dyalek, w ra9m ttilifoun dyalek (wla ra9m khayali). Ktbi l'ar9am b l7orouf (`twenty-five`), machi b l'ar9am (25).","helper_en":["I am ... years old.","My mother is ...","My brother is ...","My phone number is ..."],"min_words":20,"keywords":["years old","phone"],"model_en":"I am twenty-six years old. My father is sixty-two years old and my mother is fifty-eight. My sister is twenty. My phone number is zero six, one two, three four, five six, seven eight."}},{"id":"l06","order":6,"level":"A1.1","emoji":"🎨","title_en":"Things, colors & adjectives","title_da":"L7wayj, l'alwan w ssifat","goals_da":["Tsemmi l7wayj dyal kol nhar b lingliziya w tsta3mli `a` / `an`","Tdiri ljam3 (plural): `one book`, `two books`, `three children`","Tsewli `What is this?` / `What are these?` w tjawbi","Twesfi l7wayj b l'alwan w ssifat: `a red car`, `a big house`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"a / an = wa7ed","body_da":"F lingliziya, 9bel l'ism lmofrad (7aja we7da) kanzido dima `a` wla `an`. Kat3ni \"wa7ed\" walakin makantrjmouhach dima f darija:\n\n- `a book` = ktab (wa7ed lktab)\n- `a car` = tomobil\n- `an apple` = teffa7a\n- `an orange` = limouna\n\n**Fo9ach `a` w fo9ach `an`?** Kolchi 3la 7sab sswt li kayji men ba3d:\n\n- `a` 9bel l7orouf l3adiya (ssawamit): `a pen`, `a key`, `a bag`, `a teacher`\n- `an` 9bel l7orouf lmota7arrika `a, e, i, o, u`: `an apple`, `an egg`, `an engineer`, `an orange`, `an umbrella`\n\nSahla: ila lkelma kaybda b `a, e, i, o, u` → `an`. Ila la → `a`.\n\n**Rdi lbal:** f darija kan9oulo \"3ndi stilo\" bla \"wa7ed\". F lingliziya khass `a`: `I have a pen.` — machi `I have pen` ✗. W m3a lmihan 7ta houma: `She's a teacher.`, `I'm a student.`","examples":[{"en":"I have a pen and a book.","da":"3ndi stilo w ktab.","pron":"aï hav a pèn and a bouk"},{"en":"This is an apple.","da":"Hadi teffa7a.","pron":"this iz an a-peul"},{"en":"She's a teacher.","da":"Hiya oustada.","pron":"chiz a ti-tcheur"},{"en":"It's an orange.","da":"Hadi limouna.","pron":"its an o-rindj"},{"en":"Omar is an engineer.","da":"Omar mohandis.","pron":"o-mar iz an èn-dji-nir"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ljam3 (plural): books, buses, children","body_da":"Melli kayn kter men wa7ed, kanzido `-s` f l'akhir dyal l'ism. Hada howa ljam3 (plural):\n\n- `a book` → `two books`\n- `a car` → `three cars`\n- `a key` → `my keys`\n\nIla l'ism kaysali b `-s`, `-sh`, `-ch` wla `-x`, kanzido `-es` (w kat9ra \"iz\"):\n\n- `a bus` → `two buses`\n- `a watch` → `watches`\n- `a glass` → `glasses`\n- `a box` → `boxes`\n\nChi kelmat makaytbe3ouch had l9a3ida — khassek t7efdihom:\n\n- `a man` → `men` (rajel → rjal)\n- `a woman` → `women` (mra → 3yalat)\n- `a child` → `children` (derri → drari)\n- `a person` → `people` (chakhs → nnas)\n\n**Rdi lbal:** m3a ljam3 makaynach `a` / `an`: `a book` walakin `books` (machi `a books` ✗). W lfi3l kaywelli `are`: `The books are new.`\n\nF darija ljam3 kaytbeddel bzzaf (ktab → ktouba, tomobil → tomobilat, sarout → swaret). F lingliziya, ghaliban ghir `-s`. Sahla!","examples":[{"en":"one book, two books","da":"ktab wa7ed, jouj ktouba","pron":"wan bouk, tou bouks"},{"en":"a bus, three buses","da":"tobis, tlata dyal ttobisat","pron":"a bas, thri ba-siz"},{"en":"a man, two men","da":"rajel, jouj rjal","pron":"a man, tou mèn"},{"en":"a child, four children","da":"derri, reb3a dyal ddrari","pron":"a tchaïld, for tchil-dren"},{"en":"These people are from Fes.","da":"Had nnas men Fes.","pron":"thiz pi-peul ar from fès"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"this / that / these / those","body_da":"F dars 4 t3ellemti `This is my mother.` Daba ghadi nkemmlo lmajmou3a kamla:\n\n- `this` = hada / hadi (7aja we7da, 9riba mennek)\n- `that` = dak / dik / hadak (7aja we7da, b3ida 3lik)\n- `these` = hadou (bzzaf dyal l7wayj, 9ribin)\n- `those` = douk / hadouk (bzzaf dyal l7wayj, b3ad)\n\nSso2al w ljawab:\n\n- `What is this?` / `What's this?` = chno hada? → `It's a key.` = hada sarout.\n- `What's that?` = chno dak? → `It's a tagine.`\n- `What are these?` = chno hadou? → `They're keys.` = hadou swaret.\n- `What are those?` = chno douk? → `They're glasses.`\n\nT9edri t7ettihom 9bel l'ism 7ta houma: `this bag` (had ssak), `that car` (dik tomobil), `these keys` (had sswaret), `those shoes` (douk ssebbat).\n\n**Nnot9:** `this` 9sira w `these` twila — bhal \"thiiz\". W `th` = lsan bin ssnan, bhal f `thank you`.","examples":[{"en":"What's this?","da":"Chno hada?","pron":"wats this"},{"en":"It's a key.","da":"Hada sarout.","pron":"its a ki"},{"en":"What are those?","da":"Chno douk?","pron":"wat ar thoz"},{"en":"They're my glasses.","da":"Hadouk nnwader dyali.","pron":"thér maï gla-siz"},{"en":"That car is new.","da":"Dik tomobil jdida.","pron":"that kar iz niou"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ssifa 9bel l'ism: a red car","body_da":"Ssifa (adjective) = lkelma li katwsef: `big` (kbir), `small` (sghir), `new` (jdid), `old` (9dim), `good` (mzyan), `bad` (khayb), `beautiful` (zwin bzzaf), `cheap` (rkhis), `expensive` (ghali), w l'alwan: `red`, `blue`, `green`…\n\nKayn jouj tari9at bach twesfi:\n\n- B `to be`: `The car is red.` = tomobil 7emra. `My phone is old.` = ttilifoun dyali 9dim.\n- 9bel l'ism: `a red car` = tomobil 7emra. `an old phone` = tilifoun 9dim.\n\n**Rdi lbal l tartib!** F darija ssifa kadji **men ba3d** l'ism: \"tomobil 7emra\", \"dar kbira\". F lingliziya l3eks: ssifa **9bel** l'ism: `a red car`, `a big house`. Dima: `a` + ssifa + l'ism.\n\n**Ssifa makatbeddelch:** f darija kan9oulo \"kbir / kbira / kbar\". F lingliziya `big` kadkhol f kolchi: `a big man`, `a big woman`, `two big cars` (machi `bigs` ✗).\n\nW `a` / `an` kayt7ett 3la 7sab lkelma li men ba3do mbachara: `a new car` walakin `an old car`, `a bag` walakin `an expensive bag`.","examples":[{"en":"It's a big house.","da":"Hadi dar kbira.","pron":"its a big haws"},{"en":"My phone is old.","da":"Ttilifoun dyali 9dim.","pron":"maï fon iz old"},{"en":"She has a beautiful blue dress.","da":"3ndha keswa zer9a zwina.","pron":"chi haz a biou-ti-foul blou drès"},{"en":"These shoes are expensive!","da":"Had ssebbat ghali!","pron":"thiz chouz ar ik-spèn-siv"},{"en":"Two small black cats.","da":"Jouj 9totat sghar k7al.","pron":"tou smol blak kats"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"red","da":"7mer / 7emra","emoji":"🔴","pron":"rèd","example_en":"A red bag.","example_da":"Sak 7mer."},{"en":"blue","da":"zre9 / zer9a","emoji":"🔵","pron":"blou","example_en":"My pen is blue.","example_da":"Sstilo dyali zre9."},{"en":"green","da":"khder / khedra","emoji":"🟢","pron":"grin","example_en":"I have a green bag.","example_da":"3ndi sak khder."},{"en":"yellow","da":"sfer / sefra","emoji":"🟡","pron":"yé-lo","example_en":"The banana is yellow.","example_da":"Lbanana sefra."},{"en":"black","da":"k7el / ke7la","emoji":"⚫","pron":"blak","example_en":"My phone is black.","example_da":"Ttilifoun dyali k7el."},{"en":"white","da":"byed / bida","emoji":"⚪","pron":"waït","example_en":"Those cars are white.","example_da":"Douk ttomobilat bidin."},{"en":"book","da":"ktab","emoji":"📖","pron":"bouk","example_en":"This is an English book.","example_da":"Hada ktab dyal lingliziya."},{"en":"pen","da":"stilo","emoji":"🖊️","pron":"pèn","example_en":"I have two pens.","example_da":"3ndi jouj stilouwat."},{"en":"key","da":"sarout","emoji":"🔑","pron":"ki","example_en":"Where are my keys?","example_da":"Fin sswaret dyali?"},{"en":"bag","da":"sak","emoji":"👜","pron":"bag","example_en":"It's a small bag.","example_da":"Hada sak sghir."},{"en":"car","da":"tomobil","emoji":"🚗","pron":"kar","example_en":"Our car is old.","example_da":"Ttomobil dyalna 9dima."},{"en":"big","da":"kbir / kbira","emoji":"🐘","pron":"big","example_en":"Casablanca is a big city.","example_da":"Casa mdina kbira."},{"en":"small","da":"sghir / sghira","emoji":"🐜","pron":"smol","example_en":"These glasses are small.","example_da":"Had lkisan sghar."},{"en":"new","da":"jdid / jdida","emoji":"✨","pron":"niou","example_en":"Is your phone new?","example_da":"Wach ttilifoun dyalek jdid?"},{"en":"old","da":"9dim / 9dima (l l7wayj) — kbir f l3mer (l nnas)","emoji":"🏚️","pron":"old","example_en":"My house is old.","example_da":"Ddar dyali 9dima."},{"en":"beautiful","da":"zwin bzzaf / zwina bzzaf","emoji":"🌸","pron":"biou-ti-foul","example_en":"Marrakech is a beautiful city.","example_da":"Marrakech mdina zwina bzzaf."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"F ssou9 dyal Marrakech","context_da":"Nouha w Sarah f ssou9 l9dim dyal Marrakech. Sarah katsewel 3la l7wayj li katchouf, w Nouha katfesser liha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, what's this?","da":"Nouha, chno hada?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"It's a tagine. It's for cooking.","da":"Hada tajin. Dyal ttyab."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"It's beautiful! And what are those?","da":"Zwin bzzaf! W chno douk?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Those are tea glasses. They're small and very cheap.","da":"Douk kisan dyal atay. Sghar w rkhas bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"The blue glasses are nice. How much are they?","da":"Lkisan zzer9in zwinin. Bch7al?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Twenty dirhams for six glasses.","da":"3echrin derhem l setta dyal lkisan."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Great! And that red bag?","da":"Mzyan! W dak ssak l7mer?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"That bag is expensive. It's a hundred dirhams.","da":"Dak ssak ghali. B myat derhem."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hmm, it's a big bag. OK, the glasses and the bag, please!","da":"Hmm, sak kbir. Wakha, lkisan w ssak, 3afak!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good choice, Sarah!","da":"Khtiyar mzyan, Sarah!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Melli katwesfi, fekkri f tlata dyal l7wayj: (1) ssifa **9bel** l'ism: `a big bag`, machi `a bag big` ✗. (2) ssifa **ma3ndhach jam3**: `two big bags`, machi `bigs` ✗. (3) `a` wla `an` 3la 7sab lkelma li mbachara men ba3d: `a new car` / `an old car`. W ila nsiti `a` / `an` m3a l'ism lmofrad, l'ingliz ghadi yfehmouk, walakin kaysme3 ghalet — 7awli dima tzidiha!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen wa7da s7i7a?","options":["an apple","a apple","an pen"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`apple` kaybda b `a` (7erf mota7arrik) → `an apple`. `pen` kaybda b `p` → `a pen`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's a red car.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Hadi tomobil 7emra","Hadi tomobil zer9a","Hada tobis 7mer","Hadi tomobil khedra"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`red` = 7mer, `car` = tomobil. `It's a red car.` = hadi tomobil 7emra."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lloun b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"red","da":"7mer","emoji":"🔴"},{"en":"blue","da":"zre9","emoji":"🔵"},{"en":"green","da":"khder","emoji":"🟢"},{"en":"yellow","da":"sfer","emoji":"🟡"},{"en":"black","da":"k7el","emoji":"⚫"},{"en":"white","da":"byed","emoji":"⚪"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I have two ___.","options":["books","book","a book"],"answer":"books","hint_da":"jouj = ljam3","explain_da":"`two books` — m3a `two` kanzido `-s`. `a book` ghir l wa7ed."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno ljam3 dyal `child`?","options":["childs","children","childes"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`child` → `children`. Jam3 ghir 3adi, khassek t7efdih (bhal `man → men`, `woman → women`)."},{"type":"order","words":["is","This","a","beautiful","bag."],"answer":"This is a beautiful bag.","da":"Hada sak zwin bzzaf."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"What are these?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["3la bzzaf dyal l7wayj 9ribin (hadou)","3la 7aja we7da 9riba (hada)","3la 7aja we7da b3ida (dak)","3la chi wa7ed (chkoun)"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What are these?` = chno hadou? `these` = bzzaf, 9rib. `this` = wa7ed, 9rib."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"That ___ is very old.","options":["house","houses","a house"],"answer":"house","hint_da":"`That` + 7aja we7da","explain_da":"`That house is very old.` — `that` dima m3a l'ism lmofrad (wa7ed), w bla `a`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Hadi tomobil jdida.","answers":["This is a new car.","It's a new car.","It is a new car."],"hint_en":"This is a ... ...","explain_da":"`This is a new car.` — ssifa `new` 9bel l'ism `car`, w `a` 9belhom."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The plural of 'man' is 'mans'.","statement_da":"Ljam3 dyal `man` howa `mans`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `man` → `men`. Jam3 ghir 3adi, bhal `woman → women`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"These are my new keys.","da":"Hadou sswaret dyali jjdad.","explain_da":"`These are` = hadou. `new keys` = ssifa 9bel l'ism, w `-s` 7it bzzaf."},{"type":"order","words":["much","How","are","these","glasses?"],"answer":"How much are these glasses?","da":"Bch7al had lkisan?"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"What's that?","question_da":"Khtari ljawab ss7i7:","options":["They're keys.","These are a key.","It's a key."],"answer":2,"explain_da":"`What's that?` = chno dak? (7aja we7da) → `It's a key.` `They're keys.` howa jawab 3la `What are those?`"},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"What ___ these? — They're pens.","answers":["are"],"hint_da":"`these` = ljam3 → achmen fi3l?","explain_da":"`What are these?` — m3a `these` / `those` kansta3mlo `are`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"This is a small blue bag. It's cheap.","da":"Hada sak sghir zre9. Rkhis.","pron":"this iz a smol blou bag. its tchip"},{"type":"translate","da":"Dik tomobil 9dima w kbira.","answers":["That car is old and big.","That car is big and old."],"hint_en":"That car ... ... and ...","explain_da":"`That car is old and big.` — `that` = dik, `old` = 9dima, `big` = kbira."}],"reading":{"title_en":"My bag","title_da":"Ssak dyali","emoji":"👜","text_en":"This is my bag. It's a big black bag. It's new and it's beautiful. In my bag I have a phone, two pens, a small book and my keys. My phone is old but it's good. The pens are blue and red. The book is an English book. It's small and cheap: twenty dirhams. These are my keys. The big key is for my house and the small key is for my car. My car is old, white and small, but it's a good car!","text_da":"Hada ssak dyali. Sak kbir k7el. Jdid w zwin bzzaf. F ssak dyali 3ndi tilifoun, jouj stilouwat, ktab sghir w sswaret dyali. Ttilifoun dyali 9dim walakin mzyan. Sstilouwat zre9 w 7mer. Lktab ktab dyal lingliziya. Sghir w rkhis: 3echrin derhem. Hadou sswaret dyali. Ssarout lkbir dyal ddar w ssarout sghir dyal ttomobil. Ttomobil dyali 9dima, bida w sghira, walakin tomobil mzyana!","glossary":[{"en":"in","da":"f (ldakhel)"},{"en":"but","da":"walakin"},{"en":"good","da":"mzyan"},{"en":"for","da":"dyal / l"},{"en":"house","da":"ddar"},{"en":"cheap","da":"rkhis"},{"en":"English book","da":"ktab dyal lingliziya"},{"en":"white","da":"byed / bida"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno lloun dyal ssak dyal Nouha?","options":["byed","k7el","zre9","7mer"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`It's a big black bag.` — `black` = k7el."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The phone is new.","statement_da":"Ttilifoun jdid.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `My phone is old but it's good.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men stilo 3ndha f ssak?","options":["jouj","wa7ed","tlata","reb3a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`two pens` = jouj stilouwat."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Bch7al lktab?","options":["20 derhem","12 derhem","200 derhem","2 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`It's small and cheap: twenty dirhams.` = 20 derhem."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F l9ism: chno hada?","emoji":"🏫","pre_da":"Sem3i mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: chno l7wayj li kaysewwel 3lihom l'oustad, w chno l'alwan dyalhom? W dyal men ssak?","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Amina, what's this?","da":"Amina, chno hada?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"It's a pen. A blue pen.","da":"Hada stilo. Stilo zre9."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Very good. And what are these?","da":"Mzyan bzzaf. W chno hadou?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"They're books. Two big books.","da":"Hadou ktouba. Jouj ktouba kbar."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Excellent! And what's that?","da":"Momtaz! W chno dak?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"It's a bag. It's an old green bag.","da":"Hada sak. Sak 9dim khder."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Is it your bag?","da":"Wach hada ssak dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"No, it's not my bag. It's Omar's bag.","da":"La, machi ssak dyali. Hada ssak dyal Omar."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Thank you, Amina. Good job!","da":"Choukran, Amina. Khedma mzyana!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno lloun dyal sstilo?","options":["zre9","7mer","khder","k7el"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`A blue pen.` = stilo zre9."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men ktab, w kifach homa?","options":["jouj kbar","wa7ed sghir","tlata kbar","jouj sghar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Two big books.` = jouj ktouba kbar."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The bag is Amina's bag.","statement_da":"Ssak dyal Amina.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `It's Omar's bag.` — ssak dyal Omar."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's an old green bag.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni?","options":["Sak 9dim khder","Sak jdid khder","Sak 9dim zre9","Sak kbir byed"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`old` = 9dim, `green` = khder. W `an` 7it `old` kaybda b `o`."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What's this? It's a pen.","da":"Chno hada? Hada stilo.","pron":"wats this? its a pèn"},{"target_en":"What are these? They're keys.","da":"Chno hadou? Hadou swaret.","pron":"wat ar thiz? thér kiz"},{"target_en":"This is a big red bag.","da":"Hada sak kbir 7mer.","pron":"this iz a big rèd bag"},{"target_en":"Those cars are old.","da":"Douk ttomobilat 9dam.","pron":"thoz karz ar old"},{"target_en":"An apple, an orange, a banana.","da":"Teffa7a, limouna, banana.","pron":"an a-peul, an o-rindj, a ba-na-na"},{"target_en":"These shoes are cheap and beautiful.","da":"Had ssebbat rkhis w zwin.","pron":"thiz chouz ar tchip and biou-ti-foul"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"F ssou9 m3a Tom","context_da":"Tom sa7bek l'amriki jdid f lmeghrib. Nti m3ah f ssou9 w howa kaysewlek 3la l7wayj. Jawbi b jomal 9sira: `It's a…`, `They're…`, `It's blue…`","turns":[{"bot_en":"Nouha, what's this?","bot_da":"Nouha, chno hada?","expect_keywords":["it's a","it is a","it's an","this is a","tagine","teapot","glass","bag","pen","book","key"],"sample_en":"It's a tagine."},{"bot_en":"Nice! What color is it?","bot_da":"Zwin! Chno lloun dyalo?","expect_keywords":["red","blue","green","yellow","black","white","brown","orange","it's"],"sample_en":"It's blue and white."},{"bot_en":"And what are those?","bot_da":"W chno douk?","expect_keywords":["they're","they are","those are","these are","glasses","keys","bags","books","pens"],"sample_en":"They're tea glasses."},{"bot_en":"Are they expensive?","bot_da":"Wach ghalyin?","expect_keywords":["no","yes","cheap","expensive","dirham","they're"],"sample_en":"No, they're cheap. Twenty dirhams."},{"bot_en":"Great! Is this bag new or old?","bot_da":"Mzyan! Wach had ssak jdid wla 9dim?","expect_keywords":["new","old","it's"],"sample_en":"It's new. It's a beautiful bag."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Wsefi 3 7wayj dyalek","prompt_da":"Khtari 3 7wayj dyalek (tilifoun, sak, tomobil, ktab…) w ktbi 3lihom b lingliziya: chno homa, lloun dyalhom, w wach kbar wla sghar, jdad wla 9dam, rkhas wla ghalyin. Sta3mli `This is…` w `These are…`, w 7etti ssifa 9bel l'ism.","helper_en":["This is my ...","It's a ... (color) ...","It's big / small / new / old.","These are my ...","They're ..."],"min_words":20,"keywords":["this","is","my"],"model_en":"This is my phone. It's a black phone. It's old but it's good. This is my bag. It's a big red bag and it's new. These are my keys. They're small. The big key is for my house."}},{"id":"l07","order":7,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"⏰","title_en":"My day: present simple (I/you/we/they) & time","title_da":"Nhari: l7adir lbassit w lwa9t","goals_da":["T7kiy 3la nharek: `I get up at seven`, `I have breakfast`, `I go to work`","Tdiri nnafy b `don't` w tsewli b `Do you…?` w tjawbi `Yes, I do.` / `No, I don't.`","Tsewli `What time is it?` w tjawbi: `It's seven o'clock`, `It's half past seven`","Tsta3mli `at` + lwa9t w `every day`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L7adir lbassit: I / you / we / they","body_da":"L7adir lbassit (present simple) kansta3mlouh l l7wayj li kandirouhom **kol nhar** wla **dima**: l3adat dyalna.\n\nF darija kanzido \"ka-\" 9bel lfi3l: ka-nfi9, ka-nkhdem, ka-n9ra. F lingliziya **sahla kter**: kan7etto lfi3l (verb) kifma howa, bla ma nzido walou:\n\n- `I get up at seven.` = kanfi9 f ssab3a.\n- `You work in Casablanca.` = katkhdem f Casa.\n- `We have breakfast at eight.` = kanfetro f ttmenya.\n- `They go to work at nine.` = kaymchiw l lkhedma f tts3oud.\n\nM3a `I`, `you`, `we`, `they` lfi3l **makaytbeddelch**. (M3a `he` / `she` kayn chi 7aja sghira kanzidouha — ghadi nchoufouha f dars jay.)\n\nL'af3al dyal nhar: `get up` (nfi9), `have breakfast` (nfter), `go to work` (nmchi l lkhedma), `work` (nkhdem), `have lunch` (ntghedda), `come home` (nerje3 l ddar), `have dinner` (nt3echa), `watch TV` (ntferrej f ttelfaza), `go to bed` (nmchi n3es), `study` (n9ra).","examples":[{"en":"I get up at six o'clock.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta.","pron":"aï gèt ap at siks o-klok"},{"en":"We have breakfast at seven.","da":"Kanfetro f ssab3a.","pron":"wi hav brèk-feust at sé-ven"},{"en":"They go to work at eight.","da":"Kaymchiw l lkhedma f ttmenya.","pron":"théy go tou weurk at éyt"},{"en":"I watch TV in the evening.","da":"Kantferrej f ttelfaza f l3chiya.","pron":"aï wotch ti-vi in the iv-ning"},{"en":"You study English every day.","da":"Kat9ray lingliziya kol nhar.","pron":"you sta-di in-glich év-ri déy"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Nnafy w sso2al: don't / Do you…?","body_da":"**Nnafy** (= \"ma…ch\" f darija): kan7etto `don't` (= `do not`) 9bel lfi3l:\n\n- `I don't work in the evening.` = makankhdemch f l3chiya.\n- `We don't watch TV.` = makantferrjouch f ttelfaza.\n- `They don't drink coffee.` = makaychrbouch l9ehwa.\n\n**Sso2al** (= \"wach…?\" f darija): kanbdaw b `Do` + `you` / `we` / `they` + lfi3l:\n\n- `Do you work?` = wach katkhdmi?\n- `Do you get up early?` = wach katfi9i bekri?\n- `Do they live in Rabat?` = wach kayseknou f Rabat?\n\nLjawab l9sir: `Yes, I do.` / `No, I don't.` — bhal \"ah\" / \"la\" walakin b `do`.\n\n**Rdi lbal:** `Do` = \"wach\". Machi `You work?` ✗ w **machi** `Are you work?` ✗ — `are` ghir m3a `to be`. M3a l'af3al l'okhra (`work`, `go`, `eat`…) dima `do` / `don't`.\n\nSso2al b `What time` / `Where`: `What time do you get up?` (fo9ach katfi9i?), `Where do you work?` (fin katkhdmi?).","examples":[{"en":"I don't drink coffee.","da":"Makanchrebch l9ehwa.","pron":"aï dont drink ko-fi"},{"en":"Do you get up early?","da":"Wach katfi9i bekri?","pron":"dou you gèt ap eur-li"},{"en":"Yes, I do. / No, I don't.","da":"Ah, kanfi9 bekri. / La, makanfi9ch bekri.","pron":"yès, aï dou / no, aï dont"},{"en":"What time do you go to bed?","da":"Fo9ach katmchi tn3si?","pron":"wat taïm dou you go tou bèd"},{"en":"Where do they work?","da":"Fin kaykhdmo?","pron":"wér dou théy weurk"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lwa9t: What time is it?","body_da":"`What time is it?` = ch7al f ssa3a? Ljawab kaybda b `It's`:\n\n- `It's seven o'clock.` = hadi ssab3a (ni9ech). `o'clock` kat9al ghir melli ssa3a tamam, bla d9ay9.\n- `It's half past seven.` = hadi ssab3a w ness (7:30). `half` = ness, `past` = men ba3d.\n- `It's quarter past seven.` = hadi ssab3a w rbe3 (7:15). `quarter` = rbe3.\n- `It's quarter to eight.` = hadi ttmenya lla rbe3 (7:45). `to` = lla / 9ell.\n- `It's ten past seven.` = 7:10. `It's twenty to eight.` = 7:40.\n\nChofi ch7al bhal darija! \"ssab3a w ness\" = `half past seven`, \"ttmenya lla rbe3\" = `quarter to eight`. Nefs lfikra: 7ta l ness kan9oulo `past` (w), men ba3d ness kan9oulo `to` (lla).\n\n**Tari9a sahla:** t9edri t9oli l'ar9am b jouj, bhal ssa3a rra9miya: `seven thirty` (7:30), `seven fifteen` (7:15), `seven forty-five` (7:45). S7i7a w l'ingliz kaysta3mlouha bzzaf!\n\nSbah wla l3chiya? Zidi `in the morning` (f sbah), `in the afternoon` (f l3chiya 9bel lmghreb), `in the evening` (f l3chiya / f lil), `at night` (f lil). Wla `a.m.` (9bel 12h) w `p.m.` (men ba3d 12h).","examples":[{"en":"What time is it?","da":"Ch7al f ssa3a?","pron":"wat taïm iz it"},{"en":"It's seven o'clock.","da":"Hadi ssab3a ni9ech.","pron":"its sé-ven o-klok"},{"en":"It's half past seven.","da":"Hadi ssab3a w ness.","pron":"its haf past sé-ven"},{"en":"It's quarter past nine.","da":"Hadi tts3oud w rbe3.","pron":"its kwor-teur past naïn"},{"en":"It's quarter to eight.","da":"Hadi ttmenya lla rbe3.","pron":"its kwor-teur tou éyt"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"at + lwa9t, every day, from … to …","body_da":"Melli kan9oulo **fo9ach** kandiro chi 7aja, kansta3mlo `at` 9bel ssa3a:\n\n- `I get up at six.` = kanfi9 f ssetta.\n- `We have lunch at half past twelve.` = kantgheddaw f ttnach w ness.\n- `at night` = f lil, `at noon` = f ttnach dyal nhar.\n\nF darija kan9oulo \"f ssetta\" — `at six`. Walakin \"f sbah\" = `in the morning`, machi \"at\". Rdi lbal: `at` + ssa3a, `in` + sbah / l3chiya.\n\n`every day` = kol nhar. `every morning` = kol sbah. `every evening` = kol 3chiya. Kan7ettouhom f l'akhir dyal ljomla: `I study English every day.`\n\n`from … to …` = men … 7ta l …: `I work from nine to five.` = kankhdem men tts3oud 7ta l lkhemsa.\n\nW bach trebti nharek: `and then` = w men ba3d: `I get up at six and then I have breakfast.`","examples":[{"en":"I get up at six every day.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta kol nhar.","pron":"aï gèt ap at siks év-ri déy"},{"en":"We have lunch at one o'clock.","da":"Kantgheddaw f lwe7da.","pron":"wi hav lantch at wan o-klok"},{"en":"I work from nine to five.","da":"Kankhdem men tts3oud 7ta l lkhemsa.","pron":"aï weurk from naïn tou faïv"},{"en":"They watch TV in the evening and go to bed at eleven.","da":"Kaytferrjo f ttelfaza f l3chiya w kayn3so f l7dach.","pron":"théy wotch ti-vi in the iv-ning and go tou bèd at i-lé-ven"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"get up","da":"kanfi9 (men nn3as)","emoji":"🛏️","pron":"gèt ap","example_en":"I get up at six.","example_da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta."},{"en":"have breakfast","da":"kanfter","emoji":"🥐","pron":"hav brèk-feust","example_en":"We have breakfast at seven.","example_da":"Kanfetro f ssab3a."},{"en":"go to work","da":"kanmchi l lkhedma","emoji":"💼","pron":"go tou weurk","example_en":"I go to work at eight.","example_da":"Kanmchi l lkhedma f ttmenya."},{"en":"work","da":"kankhdem","emoji":"👩‍💻","pron":"weurk","example_en":"They work in Casablanca.","example_da":"Kaykhdmo f Casa."},{"en":"have lunch","da":"kantghedda","emoji":"🍽️","pron":"hav lantch","example_en":"I have lunch at one o'clock.","example_da":"Kantghedda f lwe7da."},{"en":"come home","da":"kanrje3 l ddar","emoji":"🏠","pron":"kam hom","example_en":"I come home at five.","example_da":"Kanrje3 l ddar f lkhemsa."},{"en":"have dinner","da":"kant3echa","emoji":"🍲","pron":"hav di-neur","example_en":"We have dinner at eight.","example_da":"Kant3echaw f ttmenya."},{"en":"watch TV","da":"kantferrej f ttelfaza","emoji":"📺","pron":"wotch ti-vi","example_en":"Do you watch TV?","example_da":"Wach kattferrji f ttelfaza?"},{"en":"go to bed","da":"kanmchi n3es","emoji":"😴","pron":"go tou bèd","example_en":"I go to bed at eleven.","example_da":"Kanmchi n3es f l7dach."},{"en":"study","da":"kan9ra","emoji":"📚","pron":"sta-di","example_en":"I study English every day.","example_da":"Kan9ra lingliziya kol nhar."},{"en":"every day","da":"kol nhar","emoji":"📅","pron":"év-ri déy","example_en":"I drink tea every day.","example_da":"Kanchreb atay kol nhar."},{"en":"o'clock","da":"ni9ech / tamam (ssa3a bla d9ay9)","emoji":"🕙","pron":"o-klok","example_en":"It's ten o'clock.","example_da":"Hadi l3echra ni9ech."},{"en":"half past","da":"w ness","emoji":"🕝","pron":"haf past","example_en":"It's half past two.","example_da":"Hadi jjouj w ness."},{"en":"quarter","da":"rbe3 (rbe3 sa3a = 15 d9i9a)","emoji":"🕒","pron":"kwor-teur","example_en":"It's quarter to six.","example_da":"Hadi ssetta lla rbe3."},{"en":"early","da":"bekri","emoji":"🌅","pron":"eur-li","example_en":"I get up early.","example_da":"Kanfi9 bekri."},{"en":"evening","da":"l3chiya","emoji":"🌆","pron":"iv-ning","example_en":"In the evening, I study.","example_da":"F l3chiya, kan9ra."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Nhar Nouha","context_da":"Sarah w Nouha kaychrbo atay men ba3d l9ism. Sarah katsewel Nouha kifach kaydouz nharha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, what time do you get up?","da":"Nouha, fo9ach katfi9i?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I get up at six o'clock every day.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta kol nhar."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Six o'clock! That's early. Do you have breakfast?","da":"Ssetta! Bekri hadik. Wach katfetri?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I do. I have tea and bread at half past six.","da":"Ah. Kanchreb atay w kanakol khobz f ssetta w ness."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"And what time do you go to work?","da":"W fo9ach katmchi l lkhedma?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"At quarter to eight. I work from eight to four.","da":"F ttmenya lla rbe3. Kankhdem men ttmenya 7ta l rreb3a."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Do you come home for lunch?","da":"Wach katrej3i l ddar bach ttgheddi?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, I don't. I have lunch at work with my friends.","da":"La. Kantghedda f lkhedma m3a s7abati."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"And in the evening?","da":"W f l3chiya?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I have dinner at eight, I watch TV and I go to bed at eleven.","da":"Kant3echa f ttmenya, kantferrej f ttelfaza w kanmchi n3es f l7dach."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Lkhata2 lmachhour dyal lmgharba: `You work?` ✗ wla `Are you work?` ✗. F lingliziya sso2al m3a l'af3al dyal l7araka dima b `Do`: `Do you work?`, `Do you drink tea?`. W men ba3d `do` / `don't` lfi3l kayb9a kifma howa, bla `to` w bla `-s`: `I don't go`, machi `I don't to go` ✗. Fekkri: `Do` = \"wach\", `don't` = \"ma…ch\"."}],"exercises":[{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's seven o'clock.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al f ssa3a?","options":["7:00","7:30","6:00","7:15"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`seven o'clock` = ssab3a ni9ech (7:00)."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"kanfi9 f ssetta\"?","options":["I am get up at six.","I get up at six.","I get up six."],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`I get up at six.` — lfi3l bla `am`, w `at` 9bel ssa3a."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lwa9t b lingliziya m3a ssa3a.","pairs":[{"en":"half past seven","da":"ssab3a w ness (7:30)","emoji":"🕢"},{"en":"quarter past nine","da":"tts3oud w rbe3 (9:15)","emoji":"🕘"},{"en":"quarter to eight","da":"ttmenya lla rbe3 (7:45)","emoji":"🕣"},{"en":"ten o'clock","da":"l3echra ni9ech (10:00)","emoji":"🕙"},{"en":"half past twelve","da":"ttnach w ness (12:30)","emoji":"🕧"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ breakfast at seven.","options":["have","has","am"],"answer":"have","hint_da":"kanfter = `have breakfast`","explain_da":"`I have breakfast at seven.` — m3a `I` lfi3l `have`, bla tebdil."},{"type":"order","words":["time","What","do","you","get","up?"],"answer":"What time do you get up?","da":"Fo9ach katfi9i?"},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"We ___ work in the evening.","options":["don't","not","no"],"answer":"don't","hint_da":"nnafy = ma…ch","explain_da":"`We don't work in the evening.` — nnafy b `don't` + lfi3l."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I go to bed at half past ten.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fo9ach kaymchi yn3es?","options":["10:30","10:15","9:30","12:30"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`half past ten` = l3echra w ness = 10:30."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Do you work in Casablanca?","question_da":"Khtari ljawab l9sir ss7i7:","options":["Yes, I am.","Yes, I don't.","Yes, I do."],"answer":2,"explain_da":"Sso2al b `Do` → ljawab b `do`: `Yes, I do.` / `No, I don't.` Machi `am`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Makanchrebch l9ehwa f sbah.","answers":["I don't drink coffee in the morning.","I do not drink coffee in the morning."],"hint_en":"I ... drink coffee in the ...","explain_da":"`I don't drink coffee in the morning.` — `don't` = ma…ch, `in the morning` = f sbah."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"'Quarter to eight' is 8:15.","statement_da":"`Quarter to eight` hiya 8:15.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `quarter to eight` = ttmenya lla rbe3 = 7:45. 8:15 = `quarter past eight`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"They have dinner at eight o'clock.","da":"Kayt3echaw f ttmenya.","explain_da":"`They have dinner` = kayt3echaw. `at eight o'clock` = f ttmenya ni9ech."},{"type":"order","words":["to","work","I","from","nine","five."],"answer":"I work from nine to five.","da":"Kankhdem men tts3oud 7ta l lkhemsa."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"What time ___ it? — It's half past two.","answers":["is"],"hint_da":"lfi3l `to be` m3a `it`","explain_da":"`What time is it?` = ch7al f ssa3a? Hna kansta3mlo `is` 7it `it` + `to be`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen jomla s7i7a?","options":["Are you have lunch at home?","Do you have lunch at home?","You have lunch at home do?"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"Sso2al: `Do` + `you` + lfi3l: `Do you have lunch at home?` Machi `are` m3a `have`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"I get up at six, I have breakfast and I go to work at eight.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta, kanfter w kanmchi l lkhedma f ttmenya.","pron":"aï gèt ap at siks, aï hav brèk-feust and aï go tou weurk at éyt"},{"type":"translate","da":"Fo9ach katmchi tn3si?","answers":["What time do you go to bed?","When do you go to bed?"],"hint_en":"What time ... you ... to bed?","explain_da":"`What time do you go to bed?` — `What time` + `do you` + lfi3l."}],"reading":{"title_en":"My day","title_da":"Nhari","emoji":"🌅","text_en":"I get up at six o'clock every day. I have breakfast at half past six: bread, olive oil and a glass of mint tea. At quarter past seven I go to work. I work in a small shop in Rabat from eight to four. I have lunch at one o'clock with my friend Amina. We don't go home for lunch; we eat at a small café. I come home at half past four. In the evening, I study English, I have dinner with my family and I watch TV. I go to bed at eleven. I don't go to bed late!","text_da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta kol nhar. Kanfter f ssetta w ness: khobz, zit l3oud w kas dyal atay b nne3na3. F ssab3a w rbe3 kanmchi l lkhedma. Kankhdem f 7anout sghira f Rabat men ttmenya 7ta l rreb3a. Kantghedda f lwe7da m3a sa7bti Amina. Makanrej3ouch l ddar bach ntgheddaw; kanaklo f 9ehwa sghira. Kanrje3 l ddar f rreb3a w ness. F l3chiya, kan9ra lingliziya, kant3echa m3a l3a2ila dyali w kantferrej f ttelfaza. Kanmchi n3es f l7dach. Makanmchich n3es m3ettla!","glossary":[{"en":"shop","da":"7anout"},{"en":"bread","da":"khobz"},{"en":"olive oil","da":"zit l3oud"},{"en":"mint tea","da":"atay b nne3na3"},{"en":"a glass of","da":"kas dyal"},{"en":"eat","da":"kanaklo (nakol)"},{"en":"café","da":"9ehwa"},{"en":"late","da":"m3ettel / m3ettla"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach katfi9 Nouha?","options":["f ssetta","f ssab3a","f ssetta w ness","f ttmenya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I get up at six o'clock.` = kanfi9 f ssetta."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha has lunch at home.","statement_da":"Nouha kattghedda f ddar.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `We don't go home for lunch; we eat at a small café.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin katkhdem Nouha?","options":["f 9ehwa f Casa","f 7anout sghira f Rabat","f lmedrasa","f ddar"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`I work in a small shop in Rabat.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach katmchi tn3es?","options":["f l7dach","f ttnach","f l3echra","f tts3oud"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I go to bed at eleven.` = f l7dach."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Omar: nhar dyal lkhedma","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: fo9ach kayfi9 Omar? fin kayfter? w fo9ach kaymchi yn3es?","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Omar, what time do you get up?","da":"Omar, fo9ach katfi9?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I get up at half past six.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta w ness."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Do you have breakfast at home?","da":"Wach katfter f ddar?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"No, I don't. I have a coffee at the café at seven.","da":"La. Kanchreb 9ehwa f l9ehwa f ssab3a."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"And what time do you go to work?","da":"W fo9ach katmchi l lkhedma?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"At quarter to eight. I work from eight to five.","da":"F ttmenya lla rbe3. Kankhdem men ttmenya 7ta l lkhemsa."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Do you watch TV in the evening?","da":"Wach kattferrej f ttelfaza f l3chiya?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"No, I don't watch TV. I study English and I go to bed at ten.","da":"La, makantferrejch f ttelfaza. Kan9ra lingliziya w kanmchi n3es f l3echra."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"At ten? You go to bed early!","da":"F l3echra? Katn3es bekri!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach kayfi9 Omar?","options":["6:30","6:00","7:30","7:45"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`half past six` = ssetta w ness = 6:30."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar has breakfast at home.","statement_da":"Omar kayfter f ddar.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `No, I don't. I have a coffee at the café.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I work from eight to five.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni?","options":["Kankhdem men ttmenya 7ta l lkhemsa","Kankhdem men ttmenya 7ta l rreb3a","Kanfi9 f ttmenya","Kanmchi n3es f lkhemsa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`from eight to five` = men ttmenya 7ta l lkhemsa."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kaydir Omar f l3chiya?","options":["Kaytferrej f ttelfaza","Kay9ra lingliziya","Kaykhdem","Kaymchi l l9ehwa"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`I study English and I go to bed at ten.`"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What time is it? It's half past seven.","da":"Ch7al f ssa3a? Hadi ssab3a w ness.","pron":"wat taïm iz it? its haf past sé-ven"},{"target_en":"I get up at six o'clock every day.","da":"Kanfi9 f ssetta kol nhar.","pron":"aï gèt ap at siks o-klok év-ri déy"},{"target_en":"Do you have breakfast? Yes, I do.","da":"Wach katfetri? Ah.","pron":"dou you hav brèk-feust? yès, aï dou"},{"target_en":"I don't watch TV in the evening.","da":"Makantferrejch f ttelfaza f l3chiya.","pron":"aï dont wotch ti-vi in the iv-ning"},{"target_en":"We go to bed at quarter to eleven.","da":"Kanmchiw nn3so f l7dach lla rbe3.","pron":"wi go tou bèd at kwor-teur tou i-lé-ven"},{"target_en":"What time do you go to work?","da":"Fo9ach katmchi l lkhedma?","pron":"wat taïm dou you go tou weurk"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Sarah katsewlek 3la nharek","context_da":"Sarah bghat t3ref kifach kaydouz nharek. Jawbi b `I` + lfi3l w `at` + lwa9t. Matensaych `Yes, I do.` / `No, I don't.`","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! What time do you get up?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Fo9ach katfi9i?","expect_keywords":["get up","at","five","six","seven","eight","o'clock","half past","quarter"],"sample_en":"I get up at six o'clock."},{"bot_en":"Do you have breakfast?","bot_da":"Wach katfetri?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i do","i don't","breakfast","tea","bread","coffee"],"sample_en":"Yes, I do. I have tea and bread."},{"bot_en":"What time do you go to work?","bot_da":"Fo9ach katmchi l lkhedma?","expect_keywords":["at","seven","eight","nine","half past","quarter","go to work","i don't work","work"],"sample_en":"I go to work at eight."},{"bot_en":"Do you watch TV in the evening?","bot_da":"Wach kattferrji f ttelfaza f l3chiya?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i do","i don't","watch","tv","study","read"],"sample_en":"No, I don't. I study English."},{"bot_en":"And what time do you go to bed?","bot_da":"W fo9ach katmchi tn3si?","expect_keywords":["at","nine","ten","eleven","twelve","half past","quarter","bed","go to bed"],"sample_en":"I go to bed at eleven."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Nhari","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal b lingliziya 3la nharek: fo9ach katfi9i, fo9ach katfetri, chno katdiri f nhar, w fo9ach katmchi tn3si. Sta3mli `I` + lfi3l, `at` + lwa9t, w jomla we7da b `don't`.","helper_en":["I get up at ...","I have breakfast at ...","I go to ... at ...","In the evening, I ...","I don't ...","I go to bed at ..."],"min_words":25,"keywords":["get up","at"],"model_en":"I get up at six o'clock. I have breakfast at half past six. I go to work at eight. I have lunch at one o'clock. In the evening, I have dinner and I study English. I don't watch TV. I go to bed at eleven."}},{"id":"l08","order":8,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"👩‍💼","title_en":"He works, she studies: present simple (he/she/it)","title_da":"Howa kaykhdem, hiya kat9ra","goals_da":["T7kiy 3la nhar dyal chi wa7ed akhor: `She works`, `He goes`, `She studies`","Tdiri nnafy w sso2al b `doesn't` / `Does she…?` w tjawbi `Yes, she does.`","Tsta3mli `always`, `usually`, `often`, `sometimes`, `never` f lblasa ss7i7a","Tsewli `How often…?` w tjawbi: `once a week`, `twice a week`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"he / she / it: kanzido -s","body_da":"F dars 7 chefti l7adir lbassit m3a `I`, `you`, `we`, `they`. M3a `he`, `she` w `it` kayn ghir fer9 wa7ed: kanzido **`-s`** f l'akhir dyal lfi3l:\n\n- `I work` → `she works`\n- `we live` → `he lives`\n- `they get up` → `she gets up`\n\nF darija kanbeddlo lbdaya: **kan**-khdem (ana), **kay**-khdem (howa), **kat**-khdem (hiya). F lingliziya kanbeddlo l'akhir: `work` → `works`. Ghir `-s` sghira, walakin mohimma bzzaf!\n\n**Chi 9awa3id sghar:**\n\n- Lfi3l li kaysali b `-s`, `-sh`, `-ch`, `-x` wla `-o` → kanzido `-es`: `go` → `goes`, `do` → `does`, `watch` → `watches`, `finish` → `finishes`.\n- Lfi3l li kaysali b 7erf 3adi + `y` → `y` katwelli `-ies`: `study` → `studies`, `try` → `tries`. (Walakin `play` → `plays`, 7it 9bel `y` kayn `a`.)\n- `have` → `has` (ghir 3adi, khassek t7efdih): `She has two children.`\n\n`it` kansta3mlouh l l7wayj: `The bus comes at eight.` = ttobis kayji f ttmenya.","examples":[{"en":"My sister works in a bank.","da":"Khti katkhdem f lbanka.","pron":"maï sis-teur weurks in a bank"},{"en":"He goes to work at eight.","da":"Kaymchi l lkhedma f ttmenya.","pron":"hi goz tou weurk at éyt"},{"en":"She watches TV in the evening.","da":"Kattferrej f ttelfaza f l3chiya.","pron":"chi wo-tchiz ti-vi in the iv-ning"},{"en":"Omar studies English every day.","da":"Omar kay9ra lingliziya kol nhar.","pron":"o-mar sta-diz in-glich év-ri déy"},{"en":"She has two children.","da":"3ndha jouj drari.","pron":"chi haz tou tchil-dren"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"doesn't / Does she…?","body_da":"**Nnafy** m3a `he` / `she` / `it`: `doesn't` (= `does not`) + lfi3l **bla `-s`**:\n\n- `She doesn't work in the evening.` = makatkhdemch f l3chiya.\n- `He doesn't drink coffee.` = makaychrebch l9ehwa.\n- `My brother doesn't have a car.` = khouya ma3ndouch tomobil.\n\n**Sso2al**: `Does` + `he` / `she` / `it` + lfi3l **bla `-s`**:\n\n- `Does she work in Casablanca?` = wach katkhdem f Casa?\n- `Does he get up early?` = wach kayfi9 bekri?\n- `What time does she get up?` = fo9ach katfi9?\n- `Where does he live?` = fin kayskon?\n\nLjawab l9sir: `Yes, she does.` / `No, she doesn't.` / `Yes, he does.` / `No, he doesn't.`\n\n**L9a3ida ddahabiya:** `-s` kayn ghir **merra we7da** f ljomla. F ljomla l3adiya kayn f lfi3l (`she works`). F sso2al w nnafy kaymchi l `does` / `doesn't`, w lfi3l kayb9a 3eryan: `Does she work?` (machi `Does she works?` ✗), `She doesn't work.` (machi `She doesn't works` ✗). W `has` kaywelli `have`: `Does she have children?`","examples":[{"en":"He doesn't drink coffee.","da":"Makaychrebch l9ehwa.","pron":"hi da-zent drink ko-fi"},{"en":"Does she work in Casablanca?","da":"Wach katkhdem f Casa?","pron":"daz chi weurk in ka-sa-blan-ka"},{"en":"Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't.","da":"Ah, katkhdem. / La, makatkhdemch.","pron":"yès, chi daz / no, chi da-zent"},{"en":"What time does he get up?","da":"Fo9ach kayfi9?","pron":"wat taïm daz hi gèt ap"},{"en":"My brother doesn't have a car.","da":"Khouya ma3ndouch tomobil.","pron":"maï bra-theur da-zent hav a kar"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"always, usually, often, sometimes, never","body_da":"Had lkelmat kay9oulo **ch7al men merra** kandiro chi 7aja:\n\n- `always` = dima (100%)\n- `usually` = 3adatan / ghaliban (80%)\n- `often` = bzzaf dyal lmerrat (60%)\n- `sometimes` = chi merrat / sa3at (30%)\n- `never` = 3emmer / abadan (0%)\n\n**Fin kan7ettouhom?** **9bel** lfi3l:\n\n- `I always have breakfast.` = dima kanfter.\n- `She usually gets up at seven.` = 3adatan katfi9 f ssab3a.\n- `We often go to the market.` = bzzaf dyal lmerrat kanmchiw l ssou9.\n\nWalakin m3a lfi3l `to be` kayjiw **men ba3d** `am` / `is` / `are`:\n\n- `He is always late.` = dima m3ettel.\n- `I am never late.` = 3emmerni ma kantt3ettel.\n\n**Rdi lbal l `never`:** hiya nafya b rasha. F darija kan9oulo \"3emmerni **ma** kanchreb\" (b \"ma\"), walakin f lingliziya `I never drink coffee.` — **bla** `don't`! `I don't never` ✗ ghalet.","examples":[{"en":"I always have breakfast.","da":"Dima kanfter.","pron":"aï ol-wéyz hav brèk-feust"},{"en":"She usually gets up at seven.","da":"3adatan katfi9 f ssab3a.","pron":"chi you-jou-a-li gèts ap at sé-ven"},{"en":"We often watch TV in the evening.","da":"Bzzaf dyal lmerrat kantferrjo f ttelfaza f l3chiya.","pron":"wi o-fen wotch ti-vi in the iv-ning"},{"en":"They sometimes have lunch at a café.","da":"Chi merrat kaytgheddaw f l9ehwa.","pron":"théy sam-taïmz hav lantch at a ka-féy"},{"en":"He is never late.","da":"3emmro ma kaytt3ettel.","pron":"hi iz né-veur léyt"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"How often…? once / twice a week — w lmihan","body_da":"`How often…?` = ch7al men merra…?\n\n- `How often do you study English?` = ch7al men merra kat9ray lingliziya?\n- `How often does she go to the market?` = ch7al men merra katmchi l ssou9?\n\nLjawab, f l'akhir dyal ljomla:\n\n- `every day` = kol nhar / `every morning` = kol sbah\n- `once a week` = merra f ssimana (`once` = merra we7da)\n- `twice a week` = jouj merrat f ssimana (`twice` = jouj merrat)\n- `three times a week` = tlata dyal lmerrat f ssimana\n- `once a month` = merra f chhar\n\nChofi: `a week` hna kat3ni \"f ssimana\" (kol simana), machi \"wa7ed ssimana\".\n\n**Lmihan (jobs):** bach tsewli 3la khedmet chi wa7ed: `What does she do?` = chno khedmetha? (7arfiyan: chno katdir?). Ljawab b `a` / `an`: `She's a nurse.` = hiya fermliya. `He's an engineer.` = howa mohandis. W fin kaykhdem: `She works in a hospital.`","examples":[{"en":"How often do you study English?","da":"Ch7al men merra kat9ray lingliziya?","pron":"haw o-fen dou you sta-di in-glich"},{"en":"Twice a week.","da":"Jouj merrat f ssimana.","pron":"twaïs a wik"},{"en":"I go to the market once a week.","da":"Kanmchi l ssou9 merra f ssimana.","pron":"aï go tou the mar-kit wans a wik"},{"en":"What does your brother do? — He's a driver.","da":"Chno khedmet khouk? — Howa chifour.","pron":"wat daz your bra-theur dou — hiz a draï-veur"},{"en":"She's a doctor. She works in a hospital.","da":"Hiya tbiba. Katkhdem f sbitar.","pron":"chiz a dok-teur. chi weurks in a hos-pi-teul"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"always","da":"dima","emoji":"💯","pron":"ol-wéyz","example_en":"She always drinks tea.","example_da":"Dima katchreb atay."},{"en":"usually","da":"3adatan / ghaliban","emoji":"🔁","pron":"you-jou-a-li","example_en":"I usually get up at six.","example_da":"3adatan kanfi9 f ssetta."},{"en":"often","da":"bzzaf dyal lmerrat","emoji":"🔂","pron":"o-fen","example_en":"We often go to the market.","example_da":"Bzzaf dyal lmerrat kanmchiw l ssou9."},{"en":"sometimes","da":"chi merrat / sa3at","emoji":"🤷‍♀️","pron":"sam-taïmz","example_en":"He sometimes works at night.","example_da":"Chi merrat kaykhdem b llil."},{"en":"never","da":"3emmer / abadan","emoji":"🚫","pron":"né-veur","example_en":"I never drink coffee.","example_da":"3emmerni ma kanchreb l9ehwa."},{"en":"once a week","da":"merra f ssimana","emoji":"1️⃣","pron":"wans a wik","example_en":"She studies English once a week.","example_da":"Kat9ra lingliziya merra f ssimana."},{"en":"twice a week","da":"jouj merrat f ssimana","emoji":"2️⃣","pron":"twaïs a wik","example_en":"He plays football twice a week.","example_da":"Kayl3eb lkora jouj merrat f ssimana."},{"en":"teacher","da":"oustad / oustada","emoji":"👩‍🏫","pron":"ti-tcheur","example_en":"My mother is a teacher.","example_da":"Mmi oustada."},{"en":"doctor","da":"tbib / tbiba","emoji":"👩‍⚕️","pron":"dok-teur","example_en":"He's a doctor in Fes.","example_da":"Howa tbib f Fes."},{"en":"nurse","da":"fermli / fermliya","emoji":"💉","pron":"neurs","example_en":"My sister is a nurse.","example_da":"Khti fermliya."},{"en":"driver","da":"chifour","emoji":"🚕","pron":"draï-veur","example_en":"Omar is a taxi driver.","example_da":"Omar chifour dyal taxi."},{"en":"shop assistant","da":"bayye3 / bayy3a f l7anout","emoji":"🛍️","pron":"chop a-sis-tent","example_en":"She's a shop assistant in Marrakech.","example_da":"Hiya bayy3a f 7anout f Marrakech."},{"en":"engineer","da":"mohandis / mohandisa","emoji":"👷‍♀️","pron":"èn-dji-nir","example_en":"My brother is an engineer.","example_da":"Khouya mohandis."},{"en":"hospital","da":"sbitar","emoji":"🏥","pron":"hos-pi-teul","example_en":"She works in a hospital.","example_da":"Katkhdem f sbitar."},{"en":"school","da":"lmedrasa","emoji":"🏫","pron":"skoul","example_en":"The children go to school at eight.","example_da":"Ddrari kaymchiw l lmedrasa f ttmenya."},{"en":"late","da":"m3ettel / m3ettla","emoji":"⏰","pron":"léyt","example_en":"She sometimes comes home late.","example_da":"Chi merrat katrje3 l ddar m3ettla."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Khti Salma","context_da":"Sarah katsewel Nouha 3la khtha Salma: chno khedmetha w kifach kaydouz nharha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, does your sister work?","da":"Nouha, wach khtek katkhdem?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, she does. She's a nurse. She works in a hospital in Casablanca.","da":"Ah. Hiya fermliya. Katkhdem f sbitar f Casa."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"What time does she go to work?","da":"Fo9ach katmchi l lkhedma?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"She gets up at five and she goes to work at six. She usually comes home at three.","da":"Katfi9 f lkhemsa w katmchi l lkhedma f ssetta. 3adatan katrje3 l ddar f ttlata."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Five o'clock! Does she have breakfast?","da":"Lkhemsa! Wach katfter?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, she doesn't. She never has breakfast at home. She has a coffee at the hospital.","da":"La. 3emmerha ma katfter f ddar. Katchreb 9ehwa f sbitar."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"And how often does she work at night?","da":"W ch7al men merra katkhdem b llil?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Twice a week. It's hard, but she's a very good nurse.","da":"Jouj merrat f ssimana. S3iba, walakin hiya fermliya mzyana bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Does she live with you?","da":"Wach katskon m3ak?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, she doesn't. She lives with her husband in Casablanca. I live in Rabat.","da":"La. Katskon m3a rajelha f Casa. Ana kanskon f Rabat."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Fekkri f `-s` bhal 9ob3a we7da: f ljomla kayn ghir rajel wa7ed li kaylbesha. F ljomla l3adiya kaylbesha lfi3l: `She works.` F sso2al w nnafy kaylbesha `does` / `doesn't`, w lfi3l kayb9a bla 9ob3a: `Does she work?`, `She doesn't work.` Ila chefti `-s` jouj merrat (`Does she works?` ✗) — kayn ghalat!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"My brother ___ in Agadir.","options":["lives","live","living"],"answer":"lives","hint_da":"`my brother` = `he` → ?","explain_da":"`My brother lives in Agadir.` — `my brother` = `he`, dakchi 3lach kanzido `-s`: `lives`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"She goes to work at seven.","question_da":"Sem3i mzyan. Chno kat3ni?","options":["Hiya katmchi l lkhedma f ssab3a","Howa kaymchi l lkhedma f ssab3a","Hiya katfi9 f ssab3a","7na kanmchiw l lkhedma f ssab3a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`She goes` = hiya katmchi. `goes` = `go` + `-es`."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lmihna b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"doctor","da":"tbib / tbiba","emoji":"👩‍⚕️"},{"en":"nurse","da":"fermli / fermliya","emoji":"💉"},{"en":"driver","da":"chifour","emoji":"🚕"},{"en":"teacher","da":"oustad / oustada","emoji":"👩‍🏫"},{"en":"engineer","da":"mohandis / mohandisa","emoji":"👷‍♀️"},{"en":"shop assistant","da":"bayye3 / bayy3a f l7anout","emoji":"🛍️"}]},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen jomla s7i7a?","options":["Does she works in Rabat?","Do she work in Rabat?","Does she work in Rabat?"],"answer":2,"explain_da":"`Does she work in Rabat?` — `-s` f `does`, w lfi3l `work` bla `-s`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"He ___ coffee. He drinks tea.","options":["doesn't drink","don't drink","doesn't drinks"],"answer":"doesn't drink","hint_da":"nnafy m3a `he`","explain_da":"`He doesn't drink coffee.` — `doesn't` + lfi3l bla `-s`."},{"type":"order","words":["often","do","How","you","go","to","the","market?"],"answer":"How often do you go to the market?","da":"Ch7al men merra katmchi l ssou9?"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I never drink coffee in the evening.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni?","options":["3emmerni ma kanchreb l9ehwa f l3chiya","Dima kanchreb l9ehwa f l3chiya","Chi merrat kanchreb l9ehwa f l3chiya","3adatan kanchreb atay f l3chiya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`never` = 3emmer / abadan (0%). Rdi lbal: bla `don't`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kan7etto `always` f ljomla?","options":["I get up always at six.","I always get up at six.","I get up at six always."],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`always`, `usually`, `often`, `sometimes`, `never` kayjiw **9bel** lfi3l: `I always get up at six.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"'Twice a week' means two times a week.","statement_da":"`Twice a week` kat3ni jouj merrat f ssimana.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `twice` = jouj merrat. `once` = merra we7da."},{"type":"translate","da":"Khti kat9ra lingliziya kol nhar.","answers":["My sister studies English every day.","My sister studies English everyday."],"hint_en":"My sister ... English every day.","explain_da":"`My sister studies English every day.` — `study` → `studies` (`y` → `ies`)."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"He usually has lunch at one o'clock.","da":"3adatan kaytghedda f lwe7da.","explain_da":"`usually` 9bel lfi3l. `has` = `have` m3a `he`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"What time ___ she get up?","answers":["does"],"hint_da":"sso2al m3a `she`","explain_da":"`What time does she get up?` — sso2al m3a `she` b `does`, w `get up` bla `-s`."},{"type":"order","words":["sister","My","doesn't","have","a","car."],"answer":"My sister doesn't have a car.","da":"Khti ma3ndhach tomobil."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach khouk kaykhdem f sbitar?","answers":["Does your brother work in a hospital?","Does your brother work in the hospital?","Does your brother work at a hospital?","Does your brother work at the hospital?"],"hint_en":"Does your ... work in a ...?","explain_da":"`Does your brother work in a hospital?` — `your brother` = `he` → `Does` + lfi3l bla `-s`."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"How often does Omar watch TV?","question_da":"Khtari ljawab lmonasib:","options":["In Casablanca.","At seven o'clock.","Twice a week.","Yes, he is."],"answer":2,"explain_da":"`How often…?` = ch7al men merra? → ljawab: `Twice a week.` (jouj merrat f ssimana)."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"My mother is a teacher. She works in a school and she never gets up late.","da":"Mmi oustada. Katkhdem f lmedrasa w 3emmerha ma katfi9 m3ettla.","pron":"maï ma-theur iz a ti-tcheur. chi weurks in a skoul and chi né-veur gèts ap léyt"}],"reading":{"title_en":"My friend Amina","title_da":"Sa7bti Amina","emoji":"👩‍🏫","text_en":"My friend Amina is twenty-nine years old. She is a teacher. She works in a small school in Marrakech. She gets up at six every day, has breakfast with her family and goes to school at half past seven. She teaches English to children. She usually finishes at four o'clock and comes home at five. In the evening, Amina doesn't watch TV. She often reads a book or studies Spanish. She goes to the market once a week and she never gets up late. She is always happy at work!","text_da":"Sa7bti Amina 3ndha tes3a w 3echrin 3am. Hiya oustada. Katkhdem f medrasa sghira f Marrakech. Katfi9 f ssetta kol nhar, katfter m3a l3a2ila dyalha w katmchi l lmedrasa f ssab3a w ness. Kat9erri lingliziya l ddrari. 3adatan katsali f rreb3a w katrje3 l ddar f lkhemsa. F l3chiya, Amina makattferrejch f ttelfaza. Bzzaf dyal lmerrat kat9ra ktab wla kat9ra sbanyoliya. Katmchi l ssou9 merra f ssimana w 3emmerha ma katfi9 m3ettla. Dima fer7ana f lkhedma!","glossary":[{"en":"school","da":"lmedrasa"},{"en":"teaches","da":"kat9erri"},{"en":"children","da":"ddrari"},{"en":"finishes","da":"katsali"},{"en":"reads","da":"kat9ra (ktab)"},{"en":"or","da":"wla"},{"en":"market","da":"ssou9"},{"en":"happy","da":"fer7ana"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khedmet Amina?","options":["tbiba","oustada","fermliya","chifoura"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`She is a teacher.` = hiya oustada."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Amina watches TV in the evening.","statement_da":"Amina kattferrej f ttelfaza f l3chiya.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `Amina doesn't watch TV.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men merra katmchi l ssou9?","options":["merra f ssimana","jouj merrat f ssimana","kol nhar","3emmerha"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`once a week` = merra f ssimana."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach katmchi l lmedrasa?","options":["f ssetta","f ssab3a w ness","f rreb3a","f lkhemsa"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`goes to school at half past seven` = f ssab3a w ness."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Laila w Tom: khou Laila","emoji":"🚕","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar mzyan. Rekkzi 3la: chno khedmet khou Laila? fo9ach kaybda lkhedma? w ch7al men merra kayl3eb lkora?","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Laila, what does your brother do?","da":"Laila, chno khedmet khouk?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"He's a taxi driver in Tangier.","da":"Howa chifour dyal taxi f Tanja."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Does he work every day?","da":"Wach kaykhdem kol nhar?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"No, he doesn't. He works six days a week.","da":"La. Kaykhdem setta dyal l'iyam f ssimana."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"What time does he start?","da":"Fo9ach kaybda?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"He starts at five in the morning and finishes at three.","da":"Kaybda f lkhemsa dyal sbah w kaysali f ttlata."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Wow, that's early! Does he have lunch at home?","da":"Waw, bekri! Wach kaytghedda f ddar?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Sometimes. He usually has a sandwich in the taxi.","da":"Chi merrat. 3adatan kayakol sandwich f ttaxi."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"And how often does he play football?","da":"W ch7al men merra kayl3eb lkora?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Twice a week, with his friends.","da":"Jouj merrat f ssimana, m3a s7abo."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khedmet khou Laila?","options":["chifour dyal taxi","oustad","tbib","mohandis"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`He's a taxi driver in Tangier.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila's brother works every day.","statement_da":"Khou Laila kaykhdem kol nhar.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `No, he doesn't. He works six days a week.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"He starts at five in the morning.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni?","options":["Kaybda f lkhemsa dyal sbah","Kaybda f ttmenya dyal sbah","Kaysali f lkhemsa","Kayfi9 f ssetta"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`starts` = kaybda. `at five in the morning` = f lkhemsa dyal sbah."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men merra kayl3eb lkora?","options":["merra f ssimana","jouj merrat f ssimana","kol nhar","3emmro"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"`Twice a week` = jouj merrat f ssimana."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"She works in a hospital.","da":"Katkhdem f sbitar.","pron":"chi weurks in a hos-pi-teul"},{"target_en":"He goes to work at eight.","da":"Kaymchi l lkhedma f ttmenya.","pron":"hi goz tou weurk at éyt"},{"target_en":"Does she have children? Yes, she does.","da":"Wach 3ndha drari? Ah.","pron":"daz chi hav tchil-dren? yès, chi daz"},{"target_en":"My brother doesn't drink coffee.","da":"Khouya makaychrebch l9ehwa.","pron":"maï bra-theur da-zent drink ko-fi"},{"target_en":"I usually go to the market once a week.","da":"3adatan kanmchi l ssou9 merra f ssimana.","pron":"aï you-jou-a-li go tou the mar-kit wans a wik"},{"target_en":"She never gets up late.","da":"3emmerha ma katfi9 m3ettla.","pron":"chi né-veur gèts ap léyt"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Tom kaysewlek 3la khouk","context_da":"Tom bgha y3ref chi 7aja 3la khouk (wla chi wa7ed men l3a2ila dyalek). Jawbi b `He` + lfi3l + `-s`, w sta3mli `always` / `usually` / `never`.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! What does your brother do?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Chno khedmet khouk?","expect_keywords":["he's a","he is a","he works","driver","teacher","doctor","engineer","student","nurse","shop assistant","works"],"sample_en":"He's a driver. He works in Rabat."},{"bot_en":"What time does he get up?","bot_da":"Fo9ach kayfi9?","expect_keywords":["gets up","get up","at","five","six","seven","eight","o'clock","half past"],"sample_en":"He gets up at six o'clock."},{"bot_en":"Does he have breakfast at home?","bot_da":"Wach kayfter f ddar?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","he does","he doesn't","breakfast","coffee","tea"],"sample_en":"Yes, he does. He has tea and bread."},{"bot_en":"How often does he watch TV?","bot_da":"Ch7al men merra kaytferrej f ttelfaza?","expect_keywords":["every day","once","twice","sometimes","never","often","usually","always","a week","times"],"sample_en":"He watches TV every day."},{"bot_en":"And you? How often do you study English?","bot_da":"W nti? Ch7al men merra kat9ray lingliziya?","expect_keywords":["every day","once","twice","three times","a week","sometimes","always","often","usually"],"sample_en":"I study English three times a week."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Nhar dyal chi wa7ed men l3a2ila dyalek","prompt_da":"Khtari chi wa7ed (khouk, khtek, mmek, sa7btek…) w ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal b lingliziya 3la nharo wla nharha: chno khedmto, fo9ach kayfi9, chno kaydir, jomla b `doesn't` w jomla b `always` / `usually` / `never`. Matensaych `-s`!","helper_en":["My ... is a ...","He / She gets up at ...","He / She works in ...","He / She usually ...","He / She doesn't ...","He / She never ..."],"min_words":25,"keywords":["is a","doesn't"],"model_en":"My sister Salma is a nurse. She works in a hospital in Casablanca. She gets up at five o'clock and goes to work at six. She usually has lunch at the hospital. In the evening, she comes home at four and she doesn't watch TV. She never gets up late!"}},{"id":"l09","order":9,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"🍲","title_en":"Food & drinks","title_da":"Lmakla w lmachroubat","goals_da":["T9oli chno kay3jbek w chno makay3jbekch f lmakla: `I like`, `I love`, `I don't like`","Tsewli `Do you like…?` w tjawbi `Yes, I do` / `No, I don't`","Tfer9i bin l7wayj li kayt7esbo (`an apple`) w li makayt7esbouch (`some bread`, `some water`)","Ttelbi lmakla f l9ehwa b adab: `I'd like…`, `Can I have…, please?`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kay3jebni… — like, love, hate","body_da":"Bach t9oli chno kay3jbek f lmakla, kansta3mlo tlata dyal l'af3al (`verbs` = lkelmat li katbyen l7araka):\n\n- `like` = kay3jebni / kanbghi\n- `love` = kan3che9 (kay3jebni bzzaf)\n- `hate` = kankreh\n\nF darija kan9oulo \"kay3jebni atay\" — atay howa li kay3jeb. F lingliziya l3eks: ana li kandir lfi3l: `I like tea.` (7arfiyan: ana kanbghi atay).\n\n- `I like couscous.` = Kay3jebni lkesksou.\n- `I love mint tea.` = Kan3che9 atay b nna3na3.\n- `I don't like fish.` = Makay3jebnich l7out.\n- `I hate coffee.` = Kankreh l9ehwa.\n\n**Redi lbal:** men ba3d `like` / `love` / `hate` makanzidouch `the`: `I like tea.` W ila kant l7aja kayt7esbo, kat9al f ljam3: `I like apples.`, `I love olives.`\n\nM3a `he` / `she` zidi `-s` bhal f dars 8: `She likes fish.`, `He doesn't like coffee.`","examples":[{"en":"I like couscous.","da":"Kay3jebni lkesksou.","pron":"aï laïk kous-kous"},{"en":"I love mint tea!","da":"Kan3che9 atay b nna3na3!","pron":"aï lav mint ti"},{"en":"I don't like fish.","da":"Makay3jebnich l7out.","pron":"aï dont laïk fich"},{"en":"She hates coffee.","da":"Hiya katkreh l9ehwa.","pron":"chi héyts ko-fi"},{"en":"My brother loves olives.","da":"Khouya kay3che9 zzitoun.","pron":"maï bra-theur lavz o-livz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Do you like…? — Wach kay3jbek…?","body_da":"Bach tsewli chi wa7ed wach kat3jbo chi makla, kanbdaw b `Do`, bhal li chefna f dars 7:\n\n- `Do you like tea?` = Wach kay3jbek atay?\n- `Yes, I do.` = Ah, kay3jebni.\n- `No, I don't.` = La, makay3jebnich.\n\nF ljawab l9ssir makan3awdouch lkelma `like`: kan9oulo ghir `Yes, I do.` Hadi bhal f darija melli kanjawbo ghir b \"ah\" wla \"la, walou\".\n\nM3a `he` / `she` kansta3mlo `Does`: `Does he like harira?` — `Yes, he does.` / `No, he doesn't.`\n\nBach tsewli 3la lmakla lmofaddala: `What's your favorite food?` (= chno hiya lmakla li kat3jbek kter?). Ljawab: `My favorite food is tagine.`","examples":[{"en":"Do you like olives?","da":"Wach kay3jbek zzitoun?","pron":"dou you laïk o-livz"},{"en":"Yes, I do.","da":"Ah, kay3jebni.","pron":"yès, aï dou"},{"en":"Do you like coffee? — No, I don't.","da":"Wach kat3jbek l9ehwa? — La, makat3jebnich.","pron":"dou you laïk ko-fi? — no, aï dont"},{"en":"Does Omar like fish? — Yes, he does.","da":"Wach kay3jeb Omar l7out? — Ah, kay3jbo.","pron":"daz o-mar laïk fich? — yès, hi daz"},{"en":"What's your favorite food?","da":"Chno hiya lmakla li kat3jbek kter?","pron":"wats your féy-vrit foud"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"An apple wla some bread? — l7wayj li kayt7esbo w li makayt7esbouch","body_da":"F lingliziya kayn jouj no3 dyal l'asma2 (`nouns` = lkelmat dyal l7wayj):\n\n**1. Li kayt7esbo:** wa7da, jouj, tlata… 3ndhom mofrad w jam3: `an apple` / `two apples`, `an egg` / `six eggs`, `a banana` / `bananas`.\n\n**2. Li makayt7esbouch:** lma, lkhobz, rrouz, ssokkar, l7lib, zzit, l9ehwa, atay… Ma3ndhomch jam3 w makanzidouch 9balhom `a` / `an`. Kan9oulo ghir `water`, `bread`, wla kanzido `some` (= chwiya dyal / chi): `some water`, `some bread`.\n\nBhal f darija: kan9oulo \"teffa7a\" w \"jouj teffa7at\", walakin \"lma\" w \"chwiya dyal lma\" — 3emmerna ma9olna \"jouj lma\".\n\n**`some` w `any`:**\n\n- `some` f ljomla l'ijabiya (+): `I want some bread.`, `We have some eggs.`\n- `any` f ssou2al (?) w f nnafi (−): `Do you have any milk?`, `We don't have any sugar.`\n- Melli kattelbi chi 7aja b adab, `some` kadkhol 7ta f ssou2al: `Can I have some water, please?`","examples":[{"en":"I eat an apple every day.","da":"Kanakol teffa7a kol nhar.","pron":"aï it an a-peul év-ri déy"},{"en":"We need some bread and some milk.","da":"Khassna chwiya dyal lkhobz w l7lib.","pron":"wi nid sam bréd and sam milk"},{"en":"Do you have any sugar?","da":"Wach 3ndek chi sokkar?","pron":"dou you hav é-ni chou-geur"},{"en":"I don't have any eggs.","da":"Ma3ndich lbid.","pron":"aï dont hav é-ni égz"},{"en":"Three bananas and some oranges, please.","da":"Tlata dyal lbanan w chwiya dyal llimoun, 3afak.","pron":"thri ba-na-naz and sam o-rin-djiz, pliz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"F l9ehwa: I'd like… / Can I have…?","body_da":"Melli kattelbi chi 7aja f l9ehwa wla f `restaurant`, ma t9olich `I want` (kat ban 9as7a chwiya). 9oli b adab:\n\n- `I'd like a coffee, please.` = Bghit 9ehwa, 3afak. (`I'd like` = `I would like`, ya3ni \"bghit\" b adab)\n- `Can I have a mint tea, please?` = Wach momkin atay b nna3na3, 3afak?\n\nLgarson (`waiter`) wla lgarsona (`waitress`) ghadi y9oul lik:\n\n- `What would you like?` = Chno bghiti?\n- `Anything else?` = Chi 7aja khra?\n- `Here you are.` = Hak / Tfeddli.\n\nW nti kat9oli: `That's all, thank you.` (= safi, choukran) w f l'akhir `The bill, please.` (= l7sab, 3afak).\n\nLwajbat dyal nhar: `breakfast` (lftour dyal sbah), `lunch` (lghda), `dinner` (l3cha). Kan9oulo `have breakfast` = kanftro: `I have breakfast at 7.`","examples":[{"en":"I'd like a coffee with milk, please.","da":"Bghit 9ehwa b l7lib, 3afak.","pron":"aïd laïk a ko-fi with milk, pliz"},{"en":"Can I have some bread, please?","da":"Wach momkin chwiya dyal lkhobz, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï hav sam bréd, pliz"},{"en":"What would you like? — A mint tea, please.","da":"Chno bghiti? — Atay b nna3na3, 3afak.","pron":"wat woud you laïk? — a mint ti, pliz"},{"en":"Anything else? — No, that's all, thank you.","da":"Chi 7aja khra? — La, safi, choukran.","pron":"é-ni-thing éls? — no, thats ol, thank you"},{"en":"The bill, please.","da":"L7sab, 3afak.","pron":"the bil, pliz"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"bread","da":"lkhobz","emoji":"🍞","pron":"bréd","example_en":"We eat bread every day.","example_da":"Kanaklo lkhobz kol nhar."},{"en":"water","da":"lma","emoji":"💧","pron":"wo-teur","example_en":"Can I have some water, please?","example_da":"Wach momkin chwiya dyal lma, 3afak?"},{"en":"mint tea","da":"atay b nna3na3","emoji":"🍵","pron":"mint ti","example_en":"Moroccans love mint tea.","example_da":"Lmgharba kay3che9o atay b nna3na3."},{"en":"coffee","da":"l9ehwa","emoji":"☕","pron":"ko-fi","example_en":"I'd like a coffee, please.","example_da":"Bghit 9ehwa, 3afak."},{"en":"milk","da":"l7lib","emoji":"🥛","pron":"milk","example_en":"She drinks milk in the morning.","example_da":"Hiya katchreb l7lib f sbah."},{"en":"egg","da":"bida","emoji":"🥚","pron":"ég","example_en":"I eat two eggs for breakfast.","example_da":"Kanakol jouj bidat f lftour."},{"en":"chicken","da":"ddjaj","emoji":"🍗","pron":"tchi-kin","example_en":"I like chicken with olives.","example_da":"Kay3jebni ddjaj b zzitoun."},{"en":"fish","da":"l7out","emoji":"🐟","pron":"fich","example_en":"Do you like fish?","example_da":"Wach kay3jbek l7out?"},{"en":"meat","da":"ll7em","emoji":"🥩","pron":"mit","example_en":"He doesn't eat meat.","example_da":"Howa makayakolch ll7em."},{"en":"vegetables","da":"lkhodra","emoji":"🥕","pron":"védj-ta-beulz","example_en":"Vegetables are good for you.","example_da":"Lkhodra mzyana lik."},{"en":"olives","da":"zzitoun","emoji":"🫒","pron":"o-livz","example_en":"We have olives with breakfast.","example_da":"Kanaklo zzitoun m3a lftour."},{"en":"couscous","da":"kesksou","emoji":"🍲","pron":"kous-kous","example_en":"We eat couscous every Friday.","example_da":"Kanaklo kesksou kol jem3a."},{"en":"tagine","da":"ttajin","emoji":"🥘","pron":"ta-jin","example_en":"My favorite food is chicken tagine.","example_da":"Lmakla li kat3jebni kter hiya ttajin dyal ddjaj."},{"en":"harira","da":"l7rira","emoji":"🍜","pron":"ha-ri-ra","example_en":"Harira is a Moroccan soup.","example_da":"L7rira hiya sobba meghribiya."},{"en":"breakfast","da":"lftour dyal sbah","emoji":"🍳","pron":"brék-feust","example_en":"I have breakfast at seven o'clock.","example_da":"Kanftro f ssb3a."},{"en":"dinner","da":"l3cha","emoji":"🍽️","pron":"di-neur","example_en":"We have dinner at eight.","example_da":"Kant3echaw f ttmenya."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Lftour f l9ehwa","context_da":"Nouha f wa7ed l9ehwa f Rabat. Lgarson (`waiter`) ja bach yakhod ttalab dyalha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Good morning! What would you like?","da":"Sbah lkhir! Chno bghiti?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good morning. I'd like a mint tea, please.","da":"Sbah lkhir. Bghit atay b nna3na3, 3afak."},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"With sugar?","da":"B ssokkar?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, please. And can I have some bread with olive oil?","da":"Ah, 3afak. W wach momkin chwiya dyal lkhobz b zit l3oud?"},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Of course. Anything else?","da":"Wakha. Chi 7aja khra?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Do you have any orange juice?","da":"Wach 3ndkom chi 3assir dyal llimoun?"},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Yes, we do. One orange juice. Is that all?","da":"Ah, kayn. Wa7ed l3assir dyal llimoun. Safi?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, that's all, thank you.","da":"Ah, safi, choukran."},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Here you are. Enjoy your breakfast!","da":"Tfeddli. Bssa7a w rra7a!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you very much!","da":"Choukran bzzaf!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`I want…` s7i7a, walakin f l9ehwa wla f l7anout kat ban 9as7a. Dima 9oli `I'd like…` wla `Can I have…, please?` — hadchi howa \"3afak\" dyal l'ingliz! W ila bghiti t9oli \"bssa7a\" l chi wa7ed 9bel ma yakol, 9oli `Enjoy your meal!` Mzyan, Nouha!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"lkhobz\" b lingliziya?","options":["bread","water","milk","meat"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`bread` = lkhobz. `water` = lma. `milk` = l7lib. `meat` = ll7em."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I love mint tea.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Kan3che9 atay b nna3na3","Makay3jebnich atay","Bghit 9ehwa","Kankreh l7lib"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I love` = kan3che9 / kay3jebni bzzaf. `mint tea` = atay b nna3na3."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lmakla b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"chicken","da":"ddjaj","emoji":"🍗"},{"en":"fish","da":"l7out","emoji":"🐟"},{"en":"egg","da":"bida","emoji":"🥚"},{"en":"olives","da":"zzitoun","emoji":"🫒"},{"en":"water","da":"lma","emoji":"💧"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Do you ___ couscous?","options":["like","likes","liking"],"answer":"like","hint_da":"M3a `you` lfi3l kayb9a bla `-s`.","explain_da":"`Do you like couscous?` = wach kay3jbek lkesksou? Men ba3d `Do`, lfi3l kayb9a bhal ma howa: `like`."},{"type":"order","words":["I","don't","like","coffee."],"answer":"I don't like coffee.","da":"Makat3jebnich l9ehwa.","explain_da":"Nnafi: `I` + `don't` + lfi3l: `I don't like coffee.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen kelma s7i7a?","question_en":"I'd like ___ water, please.","options":["some","a","an","two"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`water` makayt7esbch, lhada makan9oulouch `a` 9balha. Kan9oulo `some water` = chwiya dyal lma."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Do you like fish?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["Wach kay3jbek l7out","Wach kay3jbek ddjaj","Wach katchreb l9ehwa","Wach 3ndek lkhobz"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Do you like fish?` = wach kay3jbek l7out? `fish` = l7out."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Can I ___ a coffee, please?","answers":["have","get"],"hint_da":"Kat3ni: wach momkin 9ehwa, 3afak? Lfi3l li chefnah f dars.","explain_da":"`Can I have a coffee, please?` — `have` hna kat3ni \"nakhod\"."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Bread\" is a countable noun. You can say \"two breads\".","statement_da":"`bread` kayt7esb — momkin n9oulo jouj khobz b `two` + `-s`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `bread` makayt7esbch. Kan9oulo `some bread` = chwiya dyal lkhobz."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach kay3jbek atay?","answers":["Do you like tea?","Do you like mint tea?"],"hint_en":"Do you ... ?","explain_da":"`Do you like tea?` — ssou2al kaybda b `Do`, w `like` kayb9a bla `-s`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"I'd like a coffee with sugar, please.","da":"Bghit 9ehwa b ssokkar, 3afak.","explain_da":"`I'd like` = `I would like` = bghit (b adab). Sem3i: `I'd` – `like` – `a` – `coffee` – `with` – `sugar` – `please`."},{"type":"order","words":["We","don't","have","any","eggs."],"answer":"We don't have any eggs.","da":"Ma3ndnach lbid.","explain_da":"F nnafi kansta3mlo `any`: `We don't have any eggs.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Lgarson kay9oul lik `Anything else?`. Chno kat3ni?","options":["Chi 7aja khra?","Chno smiytek?","B ssokkar?","Ch7al l7sab?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Anything else?` = chi 7aja khra? Ila safi, jawbi: `No, that's all, thank you.`"},{"type":"translate","da":"Bghit chwiya dyal lma, 3afak.","answers":["I'd like some water, please.","I would like some water, please.","Can I have some water, please?"],"hint_en":"I'd like ... water, please.","explain_da":"`I'd like some water, please.` — `water` makayt7esbch, lhada `some`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Can I have a mint tea and some bread, please?","da":"Wach momkin atay b nna3na3 w chwiya dyal lkhobz, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï hav a mint ti and sam bréd, pliz"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Breakfast in Morocco","title_da":"Lftour f lmeghrib","emoji":"🥐","text_en":"In Morocco, breakfast is very important. Every morning, my family and I have breakfast together at eight o'clock. We eat bread with olive oil, butter and honey. My mother makes mint tea, and my father drinks coffee with milk. I don't like coffee, so I drink tea. My little brother Yassine loves eggs. He eats two eggs every day! Every Friday, we have couscous for lunch, and in the evening we eat a vegetable tagine. My favorite food is harira. It's a hot soup with tomatoes and chickpeas. Do you like Moroccan food?","text_da":"F lmeghrib, lftour mohim bzzaf. Kol sbah, ana w l3a2ila dyali kanftro m3a b3diyatna f ttmenya. Kanaklo lkhobz b zit l3oud, zzebda w l3sel. Mmi katsawb atay b nna3na3, w bba kaychreb l9ehwa b l7lib. Ana makat3jebnich l9ehwa, lhada kanchreb atay. Khouya sghir Yassine kay3che9 lbid. Kayakol jouj bidat kol nhar! Kol jem3a, kanaklo kesksou f lghda, w f l3chiya kanaklo tajin dyal lkhodra. Lmakla li kat3jebni kter hiya l7rira. Hiya sobba skhouna b matecha w l7emmes. Wach kat3jbek lmakla lmeghribiya?","glossary":[{"en":"important","da":"mohim"},{"en":"together","da":"m3a b3diyatna / mjmou3in"},{"en":"butter","da":"zzebda"},{"en":"honey","da":"l3sel"},{"en":"so","da":"lhada / 3la hadchi"},{"en":"soup","da":"sobba"},{"en":"tomatoes","da":"matecha"},{"en":"chickpeas","da":"l7emmes"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach kayftro l3a2ila dyal Nouha?","options":["F ssb3a","F ttmenya","F tts3oud","F l3chra"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"at eight o'clock\" = f ttmenya."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha likes coffee.","statement_da":"Nouha kat3jebha l9ehwa.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"I don't like coffee, so I drink tea.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kay3che9 Yassine?","options":["Lkesksou","L9ehwa","Lbid","L7out"],"answer":2,"explain_da":"\"My little brother Yassine loves eggs.\" — `eggs` = lbid."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno hiya lmakla li kat3jeb Nouha kter?","options":["L7rira","Ttajin","Lkesksou","Atay"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"My favorite food is harira.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Lghda f restora","emoji":"🍽️","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar bin Omar w lgarson (`waiter`). Rekkzi 3la: chno talb Omar bach yakol? w chno bgha ychreb?","lines":[{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Good afternoon, sir. What would you like?","da":"Msa lkhir, a ssi. Chno bghiti?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Hello. I'd like a chicken tagine, please.","da":"Salam. Bghit tajin dyal ddjaj, 3afak."},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Good choice! Would you like some bread with it?","da":"Khtyar mzyan! Bghiti chwiya dyal lkhobz m3ah?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, please. And a salad.","da":"Ah, 3afak. W chlada."},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"And to drink? We have water, orange juice and mint tea.","da":"W chno tchreb? 3ndna lma, 3assir llimoun w atay b nna3na3."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"An orange juice, please. I don't like tea.","da":"3assir dyal llimoun, 3afak. Makay3jebnich atay."},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Really? You're Moroccan and you don't like tea!","da":"Bsse7? Nta meghribi w makay3jbekch atay!"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I know! I love coffee. Can I have a coffee after lunch?","da":"3reft! Kan3che9 l9ehwa. Wach momkin 9ehwa men ba3d lghda?"},{"speaker":"Waiter","en":"Of course. Anything else?","da":"Wakha. Chi 7aja khra?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"No, that's all. Thank you.","da":"La, safi. Choukran."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno talb Omar bach yakol?","options":["Tajin dyal ddjaj","Kesksou","L7rira","L7out"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'd like a chicken tagine, please.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar likes mint tea.","statement_da":"Omar kay3jbo atay b nna3na3.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: 9al \"I don't like tea.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno bgha ychreb Omar m3a lghda?","options":["Atay","3assir dyal llimoun","Lma","L9ehwa"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"An orange juice, please.\" L9ehwa bghaha men ba3d lghda."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Would you like some bread with it?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kaysewwel lgarson?","options":["Wach bghiti lkhobz m3ah","Wach bghiti atay","Wach bghiti l7sab","Wach bghiti chlada"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Would you like…?` = wach bghiti…? `some bread` = chwiya dyal lkhobz."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"I like couscous, but I don't like fish.","da":"Kay3jebni lkesksou, walakin makay3jebnich l7out.","pron":"aï laïk kous-kous, bat aï dont laïk fich"},{"target_en":"Do you like mint tea? — Yes, I do!","da":"Wach kay3jbek atay b nna3na3? — Ah, kay3jebni!","pron":"dou you laïk mint ti? — yès, aï dou"},{"target_en":"I'd like a chicken tagine, please.","da":"Bghit tajin dyal ddjaj, 3afak.","pron":"aïd laïk a tchi-kin ta-jin, pliz"},{"target_en":"Can I have some water, please?","da":"Wach momkin chwiya dyal lma, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï hav sam wo-teur, pliz"},{"target_en":"We have breakfast at seven o'clock.","da":"Kanftro f ssb3a.","pron":"wi hav brék-feust at sé-veun o-klok"},{"target_en":"The bill, please. Thank you!","da":"L7sab, 3afak. Choukran!","pron":"the bil, pliz. thank you"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"F l9ehwa: telbi lftour","context_da":"Nti f wa7ed l9ehwa f Marrakech. Lgarson ghadi yhder m3ak. Telbi chno bghiti b adab (`I'd like…` / `Can I have…, please?`). Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning! Welcome. What would you like?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir! Mer7ba. Chno bghiti?","expect_keywords":["i'd like","i would like","can i have","please","tea","coffee","juice"],"sample_en":"I'd like a mint tea, please."},{"bot_en":"With sugar or without sugar?","bot_da":"B ssokkar wla bla sokkar?","expect_keywords":["with","without","sugar","yes","no","please"],"sample_en":"With sugar, please."},{"bot_en":"Would you like something to eat?","bot_da":"Bghiti chi 7aja takliha?","expect_keywords":["bread","egg","eggs","yes","can i have","i'd like","olive","please"],"sample_en":"Yes, can I have some bread and two eggs, please?"},{"bot_en":"Anything else?","bot_da":"Chi 7aja khra?","expect_keywords":["no","that's all","thats all","thank","nothing","juice","water"],"sample_en":"No, that's all, thank you."},{"bot_en":"Here you are. Enjoy your breakfast!","bot_da":"Tfeddli. Bssa7a!","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks"],"sample_en":"Thank you very much!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Lmakla li kat3jbek","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal 3la lmakla w lmachroubat: chno kay3jbek, chno makay3jbekch, chno katakli f lftour, w chno hiya lmakla li kat3jbek kter. Sta3mli `like`, `love`, `don't like`.","helper_en":["I like ... and ...","I don't like ...","For breakfast, I have ...","My favorite food is ...","I love ..."],"min_words":25,"keywords":["like","food","breakfast"],"model_en":"I love Moroccan food. I like couscous, tagine and harira, but I don't like fish. For breakfast, I have bread with olive oil and a mint tea. I don't drink coffee. My favorite food is chicken tagine with olives. My mother makes it every Friday."}},{"id":"l10","order":10,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"🏠","title_en":"My house: there is / there are","title_da":"Ddar dyali: there is / there are","goals_da":["Twesfi ddar dyalek b `There is…` w `There are…`","Tsewli `Is there a…?` / `Are there any…?` w tjawbi `Yes, there is` / `No, there aren't`","T9oli fin kayna chi 7aja: `in`, `on`, `under`, `next to`, `behind`, `in front of`, `between`","Tsemmi lbyout w l'atat dyal ddar b lingliziya"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"There is / There are — kayn / kaynin","body_da":"Bach n9oulo belli chi 7aja kayna f chi blasa, kansta3mlo `there is` wla `there are`. Bhal \"kayn / kayna / kaynin\" f darija.\n\n- `There is` (`There's`) + 7aja we7da: `There is a table in the kitchen.` = Kayna tabla f lkouzina.\n- `There are` + bzzaf dyal l7wayj: `There are two bedrooms.` = Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as.\n\n**Redi lbal:** `there` hna makat3nich \"tmma\" — hiya ghir bach nbdaw ljomla, bhal \"kayn\". F darija kan9oulo \"kayna tabla\", f lingliziya `There is a table`.\n\nM3a l7wayj li makayt7esbouch (dars 9) kansta3mlo `there is`: `There is some milk in the fridge.` = Kayn chwiya dyal l7lib f ttellaja.\n\n`There's` = `There is` m9essra, kat9al bzzaf f lhadra. `There are` ma3ndhach ta9sir f lhadra.","examples":[{"en":"There is a big window in the living room.","da":"Kayn cherjem kbir f ssalon.","pron":"thér iz a big win-do in the li-ving roum"},{"en":"There's a TV in the living room.","da":"Kayna tilifizyon f ssalon.","pron":"thérz a ti-vi in the li-ving roum"},{"en":"There are three bedrooms in my house.","da":"Kaynin tlata dyal byout nn3as f ddar dyali.","pron":"thér ar thri béd-roumz in maï haws"},{"en":"There are some eggs in the fridge.","da":"Kayn chi bid f ttellaja.","pron":"thér ar sam égz in the fridj"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Is there…? Are there…? — Wach kayn…?","body_da":"**Nnafi (−):** kanzido `not`:\n\n- `There isn't a garden.` (= `There is not`) = Makaynach jerda.\n- `There aren't any chairs.` (= `There are not`) = Makaynch chi kersa.\n\nF nnafi w f ssou2al kansta3mlo `any` (dars 9): `There aren't any chairs.`\n\n**Ssou2al (?):** kan9elbo lfi3l l lewwel: `Is there…?` / `Are there…?`\n\n- `Is there a bathroom?` = Wach kayn bit lma?\n- `Yes, there is.` / `No, there isn't.`\n- `Are there any windows?` = Wach kaynin chi chrajem?\n- `Yes, there are.` / `No, there aren't.`\n\nF ljawab l9ssir makanzidouch l7aja: `Yes, there is.` — safi, bhal \"ah, kayn\" f darija.\n\nBach tsewli 3la l3adad: `How many bedrooms are there?` = Ch7al men bit nn3as kayn? — `There are two.`","examples":[{"en":"Is there a fridge in the kitchen? — Yes, there is.","da":"Wach kayna tellaja f lkouzina? — Ah, kayna.","pron":"iz thér a fridj in the ki-tchin? — yès, thér iz"},{"en":"Are there any chairs? — No, there aren't.","da":"Wach kaynin chi krasa? — La, makaynch.","pron":"ar thér é-ni tchérz? — no, thér arnt"},{"en":"There isn't a garden, but there's a big balcony.","da":"Makaynach jerda, walakin kayn balkon kbir.","pron":"thér iznt a gar-deun, bat thérz a big bal-ko-ni"},{"en":"How many rooms are there? — There are five.","da":"Ch7al men bit kayn? — Kaynin khemsa.","pron":"haw mé-ni roumz ar thér? — thér ar faïv"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Fin kayna? — in, on, under, next to…","body_da":"Bach n9oulo fin kayna chi 7aja, kansta3mlo had lkelmat sghar (`prepositions` = lkelmat dyal lblasa):\n\n- `in` = f / dakhel: `The milk is in the fridge.`\n- `on` = fo9 (lasa9 b l7aja): `The book is on the table.`\n- `under` = t7t: `The cat is under the bed.`\n- `next to` = 7da: `The chair is next to the window.`\n- `behind` = mora / wra: `The garden is behind the house.`\n- `in front of` = 9eddam: `There's a car in front of the door.`\n- `between` = bin: `The bathroom is between the two bedrooms.`\n\nMen ba3d had lkelmat, ghaliban kansta3mlo `the`: `in the kitchen`, `on the table` — 7it kanhedro 3la 7aja m3rofa.\n\nBhal f darija, lkelma dyal lblasa kadji 9bel l7aja: \"f lkouzina\" → `in the kitchen`, \"7da lbab\" → `next to the door`.","examples":[{"en":"The keys are on the table.","da":"Sswaret 3la ttabla.","pron":"the kiz ar on the téy-beul"},{"en":"The cat is under the sofa.","da":"Lmech t7t ssofa.","pron":"the kat iz an-deur the so-fa"},{"en":"The fridge is next to the window.","da":"Ttellaja 7da cherjem.","pron":"the fridj iz nékst tou the win-do"},{"en":"There's a small garden behind the house.","da":"Kayna jerda sghira mora ddar.","pron":"thérz a smol gar-deun bi-haïnd the haws"},{"en":"The bathroom is between the kitchen and the bedroom.","da":"Bit lma bin lkouzina w bit nn3as.","pron":"the bath-roum iz bi-twin the ki-tchin and the béd-roum"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ddar dyali — kifach nwesfha","body_da":"Bach twesfi ddar dyalek, bdi b: `I live in a house.` (= dar) wla `I live in a flat.` (= apartma — f Amerika kay9oulo `apartment`). Men ba3d 9oli chno kayn fiha b `There is` / `There are`.\n\nLbyout dyal ddar:\n\n- `living room` = ssalon\n- `kitchen` = lkouzina\n- `bedroom` = bit nn3as\n- `bathroom` = bit lma / ddouch\n- `balcony` = lbalkon\n\nMelli kanhedro 3la bit m3rof f ddar, kansta3mlo `the`: `The kitchen is small.` W kanwesfo b ssifat dyal dars 6: `big`, `small`, `new`, `old`, `beautiful`.\n\n`My favorite room is the living room.` = Lbit li kay3jebni kter howa ssalon.","examples":[{"en":"I live in a flat in Casablanca.","da":"Kanskon f apartma f Casa.","pron":"aï liv in a flat in ka-za-blan-ka"},{"en":"There are two bedrooms and a small kitchen.","da":"Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as w kouzina sghira.","pron":"thér ar tou béd-roumz and a smol ki-tchin"},{"en":"The living room is big and beautiful.","da":"Ssalon kbir w zwin.","pron":"the li-ving roum iz big and biou-ti-foul"},{"en":"My favorite room is the kitchen.","da":"Lbit li kay3jebni kter howa lkouzina.","pron":"maï féy-vrit roum iz the ki-tchin"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"house","da":"dar","emoji":"🏠","pron":"haws","example_en":"I live in a small house.","example_da":"Kanskon f dar sghira."},{"en":"flat","da":"apartma","emoji":"🏢","pron":"flat","example_en":"My sister lives in a flat in Rabat.","example_da":"Khti kateskon f apartma f Rabat."},{"en":"living room","da":"ssalon","emoji":"🛋️","pron":"li-ving roum","example_en":"We watch TV in the living room.","example_da":"Kantferrjo f ttilifizyon f ssalon."},{"en":"kitchen","da":"lkouzina","emoji":"🍳","pron":"ki-tchin","example_en":"My mother is in the kitchen.","example_da":"Mmi f lkouzina."},{"en":"bedroom","da":"bit nn3as","emoji":"🛏️","pron":"béd-roum","example_en":"There are three bedrooms.","example_da":"Kaynin tlata dyal byout nn3as."},{"en":"bathroom","da":"bit lma","emoji":"🚿","pron":"bath-roum","example_en":"Where is the bathroom, please?","example_da":"Fin kayn bit lma, 3afak?"},{"en":"table","da":"tabla","emoji":"🍽️","pron":"téy-beul","example_en":"Dinner is on the table!","example_da":"L3cha 3la ttabla!"},{"en":"chair","da":"kersa","emoji":"🪑","pron":"tchér","example_en":"There are four chairs in the kitchen.","example_da":"Kaynin rb3a dyal lkrasa f lkouzina."},{"en":"bed","da":"namousiya","emoji":"🛌","pron":"béd","example_en":"My bed is next to the window.","example_da":"Nnamousiya dyali 7da cherjem."},{"en":"sofa","da":"ssofa","emoji":"💺","pron":"so-fa","example_en":"The cat sleeps on the sofa.","example_da":"Lmech kayn3es 3la ssofa."},{"en":"fridge","da":"ttellaja","emoji":"🧊","pron":"fridj","example_en":"Is there any water in the fridge?","example_da":"Wach kayn chi ma f ttellaja?"},{"en":"window","da":"cherjem","emoji":"🪟","pron":"win-do","example_en":"There is a big window in my bedroom.","example_da":"Kayn cherjem kbir f bit nn3as dyali."},{"en":"door","da":"bab","emoji":"🚪","pron":"dor","example_en":"There's a car in front of the door.","example_da":"Kayna tomobil 9eddam lbab."},{"en":"garden","da":"jerda","emoji":"🌳","pron":"gar-deun","example_en":"My grandmother has a beautiful garden.","example_da":"Jeddati 3ndha jerda zwina."},{"en":"wall","da":"l7it","emoji":"🧱","pron":"wol","example_en":"There's a picture on the wall.","example_da":"Kayna teswira 3la l7it."},{"en":"lamp","da":"lampa","emoji":"💡","pron":"lamp","example_en":"There's a lamp next to the bed.","example_da":"Kayna lampa 7da nnamousiya."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"L'apartma jdid dyal Nouha","context_da":"Nouha krat apartma jdid f Agadir. Sa7ebtha Laila jat tchoufo w kattsewwel 3la ddar.","lines":[{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Wow, Nouha! Your new flat is beautiful!","da":"Waw, Nouha! L'apartma jdid dyalek zwin!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you! Come in. This is the living room.","da":"Choukran! Dkhli. Hada ssalon."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"It's big! Is there a balcony?","da":"Kbir! Wach kayn balkon?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, there is. It's behind the kitchen.","da":"Ah, kayn. Mora lkouzina."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"And how many bedrooms are there?","da":"W ch7al men bit nn3as kayn?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"There are two bedrooms and one bathroom.","da":"Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as w bit lma wa7ed."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Is there a washing machine?","da":"Wach kayna machina dyal ssabon?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, there isn't. But there's a new fridge in the kitchen.","da":"La, makaynach. Walakin kayna tellaja jdida f lkouzina."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Where's your cat?","da":"Fin lmech dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Look! He's under the sofa, next to the window.","da":"Chofi! Rah t7t ssofa, 7da cherjem."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Ma tkheltich bin `there is` w `it is`! `There is a table.` = kayna tabla (kankhebro belli kayna). `It is a table.` = hadi tabla (kan9oulo chno hiya). W tfekkri: `there` f `there is` makat3nich \"tmma\". Ila bghiti t9oli \"tmma\", 9oli `over there`: `The kitchen is over there.` Mzyan, Nouha!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"lkouzina\" b lingliziya?","options":["kitchen","bedroom","bathroom","garden"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`kitchen` = lkouzina. `bedroom` = bit nn3as. `bathroom` = bit lma. `garden` = jerda."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"There are two bedrooms.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as","Kayn bit nn3as wa7ed","Kaynin jouj kouzinat","Makaynch bit nn3as"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`There are two bedrooms.` = kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as. `There are` = kaynin (bzzaf)."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli l7aja b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"table","da":"tabla","emoji":"🍽️"},{"en":"chair","da":"kersa","emoji":"🪑"},{"en":"bed","da":"namousiya","emoji":"🛌"},{"en":"window","da":"cherjem","emoji":"🪟"},{"en":"door","da":"bab","emoji":"🚪"},{"en":"fridge","da":"tellaja","emoji":"🧊"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"There ___ a sofa in the living room.","options":["is","are","am"],"answer":"is","hint_da":"Ssofa we7da.","explain_da":"7aja we7da → `There is`. `There is a sofa in the living room.` = kayna sofa f ssalon."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"There ___ four chairs in the kitchen.","options":["are","is","have"],"answer":"are","hint_da":"Rb3a dyal lkrasa = bzzaf!","explain_da":"Bzzaf dyal l7wayj → `There are`. Redi lbal: makan9oulouch `have` hna."},{"type":"order","words":["Is","there","a","bathroom?"],"answer":"Is there a bathroom?","da":"Wach kayn bit lma?","explain_da":"F ssou2al, `Is` kadji 9bel `there`: `Is there a bathroom?`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Lmech t7t ttabla. Achmen jomla s7i7a?","options":["The cat is under the table.","The cat is on the table.","The cat is in the table.","The cat is behind the table."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`under` = t7t. `on` = fo9. `in` = f / dakhel. `behind` = mora."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"The keys are next to the phone.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fin kaynin sswaret?","options":["7da ttilifoun","T7t ttilifoun","Fo9 ttilifoun","Mora ttilifoun"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`next to` = 7da. `The keys are next to the phone.` = sswaret 7da ttilifoun."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"There aren't any chairs\" means there are no chairs.","statement_da":"`There aren't any chairs` kat3ni makaynch 7ta chi kersa.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `aren't` = `are not`, w `any` f nnafi = 7ta chi / walou."},{"type":"translate","da":"Kaynin tlata dyal lbyout f ddar dyali.","answers":["There are three rooms in my house.","There are three bedrooms in my house.","There're three rooms in my house."],"hint_en":"There ... three ... in my house.","explain_da":"`There are` + ljam3. `rooms` = lbyout. `in my house` = f ddar dyali."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Is there a garden behind the house?","da":"Wach kayna jerda mora ddar?","explain_da":"Ssou2al kaybda b `Is there`. Sem3i: `Is` – `there` – `a` – `garden` – `behind` – `the` – `house`."},{"type":"order","words":["The","bathroom","is","next","to","the","kitchen."],"answer":"The bathroom is next to the kitchen.","da":"Bit lma 7da lkouzina.","explain_da":"`next to` = 7da, kelmtin dima m3a b3diyathom."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Are there ___ windows in the bedroom?","answers":["any"],"hint_da":"F ssou2al kansta3mlo lkelma li chefna f dars 9 m3a nnafi w ssou2al.","explain_da":"F ssou2al w f nnafi: `any`. `Are there any windows in the bedroom?` = wach kaynin chi chrajem f bit nn3as?"},{"type":"translate","da":"Makaynach jerda, walakin kayn balkon.","answers":["There isn't a garden, but there is a balcony.","There isn't a garden, but there's a balcony.","There is no garden, but there is a balcony.","There is not a garden, but there is a balcony."],"hint_en":"There isn't ..., but there's ...","explain_da":"`There isn't` = makaynch / makaynach. `but` = walakin."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ljawab l9ssir s7i7.","question_en":"Are there any chairs in the living room?","options":["Yes, there are.","Yes, there is.","Yes, they are.","Yes, it is."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Ssou2al b `Are there` → ljawab b `there are`: `Yes, there are.` / `No, there aren't.`"},{"type":"speak","target_en":"There are two bedrooms and a big kitchen in my flat.","da":"Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as w kouzina kbira f l'apartma dyali.","pron":"thér ar tou béd-roumz and a big ki-tchin in maï flat"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Omar's new flat","title_da":"L'apartma jdid dyal Omar","emoji":"🏢","text_en":"Omar lives in a new flat in Tangier with his wife Amina. The flat isn't very big, but it's beautiful. There is a living room with a blue sofa, a small table and a TV. There are two bedrooms: one for Omar and Amina, and one for their daughter Lina. The kitchen is next to the living room. There's a new fridge and a big window in the kitchen. There isn't a garden, but there is a balcony behind the kitchen. Omar loves the balcony. Every evening, he drinks mint tea on the balcony and looks at the sea.","text_da":"Omar kayskon f apartma jdid f Tanja m3a mrato Amina. L'apartma machi kbir bzzaf, walakin zwin. Kayn salon fih sofa zer9a, tabla sghira w tilifizyon. Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as: wa7ed l Omar w Amina, w wa7ed l bnthom Lina. Lkouzina 7da ssalon. Kayna tellaja jdida w cherjem kbir f lkouzina. Makaynach jerda, walakin kayn balkon mora lkouzina. Omar kay3che9 lbalkon. Kol 3chiya, kaychreb atay b nna3na3 f lbalkon w kaytferrej f lb7er.","glossary":[{"en":"wife","da":"mra (mrato = lmra dyalo)"},{"en":"TV","da":"tilifizyon"},{"en":"daughter","da":"bent"},{"en":"blue","da":"zre9 / zer9a"},{"en":"balcony","da":"balkon"},{"en":"looks at","da":"kaytferrej f / kaychouf"},{"en":"sea","da":"lb7er"},{"en":"every evening","da":"kol 3chiya"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kayskon Omar?","options":["F Casa","F Tanja","F Agadir","F Fes"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"Omar lives in a new flat in Tangier\" — `Tangier` = Tanja."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"There are three bedrooms in the flat.","statement_da":"Kaynin tlata dyal byout nn3as f l'apartma.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"There are two bedrooms.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kayn lbalkon?","options":["9eddam ssalon","7da bit lma","Mora lkouzina","T7t ddar"],"answer":2,"explain_da":"\"there is a balcony behind the kitchen\" — `behind` = mora."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kaydir Omar kol 3chiya?","options":["Kaychreb atay f lbalkon","Kaytferrej f ttilifizyon","Kaytiyeb f lkouzina","Kayn3es"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Every evening, he drinks mint tea on the balcony and looks at the sea.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Kat9elleb 3la apartma","emoji":"🔑","pre_da":"Sarah bghat tekri apartma f Rabat. Kathder f ttilifoun m3a ssemsar (`agent`) Mr. Alami. Rekkzi 3la: ch7al men bit nn3as kayn? w wach kayna jerda?","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Alami","en":"Hello, Sarah. I have a nice flat for you in Agdal.","da":"Salam, Sarah. 3ndi apartma zwin lik f Agdal."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Great! How many bedrooms are there?","da":"Mzyan! Ch7al men bit nn3as kayn?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Alami","en":"There are two bedrooms and a big living room.","da":"Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as w salon kbir."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Is there a garden?","da":"Wach kayna jerda?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Alami","en":"No, there isn't a garden, but there's a small balcony.","da":"La, makaynach jerda, walakin kayn balkon sghir."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"OK. And the kitchen? Is there a fridge?","da":"Wakha. W lkouzina? Wach kayna tellaja?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Alami","en":"Yes, there is. There's a fridge, a table and four chairs.","da":"Ah, kayna. Kayna tellaja, tabla w rb3a dyal lkrasa."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Perfect! Is there a bus stop near the flat?","da":"Mzyan bzzaf! Wach kayn mo9af dyal ttobis 9rib men l'apartma?"},{"speaker":"Mr. Alami","en":"Yes, there's one in front of the building.","da":"Ah, kayn wa7ed 9eddam l3imara."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Wonderful. Can I see it tomorrow?","da":"Ra2i3. Wach momkin nchoufo ghedda?"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kayn l'apartma?","options":["F Agdal","F Casa","F Tanja","F Marrakech"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I have a nice flat for you in Agdal.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men bit nn3as kayn?","options":["Wa7ed","Jouj","Tlata","Rb3a"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"There are two bedrooms and a big living room.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"There is a big garden.","statement_da":"Kayna jerda kbira.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"there isn't a garden, but there's a small balcony.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"There's a bus stop in front of the building.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fin kayn mo9af ttobis?","options":["9eddam l3imara","Mora l3imara","7da lkouzina","F lbalkon"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`in front of` = 9eddam. `building` = l3imara."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"There's a big kitchen in my house.","da":"Kayna kouzina kbira f ddar dyali.","pron":"thérz a big ki-tchin in maï haws"},{"target_en":"There are two bedrooms and one bathroom.","da":"Kaynin jouj byout dyal nn3as w bit lma wa7ed.","pron":"thér ar tou béd-roumz and wan bath-roum"},{"target_en":"Is there a fridge? — Yes, there is.","da":"Wach kayna tellaja? — Ah, kayna.","pron":"iz thér a fridj? — yès, thér iz"},{"target_en":"The cat is under the table.","da":"Lmech t7t ttabla.","pron":"the kat iz an-deur the téy-beul"},{"target_en":"My bed is next to the window.","da":"Nnamousiya dyali 7da cherjem.","pron":"maï béd iz nékst tou the win-do"},{"target_en":"There isn't a garden, but there's a balcony.","da":"Makaynach jerda, walakin kayn balkon.","pron":"thér iznt a gar-deun, bat thérz a bal-ko-ni"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Wesfi ddar dyalek","context_da":"Sa7ebtek Sarah bghat t3ref kifach ddar dyalek. Jawbi 3la l'as2ila dyalha b `There is` / `There are` w lkelmat dyal lblasa. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! Do you live in a house or a flat?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Wach kattskni f dar wla f apartma?","expect_keywords":["house","flat","apartment","i live"],"sample_en":"I live in a flat."},{"bot_en":"How many bedrooms are there?","bot_da":"Ch7al men bit nn3as kayn?","expect_keywords":["there are","there is","there's","one","two","three","four","bedroom"],"sample_en":"There are two bedrooms."},{"bot_en":"Is there a garden or a balcony?","bot_da":"Wach kayna jerda wla balkon?","expect_keywords":["there is","there's","there isn't","yes","no","garden","balcony"],"sample_en":"There isn't a garden, but there's a balcony."},{"bot_en":"What is there in your living room?","bot_da":"Chno kayn f ssalon dyalek?","expect_keywords":["there is","there's","there are","sofa","table","tv","chair","chairs","window"],"sample_en":"There's a sofa, a table and a TV."},{"bot_en":"Nice! Where is the kitchen?","bot_da":"Zwin! Fin kayna lkouzina?","expect_keywords":["next to","behind","in front of","between","near","the kitchen is","it's","it is"],"sample_en":"The kitchen is next to the living room."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ddar dyali","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal 3la ddar dyalek: wach dar wla apartma, ch7al men bit kayn, chno kayn f ssalon w f lkouzina, w fin kayna kol 7aja. Sta3mli `There is`, `There are` w lkelmat dyal lblasa (`in`, `on`, `next to`…).","helper_en":["I live in a ...","There are ... bedrooms.","In the living room, there is ...","The kitchen is next to ...","There isn't a ..., but there is ..."],"min_words":30,"keywords":["there","room","kitchen"],"model_en":"I live in a flat in Casablanca. There are two bedrooms, a kitchen and a bathroom. In the living room, there is a big sofa, a table and a TV. The kitchen is next to the living room. There isn't a garden, but there is a small balcony behind the kitchen. My bed is next to the window."}},{"id":"l11","order":11,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"📅","title_en":"Days, months, dates & weather","title_da":"L'iyam, chhour, ttarikh w ljow","goals_da":["T9oli l'iyam dyal ssimana w chhour dyal l3am b lingliziya","Tsewli w tjawbi 3la ttarikh: `What's the date today?` — `It's the 5th of May.`","Tsta3mli `in`, `on`, `at` m3a lwa9t: `in May`, `on Monday`, `at 7`","Thedri 3la ljow: `What's the weather like?` — `It's sunny / cold / raining.`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'iyam dyal ssimana","body_da":"Ssimana (`week`) fiha sb3a dyal l'iyam (`days`). F lingliziya, smiyat l'iyam dima kaybdaw b 7arf kbir:\n\n- `Monday` = ttnin\n- `Tuesday` = ttlat\n- `Wednesday` = larb3\n- `Thursday` = lkhmis\n- `Friday` = jjem3a\n- `Saturday` = ssebt\n- `Sunday` = l7ed\n\nLwikend (`weekend`) howa ssebt w l7ed. `Today` = lyouma, `tomorrow` = ghedda, `yesterday` = lbare7.\n\nBach tsewli: `What day is it today?` = Chno lyouma f ssimana? Ljawab: `It's Friday.` / `Today is Friday.`\n\nM3a l'iyam kansta3mlo `on`: `on Monday` = nhar ttnin. `on Fridays` (b `-s`) = kol jem3a.","examples":[{"en":"What day is it today? — It's Wednesday.","da":"Chno lyouma? — Lyouma larb3.","pron":"wat déy iz it tou-déy? — its wénz-déy"},{"en":"I don't work on Sundays.","da":"Makankhdemch nhar l7ed.","pron":"aï dont weurk on san-déyz"},{"en":"We eat couscous on Fridays.","da":"Kanaklo kesksou kol jem3a.","pron":"wi it kous-kous on fraï-déyz"},{"en":"See you on Monday!","da":"Nchoufouk nhar ttnin!","pron":"si you on man-déy"},{"en":"Tomorrow is Saturday. It's the weekend!","da":"Ghedda ssebt. Lwikend!","pron":"tou-mo-ro iz sa-teur-déy. its the wik-énd"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Chhour w ttarikh — the 5th of May","body_da":"Chhour (`months`) dyal l3am, 7ta houma b 7arf kbir:\n\n`January` (yanayer), `February` (fibrayer), `March` (mars), `April` (abril), `May` (may), `June` (younyou), `July` (youlyouz), `August` (ghocht), `September` (chotanbir), `October` (oktobr), `November` (nowanbir), `December` (dojanbir).\n\n**L'ar9am ttartibiya** (`ordinal numbers` = lewwel, ttani, ttalet…): bach n9oulo ttarikh, makansta3mlouch `one`, `two`, `three`, kansta3mlo:\n\n- `1st` = `first`, `2nd` = `second`, `3rd` = `third`\n- men 4 l 20 kanzido `-th`: `4th` = `fourth`, `5th` = `fifth`, `6th` = `sixth`, `10th` = `tenth`, `12th` = `twelfth`, `20th` = `twentieth`\n- `21st` = `twenty-first`, `22nd` = `twenty-second`, `23rd` = `twenty-third`, `30th` = `thirtieth`, `31st` = `thirty-first`\n\n**Ttarikh:** `What's the date today?` = Chno ttarikh dyal lyouma?\n\n- `It's the fifth of May.` (kanktbo `5th May` wla `May 5th`)\n- `It's May the fifth.` — nefs lma3na.\n\nF lhadra kanzido `the` 9bel rra9m w `of` 9bel chhar: `the fifth of May`. L3am kay9al b jouj jouj: `2026` = `twenty twenty-six`.","examples":[{"en":"What's the date today? — It's the third of March.","da":"Chno ttarikh dyal lyouma? — Tlata mars.","pron":"wats the déyt tou-déy? — its the theurd ov martch"},{"en":"My birthday is on the 12th of August.","da":"3id miladi nhar 12 ghocht.","pron":"maï beurth-déy iz on the twélfth ov o-geust"},{"en":"Ramadan starts in February this year.","da":"Ramdan kaybda f fibrayer had l3am.","pron":"ra-ma-dan starts in féb-rou-é-ri this yir"},{"en":"The first of January is a holiday.","da":"Wa7ed yanayer 3otla.","pron":"the feurst ov dja-niou-é-ri iz a ho-li-déy"},{"en":"Today is Friday, the 21st of November.","da":"Lyouma jjem3a, 21 nowanbir.","pron":"tou-déy iz fraï-déy, the twén-ti-feurst ov no-vém-beur"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"in, on, at — m3a lwa9t","body_da":"Had tlata dyal lkelmat sghar kaykhelto nnas bzzaf. 7fediha hakka:\n\n- `at` + ssa3a: `at 7 o'clock`, `at half past eight`, `at noon` (= f ttnach dyal nhar), `at night` (= f lil)\n- `on` + nhar wla tarikh: `on Monday`, `on Friday morning`, `on the 5th of May`, `on my birthday`\n- `in` + chhar, fasl, 3am, wla jouz2 dyal nhar: `in May`, `in summer`, `in 2026`, `in the morning`, `in the afternoon`, `in the evening`\n\nBhal wa7ed l9a3ida sahla: `at` l 7aja sghira (ssa3a), `on` l nhar, `in` l 7aja kbira (chhar, 3am).\n\n**Redi lbal:** `at night` walakin `in the morning` — hadi istithna2, 7fediha bhal ma hiya.\n\nMakansta3mlouch `in` / `on` / `at` m3a `today`, `tomorrow`, `every day`, `this week`: `I work tomorrow.` (bla `on`).","examples":[{"en":"The class starts at nine o'clock.","da":"L9ism kaybda f tts3oud.","pron":"the klas starts at naïn o-klok"},{"en":"I go to the market on Saturday morning.","da":"Kanmchi l ssou9 nhar ssebt f sbah.","pron":"aï go tou the mar-kit on sa-teur-déy mor-ning"},{"en":"My sister's birthday is in June.","da":"3id milad khti f younyou.","pron":"maï sis-teurz beurth-déy iz in djoun"},{"en":"We visit my grandmother in the afternoon.","da":"Kanzouro jeddati f l3chiya.","pron":"wi vi-zit maï grand-ma-theur in the af-teur-noun"},{"en":"I don't work at night.","da":"Makankhdemch f lil.","pron":"aï dont weurk at naït"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ljow — What's the weather like?","body_da":"Bach tsewli 3la ljow: `What's the weather like?` (7arfiyan: ljow kif dayer?) wla `How's the weather today?`\n\nLjawab dima kaybda b `It's`:\n\n- `It's sunny.` = Chemch. / Ljow mchemmes.\n- `It's hot.` = Skhoun. / Ssehd.\n- `It's warm.` = Dafi.\n- `It's cold.` = Lberd.\n- `It's cloudy.` = Mghiyyem (kayn ss7ab).\n- `It's windy.` = Kayn rri7.\n- `It's raining.` = Katsob chta.\n\nRedi lbal: `It's raining` fiha `-ing` 7it chta katsob daba. `rain` (l'ism) = chta: `I don't like the rain.`\n\n**Lfosoul** (`seasons`): `spring` (rrbi3), `summer` (ssif), `autumn` (lkhrif — f Amerika kay9oulo `fall`), `winter` (chtwa).\n\nBach tsewli 3la 3id lmilad: `When is your birthday?` = Fo9ach 3id miladek? — `It's on the 2nd of July.` / `It's in July.`","examples":[{"en":"What's the weather like today? — It's sunny and hot.","da":"Kif dayer ljow lyouma? — Chemch w skhoun.","pron":"wats the wé-theur laïk tou-déy? — its sa-ni and hot"},{"en":"It's cold and windy in Ifrane in winter.","da":"Lberd w rri7 f Ifran f chtwa.","pron":"its kold and win-di in if-ran in win-teur"},{"en":"It's raining in Tangier today.","da":"Katsob chta f Tanja lyouma.","pron":"its réy-ning in tan-djir tou-déy"},{"en":"Summer in Marrakech is very hot.","da":"Ssif f Marrakech skhoun bzzaf.","pron":"sa-meur in ma-ra-kéch iz vé-ri hot"},{"en":"When is your birthday? — It's in April.","da":"Fo9ach 3id miladek? — F abril.","pron":"wén iz your beurth-déy? — its in éy-pril"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"Monday","da":"ttnin","emoji":"💼","pron":"man-déy","example_en":"I work on Monday.","example_da":"Kankhdem nhar ttnin."},{"en":"Friday","da":"jjem3a","emoji":"🕌","pron":"fraï-déy","example_en":"My father goes to the mosque on Friday.","example_da":"Bba kaymchi l jjame3 nhar jjem3a."},{"en":"Sunday","da":"l7ed","emoji":"☀️","pron":"san-déy","example_en":"On Sunday, we visit my grandmother.","example_da":"Nhar l7ed, kanzouro jeddati."},{"en":"week","da":"ssimana","emoji":"📅","pron":"wik","example_en":"There are seven days in a week.","example_da":"Kaynin sb3a dyal l'iyam f ssimana."},{"en":"weekend","da":"lwikend","emoji":"🎉","pron":"wik-énd","example_en":"The weekend is Saturday and Sunday.","example_da":"Lwikend howa ssebt w l7ed."},{"en":"month","da":"chhar","emoji":"📆","pron":"manth","example_en":"May is my favorite month.","example_da":"May howa chhar li kay3jebni kter."},{"en":"year","da":"3am","emoji":"🎆","pron":"yir","example_en":"There are twelve months in a year.","example_da":"Kaynin tnach chhar f l3am."},{"en":"birthday","da":"3id lmilad","emoji":"🎂","pron":"beurth-déy","example_en":"Happy birthday, Nouha!","example_da":"3id milad sa3id, Nouha!"},{"en":"weather","da":"ljow","emoji":"🌤️","pron":"wé-theur","example_en":"What's the weather like in Agadir?","example_da":"Kif dayer ljow f Agadir?"},{"en":"sunny","da":"mchemmes / chemch","emoji":"🌞","pron":"sa-ni","example_en":"It's sunny in Marrakech.","example_da":"Chemch f Marrakech."},{"en":"cloudy","da":"mghiyyem","emoji":"☁️","pron":"klaw-di","example_en":"It's cloudy in Casablanca today.","example_da":"Mghiyyem f Casa lyouma."},{"en":"hot","da":"skhoun","emoji":"🥵","pron":"hot","example_en":"It's very hot in August.","example_da":"Skhoun bzzaf f ghocht."},{"en":"cold","da":"bared / lberd","emoji":"❄️","pron":"kold","example_en":"It's cold in the mountains.","example_da":"Lberd f jjbel."},{"en":"rain","da":"chta","emoji":"🌧️","pron":"réyn","example_en":"It's raining today. I love the rain!","example_da":"Katsob chta lyouma. Kan3che9 chta!"},{"en":"summer","da":"ssif","emoji":"🏖️","pron":"sa-meur","example_en":"We go to the beach in summer.","example_da":"Kanmchiw l lb7er f ssif."},{"en":"winter","da":"chtwa","emoji":"🧣","pron":"win-teur","example_en":"In winter, it's cold and it rains.","example_da":"F chtwa, lberd w katsob chta."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"3id lmilad dyal Sarah","context_da":"Nouha w Sarah kayhedro 3la 3id lmilad w 3la ljow. Sarah bghat tdir 7afla sghira.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, when is your birthday?","da":"Nouha, fo9ach 3id miladek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"It's on the 14th of March. And you?","da":"Nhar 14 mars. W nti?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"My birthday is next Saturday, the 7th of November!","da":"3id miladi ssebt jjay, 7 nowanbir!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Really? Happy birthday! What's the weather like in Canada in November?","da":"Bsse7? 3id milad sa3id! Kif dayer ljow f Canada f nowanbir?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"It's very cold, and sometimes it snows. But here in Rabat it's warm and sunny.","da":"Lberd bzzaf, w chi merrat kattiy7 ttelj. Walakin hna f Rabat dafi w chemch."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I love autumn in Morocco. Do you have a party on Saturday?","da":"Ah, kan3che9 lkhrif f lmeghrib. Wach 3ndek 7afla nhar ssebt?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Yes! A small party at my flat at 7 o'clock. Are you free?","da":"Ah! 7afla sghira f l'apartma dyali f ssb3a. Wach nti fadya?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Of course! I don't work on Saturdays.","da":"Akid! Makankhdemch nhar ssebt."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Great! See you on Saturday at seven.","da":"Mzyan! Nchoufouk ssebt f ssb3a."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"See you! And happy birthday again!","da":"Nchoufouk! W 3id milad sa3id merra khra!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Smiyat l'iyam w chhour dima b 7arf kbir f lingliziya: `Monday`, `May`. W ila nsiti `in` / `on` / `at`, tfekkri hakka: `at` ssa3a, `on` nhar, `in` chhar. Mzyan, Nouha! Jarrbi t9oli ttarikh dyal lyouma kol sbah b lingliziya: `Today is Monday, the 3rd of November.`"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"jjem3a\" b lingliziya?","options":["Friday","Monday","Sunday","Saturday"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Friday` = jjem3a. `Monday` = ttnin. `Sunday` = l7ed. `Saturday` = ssebt."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's cold and windy today.","question_da":"Sem3i. Kif dayer ljow?","options":["Lberd w rri7","Chemch w skhoun","Katsob chta","Mghiyyem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`cold` = bared / lberd. `windy` = kayn rri7."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli nhar b lingliziya m3a smiyto b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"Monday","da":"ttnin","emoji":"1️⃣"},{"en":"Wednesday","da":"larb3","emoji":"3️⃣"},{"en":"Thursday","da":"lkhmis","emoji":"4️⃣"},{"en":"Saturday","da":"ssebt","emoji":"6️⃣"},{"en":"Sunday","da":"l7ed","emoji":"7️⃣"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"My birthday is ___ May.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":"in","hint_da":"Chhar → achmen kelma?","explain_da":"M3a chhar kansta3mlo `in`: `in May`, `in July`."},{"type":"order","words":["What's","the","date","today?"],"answer":"What's the date today?","da":"Chno ttarikh dyal lyouma?","explain_da":"`What's the date today?` — ssou2al dyal ttarikh."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"`3rd` kifach kat9ra?","options":["third","three","thirty","thirteenth"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`3rd` = `third` (ttalet). `three` = tlata (3adi). `thirty` = tlatin. `thirteenth` = `13th`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"The party is on Saturday at eight o'clock.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fo9ach l7afla?","options":["Ssebt f ttmenya","L7ed f ttmenya","Ssebt f ssb3a","Jjem3a f ttmenya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`on Saturday` = nhar ssebt. `at eight o'clock` = f ttmenya."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"The class starts ___ nine o'clock.","options":["at","in","on"],"answer":"at","hint_da":"Ssa3a → achmen kelma?","explain_da":"M3a ssa3a kansta3mlo `at`: `at nine o'clock`."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"It's raining\" means the weather is sunny.","statement_da":"`It's raining` kat3ni ljow mchemmes.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `It's raining` = katsob chta. `sunny` = chemch."},{"type":"translate","da":"Kif dayer ljow lyouma?","answers":["What's the weather like today?","What is the weather like today?","How's the weather today?","How is the weather today?"],"hint_en":"What's the ... like today?","explain_da":"`What's the weather like today?` — `like` hna makat3nich \"kay3jeb\", hiya jouz2 men ssou2al."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"My birthday is on the second of July.","da":"3id miladi nhar jouj youlyouz.","explain_da":"`on the second of July` = nhar 2 youlyouz. Sem3i mzyan `second` (`2nd`) w `July`."},{"type":"order","words":["It's","sunny","and","hot","in","Agadir."],"answer":"It's sunny and hot in Agadir.","da":"Chemch w skhoun f Agadir.","explain_da":"Ljow dima kaybda b `It's`: `It's sunny and hot…`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Lyouma larb3. Ghedda achmen nhar?","options":["Thursday","Tuesday","Friday","Wednesday"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Wednesday` = larb3, men ba3do kayji `Thursday` = lkhmis."},{"type":"translate","da":"Makankhdemch nhar l7ed.","answers":["I don't work on Sunday.","I don't work on Sundays.","I do not work on Sunday.","I do not work on Sundays."],"hint_en":"I don't ... on ...","explain_da":"M3a nhar: `on`. `on Sundays` (b `-s`) = kol 7ed."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"January, February, ___, April.","answers":["March","march"],"hint_da":"Chhar ttalet f l3am.","explain_da":"`March` = mars, chhar 3. Men ba3do `April` = abril."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"What's the weather like today? It's sunny and warm.","da":"Kif dayer ljow lyouma? Chemch w dafi.","pron":"wats the wé-theur laïk tou-déy? its sa-ni and worm"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Four seasons in Morocco","title_da":"Rb3a dyal lfosoul f lmeghrib","emoji":"🌦️","text_en":"Morocco has four seasons. In spring, from March to May, the weather is warm and sunny. The gardens are green and beautiful. Summer is in June, July and August. It's very hot in Marrakech and Fes, sometimes 40 degrees! Many families go to the beach in Agadir or Tangier. Autumn starts in September. The weather is nice, not very hot and not very cold. Winter is from December to February. It's cold and it rains a lot in the north. In Ifrane, it snows, and the mountains are white. My favorite season is spring, because my birthday is on the 20th of April!","text_da":"Lmeghrib fih rb3a dyal lfosoul. F rrbi3, men mars 7ta l may, ljow dafi w mchemmes. Jjnanat khder w zwinin. Ssif f younyou, youlyouz w ghocht. Skhoun bzzaf f Marrakech w Fes, chi merrat 40 daraja! Bzzaf dyal l3a2ilat kaymchiw l lb7er f Agadir wla Tanja. Lkhrif kaybda f chotanbir. Ljow zwin, machi skhoun bzzaf w machi bared bzzaf. Chtwa men dojanbir 7ta l fibrayer. Lberd w katsob chta bzzaf f chamal. F Ifran, kattiy7 ttelj, w jjbal kaywelliw byed. Lfasl li kay3jebni kter howa rrbi3, 7it 3id miladi nhar 20 abril!","glossary":[{"en":"season","da":"fasl"},{"en":"warm","da":"dafi"},{"en":"degrees","da":"daraja"},{"en":"many","da":"bzzaf dyal"},{"en":"beach","da":"lb7er / chatt"},{"en":"it rains a lot","da":"katsob chta bzzaf"},{"en":"north","da":"chamal"},{"en":"it snows","da":"kattiy7 ttelj"},{"en":"mountains","da":"jjbal"},{"en":"because","da":"7it"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach ljow skhoun bzzaf f Marrakech?","options":["F ssif","F chtwa","F rrbi3","F lkhrif"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Summer is in June, July and August. It's very hot in Marrakech and Fes.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"In winter, it rains a lot in the north of Morocco.","statement_da":"F chtwa, katsob chta bzzaf f chamal lmeghrib.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"It's cold and it rains a lot in the north.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen fasl kay3jeb lkatiba kter?","options":["Ssif","Rrbi3","Lkhrif","Chtwa"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"My favorite season is spring.\" — `spring` = rrbi3."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach 3id milad lkatiba?","options":["20 mars","20 may","20 abril","12 abril"],"answer":2,"explain_da":"\"my birthday is on the 20th of April\" — `April` = abril."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Ljow f London w f Casa","emoji":"🌤️","pre_da":"Tom f London kayhder f ttilifoun m3a sa7ebto Amina f Casa. Rekkzi 3la: kif dayer ljow f London? w f achmen chhar l3otla dyal Tom?","lines":[{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Hi Tom! How are you? What's the weather like in London?","da":"Ahlan Tom! Kidayer? Kif dayer ljow f London?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Hello Amina! It's cold and cloudy, and it's raining. I hate November!","da":"Salam Amina! Lberd w mghiyyem, w katsob chta. Kankreh nowanbir!"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Oh no! Here in Casablanca it's sunny and warm. It's 22 degrees.","da":"Wili! Hna f Casa chemch w dafi. 22 daraja."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Lucky you! When is a good month to visit Morocco?","da":"3ndek zzher! Achmen chhar mzyan bach nzour lmeghrib?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"April or May. In spring the weather is perfect, not very hot.","da":"Abril wla may. F rrbi3 ljow mzyan bzzaf, machi skhoun bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Great. My holiday is in April, from the 10th to the 20th.","da":"Mzyan. L3otla dyali f abril, men 10 7ta l 20."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Perfect! My birthday is on the 15th of April. Come to my party!","da":"Mzyan bzzaf! 3id miladi nhar 15 abril. Aji l l7afla dyali!"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Wonderful! What day is the 15th?","da":"Ra2i3! Achmen nhar howa 15?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"It's a Saturday. The party is at 8 o'clock in the evening.","da":"Ssebt. L7afla f ttmenya dyal l3chiya."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Saturday the 15th of April at eight. See you in spring, Amina!","da":"Ssebt 15 abril f ttmenya. Nchoufouk f rrbi3, Amina!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kif dayer ljow f London?","options":["Lberd w katsob chta","Chemch w dafi","Skhoun bzzaf","Kayn rri7"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"It's cold and cloudy, and it's raining.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"F achmen chhar l3otla dyal Tom?","options":["F nowanbir","F abril","F may","F dojanbir"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"My holiday is in April, from the 10th to the 20th.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Amina's birthday is on the 15th of May.","statement_da":"3id milad Amina nhar 15 may.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"My birthday is on the 15th of April.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"The party is at 8 o'clock in the evening.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fo9ach l7afla?","options":["F ttmenya dyal l3chiya","F ttmenya dyal sbah","F ssb3a dyal l3chiya","F tts3oud dyal l3chiya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`at 8 o'clock` = f ttmenya. `in the evening` = dyal l3chiya."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Today is Monday, the first of June.","da":"Lyouma ttnin, wa7ed younyou.","pron":"tou-déy iz man-déy, the feurst ov djoun"},{"target_en":"What's the weather like? — It's sunny and hot.","da":"Kif dayer ljow? — Chemch w skhoun.","pron":"wats the wé-theur laïk? — its sa-ni and hot"},{"target_en":"My birthday is on the twentieth of October.","da":"3id miladi nhar 20 oktobr.","pron":"maï beurth-déy iz on the twén-ti-eth ov ok-to-beur"},{"target_en":"It's cold and it's raining in Tangier.","da":"Lberd w katsob chta f Tanja.","pron":"its kold and its réy-ning in tan-djir"},{"target_en":"I don't work on Saturday and Sunday.","da":"Makankhdemch ssebt w l7ed.","pron":"aï dont weurk on sa-teur-déy and san-déy"},{"target_en":"See you on Thursday at ten o'clock!","da":"Nchoufouk nhar lkhmis f l3chra!","pron":"si you on theurz-déy at tén o-klok"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Ttarikh, ljow w 3id lmilad","context_da":"L'oustad Mr. Brown kaysewlek 3la lyouma, ttarikh w ljow. Jawbi b jomal kamla: `It's…`, `Today is…`. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning, Nouha! What day is it today?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha! Chno lyouma f ssimana?","expect_keywords":["monday","tuesday","wednesday","thursday","friday","saturday","sunday"],"sample_en":"Today is Monday."},{"bot_en":"And what's the date today?","bot_da":"W chno ttarikh dyal lyouma?","expect_keywords":["it's the","first","second","third","fourth","fifth","sixth","seventh","eighth","ninth","tenth","january","february","march","april","may","june","july","august","september","october","november","december"],"sample_en":"It's the fifth of May."},{"bot_en":"What's the weather like today?","bot_da":"Kif dayer ljow lyouma?","expect_keywords":["sunny","hot","cold","cloudy","windy","raining","warm","nice","it's"],"sample_en":"It's sunny and warm."},{"bot_en":"Nice. When is your birthday?","bot_da":"Mzyan. Fo9ach 3id miladek?","expect_keywords":["my birthday is","it's on","it's in","january","february","march","april","may","june","july","august","september","october","november","december"],"sample_en":"My birthday is on the 14th of March."},{"bot_en":"What's your favorite season, and why?","bot_da":"Achmen fasl kay3jbek kter, w 3lach?","expect_keywords":["spring","summer","autumn","fall","winter","because","favorite"],"sample_en":"My favorite season is spring, because the weather is warm."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ssimana dyali w ljow","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal: achmen iyam katkhdmi wla kat9ray, chno katdiri f lwikend, fo9ach 3id miladek, w kif dayer ljow f mdintek f ssif w f chtwa. Sta3mli `on`, `in`, `at`.","helper_en":["I work from Monday to ...","On Sunday, I ...","My birthday is on the ... of ...","In summer, it's ...","In winter, it's ..."],"min_words":30,"keywords":["on","in","birthday"],"model_en":"I work from Monday to Friday. I start at nine o'clock and I finish at six. On Saturday, I go to the market with my mother, and on Sunday we visit my grandmother. My birthday is on the 14th of March, in spring. In summer, it's hot and sunny in Casablanca. In winter, it's cold and it rains a lot."}},{"id":"l12","order":12,"level":"A1.2","emoji":"🛍️","title_en":"Shopping & clothes","title_da":"Tte9ssira w l7wayj","goals_da":["Tsemmi l7wayj (`dress`, `shirt`, `shoes`…) w l9yas (`small`, `medium`, `large`)","Tfehmi lbay3a melli kat9oul `Can I help you?` w tjawbi `I'm looking for…`","Tsewli 3la ttaman w t9isi l7wayj: `How much is it?`, `Can I try it on?`, `It's too big`","Tsta3mli ddama2ir dyal lmaf3oul: `me`, `you`, `him`, `her`, `it`, `us`, `them`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"F l7anout: Can I help you?","body_da":"Melli katdekhli l chi ma7al dyal l7wayj, lbay3 wla lbay3a (`shop assistant`) kay9oul lik:\n\n- `Can I help you?` = Wach n3awnek? / Chno bghiti?\n- `Are you looking for something?` = Wach kat9ellbi 3la chi 7aja?\n\nNti kat9oli:\n\n- `I'm looking for a dress.` = Kan9elleb 3la keswa. (`look for` = 9elleb 3la)\n- `I'm just looking, thanks.` = Ghir kanchouf, choukran. (ila mabghitich lmosa3ada)\n- `Do you have this in blue?` = Wach 3ndek hada b lezre9?\n- `Do you have it in a medium?` = Wach 3ndek menno l9yas lwast?\n\nL9yasat (`sizes`): `small` (`S`) = sghir, `medium` (`M`) = wast, `large` (`L`) = kbir, `extra large` (`XL`) = kbir bzzaf.\n\n`What size are you?` = Achmen 9yas dyalek? — `I'm a medium.` = L9yas dyali lwast.","examples":[{"en":"Can I help you? — Yes, please. I'm looking for a jacket.","da":"Wach n3awnek? — Ah, 3afak. Kan9elleb 3la jakita.","pron":"kan aï hélp you? — yès, pliz. aïm lou-king for a dja-kit"},{"en":"I'm just looking, thank you.","da":"Ghir kanchouf, choukran.","pron":"aïm djast lou-king, thank you"},{"en":"Do you have this shirt in a large?","da":"Wach 3ndek had l9amija b l9yas lkbir?","pron":"dou you hav this cheurt in a lardj"},{"en":"What size are you? — I'm a medium.","da":"Achmen 9yas dyalek? — L9yas lwast.","pron":"wat saïz ar you? — aïm a mi-di-eum"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ch7al ttaman? w t9isi l7wayj","body_da":"**Ttaman:** f dars 5 chefna `How much is it?`. Daba:\n\n- `How much is` + 7aja we7da: `How much is this dress?` = Ch7al had lkeswa?\n- `How much are` + bzzaf dyal l7wayj: `How much are these shoes?` = Ch7al had ssebbat?\n\nRedi lbal: `trousers`, `jeans` w `shoes` dima f ljam3 f lingliziya, 7ta ila kan serwal wa7ed: `These trousers are nice.`\n\n**T9isi:** `Can I try it on?` = Wach n9eddar n9isha? (`try on` = 9as l7wayj). M3a ljam3: `Can I try them on?`\n\n`Where is the fitting room?` = Fin kayna lkabina dyal l9yas?\n\n**Men ba3d l9yas:**\n\n- `It's too big.` / `It's too small.` = Kbira bzzaf. / Sghira bzzaf. (`too` = bzzaf, kter men lma39oul)\n- `It's perfect!` = 3la 9eddi, mzyana bzzaf!\n- `I'll take it.` = Ghadi nakhodha. (ya3ni: bghitha, ghadi nkhellesha)\n- `I'll think about it.` = Ghadi nfekker. (ila mabghitihach, b adab)\n\n`too` machi bhal `very`: `very big` = kbira bzzaf (3adi, wasf), `too big` = kbira bzzaf w makatsla7ch lik.","examples":[{"en":"How much is this scarf? — It's 50 dirhams.","da":"Ch7al had zzif? — 50 derhem.","pron":"haw match iz this skarf? — its fif-ti deur-hamz"},{"en":"How much are these shoes? — They're 100 dirhams.","da":"Ch7al had ssebbat? — 100 derhem.","pron":"haw match ar thiz chouz? — thér a han-dreud deur-hamz"},{"en":"Can I try it on, please?","da":"Wach momkin n9isha, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï traï it on, pliz"},{"en":"It's too small. Do you have a medium?","da":"Sghira bzzaf. Wach 3ndek l9yas lwast?","pron":"its tou smol. dou you hav a mi-di-eum"},{"en":"It's perfect. I'll take it!","da":"3la 9eddi. Ghadi nakhodha!","pron":"its peur-fikt. aïl téyk it"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"me, you, him, her, it, us, them — ddama2ir dyal lmaf3oul","body_da":"F dars 3 t3ellemti ddama2ir dyal lfa3il (`I`, `you`, `he`…) — li kaydir l7araka. Daba kayn ddama2ir dyal lmaf3oul (`object pronouns`) — li kaytdar 3lih l7araka. Kayjiw **men ba3d** lfi3l, wla men ba3d `for`, `with`, `to`.\n\n- `I` → `me` (ni / liya): `Help me, please.` = 3awenni, 3afak.\n- `you` → `you` (k / lik): `I love you.` = Kanbghik.\n- `he` → `him` (h / lih): `This jacket is for him.` = Had jjakita lih.\n- `she` → `her` (ha / liha): `I know her.` = Kan3refha.\n- `it` → `it` (h / ha, l 7aja): `I like it.` = 3jbatni.\n- `we` → `us` (na / lina): `Can you help us?` = Wach t9eder t3awenna?\n- `they` → `them` (hom / lihom): `I love these shoes. I'll take them!` = Kan3che9 had ssebbat. Ghadi nakhodhom!\n\nBhal f darija: \"kan3ref**ha**\" — \"ha\" f l'akhir hiya `her`. F lingliziya kelma we7dha men ba3d lfi3l: `I know her.`\n\nRedi lbal: `you` w `it` makaytbeddlouch. W `her` hiya 7ta \"dyalha\" (`her bag`) w 7ta \"ha\" (`I see her`).","examples":[{"en":"Do you like this dress? — Yes, I love it!","da":"Wach 3jbatek had lkeswa? — Ah, 3jbatni bzzaf!","pron":"dou you laïk this drés? — yès, aï lav it"},{"en":"These shoes are nice. I'll take them.","da":"Had ssebbat zwin. Ghadi nakhodhom.","pron":"thiz chouz ar naïs. aïl téyk thèm"},{"en":"This scarf is for my mother. It's a present for her.","da":"Had zzif l mmi. Hadi hdiya liha.","pron":"this skarf iz for maï ma-theur. its a pré-zeunt for heur"},{"en":"Can you help me, please?","da":"Wach t9edri t3awenni, 3afak?","pron":"kan you hélp mi, pliz"},{"en":"Omar is in the shop. I see him.","da":"Omar f l7anout. Kanchoufo.","pron":"o-mar iz in the chop. aï si him"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"L7wayj w l'alwan — a black dress","body_da":"Lfi3l `wear` = lbes: `I wear a black dress to work.` = Kanlbes keswa ke7la l lkhedma.\n\nF lingliziya, ssifa (lloun, l7ajm) kadji **9bel** l7aja — l3eks dyal darija: \"keswa ke7la\" → `a black dress`; \"sebbat byed\" → `white shoes`; \"jakita kbira\" → `a big jacket`.\n\nL'alwan li chefna f dars 6: `red` (7mer), `blue` (zre9), `green` (khder), `black` (k7el), `white` (byed), `yellow` (sfer), `brown` (9ehwi), `pink` (wardi), `grey` (rmadi).\n\n`a pair of` = zouj dyal: `a pair of shoes` (sebbat), `a pair of trousers` (serwal), `a pair of socks` (t9acher).\n\nF chtwa kanlebso `a coat` (kabbout) w `a scarf` (zif); f ssif `a T-shirt` w `sandals` (sandala).","examples":[{"en":"I wear a white shirt and black trousers to work.","da":"Kanlbes 9amija bida w serwal k7el l lkhedma.","pron":"aï wér a waït cheurt and blak traw-zeurz tou weurk"},{"en":"She wears a red scarf.","da":"Hiya katlbes zif 7mer.","pron":"chi wérz a réd skarf"},{"en":"I need a new pair of shoes.","da":"Khassni sebbat jdid.","pron":"aï nid a niou pér ov chouz"},{"en":"My favorite color is blue.","da":"Lloun li kay3jebni kter howa lezre9.","pron":"maï féy-vrit ka-leur iz blou"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"dress","da":"keswa","emoji":"👗","pron":"drés","example_en":"This dress is beautiful!","example_da":"Had lkeswa zwina!"},{"en":"shirt","da":"9amija","emoji":"👔","pron":"cheurt","example_en":"I'm looking for a white shirt.","example_da":"Kan9elleb 3la 9amija bida."},{"en":"T-shirt","da":"tichert","emoji":"👕","pron":"ti-cheurt","example_en":"He wears a T-shirt in summer.","example_da":"Howa kaylbes tichert f ssif."},{"en":"trousers","da":"serwal","emoji":"👖","pron":"traw-zeurz","example_en":"These trousers are too big.","example_da":"Had sserwal kbir bzzaf."},{"en":"jacket","da":"jakita","emoji":"🧥","pron":"dja-kit","example_en":"I need a warm jacket for winter.","example_da":"Khassni jakita dafya l chtwa."},{"en":"scarf","da":"zif","emoji":"🧣","pron":"skarf","example_en":"My grandmother wears a blue scarf.","example_da":"Jeddati katlbes zif zre9."},{"en":"shoes","da":"sebbat","emoji":"👟","pron":"chouz","example_en":"I love your shoes!","example_da":"3jebni ssebbat dyalek!"},{"en":"socks","da":"t9acher","emoji":"🧦","pron":"soks","example_en":"I need a pair of black socks.","example_da":"Khassni t9acher k7el."},{"en":"hat","da":"chapo","emoji":"🧢","pron":"hat","example_en":"He wears a hat in the sun.","example_da":"Kaylbes chapo f chemch."},{"en":"bag","da":"sak","emoji":"👜","pron":"bag","example_en":"This bag is for my sister.","example_da":"Had ssak l khti."},{"en":"size","da":"l9yas","emoji":"📏","pron":"saïz","example_en":"What size are you? — Medium.","example_da":"Achmen 9yas dyalek? — Lwast."},{"en":"price","da":"ttaman","emoji":"🏷️","pron":"praïs","example_en":"What's the price of this bag?","example_da":"Ch7al taman had ssak?"},{"en":"cheap","da":"rkhis","emoji":"💸","pron":"tchip","example_en":"These socks are cheap: 10 dirhams.","example_da":"Had tt9acher rkhas: 10 derhem."},{"en":"expensive","da":"ghali","emoji":"💎","pron":"ik-spén-siv","example_en":"This jacket is too expensive.","example_da":"Had jjakita ghalya bzzaf."},{"en":"shop","da":"7anout / ma7al","emoji":"🏬","pron":"chop","example_en":"There's a new shoe shop in Maarif.","example_da":"Kayn 7anout jdid dyal ssebbat f lma3arif."},{"en":"wear","da":"lbes","emoji":"👚","pron":"wér","example_en":"What do you wear to work?","example_da":"Chno katlebsi l lkhedma?"}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"F ma7al dyal l7wayj f Casa","context_da":"Nouha dkhlat l wa7ed ma7al dyal l7wayj f Casa bach tchri keswa l 3ers khtha. Lbay3a (`shop assistant`) smiytha Laila.","lines":[{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Good afternoon! Can I help you?","da":"Msa lkhir! Wach n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, please. I'm looking for a dress for a wedding.","da":"Ah, 3afak. Kan9elleb 3la keswa l 3ers."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"What size are you?","da":"Achmen 9yas dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm a medium. How much is this blue dress?","da":"L9yas lwast. Ch7al had lkeswa zzer9a?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"It's 300 dirhams. The fitting room is over there, next to the door.","da":"300 derhem. Lkabina dyal l9yas tmma, 7da lbab."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you. Can I try it on?","da":"Choukran. Wach n9eddar n9isha?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Of course! … How is it?","da":"Wakha! … Kif jatek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"It's too big. Do you have it in a small?","da":"Kbira bzzaf. Wach 3ndek menha l9yas sghir?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, here you are. … Oh, that's perfect on you!","da":"Ah, hak. … Wah, jatek 3la 9eddek!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I love it! I'll take it. Thank you!","da":"3jbatni bzzaf! Ghadi nakhodha. Choukran!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"F lma7alat lkbar f lmeghrib ttaman tabet, walakin f ssou9 momkin tsawmi! B lingliziya kat9oli: `That's too expensive for me.` (= ghali bzzaf 3liya) w katchoufi wach lbay3 ynzel f ttaman. W ila bghiti tkherji bla ma tchri: `Thank you, I'll think about it.` — b adab w safi. W tfekkri: `trousers`, `jeans` w `shoes` dima jam3: `How much are they?`"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"ssebbat\" b lingliziya?","options":["shoes","socks","shirt","scarf"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`shoes` = ssebbat. `socks` = tt9acher. `shirt` = l9amija. `scarf` = zzif."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Can I help you?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat9oul lbay3a?","options":["Wach n3awnek?","Ch7al ttaman?","Wach 3ndek sghir?","Fin lkabina?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Can I help you?` = wach n3awnek? Hadi lkelma lewla li kat9oul lbay3a."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli l7aja b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"dress","da":"keswa","emoji":"👗"},{"en":"trousers","da":"serwal","emoji":"👖"},{"en":"jacket","da":"jakita","emoji":"🧥"},{"en":"scarf","da":"zif","emoji":"🧣"},{"en":"hat","da":"chapo","emoji":"🧢"},{"en":"bag","da":"sak","emoji":"👜"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I'm ___ for a red dress.","options":["looking","look","like"],"answer":"looking","hint_da":"Kan9elleb 3la… = `I'm … for`","explain_da":"`I'm looking for…` = kan9elleb 3la… Dima b `-ing` men ba3d `I'm`."},{"type":"order","words":["How","much","is","this","jacket?"],"answer":"How much is this jacket?","da":"Ch7al had jjakita?","explain_da":"7aja we7da → `How much is`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"L9yas lwast b lingliziya howa:","options":["medium","small","large","big"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`small` (S) = sghir, `medium` (M) = wast, `large` (L) = kbir."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"These shoes are too small. I don't like ___.","options":["them","it","they"],"answer":"them","hint_da":"Ssebbat = jam3 → achmen damir dyal lmaf3oul?","explain_da":"`shoes` jam3 → `them`. `I don't like them.` = ma3jbounich."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's too big. Do you have a small?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno lmochkil?","options":["Kbira bzzaf, bghat sghira","Sghira bzzaf, bghat kbira","Ghalya bzzaf","Makay3jebhach lloun"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`too big` = kbira bzzaf. Katsewwel 3la `a small` = l9yas sghir."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"I'll take it\" means you want to buy it.","statement_da":"`I'll take it` kat3ni bghiti tchriha.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `I'll take it.` = ghadi nakhodha, ya3ni bghitiha w ghadi tkhellsiha."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach n9eddar n9isha?","answers":["Can I try it on?","Can I try it on, please?","Could I try it on?"],"hint_en":"Can I ... it ...?","explain_da":"`try on` = 9as l7wayj. `Can I try it on?` — `it` kadji bin `try` w `on`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"How much are these trousers?","da":"Ch7al had sserwal?","explain_da":"`trousers` dima jam3 → `How much are`. Sem3i: `How` – `much` – `are` – `these` – `trousers`."},{"type":"order","words":["This","present","is","for","her."],"answer":"This present is for her.","da":"Had lhdiya liha.","explain_da":"Men ba3d `for` kansta3mlo ddamir dyal lmaf3oul: `for her`."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Where is Omar? I don't see ___.","question_da":"Kemmli b ddamir s7i7.","options":["him","he","his","her"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Omar = rajel → `him`. `he` = fa3il (9bel lfi3l), `his` = dyalo, `her` = l mra."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"This scarf is for my mother. It's a present for ___.","answers":["her"],"hint_da":"Mmi = mra → achmen damir?","explain_da":"Mra → `her`. `It's a present for her.` = hadi hdiya liha."},{"type":"translate","da":"Had lkeswa ghalya bzzaf (kter men lma39oul).","answers":["This dress is too expensive.","The dress is too expensive.","This dress is too expensive for me."],"hint_en":"This dress is too ...","explain_da":"`too expensive` = ghalya bzzaf, kter men lma39oul. `expensive` = ghali."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Excuse me, I'm looking for a black jacket. Can I try it on?","da":"Sme7 liya, kan9elleb 3la jakita ke7la. Wach n9eddar n9isha?","pron":"ik-skiouz mi, aïm lou-king for a blak dja-kit. kan aï traï it on"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Shopping in the medina","title_da":"Tte9ssira f lmdina l9dima","emoji":"🧺","text_en":"Every Saturday morning, Amina goes shopping in the old medina of Fes with her friend Sarah. Sarah is from Canada and she loves Moroccan clothes. Today, she needs a present for her mother. In a small shop, she sees a beautiful blue scarf. \"How much is it?\" she asks. \"It's 80 dirhams,\" says the shop assistant. Sarah thinks it's a bit expensive, but she likes it very much, so she takes it. Amina buys a pair of yellow babouches, the traditional Moroccan shoes, for her father. They're small and cheap, only 60 dirhams. After shopping, they drink mint tea in a café and look at the people.","text_da":"Kol sebt f sbah, Amina katmchi tte9ssira f lmdina l9dima dyal Fes m3a sa7ebtha Sarah. Sarah men Canada w kat3che9 l7wayj lmeghribiya. Lyouma, khassha hdiya l mmha. F wa7ed l7anout sghir, chafet zif zre9 zwin. \"Ch7al?\" katsewwel. \"80 derhem,\" kat9oul lbay3a. Sarah chafetha ghalya chwiya, walakin 3jbatha bzzaf, lhada khdatha. Amina chrat belgha sefra, ssebbat lmeghribi tta9lidi, l bbaha. Sghira w rkhisa, ghir 60 derhem. Men ba3d tte9ssira, katcherbo atay b nna3na3 f l9ehwa w kaytferrjo f nnas.","glossary":[{"en":"goes shopping","da":"katmchi tte9ssira"},{"en":"clothes","da":"l7wayj"},{"en":"present","da":"hdiya"},{"en":"asks","da":"katsewwel"},{"en":"says","da":"kat9oul"},{"en":"a bit","da":"chwiya"},{"en":"babouches","da":"belgha"},{"en":"traditional","da":"tta9lidi"},{"en":"only","da":"ghir"},{"en":"people","da":"nnas"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach katmchi Amina tte9ssira?","options":["Kol sebt f sbah","Kol jem3a f l3chiya","Kol nhar","Kol 7ed"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Every Saturday morning, Amina goes shopping…\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno chrat Sarah?","options":["Belgha sefra","Zif zre9","Keswa 7emra","Jakita"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"she sees a beautiful blue scarf… so she takes it.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The scarf is 60 dirhams.","statement_da":"Zzif b 60 derhem.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: zzif b 80 derhem. Lbelgha hiya li b 60."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"L men chrat Amina lbelgha?","options":["L bbaha","L mmha","L khtha","L Sarah"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Amina buys a pair of yellow babouches… for her father.\" — `father` = bba."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F l7anout dyal ssebbat","emoji":"👟","pre_da":"Omar f 7anout dyal ssebbat f Marrakech. Sem3i l7iwar m3a lbay3 (`shop assistant`) Hassan. Rekkzi 3la: achmen 9yas khda Omar? w ch7al ttaman?","lines":[{"speaker":"Hassan","en":"Good morning! Can I help you?","da":"Sbah lkhir! Wach n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, please. I'm looking for black shoes for work.","da":"Ah, 3afak. Kan9elleb 3la sebbat k7el l lkhedma."},{"speaker":"Hassan","en":"What size are you?","da":"Achmen 9yas dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I'm a 43.","da":"43."},{"speaker":"Hassan","en":"Here you are. These are very comfortable.","da":"Hak. Hadou mrye7in bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Can I try them on? … Hmm, they're too small.","da":"Wach n9eddar n9ishom? … Hmm, sghar bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Hassan","en":"No problem. Here's a 44.","da":"Machi mochkil. Hak 44."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, these are perfect! How much are they?","da":"Ah, hadou 3la 9eddi! Ch7al?"},{"speaker":"Hassan","en":"They're 300 dirhams.","da":"300 derhem."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"OK, I'll take them. Thank you very much!","da":"Wakha, ghadi nakhodhom. Choukran bzzaf!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3la ach kay9elleb Omar?","options":["Sebbat k7el l lkhedma","Sebbat byed l rryada","Jakita","Serwal"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm looking for black shoes for work.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The first pair of shoes is too big.","statement_da":"Ssebbat lewwel kbir bzzaf.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: 9al \"they're too small\" = sghar bzzaf."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen 9yas khda Omar f l'akhir?","options":["43","44","42","45"],"answer":1,"explain_da":"\"Here's a 44.\" — \"Yes, these are perfect!\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"They're 300 dirhams.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al ttaman?","options":["300 derhem","200 derhem","30 derhem","100 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`three hundred` = 300."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Can I help you? — I'm looking for a dress.","da":"Wach n3awnek? — Kan9elleb 3la keswa.","pron":"kan aï hélp you? — aïm lou-king for a drés"},{"target_en":"How much is this shirt?","da":"Ch7al had l9amija?","pron":"haw match iz this cheurt"},{"target_en":"Can I try it on, please?","da":"Wach n9eddar n9isha, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï traï it on, pliz"},{"target_en":"It's too big. Do you have a medium?","da":"Kbira bzzaf. Wach 3ndek l9yas lwast?","pron":"its tou big. dou you hav a mi-di-eum"},{"target_en":"I love these shoes. I'll take them!","da":"3jebni had ssebbat. Ghadi nakhodhom!","pron":"aï lav thiz chouz. aïl téyk thèm"},{"target_en":"This scarf is for my mother. It's for her.","da":"Had zzif l mmi. Hadi liha.","pron":"this skarf iz for maï ma-theur. its for heur"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"F ma7al dyal l7wayj","context_da":"Nti f ma7al dyal l7wayj f Rabat. Lbay3a ghadi thder m3ak. 9oli 3la ach kat9ellbi, sewli 3la ttaman w 9isi l7aja. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good afternoon! Can I help you?","bot_da":"Msa lkhir! Wach n3awnek?","expect_keywords":["looking for","i'm looking","i need","i want","dress","jacket","shirt","shoes","trousers","scarf","yes"],"sample_en":"Yes, please. I'm looking for a jacket."},{"bot_en":"Sure. What size are you?","bot_da":"Wakha. Achmen 9yas dyalek?","expect_keywords":["small","medium","large","i'm a","size"],"sample_en":"I'm a medium."},{"bot_en":"Here you are. This one is very nice. Do you like it?","bot_da":"Hak. Hadi zwina bzzaf. Wach 3jbatek?","expect_keywords":["yes","i like","i love","how much","can i try","try it on","beautiful","nice"],"sample_en":"Yes, I like it. How much is it?"},{"bot_en":"It's 200 dirhams. Do you want to try it on?","bot_da":"200 derhem. Bghiti t9isiha?","expect_keywords":["yes","please","try","where","fitting room","ok","okay"],"sample_en":"Yes, please. Where is the fitting room?"},{"bot_en":"It's over there, next to the door. … So, how is it?","bot_da":"Tmma, 7da lbab. … Iwa, kif jatek?","expect_keywords":["too big","too small","perfect","i'll take","take it","i like","it's","good","great"],"sample_en":"It's perfect. I'll take it!"},{"bot_en":"Great! Anything else?","bot_da":"Mzyan! Chi 7aja khra?","expect_keywords":["no","that's all","thats all","thank","thanks","how much are","shoes"],"sample_en":"No, that's all, thank you."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"L7wayj li kay3jbouk","prompt_da":"Ktbi 4 wla 5 jomal 3la l7wayj: chno katlebsi l lkhedma wla f ddar, chno hiya l7aja li kat3jbek kter w chno lounha, fin katchri l7wayj dyalek (f ssou9, f lma7al…), w wach rkhas wla ghalyin. Sta3mli `wear`, `like`, `too`, `them`.","helper_en":["I usually wear ...","My favorite ... is ...","It's ... (color)","I buy my clothes in ...","They're cheap / expensive."],"min_words":30,"keywords":["wear","clothes"],"model_en":"I usually wear a black dress and a blue scarf to work. At home, I wear trousers and a T-shirt. My favorite thing is my red jacket. It's old, but I love it! I buy my clothes in the souk. The clothes there are cheap. The shoes in the big shops are too expensive, so I don't buy them."}},{"id":"l13","order":13,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"🏃‍♀️","title_en":"What are you doing now? Present continuous","title_da":"Chno katdiri daba?","goals_da":["T9oli chno katdiri daba b `am` / `is` / `are` + fi3l + `-ing`","Tsewli `What are you doing?` w tjawbi 3liha","Tferr9i bin daba (`now`) w dima (`usually`)","Thedri 3la lhiwayat dyalek: `cooking`, `reading`, `watching TV`, `listening to music`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Chno katdiri daba? — am / is / are + -ing","body_da":"Melli bghiti t9oli chno katdiri **daba, f had llo7da**, f lingliziya kanst3mlo `am` / `is` / `are` + l fi3l + `-ing`. Smiytha `present continuous` (l7adir li kaywe9e3 daba).\n\nF darija kan9oulo \"rani kantiyeb\" wla \"daba kantiyeb\" — had \"rani / daba\" hiya li kat3ti lma3na dyal 'f had llo7da'. F lingliziya, had lma3na kaydih `-ing`.\n\n- `I am cooking.` / `I'm cooking.` = (daba) kantiyeb.\n- `You are reading.` / `You're reading.` = kat9ray.\n- `He is working.` / `He's working.` = kaykhdem.\n- `She is studying.` / `She's studying.` = kat9ra.\n- `It is raining.` / `It's raining.` = katsob chta.\n- `We are watching TV.` / `We're watching TV.` = kanchoufou ttelfaza.\n- `They are playing football.` / `They're playing football.` = kayl3bou lkora.\n\nL9a3ida sahla: `to be` (li 3refti f dars 3) + fi3l + `-ing`. F lhadra, dima kanst3mlo lforma lm9essra: `I'm`, `she's`, `they're`.","examples":[{"en":"I'm cooking couscous now.","da":"Daba kantiyeb lkesksou.","pron":"aïm kou-king kous-kous naw"},{"en":"She's reading a book.","da":"Hiya kat9ra chi ktab.","pron":"chiz ri-ding a bouk"},{"en":"They're playing football in the street.","da":"Houma kayl3bou lkora f zzen9a.","pron":"théyr pléy-ing fout-bol in the strit"},{"en":"Look! It's raining.","da":"Chofi! Katsob chta.","pron":"louk! its réy-ning"},{"en":"We're watching a film.","da":"Kanchoufou wa7ed lfilm.","pron":"wir wo-tching a film"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"-ing: kifach nktbouha","body_da":"Bach nzido `-ing`, kaynin 3 9wa3ed sghar:\n\n**1. L'aghlabiya:** ghir zidi `-ing`: `read → reading`, `cook → cooking`, `play → playing`, `watch → watching`, `go → going`, `sleep → sleeping`, `study → studying` (l `y` kaytb9a!).\n\n**2. L fi3l li kaysali b `e`:** 7eyydi l `e` w zidi `-ing`: `make → making`, `write → writing`, `come → coming`, `dance → dancing`, `take → taking`, `have → having`.\n\n**3. L fi3l l9sir li kaysali b 7arf wa7ed men ba3d `a`, `e`, `i`, `o` wla `u`:** dewbli l7arf l'akhir: `sit → sitting`, `run → running`, `swim → swimming`, `shop → shopping`, `get → getting`, `stop → stopping`.\n\nRedi lbal: `studying` machi bhal `studies` (dars 8)! M3a `-ing`, l `y` makatbeddelch.","examples":[{"en":"I'm making tea.","da":"Kan3mel atay.","pron":"aïm méy-king ti"},{"en":"We're sitting in the café.","da":"7na galsin f l9ehwa.","pron":"wir si-ting in the ka-féy"},{"en":"He's running to the bus.","da":"Howa kayjri l ttobis.","pron":"hiz ra-ning tou the beus"},{"en":"Omar is writing a letter.","da":"Omar kaykteb bra.","pron":"o-mar iz raï-ting a lé-teur"},{"en":"I'm studying English now.","da":"Daba kan9ra lingliziya.","pron":"aïm steu-di-ing in-glich naw"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Nnafi w sso2al: not / Are you…? Is she…?","body_da":"**Nnafi:** zidi `not` men ba3d `am` / `is` / `are`:\n\n- `I'm not sleeping.` = makann3esch.\n- `She isn't cooking.` = makattiyebch.\n- `They aren't working today.` = makaykhedmouch lyouma.\n\n**Sso2al:** 9elbi: `am` / `is` / `are` kaydouz 9bel `I` / `she` / `you`… Bhal `to be`: `Are you…?`, `Is she…?`\n\n- `Are you working?` = wach katkhedmi?\n- `Is she cooking?` = wach kattiyeb?\n- `What are you doing?` = chno katdiri?\n- `Where is he going?` = fin ghadi?\n\n**Ljawab l9sir:** `Yes, I am.` / `No, I'm not.` — `Yes, she is.` / `No, she isn't.` — `Yes, they are.` / `No, they aren't.` Nefs ljawabat li t3ellemti m3a `to be`.\n\nF darija kanzido \"wach\" f lbdya; f lingliziya makanzidouch walou, ghir kan9elbo `are` l lowwel.","examples":[{"en":"What are you doing?","da":"Chno katdiri?","pron":"wat ar you dou-ing"},{"en":"I'm not watching TV, I'm studying.","da":"Makanchoufch ttelfaza, kan9ra.","pron":"aïm not wo-tching ti-vi, aïm steu-di-ing"},{"en":"Is Sarah sleeping? — No, she isn't.","da":"Wach Sarah na3sa? — La.","pron":"iz sé-ra sli-ping? — no, chi i-zent"},{"en":"Are the kids playing outside? — Yes, they are.","da":"Wach drari kayl3bou berra? — Ah.","pron":"ar the kidz pléy-ing awt-saïd? — yès, théy ar"},{"en":"Where are you going?","da":"Fin ghadya?","pron":"wér ar you go-ing"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Daba wla dima? — now / usually","body_da":"Kayn far9 kbir bin jouj dyal l'azmina:\n\n**L7adir lbassit** (dars 7 w 8) = l3ada, chi 7aja katdiriha dima, kol nhar: `I cook every day.` (kantiyeb kol nhar), `She works in a bank.` (katkhdem f banka).\n\n**`am / is / are` + `-ing`** = daba, f had llo7da: `I'm cooking now.` (daba kantiyeb), `She's working at the moment.` (daba khddama).\n\nLkelmat li kat3awnek:\n\n- Daba → `now`, `right now`, `at the moment`, `today`, `Look!`, `Listen!`\n- Dima → `every day`, `usually`, `always`, `often`, `sometimes`, `never`, `on Mondays`\n\nMital: `I usually drink coffee, but today I'm drinking tea.` = 3adatan kanchreb l9ehwa, walakin lyouma kanchreb atay. Chofi: f darija nefs lkelma \"kanchreb\" f jouj l7alat, walakin f lingliziya kaytbeddel l fi3l!\n\n**Redi lbal:** chi af3al ma kayakhdouch `-ing` 7ta ila kan lma3na daba: `like`, `love`, `hate`, `want`, `know`, `understand`. Kan9oulo `I want tea` (machi `I'm wanting`), `I know` (machi `I'm knowing`).","examples":[{"en":"I usually drink coffee, but today I'm drinking tea.","da":"3adatan kanchreb l9ehwa, walakin lyouma kanchreb atay.","pron":"aï you-jou-a-li drink ko-fi, beut tou-déy aïm drin-king ti"},{"en":"She works in Rabat. She's working at home today.","da":"Hiya katkhdem f Rabat. Lyouma khddama f ddar.","pron":"chi weurks in ra-bat. chiz weur-king at hom tou-déy"},{"en":"We watch TV every evening.","da":"Kanchoufou ttelfaza kol 3chiya.","pron":"wi wotch ti-vi év-ri iv-ning"},{"en":"Listen! The children are singing.","da":"Sem3i! Drari kayghenniw.","pron":"li-sen! the tchil-dren ar sin-ging"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"cooking","da":"ttyab (kantiyeb)","emoji":"🍳","pron":"kou-king","example_en":"I'm cooking dinner.","example_da":"Kantiyeb l3cha."},{"en":"reading","da":"l9raya (kan9ra)","emoji":"📖","pron":"ri-ding","example_en":"She's reading a magazine.","example_da":"Kat9ra majalla."},{"en":"watching TV","da":"kanchouf ttelfaza","emoji":"📺","pron":"wo-tching ti-vi","example_en":"We're watching TV.","example_da":"Kanchoufou ttelfaza."},{"en":"playing football","da":"kanl3eb lkora","emoji":"⚽","pron":"pléy-ing fout-bol","example_en":"The boys are playing football.","example_da":"Ddrari kayl3bou lkora."},{"en":"listening to music","da":"kansme3 lmousi9a","emoji":"🎧","pron":"li-se-ning tou miou-zik","example_en":"I'm listening to music.","example_da":"Kansme3 lmousi9a."},{"en":"studying","da":"kan9ra (l l'imti7an)","emoji":"📚","pron":"steu-di-ing","example_en":"He's studying for an exam.","example_da":"Kay9ra l l'imti7an."},{"en":"sleeping","da":"na3es / na3sa","emoji":"😴","pron":"sli-ping","example_en":"The baby is sleeping.","example_da":"Lbebe na3es."},{"en":"running","da":"kanjri","emoji":"🏃‍♀️","pron":"ra-ning","example_en":"They're running in the park.","example_da":"Kayjriw f lpark."},{"en":"swimming","da":"kan3oum","emoji":"🏊‍♀️","pron":"swi-ming","example_en":"Omar is swimming in the sea.","example_da":"Omar kay3oum f lb7er."},{"en":"dancing","da":"kanchte7","emoji":"💃","pron":"dan-sing","example_en":"She's dancing at the wedding.","example_da":"Katchte7 f l3ers."},{"en":"shopping","da":"tte9ssira (kant9edda)","emoji":"🛍️","pron":"cho-ping","example_en":"We're shopping at the souk.","example_da":"Kant9eddaw f ssou9."},{"en":"talking on the phone","da":"kanhder f ttilifoun","emoji":"📱","pron":"to-king on the fon","example_en":"My sister is talking on the phone.","example_da":"Khti kathder f ttilifoun."},{"en":"waiting","da":"kantsenna","emoji":"⏳","pron":"wéy-ting","example_en":"I'm waiting for the bus.","example_da":"Kantsenna ttobis."},{"en":"now","da":"daba","emoji":"⏱️","pron":"naw","example_en":"What are you doing now?","example_da":"Chno katdiri daba?"},{"en":"at the moment","da":"daba, f had llo7da","emoji":"⏰","pron":"at the mo-ment","example_en":"She's busy at the moment.","example_da":"Hiya mechghoula daba."},{"en":"hobby","da":"lhiwaya (chi 7aja kat3jbek diriha f lwa9t lkhawi)","emoji":"🎨","pron":"ho-bi","example_en":"Reading is my hobby.","example_da":"L9raya hiya lhiwaya dyali."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"F ttilifoun: chno katdiri?","context_da":"Nhar l7ed f l3chiya. Nouha 3eytat l Sarah f ttilifoun bach tchouf chno katdir.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hi Nouha! How are you?","da":"Ahlan Nouha! Kidayra?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm fine, thanks. What are you doing?","da":"Labas, choukran. Chno katdiri?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I'm cooking. I'm making a tagine for the first time!","da":"Kantiyeb. Kan3mel ttajin l'awwal merra!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Really? Is Tom helping you?","da":"Bsse7? Wach Tom kay3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"No, he isn't. He's watching football with his friends.","da":"La. Rah kaychouf lkora m3a s7abo."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Ha ha! And what are the kids doing?","da":"Hahaha! W drari chno kaydiro?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"They're playing in the garden. And you? Are you studying?","da":"Kayl3bou f jjerda. W nti? Wach kat9ray?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, I'm not. I'm sitting in a café with my sister. We're drinking mint tea.","da":"La. Galsa f l9ehwa m3a khti. Kanchrbou atay b nne3na3."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nice! Enjoy your tea. Talk to you later!","da":"Zwin! Tehnnay b atayek. Nhedro men ba3d!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Bye, Sarah! Good luck with the tagine!","da":"Bslama, Sarah! Llah y3awnek m3a ttajin!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`What are you doing?` w `What do you do?` kaytchabhou, walakin lma3na mkhtalef bzzaf! `What are you doing?` = chno katdiri **daba**. `What do you do?` = chno **khedmtek** (chno katkhdmi f l7ayat). Ila sewlek chi wa7ed `What do you do?`, mat9olich `I'm sitting`! Jawbi: `I'm a nurse` wla `I work in a shop`."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"chno katdiri daba?\" b lingliziya?","options":["What are you doing?","What do you do?","Where are you?","How are you?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What are you doing?` = chno katdiri daba. `What do you do?` = chno khedmtek."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli l fi3l b `-ing` m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"cooking","da":"kantiyeb","emoji":"🍳"},{"en":"reading","da":"kan9ra","emoji":"📖"},{"en":"sleeping","da":"kann3es","emoji":"😴"},{"en":"swimming","da":"kan3oum","emoji":"🏊‍♀️"},{"en":"listening to music","da":"kansme3 lmousi9a","emoji":"🎧"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"She's reading a book.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno katdir?","options":["Kat9ra ktab","Kattiyeb","Katchouf ttelfaza","Katn3es"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`She's reading a book.` = kat9ra ktab. `reading` = l9raya."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ cooking dinner now.","options":["am","is","are"],"answer":"am","hint_da":"M3a `I` dima…","explain_da":"`I am cooking` = `I'm cooking`. M3a `I` kanst3mlo `am`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen kitaba s7i7a?","question_en":"make → ?","options":["making","makeing","makking","maiking"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`make` kaysali b `e`: kan7eyydo l `e` w kanzido `-ing` → `making`."},{"type":"order","words":["is","She","to","listening","music."],"answer":"She is listening to music.","da":"Hiya katsme3 lmousi9a."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Are you watching TV?","question_da":"Sem3i. Achmen so2al sme3ti?","options":["Wach katchoufi ttelfaza daba?","Wach katchoufi ttelfaza kol nhar?","Wach kat9ray daba?","Fin ttelfaza?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Are you watching TV?` = wach katchoufi ttelfaza (daba)? `Do you watch TV every day?` = kol nhar."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Look! It's ___ (rain).","answers":["raining"],"hint_da":"`rain` + `-ing`.","explain_da":"`It's raining.` = katsob chta. `Look!` = chofi! → chi 7aja kat we9e3 daba."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"What do you do?\" means \"What are you doing now?\"","statement_da":"`What do you do?` kat3ni \"chno katdiri daba?\".","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! `What do you do?` = chno khedmtek. `What are you doing?` = chno katdiri daba."},{"type":"translate","da":"Houma kayl3bou lkora daba.","answers":["They are playing football now.","They're playing football now.","Now they are playing football.","Now they're playing football."],"hint_en":"They ... playing ... now.","explain_da":"`They are playing football now.` — `they` + `are` + `playing`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"We're waiting for the bus.","da":"Kantsennaw ttobis.","explain_da":"`wait for` = tsenna. `We're` = `We are`."},{"type":"order","words":["What","your","is","brother","doing?"],"answer":"What is your brother doing?","da":"Chno kaydir khouk?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ljomla s7i7a:","options":["I usually drink coffee, but today I'm drinking tea.","I usually am drinking coffee, but today I drink tea.","I'm usually drinking coffee, but today I'm drink tea.","I usually drinks coffee, but today I drinking tea."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`usually` (3adatan) → l7adir lbassit: `I drink`. `today` (lyouma, daba) → `am` + `-ing`: `I'm drinking`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Sarah ___ at the moment. Call her later.","options":["is sleeping","sleeps","sleep"],"answer":"is sleeping","hint_da":"`at the moment` = daba.","explain_da":"`at the moment` = daba, f had llo7da → `is sleeping`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Makanchoufch ttelfaza daba, rani kantiyeb.","answers":["I'm not watching TV now, I'm cooking.","I am not watching TV now, I am cooking.","I'm not watching TV now. I'm cooking.","I am not watching TV now. I am cooking."],"hint_en":"I'm not ... TV now, I'm ...","explain_da":"Nnafi: `I'm not watching`. `rani kantiyeb` = `I'm cooking`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"What are you doing? I'm cooking dinner for my family.","da":"Chno katdiri? Kantiyeb l3cha l l3a2ila dyali.","pron":"wat ar you dou-ing? aïm kou-king di-neur for maï fa-mi-li"}],"reading":{"title_en":"A Sunday afternoon in Casablanca","title_da":"L7ed f l3chiya f Casa","emoji":"🏡","text_en":"It's Sunday afternoon and the weather is beautiful. Nouha is sitting on the balcony with a cup of mint tea. She isn't working today. She's reading a book about Marrakech. Her sister Hind is in the kitchen. She's cooking a tagine with chicken and olives, and she's listening to music on her phone. Their mother is sleeping in her room because she's tired. Their father is not at home. He's playing cards with his friends at the café. Outside, the children are playing football in the street and a cat is sleeping under a car. At six o'clock, the phone rings. It's Sarah! \"What are you doing, Nouha?\" she asks. \"Nothing special. I'm reading and drinking tea. Come and have dinner with us!\"","text_da":"Nhar l7ed f l3chiya w ljow zwin. Nouha galsa f lbalkon m3a kas d atay b nne3na3. Lyouma makatkhdemch. Kat9ra ktab 3la Marrakech. Khtha Hind f lkouzina. Kattiyeb tajin b ddjaj w zzitoun, w katsme3 lmousi9a f lportable dyalha. Mmhom na3sa f bitha 7it 3iyana. Bbahom machi f ddar. Kayl3eb lkarta m3a s7abo f l9ehwa. Berra, drari kayl3bou lkora f zzen9a w wa7ed l9etta na3sa t7t tomobil. M3a ssetta, ttilifoun sunna. Hadi Sarah! \"Chno katdiri, Nouha?\" sewlatha. \"Walou khass. Kan9ra w kanchreb atay. Aji t3echchay m3ana!\"","glossary":[{"en":"balcony","da":"lbalkon"},{"en":"a cup of","da":"kas d…"},{"en":"olives","da":"zzitoun"},{"en":"tired","da":"3iyan / 3iyana"},{"en":"cards","da":"lkarta"},{"en":"outside","da":"berra"},{"en":"rings","da":"kaysunni (ttilifoun)"},{"en":"nothing special","da":"walou khass"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno katdir Nouha?","options":["Kat9ra ktab","Kattiyeb tajin","Katkhdem","Katn3es"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`She's reading a book about Marrakech.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Hind is listening to music in the kitchen.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: `she's listening to music on her phone` w hiya f lkouzina."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin bbahom?","options":["F l9ehwa m3a s7abo","F ddar kayn3es","F zzen9a kayl3eb lkora","F lkouzina"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`He's playing cards with his friends at the café.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The children are playing football in the garden.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: kayl3bou `in the street` = f zzen9a, machi f jjerda."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Mama kat3eyyet l Omar","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Amina kat3eyyet l weldha Omar f ttilifoun. Sem3i mzyan: fin Omar daba? w chno katdir khto Laila?","lines":[{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Hello, Omar? It's Mom. Where are you?","da":"Alo, Omar? Ana mamak. Fin nta?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Hi Mom. I'm at the beach with Karim. We're swimming.","da":"Ahlan mama. Ana f lb7er m3a Karim. Kan3oumou."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Swimming? It's five o'clock! Are you coming home for dinner?","da":"Kat3oumou? Rah lkhemsa! Wach jay l ddar l l3cha?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, I'm coming. Is Dad cooking?","da":"Ah, jay. Wach bba kaytiyeb?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"No, he isn't. He's sleeping. I'm making couscous.","da":"La. Rah na3es. Ana kan3mel lkesksou."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Great! And what's Laila doing?","da":"Mzyan! W Laila chno katdir?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"She's studying in her room. She has an exam tomorrow.","da":"Kat9ra f bitha. 3ndha imti7an ghedda."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"OK. We're leaving now. See you at seven!","da":"Wakha. Ghadyin daba. Nchoufek m3a ssb3a!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin Omar?","options":["F lb7er","F ddar","F l9ehwa","F lmedrasa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm at the beach with Karim.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"He's sleeping.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kaydir bbah?","options":["Kayn3es","Kaytiyeb","Kaykhdem","Kay3oum"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`He's sleeping.` = rah na3es."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila is watching TV in her room.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `She's studying in her room.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kat3mel Amina l l3cha?","options":["Lkesksou","Ttajin","Lpizza","L7out"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm making couscous.`"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What are you doing?","da":"Chno katdiri?","pron":"wat ar you dou-ing"},{"target_en":"I'm cooking dinner.","da":"Kantiyeb l3cha.","pron":"aïm kou-king di-neur"},{"target_en":"She's studying English at the moment.","da":"Hiya kat9ra lingliziya daba.","pron":"chiz steu-di-ing in-glich at the mo-ment"},{"target_en":"They aren't working today.","da":"Houma makaykhedmouch lyouma.","pron":"théy a-rent weur-king tou-déy"},{"target_en":"Are you listening to me?","da":"Wach katsem3i liya?","pron":"ar you li-se-ning tou mi"},{"target_en":"Look! It's raining.","da":"Chofi! Katsob chta.","pron":"louk! its réy-ning"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Mokalama m3a Sarah","context_da":"Sarah 3eytat lik f ttilifoun nhar ssebt. Jawbi 3la l'as2ila dyalha b `I'm` + fi3l + `-ing`. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! It's Sarah. What are you doing right now?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Ana Sarah. Chno katdiri daba?","expect_keywords":["i'm","i am","ing"],"sample_en":"I'm cooking lunch for my family."},{"bot_en":"Nice! Are you watching TV too?","bot_da":"Zwin! Wach katchoufi ttelfaza 7ta hiya?","expect_keywords":["no","yes","i'm not","i am","watching"],"sample_en":"No, I'm not. I'm listening to music."},{"bot_en":"What's your family doing?","bot_da":"W l3a2ila dyalek chno kaydiro?","expect_keywords":["is","are","ing","sleeping","playing","working","reading"],"sample_en":"My mother is reading and my brother is playing football."},{"bot_en":"And what do you usually do on Saturdays?","bot_da":"W 3adatan chno katdiri nhar ssebt?","expect_keywords":["usually","i go","i cook","i visit","i watch","i read","i clean","i study","i play","i have"],"sample_en":"I usually visit my grandmother and we have lunch together."},{"bot_en":"Sounds good! OK, enjoy your day. Talk to you later!","bot_da":"Mzyan! Wakha, nhar sa3id. Nhedro men ba3d!","expect_keywords":["bye","later","thank","see you","you too"],"sample_en":"Thanks, Sarah! Talk to you later. Bye!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Chno kaydiro nnas f ddar dyalek daba?","prompt_da":"Tkhayli rak f ddar lyouma f l3chiya. Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal: chno katdiri nti daba, w chno kaydiro nnas dyal ddar (mmek, khouk, khtek…). Sta3mli `am` / `is` / `are` + `-ing`, w zidi `now` wla `at the moment`. Ktbi 7ta jomla wa7da b nnafi (`isn't` / `aren't`).","helper_en":["Right now, I'm ...","My mother is ...","My brother isn't ...; he's ...","The children are ...","Today we're ..."],"min_words":35,"keywords":["ing","now"],"model_en":"It's Sunday evening and I'm at home. Right now, I'm sitting in the living room and I'm writing in English. My mother is making dinner in the kitchen and she's listening to the radio. My father isn't here; he's praying at the mosque. My little brother is playing a video game and my sister is studying for her exam. Outside, it's raining, so the children aren't playing in the street."}},{"id":"l14","order":14,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"💪","title_en":"Can / can't: ability & polite requests","title_da":"Can / can't","goals_da":["T9oli chno kat3rfi diri w chno makat3rfich: `I can swim`, `I can't drive`","Tsewli `Can you…?` w tjawbi b `Yes, I can` / `No, I can't`","Ttelbi l'idn b `Can I…?` w ttelbi chi 7aja b adab: `Could you…, please?`","Thedri 3la lmaharat dyalek b `well`, `very well`, `a little`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Can = kan9der / kan3ref ndir","body_da":"`can` kat3ni \"n9der\" wla \"kan3ref ndir chi 7aja\". Kelma sahla bzzaf 7it:\n\n- Nefs lforma m3a kolchi: `I can`, `you can`, `she can`, `we can`, `they can`. Ma kaynach `-s` m3a `he` / `she` (machi `she cans`).\n- Men ba3d `can`, l fi3l kayb9a 3la 7alto: bla `to` w bla `-ing`: `I can swim` (machi `I can to swim`, machi `I can swimming`).\n\nBhal f darija \"kan3ref n3oum\", \"kay9der ysou9\": f lingliziya `I can swim`, `he can drive`.\n\n- `I can swim.` = kan3ref n3oum.\n- `She can cook very well.` = hiya kat3ref ttiyeb mzyan bzzaf.\n- `We can speak English a little.` = kan3erfo nhedro lingliziya chwiya.\n- `My brother can drive.` = khouya kay3ref ysou9.\n\n**Nnot9:** f west ljomla, `can` kat9ra khfifa w 9sira: 'ken' → `I can swim` = 'aï ken swim'.","examples":[{"en":"I can swim.","da":"Kan3ref n3oum.","pron":"aï kan swim"},{"en":"My brother can drive.","da":"Khouya kay3ref ysou9.","pron":"maï bra-theur kan draïv"},{"en":"Sarah can speak three languages.","da":"Sarah kat3ref thder b tlata dyal llogat.","pron":"sé-ra kan spik thri lan-gwi-djiz"},{"en":"You can do it!","da":"Nti t9edri diriha!","pron":"you kan dou it"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Can't, Can you…? w ljawab l9sir","body_da":"**Nnafi:** `can't` (= `cannot`). Kelma wa7da, nefs lforma m3a kolchi:\n\n- `I can't drive.` = makan3refch nsou9.\n- `He can't swim.` = makay3refch y3oum.\n- `We can't come tomorrow.` = ma n9drouch njiw ghedda.\n\n**Sso2al:** `can` kaydouz l lowwel, 9bel `you` / `she` / `they`. Bla `do` / `does`! (machi `Do you can…?`)\n\n- `Can you swim?` = wach kat3rfi t3oumi?\n- `Can she cook?` = wach kat3ref ttiyeb?\n- `What can you do?` = chno kat3rfi diri?\n\n**Ljawab l9sir:** `Yes, I can.` / `No, I can't.` — `Yes, she can.` / `No, she can't.`\n\n**Redi lbal l nnot9:** `can` kat9ra khfifa 'ken', walakin `can't` kat9ra 9wiya w twila chwiya 'kant'. Hada howa lfar9 li kaysem3o l'ingliz. Ila ma fhemtich, sewli: `Can or can't?`","examples":[{"en":"I can't drive.","da":"Makan3refch nsou9.","pron":"aï kant draïv"},{"en":"Can you swim? — Yes, I can.","da":"Wach kat3rfi t3oumi? — Ah, kan3ref.","pron":"kan you swim? — yès, aï kan"},{"en":"Can he speak English? — No, he can't.","da":"Wach kay3ref yhder lingliziya? — La, makay3refch.","pron":"kan hi spik in-glich? — no, hi kant"},{"en":"My grandmother can't use a computer.","da":"Jeddati makat3refch tkhdem b lpc.","pron":"maï grand-ma-theur kant youz a kom-piou-teur"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Can I…? Can you…? Could you…? — l'idn w ttalab b adab","body_da":"`can` makat3nich ghir l9odra. Kanst3mlouha 7ta bach **ntelbo l'idn** w bach **ntelbo chi 7aja b adab**.\n\n**1. Ttelb l'idn — `Can I…?`** = wach n9der…? / wach ymken liya…?\n\n- `Can I sit here?` = wach n9der ngles hna?\n- `Can I open the window?` = wach n9der n7el cherjem?\n- `Can I have a glass of water, please?` = wach ymken liya kas d lma, 3afak? (3refti had ljomla f dars 9)\n\nLjawab: `Yes, of course.` / `Sure.` (= ah, tab3an) wla `Sorry, you can't.` (= sme7 liya, ma ymkench).\n\n**2. Ttelb men chi wa7ed — `Can you…, please?`** = wach t9der…, 3afak?\n\n- `Can you help me, please?` = wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak?\n- `Can you repeat that, please?` = wach t9der t3awed, 3afak?\n\n**3. B adab kter — `Could you…, please?`** Nefs lma3na, walakin fiha adab kter. Sta3mliha m3a nnas li makat3rfihomch, f lkhedma, f l'idara: `Could you speak slowly, please?`\n\n**Bach t9oli la b adab:** `Sorry, I can't.` + ssabab: `Sorry, I can't. I'm busy today.` = sme7 liya, ma n9derch. Ana mechghoula lyouma.","examples":[{"en":"Can I sit here?","da":"Wach n9der ngles hna?","pron":"kan aï sit hir"},{"en":"Can you help me, please?","da":"Wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak?","pron":"kan you hélp mi, pliz"},{"en":"Could you speak slowly, please?","da":"Wach ymken lik thder b chwiya, 3afak?","pron":"koud you spik slo-li, pliz"},{"en":"Sorry, I can't. I'm busy today.","da":"Sme7 liya, ma n9derch. Ana mechghoula lyouma.","pron":"so-ri, aï kant. aïm bi-zi tou-déy"},{"en":"Yes, of course!","da":"Ah, tab3an!","pron":"yès, ov kors"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Well, very well, a little — ch7al kat3rfi?","body_da":"Bach t9oli **ch7al** kat3rfi ddiri chi 7aja, zidi wa7da men had lkelmat f l'akhir dyal ljomla:\n\n- `well` = mzyan: `I can cook well.`\n- `very well` = mzyan bzzaf: `She can swim very well.`\n- `a little` = chwiya: `I can speak English a little.` (wla `I can speak a little English.`)\n- `not very well` = machi mzyan bzzaf: `I can drive, but not very well.`\n- `at all` = walou (m3a `can't`): `I can't sing at all.` = makan3refch nghenni walou.\n\nBhal f darija: \"kan3ref ntiyeb mzyan\", \"kanhder lingliziya chwiya\" — lkelma katji f l'akhir.","examples":[{"en":"I can speak English a little.","da":"Kan3ref nhder lingliziya chwiya.","pron":"aï kan spik in-glich a li-teul"},{"en":"My mother can cook very well.","da":"Mama kat3ref ttiyeb mzyan bzzaf.","pron":"maï ma-theur kan kouk vé-ri wél"},{"en":"He can play the guitar, but not very well.","da":"Kay3ref yl3eb lgitar, walakin machi mzyan bzzaf.","pron":"hi kan pléy the gi-tar, beut not vé-ri wél"},{"en":"I can't sing at all!","da":"Makan3refch nghenni walou!","pron":"aï kant sing at ol"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"swim","da":"3oum","emoji":"🏊‍♀️","pron":"swim","example_en":"I can swim.","example_da":"Kan3ref n3oum."},{"en":"drive","da":"sou9 (tomobil)","emoji":"🚗","pron":"draïv","example_en":"My sister can't drive.","example_da":"Khti makat3refch tsou9."},{"en":"cook","da":"tiyeb","emoji":"🍳","pron":"kouk","example_en":"Can you cook couscous?","example_da":"Wach kat3rfi ttiybi lkesksou?"},{"en":"speak English","da":"hder b lingliziya","emoji":"🗣️","pron":"spik in-glich","example_en":"I can speak English a little.","example_da":"Kan3ref nhder lingliziya chwiya."},{"en":"play the guitar","da":"l3eb lgitar","emoji":"🎸","pron":"pléy the gi-tar","example_en":"Omar can play the guitar.","example_da":"Omar kay3ref yl3eb lgitar."},{"en":"ride a bike","da":"sou9 lbisklita","emoji":"🚲","pron":"raïd a baïk","example_en":"The children can ride a bike.","example_da":"Drari kay3erfo ysou9o lbisklita."},{"en":"use a computer","da":"khdem b lpc","emoji":"💻","pron":"youz a kom-piou-teur","example_en":"Can you use a computer?","example_da":"Wach kat3rfi tkhedmi b lpc?"},{"en":"sing","da":"ghenni","emoji":"🎤","pron":"sing","example_en":"She can sing very well.","example_da":"Kat3ref tghenni mzyan bzzaf."},{"en":"draw","da":"ressem","emoji":"🎨","pron":"dro","example_en":"I can't draw.","example_da":"Makan3refch nressem."},{"en":"sew","da":"khiyet","emoji":"🧵","pron":"so","example_en":"My grandmother can sew.","example_da":"Jeddati kat3ref tkhiyet."},{"en":"help","da":"3awen","emoji":"🤝","pron":"hélp","example_en":"Can you help me, please?","example_da":"Wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak?"},{"en":"open","da":"7el","emoji":"🪟","pron":"o-pen","example_en":"Can I open the window?","example_da":"Wach n9der n7el cherjem?"},{"en":"well","da":"mzyan","emoji":"👍","pron":"wél","example_en":"He can cook well.","example_da":"Kay3ref ytiyeb mzyan."},{"en":"a little","da":"chwiya","emoji":"🤏","pron":"a li-teul","example_en":"I can speak Spanish a little.","example_da":"Kan3ref nhder sbliouniya chwiya."},{"en":"of course","da":"tab3an / bla chek","emoji":"✅","pron":"ov kors","example_en":"Can I sit here? — Yes, of course.","example_da":"Wach n9der ngles hna? — Ah, tab3an."},{"en":"busy","da":"mechghoul / mechghoula","emoji":"⏳","pron":"bi-zi","example_en":"Sorry, I can't. I'm busy.","example_da":"Sme7 liya, ma n9derch. Ana mechghoula."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Chno kat3rfi diri?","context_da":"Nouha w Sarah galsin f l9ehwa, kayhedro 3la l7wayj li kay3erfo ydirou w li makay3erfouch.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, can you drive?","da":"Nouha, wach kat3rfi tsou9i?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, I can't, but I can ride a bike. And you?","da":"La, makan3refch, walakin kan3ref nsou9 lbisklita. W nti?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I can drive, but I can't drive in Casablanca! The traffic is crazy.","da":"Kan3ref nsou9, walakin ma n9derch nsou9 f Casa! Zz7am khayb bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Ha ha, that's true. Can you cook Moroccan food?","da":"Hahaha, s7i7. Wach kat3rfi ttiybi lmakla lmeghribiya?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I can make mint tea, but I can't make couscous. Can you teach me?","da":"Kan3ref n3mel atay b nne3na3, walakin makan3refch n3mel lkesksou. Wach t9edri t3ellmini?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Of course! Come to my house on Friday.","da":"Tab3an! Aji l ddari nhar jjem3a."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Great! Could you write the recipe for me, please?","da":"Mzyan! Wach ymken lik tketbi liya kifach kandirouh, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Sure. And can you help me with my English?","da":"Wakha. W nti wach t9edri t3awnini f lingliziya?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Yes, I can! You can already speak very well.","da":"Ah, n9der! Nti men daba kathedri mzyan bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you, Sarah! See you on Friday.","da":"Choukran, Sarah! Nchoufek nhar jjem3a."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`can` w `can't` kaytsem3o 9rab men b3diyathom, 7ta l'ingliz chi merrat kaykhelto! F lhadra ssri3a, `can` kat9ra khfifa w 9sira ('ken'), w `can't` kat9ra 9wiya w twila chwiya ('kant'). Ila ma fhemtich, sewli b kol bassata: `Can or can't?` W melli nti kathedri, f `can't` zidi chwiya dyal l9owwa 3la lkelma bach yfehmouk."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno ma3na `I can swim`?","options":["Kan3ref n3oum","Makan3refch n3oum","Bghit n3oum","Kan3oum kol nhar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`can` = kan9der / kan3ref ndir. `I can swim` = kan3ref n3oum."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I can't drive.","question_da":"Sem3i mzyan: `can` wla `can't`?","options":["Makan3refch nsou9","Kan3ref nsou9","Kan3ref n3oum","Makan3refch ntiyeb"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`can't` = ma n9derch (kat9ra 9wiya 'kant'). `drive` = sou9."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lmahara m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"drive","da":"sou9 tomobil","emoji":"🚗"},{"en":"swim","da":"3oum","emoji":"🏊‍♀️"},{"en":"sew","da":"khiyet","emoji":"🧵"},{"en":"draw","da":"ressem","emoji":"🎨"},{"en":"ride a bike","da":"sou9 lbisklita","emoji":"🚲"},{"en":"sing","da":"ghenni","emoji":"🎤"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"She ___ cook very well.","options":["can","cans","can to"],"answer":"can","hint_da":"`can` makatbeddelch m3a `she`.","explain_da":"`can` nefsha m3a kolchi: `she can`, machi `she cans`. W men ba3dha l fi3l bla `to`."},{"type":"order","words":["you","Can","English?","speak"],"answer":"Can you speak English?","da":"Wach kat3rfi thedri lingliziya?"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Can you swim?","question_da":"Achmen jawab 9sir s7i7?","options":["Yes, I can.","Yes, I do.","Yes, I am.","Yes, I cans."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Ljawab l9sir m3a `can` howa `Yes, I can.` / `No, I can't.` — machi `do`, machi `am`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Sorry, I ___ help you now. I'm busy.","answers":["can't","cannot","can not"],"hint_da":"Nnafi dyal `can`.","explain_da":"`Sorry, I can't.` = sme7 liya, ma n9derch. `can't` = `cannot`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Could you open the window, please?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno talbet menek?","options":["Bach t7elli cherjem","Bach tseddi lbab","Bach tjelsi","Bach t3awniha f lkouzina"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Could you…, please?` = talab b adab. `open the window` = 7elli cherjem."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Could you help me, please?\" is more polite than \"Help me!\"","statement_da":"`Could you help me, please?` fiha adab kter men `Help me!`","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `Could you…, please?` hiya l'adab kter. `Help me!` kaddouz ghir m3a s7ab wla f l7alat lmosta3jala."},{"type":"translate","da":"Khouya kay3ref yl3eb lgitar mzyan bzzaf.","answers":["My brother can play the guitar very well.","My brother can play guitar very well."],"hint_en":"My brother can ... the guitar ... ...","explain_da":"`play the guitar` — m3a l'alat lmousi9iya kanzido `the`. `very well` = mzyan bzzaf, f l'akhir."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Can I sit here, please?","da":"Wach n9der ngles hna, 3afak?","explain_da":"`Can I…?` = ttelb l'idn. `sit` = gles."},{"type":"order","words":["He","can","sing,","but","he","can't","dance."],"answer":"He can sing, but he can't dance.","da":"Howa kay3ref yghenni, walakin makay3refch ychte7."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Nti f l'idara. Bghiti ttelbi men lmowaddaf yhder b chwiya. Chno t9oli?","options":["Could you speak slowly, please?","Speak slowly!","You can speak slowly.","Can I speak slowly?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Talab b adab m3a chi wa7ed makat3rfihch: `Could you…, please?`. `Can I speak slowly?` = wach n9der ana nhder b chwiya — machi howa."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I can speak English, but not ___ well.","options":["very","a little","much"],"answer":"very","hint_da":"machi mzyan bzzaf.","explain_da":"`not very well` = machi mzyan bzzaf. `a little` katji m3a l'ijab: `I can speak English a little.`"},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak? Ma n9derch n7el had lbab.","answers":["Can you help me, please? I can't open this door.","Could you help me, please? I can't open this door.","Can you help me please? I can't open this door.","Could you help me please? I can't open this door."],"hint_en":"Can you ... me, ...? I ... open this ...","explain_da":"`Can you help me, please?` (wla `Could you…`) + `I can't open this door.` — `this door` = had lbab."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Can you help me, please? I can't find my keys.","da":"Wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak? Mal9itch sswaret dyali.","pron":"kan you hélp mi, pliz? aï kant faïnd maï kiz"}],"reading":{"title_en":"My talented family","title_da":"L3a2ila dyali lmawhouba","emoji":"👨‍👩‍👧‍👦","text_en":"Everybody in my family can do something special. My mother can cook very well. Everybody loves her couscous! She can also sew; she makes beautiful kaftans for weddings. My father can speak four languages: Arabic, French, English and a little Spanish. He can't cook at all, but he can fix anything in the house. My brother Youssef can play the guitar and he can sing. He can't drive yet, so he rides his bike to work. My little sister Hind is only eight, but she can already swim and she can draw very well. And me? I can use a computer, I can ride a bike and I can speak English a little. I can't swim and I can't drive, but I'm learning. What can you do?","text_da":"Kol wa7ed f l3a2ila dyali kay3ref ydir chi 7aja khassa. Mama kat3ref ttiyeb mzyan bzzaf. Kolchi kaybghi lkesksou dyalha! Kat3ref 7ta tkhiyet; kat3mel 9fatn zwinin l l3rasat. Bba kay3ref yhder b reb3a dyal llogat: l3arbiya, lfransawiya, lingliziya w chwiya dyal sbliouniya. Makay3refch ytiyeb walou, walakin kay3ref ysawb ay 7aja f ddar. Khouya Youssef kay3ref yl3eb lgitar w kay3ref yghenni. Mazal makay3refch ysou9, 3la hadchi kaymchi l lkhedma b lbisklita dyalo. Khti sghira Hind 3ndha ghir tmen snin, walakin men daba kat3ref t3oum w kat3ref tressem mzyan bzzaf. W ana? Kan3ref nkhdem b lpc, kan3ref nsou9 lbisklita w kan3ref nhder lingliziya chwiya. Makan3refch n3oum w makan3refch nsou9, walakin rani kant3ellem. W nti, chno kat3rfi diri?","glossary":[{"en":"everybody","da":"kol wa7ed / kolchi"},{"en":"something special","da":"chi 7aja khassa"},{"en":"weddings","da":"l3rasat"},{"en":"fix","da":"sawb / sle7"},{"en":"yet","da":"mazal (f nnafi)"},{"en":"already","da":"men daba"},{"en":"only","da":"ghir"},{"en":"learning","da":"kant3ellem"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kat3ref ddir mama dyal Nouha?","options":["Ttiyeb w tkhiyet","Tsou9 w t3oum","Tghenni w tchte7","Thder reb3a dyal llogat"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`My mother can cook very well. She can also sew.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha's father can cook very well.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `He can't cook at all.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kaymchi Youssef l lkhedma?","options":["B lbisklita","B tomobil","B ttobis","3la rejlih"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`He rides his bike to work.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha can't swim.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: `I can't swim and I can't drive, but I'm learning.`"}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Mo9abala dyal khedma f lotil","emoji":"🏨","pre_da":"Laila f mo9abala dyal khedma f wa7ed lotil sghir. Sem3i mzyan: chno kat3ref ddir Laila, w chno makat3refch?","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Good morning, Laila. Please sit down. So, can you speak English?","da":"Sbah lkhir, Laila. Glsi 3afak. Iwa, wach kat3rfi thedri lingliziya?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, I can. I can also speak Spanish a little.","da":"Ah, kan3ref. Kan3ref 7ta nhder sbliouniya chwiya."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Very good. Can you use a computer?","da":"Mzyan bzzaf. Wach kat3rfi tkhedmi b lpc?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, I can. I use one every day at home.","da":"Ah. Kankhdem b wa7ed kol nhar f ddar."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"And can you drive? Sometimes we take guests to the airport.","da":"W wach kat3rfi tsou9i? Chi merrat kanddiw ddyaf l lmatar."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"No, I can't drive, sorry. But I can start early in the morning.","da":"La, makan3refch nsou9, sme7 liya. Walakin n9der nbda bekri f sbah."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"That's fine. Can you start on Monday?","da":"Makayn mochkil. Wach t9edri tbdi nhar ttnin?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, of course! Thank you very much, Mr. Brown.","da":"Ah, tab3an! Choukran bzzaf, a ssi Brown."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen logha kat3ref Laila thder biha chwiya?","options":["Sbliouniya","Lingliziya","Ttaliya","L'almaniya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I can also speak Spanish a little.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila can drive.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `No, I can't drive, sorry.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Can you start on Monday?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach sewelha Mr. Brown?","options":["Wach t9der tbda nhar ttnin","Wach t9der tsou9 nhar ttnin","Wach kat3ref tkhdem b lpc","Wach kathder lingliziya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Can you start on Monday?` = wach t9edri tbdi nhar ttnin?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach t9der Laila tbda lkhedma f nhar?","options":["Bekri f sbah","F l3chiya","F lil","Ghir f lwikand"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I can start early in the morning.`"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"I can swim, but I can't drive.","da":"Kan3ref n3oum, walakin makan3refch nsou9.","pron":"aï kan swim, beut aï kant draïv"},{"target_en":"Can you help me, please?","da":"Wach t9der t3awenni, 3afak?","pron":"kan you hélp mi, pliz"},{"target_en":"Could you repeat that, please?","da":"Wach ymken lik t3awed, 3afak?","pron":"koud you ri-pit that, pliz"},{"target_en":"She can cook very well.","da":"Hiya kat3ref ttiyeb mzyan bzzaf.","pron":"chi kan kouk vé-ri wél"},{"target_en":"Can I open the window? — Yes, of course.","da":"Wach n9der n7el cherjem? — Ah, tab3an.","pron":"kan aï o-pen the win-do? — yès, ov kors"},{"target_en":"Sorry, I can't. I'm busy today.","da":"Sme7 liya, ma n9derch. Ana mechghoula lyouma.","pron":"so-ri, aï kant. aïm bi-zi tou-déy"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Mo9abala sghira: chno kat3rfi diri?","context_da":"Omar kaykhdem f wa7ed cherika w kay9elleb 3la chi wa7ed y3awno. Ghadi ysewlek 3la lmaharat dyalek. Jawbi b `Yes, I can` / `No, I can't` w zidi chi tafsil sghir.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hello! Thanks for coming. First question: can you speak English?","bot_da":"Salam! Choukran 7it jiti. L'awwal so2al: wach kat3rfi thedri lingliziya?","expect_keywords":["yes","i can","a little","little"],"sample_en":"Yes, I can. I can speak English a little."},{"bot_en":"Good. Can you use a computer?","bot_da":"Mzyan. Wach kat3rfi tkhedmi b lpc?","expect_keywords":["yes","i can","no","i can't","computer"],"sample_en":"Yes, I can. I use a computer every day."},{"bot_en":"Can you drive?","bot_da":"Wach kat3rfi tsou9i?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i can","i can't","drive","bike"],"sample_en":"No, I can't drive, but I can ride a bike."},{"bot_en":"What else can you do well?","bot_da":"Chno kat3rfi ddiri mzyan 7ta howa?","expect_keywords":["i can","cook","sew","swim","sing","draw","speak","well"],"sample_en":"I can cook very well, and I can sew."},{"bot_en":"Excellent. Can you start on Monday morning?","bot_da":"Momtaz. Wach t9edri tbdi nhar ttnin f sbah?","expect_keywords":["yes","of course","sure","i can","sorry","i can't"],"sample_en":"Yes, of course. I can start on Monday."},{"bot_en":"Great! Do you have any questions for me?","bot_da":"Mzyan! Wach 3ndek chi so2al liya?","expect_keywords":["can i","could you","no","thank","question","what time"],"sample_en":"Yes. Can I start at nine o'clock?"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Chno kat3rfi diri?","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal 3la lmaharat dyalek w dyal chi wa7ed men l3a2ila dyalek: chno kat3rfi diri mzyan, chno chwiya, w chno makat3rfich. Sta3mli `can`, `can't`, `well`, `very well`, `a little`.","helper_en":["I can ... very well.","I can ... a little.","I can't ... at all.","My ... can ..., but he/she can't ...","I want to learn ..."],"min_words":40,"keywords":["can","can't"],"model_en":"I can do many things. I can cook very well; my family loves my chicken tagine. I can also sew a little and I can use a computer. I can speak English a little, but I can't speak Spanish at all. I can't drive, so I take the bus to work. My sister can drive, but she can't cook! My brother can play the guitar very well. This year, I want to learn to swim."}},{"id":"l15","order":15,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"📆","title_en":"Yesterday: was / were","title_da":"Lbare7: was / were","goals_da":["T9oli fin konti lbare7 b `was` / `were`","Tsewli `Where were you?` w `Was it good?` w tjawbi 3lihom","Tsta3mli kelmat lwa9t dyal lmadi: `yesterday`, `last week`, `two days ago`, `in 2020`","T9oli `there was` / `there were` w twesfi l'i7sas dyalek: `tired`, `busy`, `happy`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Was / were = kont, kan, kanet, konna, kanou","body_da":"Lmadi = li fat, li daz (lbare7, l3am li fat…). L fi3l `to be` f lmadi 3ndo ghir jouj dyal lformat:\n\n- `am` / `is` → `was`\n- `are` → `were`\n\nYa3ni:\n\n- `I was` = kont\n- `you were` = konti\n- `he was` = kan\n- `she was` = kanet\n- `it was` = kan / kanet\n- `we were` = konna\n- `they were` = kanou\n\nBhal f darija melli kat9oli \"lbare7 kont 3iyana\": `Yesterday I was tired.` W \"konna f lb7er\": `We were at the beach.`\n\nRedi lbal: f l'ijab, `was` w `were` makayt9essrouch: `I was`, `we were` (machi bhal `I'm`).","examples":[{"en":"I was at home yesterday.","da":"Lbare7 kont f ddar.","pron":"aï woz at hom yès-teur-déy"},{"en":"She was very tired last night.","da":"Lbare7 f lil kanet 3iyana bzzaf.","pron":"chi woz vé-ri taï-eurd last naït"},{"en":"We were at the beach on Sunday.","da":"Nhar l7ed konna f lb7er.","pron":"wi weur at the bitch on seun-déy"},{"en":"It was hot in Marrakech.","da":"Kanet skhouna f Marrakech.","pron":"it woz hot in ma-ra-kech"},{"en":"My parents were in Fes last week.","da":"Walidiya kanou f Fes ssimana li fatet.","pron":"maï pé-rents weur in fès last wik"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Wasn't / weren't, Were you…? Was it…?","body_da":"**Nnafi:** `was not` = `wasn't`, `were not` = `weren't`.\n\n- `I wasn't at work.` = makontch f lkhedma.\n- `They weren't happy.` = makanouch fer7anin.\n- `It wasn't expensive.` = makanch ghali.\n\n**Sso2al:** 9elbi, bhal `to be` f l7adir: `was` / `were` kaydouzo 9bel `you` / `it` / `they`.\n\n- `Were you at home?` = wach konti f ddar?\n- `Was it good?` = wach kan mzyan?\n- `Where were you yesterday?` = fin konti lbare7?\n- `How was your weekend?` = kifach kan lwikand dyalek?\n\n**Ljawab l9sir:** `Yes, I was.` / `No, I wasn't.` — `Yes, they were.` / `No, they weren't.`\n\n`How was…?` so2al mohim bzzaf: kaysewlouk bih 3la chi 7aja derti: `How was the party?` → `It was great!` (kanet zwina bzzaf) / `It was boring.` (kanet mmella).","examples":[{"en":"Where were you yesterday?","da":"Fin konti lbare7?","pron":"wér weur you yès-teur-déy"},{"en":"I wasn't at work. I was sick.","da":"Makontch f lkhedma. Kont mrida.","pron":"aï wo-zent at weurk. aï woz sik"},{"en":"Was the film good? — Yes, it was.","da":"Wach lfilm kan mzyan? — Ah, kan mzyan.","pron":"woz the film goud? — yès, it woz"},{"en":"Were they late? — No, they weren't.","da":"Wach t3ettlou? — La, ma t3ettlouch.","pron":"weur théy léyt? — no, théy weu-rent"},{"en":"How was your weekend?","da":"Kifach kan lwikand dyalek?","pron":"haw woz your wik-énd"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kelmat lwa9t dyal lmadi: yesterday, last…, ago, in 2020","body_da":"Bach t9oli **fo9ach**, 3ndek had lkelmat:\n\n- `yesterday` = lbare7. `yesterday morning` / `yesterday afternoon` / `yesterday evening` = lbare7 f sbah / f l3chiya / f l3chiya m3a lil.\n- `last night` = lbare7 f lil. (Machi `yesterday night`!)\n- `last` + wa9t = …li fat(et): `last week` = ssimana li fatet, `last month` = chhar li fat, `last year` = l3am li fat, `last Friday` = jjem3a li fatet, `last summer` = ssif li fat.\n- ra9m + `ago` = hadi…: `two days ago` = hadi youmayn, `an hour ago` = hadi sa3a, `ten years ago` = hadi 3echr snin. Redi lbal: `ago` kayji **men ba3d** lwa9t, l3eks dyal darija.\n- `in` + l3am: `in 2020` = f 2020. L'a3wam kay9raw b jouj jouj: `2020` = 'twén-ti twén-ti', `1995` = 'naïn-tin naïn-ti faïv'.\n\nKelmat lwa9t kaymchiw f lbdya wla f l'akhir dyal ljomla: `Yesterday I was busy.` = `I was busy yesterday.`","examples":[{"en":"I was in Agadir two years ago.","da":"Kont f Agadir hadi 3amayn.","pron":"aï woz in a-ga-dir tou yirz a-go"},{"en":"Last night we were at a wedding.","da":"Lbare7 f lil konna f 3ers.","pron":"last naït wi weur at a wé-ding"},{"en":"He was a student in 2015.","da":"Kan talib f 2015.","pron":"hi woz a stiou-dent in twén-ti fif-tin"},{"en":"Where were you an hour ago?","da":"Fin konti hadi sa3a?","pron":"wér weur you an a-weur a-go"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"There was / there were, w l'i7sas: tired, busy, happy…","body_da":"**`There was` / `there were`** = kan / kanet / kanou (chi 7aja kayna f lmadi). Hiya `there is` / `there are` dyal dars 10, walakin f lmadi:\n\n- `There was a big party.` = kanet 7efla kbira.\n- `There were many people at the souk.` = kanou bzzaf dyal nnas f ssou9.\n- `There wasn't any bread.` = makanch lkhobz.\n- `Were there many people?` = wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas?\n\n**L'i7sas w l7ala** m3a `was` / `were`: bhal f darija \"kan m3ettel\", \"kont 3iyana\":\n\n- `tired` = 3iyan / 3iyana\n- `busy` = mechghoul / mechghoula\n- `happy` = fer7an / fer7ana\n- `sad` = 7azin / 7azina\n- `late` = m3ettel / m3ettla\n- `sick` = mrid / mrida\n- `hungry` = ji3an / ji3ana\n- `at home` = f ddar, `at work` = f lkhedma, `on holiday` = f l3otla\n\n`I was tired and hungry after work.` = kont 3iyana w ji3ana men ba3d lkhedma.","examples":[{"en":"There was a lot of traffic this morning.","da":"Kan zz7am bzzaf had sbah.","pron":"thér woz a lot ov tra-fik this mor-ning"},{"en":"There were many people at the souk.","da":"Kanou bzzaf dyal nnas f ssou9.","pron":"thér weur mé-ni pi-peul at the souk"},{"en":"There wasn't any milk in the fridge.","da":"Makanch l7lib f ttellaja.","pron":"thér wo-zent é-ni milk in the fridj"},{"en":"I was tired and hungry after work.","da":"Kont 3iyana w ji3ana men ba3d lkhedma.","pron":"aï woz taï-eurd and hen-gri af-teur weurk"},{"en":"He was late for the meeting.","da":"T3ettel 3la l'ijtima3.","pron":"hi woz léyt for the mi-ting"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"yesterday","da":"lbare7","emoji":"📆","pron":"yès-teur-déy","example_en":"I was at home yesterday.","example_da":"Lbare7 kont f ddar."},{"en":"last night","da":"lbare7 f lil","emoji":"🌙","pron":"last naït","example_en":"Where were you last night?","example_da":"Fin konti lbare7 f lil?"},{"en":"last week","da":"ssimana li fatet","emoji":"🗓️","pron":"last wik","example_en":"She was in Tangier last week.","example_da":"Kanet f Tanja ssimana li fatet."},{"en":"last year","da":"l3am li fat","emoji":"📅","pron":"last yir","example_en":"We were in Agadir last year.","example_da":"Konna f Agadir l3am li fat."},{"en":"ago","da":"hadi… (hadi youmayn, hadi sa3a)","emoji":"⏪","pron":"a-go","example_en":"He was here ten minutes ago.","example_da":"Kan hna hadi 3echr d9ay9."},{"en":"tired","da":"3iyan / 3iyana","emoji":"😩","pron":"taï-eurd","example_en":"I was very tired last night.","example_da":"Lbare7 f lil kont 3iyana bzzaf."},{"en":"busy","da":"mechghoul / mechghoula","emoji":"📵","pron":"bi-zi","example_en":"The doctor was busy this morning.","example_da":"Ttbib kan mechghoul had sbah."},{"en":"happy","da":"fer7an / fer7ana","emoji":"😊","pron":"ha-pi","example_en":"The children were happy at the party.","example_da":"Drari kanou fer7anin f l7efla."},{"en":"sad","da":"7azin / 7azina","emoji":"😢","pron":"sad","example_en":"Why were you sad?","example_da":"3lach konti 7azna?"},{"en":"late","da":"m3ettel / m3ettla","emoji":"⏰","pron":"léyt","example_en":"Sorry, I was late.","example_da":"Sme7 liya, t3ettelt."},{"en":"sick","da":"mrid / mrida","emoji":"🤒","pron":"sik","example_en":"He wasn't at work because he was sick.","example_da":"Makanch f lkhedma 7it kan mrid."},{"en":"at home","da":"f ddar","emoji":"🏠","pron":"at hom","example_en":"We were at home all day.","example_da":"Konna f ddar nhar kamel."},{"en":"at work","da":"f lkhedma","emoji":"🏢","pron":"at weurk","example_en":"I was at work until six.","example_da":"Kont f lkhedma 7ta l ssetta."},{"en":"on holiday","da":"f l3otla","emoji":"🏖️","pron":"on ho-li-déy","example_en":"They were on holiday in Spain.","example_da":"Kanou f l3otla f Sbanya."},{"en":"party","da":"7efla","emoji":"🎉","pron":"par-ti","example_en":"There was a party at my cousin's house.","example_da":"Kanet 7efla f dar bent 3emmi."},{"en":"weekend","da":"lwikand (ssebt w l7ed)","emoji":"🛋️","pron":"wik-énd","example_en":"How was your weekend?","example_da":"Kifach kan lwikand dyalek?"}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Fin konti lbare7?","context_da":"Nouha makanetch f l9ism dyal lingliziya lbare7. Lyouma Sarah tla9atha w sewlatha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hi Nouha! Where were you yesterday? You weren't in class.","da":"Ahlan Nouha! Fin konti lbare7? Makontich f l9ism."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Hi Sarah. I was at the hospital with my mother.","da":"Ahlan Sarah. Kont f sbitar m3a mama."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Oh no! Was she sick?","da":"Oh la! Wach kanet mrida?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, she was a little sick, but she's fine now.","da":"Ah, kanet mrida chwiya, walakin daba labas 3liha."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Good. Were you there all day?","da":"Mzyan. Wach konti tema nhar kamel?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, we were there from nine to five. There were a lot of people.","da":"Ah, konna tema men tts3oud 7ta l lkhemsa. Kanou bzzaf dyal nnas."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"That's a long day. You were tired, I'm sure.","da":"Nhar twil. Konti 3iyana, akid."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Very tired! And how was the class? Was it difficult?","da":"3iyana bzzaf! W kifach kan l9ism? Wach kan s3ib?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"No, it wasn't difficult. It was fun! Here's my notebook.","da":"La, makanch s3ib. Kan zwin! Hak lkoras dyali."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you, Sarah. You're a good friend.","da":"Choukran, Sarah. Nti sa7ba mzyana."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Mat9olich `yesterday night`! F lingliziya kan9oulo `last night` (= lbare7 f lil). Walakin `yesterday morning`, `yesterday afternoon` w `yesterday evening` s7a7. W `ago` dima kayji men ba3d lwa9t: `two days ago` (machi `ago two days`) — l3eks dyal darija \"hadi youmayn\"."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"lbare7 kont f ddar\" b lingliziya?","options":["I was at home yesterday.","I am at home yesterday.","I were at home yesterday.","I is at home yesterday."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I` → `was`. `yesterday` = lbare7 → lmadi."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"They ___ at the beach on Sunday.","options":["were","was","are"],"answer":"were","hint_da":"`they` + ? (f lmadi)","explain_da":"`we` / `you` / `they` → `were`. `I` / `he` / `she` / `it` → `was`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Where were you last night?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["Fin konti lbare7 f lil","Fin nti daba","Fin ghadi tkoni ghedda","Fin konti ssimana li fatet"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Where were you…?` = fin konti…? `last night` = lbare7 f lil."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli kelmat lwa9t m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"yesterday","da":"lbare7","emoji":"📆"},{"en":"last night","da":"lbare7 f lil","emoji":"🌙"},{"en":"last week","da":"ssimana li fatet","emoji":"🗓️"},{"en":"two days ago","da":"hadi youmayn","emoji":"⏪"},{"en":"last year","da":"l3am li fat","emoji":"📅"}]},{"type":"order","words":["was","She","yesterday.","tired","very"],"answer":"She was very tired yesterday.","da":"Lbare7 kanet 3iyana bzzaf."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Was the party good?","question_da":"Achmen jawab 9sir s7i7?","options":["Yes, it was.","Yes, it is.","Yes, it were.","Yes, it did."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"So2al b `Was it…?` → jawab `Yes, it was.` / `No, it wasn't.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Yesterday night\" is correct English.","statement_da":"`Yesterday night` kelma s7i7a f lingliziya.","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! Kan9oulo `last night`. Walakin `yesterday morning` s7i7a."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ at work yesterday. I was at home.","answers":["wasn't","was not"],"hint_da":"Nnafi dyal `was`.","explain_da":"`I wasn't at work.` = makontch f lkhedma. `wasn't` = `was not`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"There were a lot of people at the souk.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno fhemti?","options":["Kanou bzzaf dyal nnas f ssou9","Makanch 7ta chi wa7ed f ssou9","Kaynin bzzaf dyal nnas f ssou9 daba","Kan ghir wa7ed f ssou9"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`There were` = kanou (lmadi). `a lot of people` = bzzaf dyal nnas."},{"type":"translate","da":"Fin konti lbare7? Makontich f lkhedma.","answers":["Where were you yesterday? You weren't at work.","Where were you yesterday? You were not at work."],"hint_en":"Where ... you ...? You ... at work.","explain_da":"`Where were you yesterday?` + `You weren't at work.` — `weren't` = `were not`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"We were at a wedding last night.","da":"Lbare7 f lil konna f 3ers.","explain_da":"`We were` = konna. `last night` = lbare7 f lil. `wedding` = 3ers."},{"type":"order","words":["in","Agadir","two","ago.","were","years","They"],"answer":"They were in Agadir two years ago.","da":"Kanou f Agadir hadi 3amayn."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"There ___ any bread in the kitchen this morning.","options":["wasn't","weren't","isn't"],"answer":"wasn't","hint_da":"`bread` makayt3eddch (bla `-s`) → mofrad. W `this morning` daz.","explain_da":"`bread` ma3ndouch jam3 → `there wasn't any bread`. `this morning` = had sbah (daz) → lmadi."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ljomla s7i7a:","options":["I was in Tangier two weeks ago.","I was in Tangier ago two weeks.","I was in Tangier two weeks before.","I was in Tangier last two weeks."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`ago` kayji men ba3d lwa9t: `two weeks ago` = hadi jouj simanat."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach kanet mrida? — La, kanet ghir 3iyana.","answers":["Was she sick? — No, she was just tired.","Was she sick? No, she was just tired.","Was she ill? — No, she was just tired.","Was she sick? — No, she was only tired."],"hint_en":"Was she ...? — No, she was just ...","explain_da":"`Was she sick?` → `No, she was just tired.` — `just` / `only` = ghir."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"How was your weekend? — It was great. I was at the beach with my family.","da":"Kifach kan lwikand dyalek? — Kan zwin bzzaf. Kont f lb7er m3a l3a2ila dyali.","pron":"haw woz your wik-énd? — it woz gréyt. aï woz at the bitch with maï fa-mi-li"}],"reading":{"title_en":"A day in Marrakech","title_da":"Nhar f Marrakech","emoji":"🕌","text_en":"Last Saturday, my sister and I were in Marrakech for the first time. We were there for one day only. In the morning, we were at Jemaa el-Fna square. There were a lot of people, musicians and orange juice sellers. The weather was hot, but it wasn't a problem. At lunchtime, we were hungry, so we were at a small restaurant near the square. The tagine was delicious and it was cheap: only forty dirhams! In the afternoon, we were at the souk. The shops were full of colors: lamps, carpets, bags and babouches. My sister was happy because the prices weren't expensive. At seven o'clock, we were at the bus station. The bus was late and we were very tired, but it was a wonderful day.","text_da":"Ssebt li fat, ana w khti konna f Marrakech l'awwal merra. Konna tema ghir nhar wa7ed. F sbah, konna f sa7at Jama3 lefna. Kanou bzzaf dyal nnas, lmousi9iyin w li kaybi3o 3asir llimoun. Ljow kan skhoun, walakin makanch mochkil. F lwa9t dyal lghda, konna ji3anin, 3la hadchi konna f wa7ed rristora sghira 9rib men ssa7a. Ttajin kan bnin w kan rkhis: ghir reb3in derhem! F l3chiya, konna f ssou9. L7wanet kanou 3amrin b l'alwan: lmsabe7, zzrabi, ssakan w lbelgha. Khti kanet fer7ana 7it l'atmina makanouch ghalyin. M3a ssb3a, konna f lma7atta dyal lkiran. Lkar t3ettel w konna 3iyanin bzzaf, walakin kan nhar ra2i3.","glossary":[{"en":"square","da":"ssa7a"},{"en":"sellers","da":"li kaybi3o"},{"en":"lunchtime","da":"lwa9t dyal lghda"},{"en":"hungry","da":"ji3an / ji3ana"},{"en":"delicious","da":"bnin"},{"en":"cheap","da":"rkhis"},{"en":"full of","da":"3amer b"},{"en":"carpets","da":"zzrabi"},{"en":"bus station","da":"lma7atta dyal lkiran"},{"en":"wonderful","da":"ra2i3"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men nhar b9aw f Marrakech?","options":["Nhar wa7ed","Youmayn","Simana","Chhar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`We were there for one day only.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The weather was cold in Marrakech.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `The weather was hot.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al kan ttaman dyal ttajin?","options":["40 derhem","14 derhem","4 derhem","400 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`only forty dirhams` = ghir reb3in derhem."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The bus was late.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: `The bus was late and we were very tired.`"}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Kifach kan lwikand?","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Omar w Laila kayhedro nhar ttnin f sbah 3la lwikand. Sem3i mzyan: fin kan Omar nhar ssebt? w 3lach Laila kanet f ddar?","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Hi Laila! How was your weekend?","da":"Ahlan Laila! Kifach kan lwikand dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"It was OK, but I was at home all weekend. I was sick.","da":"Kan 3adi, walakin kont f ddar lwikand kamel. Kont mrida."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Oh, I'm sorry. Are you OK now?","da":"Oh, sme7 liya. Wach daba labas 3lik?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, thanks. And you? Where were you on Saturday?","da":"Ah, choukran. W nta? Fin konti nhar ssebt?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I was at my cousin's wedding in Rabat. It was fantastic!","da":"Kont f l3ers dyal weld 3emmi f Rabat. Kan ra2i3!"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Nice! Were there many people?","da":"Zwin! Wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, there were about three hundred people. The music was great, but the food was late.","da":"Ah, kanou chi tlata myat wa7ed. Lmousi9a kanet zwina, walakin lmakla t3ettlet."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Ha ha! Moroccan weddings. What time were you at home?","da":"Hahaha! L3rasat lmeghribiya. Chno men sa3a konti f ddar?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"At five in the morning! I was so tired on Sunday.","da":"M3a lkhemsa dyal sbah! Kont 3iyan bzzaf nhar l7ed."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach Laila kanet f ddar lwikand kamel?","options":["7it kanet mrida","7it kanet mechghoula","7it kan ljow bard","7it kanet katkhdem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I was at home all weekend. I was sick.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kan Omar nhar ssebt?","options":["F 3ers f Rabat","F ddar f Casa","F lb7er","F lkhedma"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I was at my cousin's wedding in Rabat.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Were there many people?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno sewlat Laila?","options":["Wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas","Wach kaynin bzzaf dyal nnas daba","Wach lmakla kanet bnina","Wach kan Omar 3iyan"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Were there many people?` = wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas? (lmadi)"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar was at home at midnight.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `At five in the morning!` = m3a lkhemsa dyal sbah."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Where were you yesterday?","da":"Fin konti lbare7?","pron":"wér weur you yès-teur-déy"},{"target_en":"I was at home with my family.","da":"Kont f ddar m3a l3a2ila dyali.","pron":"aï woz at hom with maï fa-mi-li"},{"target_en":"We weren't at work last Friday.","da":"Makonnach f lkhedma jjem3a li fatet.","pron":"wi weu-rent at weurk last fraï-déy"},{"target_en":"Was it expensive? — No, it wasn't.","da":"Wach kan ghali? — La, makanch.","pron":"woz it ik-spén-siv? — no, it wo-zent"},{"target_en":"There were a lot of people at the party.","da":"Kanou bzzaf dyal nnas f l7efla.","pron":"thér weur a lot ov pi-peul at the par-ti"},{"target_en":"I was very tired two days ago.","da":"Kont 3iyana bzzaf hadi youmayn.","pron":"aï woz vé-ri taï-eurd tou déyz a-go"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Lwikand dyalek","context_da":"Nhar ttnin f sbah. Sa7btek Sarah kattsewlek 3la lwikand. Jawbi b `I was` / `we were` / `it was`. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning, Nouha! How was your weekend?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha! Kifach kan lwikand dyalek?","expect_keywords":["it was","was","great","good","nice","ok","fine","boring"],"sample_en":"It was great, thanks!"},{"bot_en":"Where were you on Saturday?","bot_da":"Fin konti nhar ssebt?","expect_keywords":["i was","we were","at home","at the","in","with"],"sample_en":"I was at the beach with my family."},{"bot_en":"Nice! Was the weather good?","bot_da":"Zwin! Wach kan ljow mzyan?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","it was","wasn't","sunny","hot","cold","rainy"],"sample_en":"Yes, it was. It was sunny and hot."},{"bot_en":"And were there many people?","bot_da":"W wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","there were","there weren't","people","many","a lot"],"sample_en":"Yes, there were a lot of people."},{"bot_en":"Sounds fun. Were you tired on Sunday?","bot_da":"Mzyan. Wach konti 3iyana nhar l7ed?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i was","i wasn't","tired","busy"],"sample_en":"Yes, I was very tired, so I was at home all day."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Lwikand li fat","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal 3la lwikand li fat (wla nhar lbare7): fin konti, m3a men, kifach kan ljow, kifach kan l'i7sas dyalek (`tired`, `happy`, `busy`…), w wach kanou bzzaf dyal nnas. Sta3mli `was`, `were`, `wasn't`, `weren't` w kelmat lwa9t (`last Saturday`, `yesterday`, `ago`).","helper_en":["Last Saturday, I was ...","I was with ...","The weather was ...","There were ...","It was a ... day."],"min_words":40,"keywords":["was","were"],"model_en":"Last Saturday, I was in Rabat with my sister. We were at the medina in the morning. There were a lot of tourists and the weather was sunny. At lunchtime, we were at a small restaurant near the river. The fish was delicious and it wasn't expensive. In the afternoon, we were at my aunt's house. Her children were very happy because we were there. I was tired on Sunday, but it was a wonderful weekend!"}},{"id":"l16","order":16,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"🕰️","title_en":"Past simple: regular & irregular verbs","title_da":"Lmadi: l'af3al","goals_da":["T7ki 3la lwikand dyalek b lmadi: `I went`, `I visited`, `I ate`","Tzidi `-ed` l l'af3al l3adiya w tent9iha mzyan: /t/, /d/, /id/","T7efdi l'af3al li 3ndhom forma khassa: `went`, `had`, `saw`, `ate`, `did`, `bought`…","Tsta3mli `didn't` w `Did you…?`, w tratbi l7kaya b `first`, `then`, `after that`, `finally`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'af3al l3adiya: fi3l + -ed","body_da":"F lmadi, l'aghlabiya dyal l'af3al (`regular` = l3adiyin) kanzido lihom ghir `-ed`:\n\n- `work → worked`, `play → played`, `visit → visited`, `watch → watched`, `cook → cooked`, `clean → cleaned`, `listen → listened`, `talk → talked`, `call → called`, `help → helped`, `want → wanted`, `start → started`.\n\nW **nefs lforma m3a kolchi**: `I worked`, `she worked`, `they worked`. Ma kaynach `-s`. F darija kanbeddlo l fi3l kamel (\"khdemt\", \"khdem\", \"khdemna\"), f lingliziya ghir `-ed` w safi!\n\n**Lkitaba:**\n\n- L fi3l li kaysali b `e`: zidi ghir `d`: `live → lived`, `like → liked`, `dance → danced`, `arrive → arrived`.\n- L fi3l li kaysali b 7arf + `y`: l `y` katwelli `ied`: `study → studied`, `try → tried`. (Walakin `play → played`, `stay → stayed`.)\n- L fi3l l9sir (bhal m3a `-ing`): dewbli l7arf l'akhir: `stop → stopped`, `shop → shopped`, `plan → planned`.","examples":[{"en":"I worked on Saturday.","da":"Khdemt nhar ssebt.","pron":"aï weurkt on sa-teur-déy"},{"en":"We visited my grandmother in Fes.","da":"Zorna jeddati f Fes.","pron":"wi vi-zi-tid maï grand-ma-theur in fès"},{"en":"She watched a film last night.","da":"Lbare7 f lil chafet wa7ed lfilm.","pron":"chi wotcht a film last naït"},{"en":"They played football in the park.","da":"L3bou lkora f lpark.","pron":"théy pléyd fout-bol in the park"},{"en":"He studied English for two hours.","da":"9ra lingliziya jouj swaye3.","pron":"hi steu-did in-glich for tou a-weurz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kifach kant9o -ed: /t/, /d/, /id/","body_da":"`-ed` kat9ra b 3 dyal ttori9at, 3la 7sab ssout li 9belha. Hadi mohimma bach yfehmouk!\n\n**1. /t/** — men ba3d ssout khfif (`k`, `p`, `s`, `sh`, `ch`, `f`): `worked` = 'weurkt', `watched` = 'wotcht', `cooked` = 'koukt', `helped` = 'hélpt', `washed` = 'wacht', `talked` = 'tokt'.\n\n**2. /d/** — men ba3d ssout 9wi wla `a`, `e`, `i`, `o`, `u`, `y`: `played` = 'pléyd', `cleaned` = 'klind', `lived` = 'livd', `called` = 'kold', `listened` = 'li-send', `arrived` = 'a-raïvd'.\n\n**3. /id/** — ghir men ba3d `t` wla `d`, w hna kayzid ma9ta3: `visited` = 'vi-zi-tid', `wanted` = 'won-tid', `needed` = 'ni-did', `started` = 'star-tid'.\n\nLmohim: f /t/ w /d/ **ma kaynach ma9ta3 jdid**. `worked` ma9ta3 wa7ed, machi 'weur-ked'!","examples":[{"en":"I cooked and cleaned all day.","da":"Tiyebt w ne9it nhar kamel.","pron":"aï koukt and klind ol déy"},{"en":"We wanted to visit the museum.","da":"Bghina nzouro lmat7af.","pron":"wi won-tid tou vi-zit the miou-zi-om"},{"en":"She called her mother yesterday.","da":"3eytat l mmha lbare7.","pron":"chi kold heur ma-theur yès-teur-déy"},{"en":"The bus stopped and we walked home.","da":"Ttobis w9ef w mchina l ddar 3la rejlina.","pron":"the beus stopt and wi wokt hom"},{"en":"It started at eight and finished at ten.","da":"Bda m3a ttmenya w sala m3a l3echra.","pron":"it star-tid at éyt and fi-nicht at tén"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"L'af3al li 3ndhom forma khassa: went, had, saw, ate…","body_da":"Bzzaf dyal l'af3al lmohimma ma kayakhdouch `-ed` — kol wa7ed 3ndo lforma dyalo f lmadi (`irregular`). Khassek t7efdihom, bhal jadwal ddarb. Hadou li kaytsta3mlo kter:\n\n- `go → went` = mcha\n- `have → had` = kan 3ndo / kla (`had breakfast`)\n- `see → saw` = chaf\n- `eat → ate` = kla\n- `do → did` = dar\n- `make → made` = 3mel / sawb\n- `get → got` = jab / 7essel, `get up → got up` = nad\n- `come → came` = ja\n- `take → took` = khda / dda\n- `buy → bought` = chra\n- `say → said` = 9al\n- `drink → drank` = chreb\n- `sleep → slept` = n3es\n- `read → read` = 9ra (nefs lkitaba, walakin kat9ra 'réd')\n- `write → wrote` = kteb\n- `be → was / were` = kan (dars 15)\n\nNefs lforma m3a kolchi 7ta hna: `I went`, `she went`, `they went`.","examples":[{"en":"I went to the souk and bought some vegetables.","da":"Mchit l ssou9 w chrit chwiya dyal lkhodra.","pron":"aï wént tou the souk and bot som védj-ta-beulz"},{"en":"We had couscous and drank mint tea.","da":"Klina lkesksou w chrebna atay b nne3na3.","pron":"wi had kous-kous and drank mint ti"},{"en":"She got up late and took a taxi.","da":"Nadet m3ettla w khdat taxi.","pron":"chi got eup léyt and touk a tak-si"},{"en":"My brother came home at midnight.","da":"Khouya ja l ddar f ness llil.","pron":"maï bra-theur kéym hom at mid-naït"},{"en":"He said hello and made some tea.","da":"Sellem w 3mel chwiya d atay.","pron":"hi séd hé-lo and méyd som ti"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Nnafi w sso2al: didn't / Did you…?","body_da":"**Nnafi:** `didn't` (= `did not`) + l fi3l **3la 7alto** (bla `-ed`, bla lforma lkhassa):\n\n- `I didn't go to work.` (machi `I didn't went`)\n- `She didn't like the film.` (machi `didn't liked`)\n- `We didn't have time.` = makanch 3ndna lwa9t.\n\n3lach? 7it `did` howa li kayhez lmadi, w l fi3l kayb9a 3adi. Bhal `doesn't` f l7adir: `She doesn't work.`\n\n**Sso2al:** `Did` + `you` / `she` / `they` + l fi3l 3la 7alto:\n\n- `Did you go out?` = wach khrejti?\n- `Did she call you?` = wach 3eytat lik?\n- `What did you do yesterday?` = chno derti lbare7?\n- `Where did you go?` = fin mchiti?\n- `What time did you get up?` = chno men sa3a nedti?\n\n**Ljawab l9sir:** `Yes, I did.` / `No, I didn't.` — `Yes, she did.` / `No, she didn't.`\n\nW nefs `did` m3a kolchi: `Did I…?`, `Did he…?`, `Did we…?`","examples":[{"en":"I didn't go to work yesterday.","da":"Lbare7 mamchitch l lkhedma.","pron":"aï di-dent go tou weurk yès-teur-déy"},{"en":"She didn't like the film.","da":"Ma3jebhach lfilm.","pron":"chi di-dent laïk the film"},{"en":"Did you sleep well? — Yes, I did.","da":"Wach n3esti mzyan? — Ah, n3est mzyan.","pron":"did you slip wél? — yès, aï did"},{"en":"What did you do last weekend?","da":"Chno derti lwikand li fat?","pron":"wat did you dou last wik-énd"},{"en":"Did they come? — No, they didn't.","da":"Wach jaw? — La, majawch.","pron":"did théy keum? — no, théy di-dent"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"7ki lwikand dyalek: first, then, after that, finally","body_da":"Bach t7ki chi 7aja b ttartib (lwikand, nhar, re7la), sta3mli had lkelmat f lbdya dyal ljomla, w men ba3dhom lfasila (`,`):\n\n- `First,` = lowwel\n- `Then,` = men ba3d\n- `After that,` = men ba3d hadchi\n- `Finally,` = f l'akhir\n\nKat9edri tzidi 7ta: `In the morning,` / `In the afternoon,` / `In the evening,` / `At night,` / `Later,` (= men ba3d chwiya).\n\nMital kamel: `On Saturday, I got up at nine. First, I had breakfast with my family. Then, I went to the hammam with my sister. After that, we had lunch at my aunt's house. Finally, we watched a film at home.`\n\nBhal f darija: \"lowwel… men ba3d… w f l'akhir…\" — nefs ttartib.","examples":[{"en":"First, I had breakfast.","da":"Lowwel, ftert.","pron":"feurst, aï had brék-fast"},{"en":"Then, I went to the market.","da":"Men ba3d, mchit l ssou9.","pron":"thén, aï wént tou the mar-kit"},{"en":"After that, we visited my aunt.","da":"Men ba3d hadchi, zorna khalti.","pron":"af-teur that, wi vi-zi-tid maï ant"},{"en":"Finally, we watched a film at home.","da":"F l'akhir, chefna film f ddar.","pron":"faï-na-li, wi wotcht a film at hom"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"went","da":"mcha (lmadi dyal `go`)","emoji":"🚶‍♀️","pron":"wént","example_en":"I went to Rabat on Sunday.","example_da":"Mchit l Rabat nhar l7ed."},{"en":"had","da":"kan 3ndo / kla (lmadi dyal `have`)","emoji":"🍽️","pron":"had","example_en":"We had breakfast at nine.","example_da":"Fterna m3a tts3oud."},{"en":"saw","da":"chaf (lmadi dyal `see`)","emoji":"👀","pron":"so","example_en":"I saw my friends at the café.","example_da":"Cheft s7abi f l9ehwa."},{"en":"ate","da":"kla (lmadi dyal `eat`)","emoji":"🍲","pron":"éyt","example_en":"We ate couscous on Friday.","example_da":"Klina lkesksou nhar jjem3a."},{"en":"did","da":"dar (lmadi dyal `do`)","emoji":"✅","pron":"did","example_en":"What did you do yesterday?","example_da":"Chno derti lbare7?"},{"en":"made","da":"3mel / sawb (lmadi dyal `make`)","emoji":"🫖","pron":"méyd","example_en":"My mother made tea.","example_da":"Mama 3emlat atay."},{"en":"got up","da":"nad (lmadi dyal `get up`)","emoji":"⏰","pron":"got eup","example_en":"I got up at seven.","example_da":"Nedt m3a ssb3a."},{"en":"came","da":"ja (lmadi dyal `come`)","emoji":"🚪","pron":"kéym","example_en":"My cousin came to our house.","example_da":"Bent 3emmi jat l darna."},{"en":"took","da":"khda / dda (lmadi dyal `take`)","emoji":"🚕","pron":"touk","example_en":"We took a taxi to the station.","example_da":"Khdina taxi l lma7atta."},{"en":"bought","da":"chra (lmadi dyal `buy`)","emoji":"🛒","pron":"bot","example_en":"She bought a new dress.","example_da":"Chrat keswa jdida."},{"en":"said","da":"9al (lmadi dyal `say`)","emoji":"💬","pron":"séd","example_en":"He said thank you.","example_da":"9al choukran."},{"en":"drank","da":"chreb (lmadi dyal `drink`)","emoji":"☕","pron":"drank","example_en":"They drank coffee after lunch.","example_da":"Cherbou l9ehwa men ba3d lghda."},{"en":"slept","da":"n3es (lmadi dyal `sleep`)","emoji":"😴","pron":"slépt","example_en":"I slept until ten.","example_da":"N3est 7ta l l3echra."},{"en":"visited","da":"zar (lmadi dyal `visit`)","emoji":"🏡","pron":"vi-zi-tid","example_en":"We visited my grandmother.","example_da":"Zorna jeddati."},{"en":"then","da":"men ba3d","emoji":"➡️","pron":"thén","example_en":"First I cooked, then I cleaned.","example_da":"Lowwel tiyebt, men ba3d ne9it."},{"en":"finally","da":"f l'akhir","emoji":"🏁","pron":"faï-na-li","example_en":"Finally, we went home.","example_da":"F l'akhir, mchina l ddar."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Lwikand: Nouha w Omar","context_da":"Nhar ttnin f sbah f lkhedma. Omar kaysewwel Nouha 3la lwikand dyalha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good morning, Nouha! Did you have a good weekend?","da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha! Wach dewwezti wikand mzyan?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I did. On Saturday, I went to the souk with my mother.","da":"Ah. Nhar ssebt, mchit l ssou9 m3a mama."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"What did you buy?","da":"Chno chriti?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"We bought vegetables, fruit and a big fish. Then we cooked lunch together.","da":"Chrina lkhodra, lfakiya w wa7ed l7outa kbira. Men ba3d tiyebna lghda m3a b3diyatna."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Nice! And on Sunday?","da":"Zwin! W nhar l7ed?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I got up late. After that, I visited my aunt in Mohammedia. We had tea and talked for hours.","da":"Nedt m3ettla. Men ba3d hadchi, zert khalti f lMo7ammadiya. Chrebna atay w hderna swaye3."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Did you go to the beach?","da":"Wach mchiti l lb7er?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, we didn't. It was windy. And you? What did you do?","da":"La, mamchinach. Kan rri7. W nta? Chno derti?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Nothing special. I slept, I watched football and I ate a lot!","da":"Walou khass. N3est, cheft lkora w klit bzzaf!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Ha ha! A perfect weekend!","da":"Hahaha! Wikand mithali!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Melli kat3ellmi chi fi3l jdid, 7efdih m3a lmadi dyalo bjouj, bhal zouj: `go – went`, `buy – bought`, `eat – ate`. Diri lista f lportable dyalek w 9rayha 5 d9ay9 kol nhar. W fekkri dima: m3a `didn't` w `Did…?` l fi3l kayrje3 3adi: `I didn't go` (machi `didn't went`)!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno howa lmadi dyal `go`?","options":["went","goed","goes","going"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`go` 3ndo forma khassa: `go → went`. `goed` makaynach!"},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli l fi3l f lmadi m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"went","da":"mcha","emoji":"🚶‍♀️"},{"en":"ate","da":"kla","emoji":"🍲"},{"en":"bought","da":"chra","emoji":"🛒"},{"en":"saw","da":"chaf","emoji":"👀"},{"en":"slept","da":"n3es","emoji":"😴"},{"en":"made","da":"3mel / sawb","emoji":"🫖"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I worked on Saturday.","question_da":"Sem3i mzyan l'akhir dyal l fi3l. Chno fhemti?","options":["Khdemt nhar ssebt li fat","Kankhdem kol nhar ssebt","Ghadi nkhdem nhar ssebt","Kankhdem daba"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`worked` = `work` + `-ed` → lmadi. Sem3i ssout /t/ f l'akhir: 'weurkt'."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Yesterday, she ___ her grandmother in Fes.","options":["visited","visits","visit"],"answer":"visited","hint_da":"`Yesterday` → lmadi.","explain_da":"`Yesterday` = lbare7 → `visited`. Lmadi nefso m3a `she`: ma kaynach `-s`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen fi3l kay9ra b /id/ (b ma9ta3 zayd)?","options":["wanted","worked","played","cooked"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"/id/ ghir men ba3d `t` wla `d`: `wanted` = 'won-tid'. `worked` = 'weurkt', `played` = 'pléyd', `cooked` = 'koukt'."},{"type":"order","words":["went","We","to","the","beach","Sunday.","on"],"answer":"We went to the beach on Sunday.","da":"Mchina l lb7er nhar l7ed."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Did you sleep well?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kaysewlek?","options":["Wach n3esti mzyan?","Wach katn3si mzyan?","Wach nti 3iyana?","Fo9ach n3esti?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Did you sleep well?` = wach n3esti mzyan? `Did` → so2al f lmadi."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ (not / go) to work yesterday because I was sick.","answers":["didn't go","did not go"],"hint_da":"`didn't` + l fi3l 3la 7alto.","explain_da":"`I didn't go` — men ba3d `didn't`, l fi3l kayb9a 3adi: `go`, machi `went`."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"She didn't went to the party\" is correct.","statement_da":"`She didn't went to the party` jomla s7i7a.","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! Men ba3d `didn't` kanst3mlo l fi3l 3la 7alto: `She didn't go to the party.`"},{"type":"translate","da":"Lbare7 klit lkesksou w chrebt atay.","answers":["Yesterday I ate couscous and drank tea.","Yesterday I ate couscous and I drank tea.","I ate couscous and drank tea yesterday.","I ate couscous and I drank tea yesterday."],"hint_en":"Yesterday I ... couscous and ... tea.","explain_da":"`eat → ate`, `drink → drank`. Bjouj 3ndhom forma khassa!"},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"What did you do last weekend?","da":"Chno derti lwikand li fat?","explain_da":"`What did you do?` — `did` kayhez lmadi, w `do` kayb9a 3adi."},{"type":"order","words":["Did","buy","she","a","new","dress?"],"answer":"Did she buy a new dress?","da":"Wach chrat keswa jdida?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ttartib s7i7 dyal l7kaya:","question_en":"___, I got up. ___, I had breakfast. ___, I went to work.","options":["First / Then / After that","After that / First / Then","Finally / Then / First","Then / Finally / First"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`First` = lowwel, `Then` = men ba3d, `After that` = men ba3d hadchi, `Finally` = f l'akhir."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"My brother ___ home at midnight last night.","options":["came","come","comed"],"answer":"came","hint_da":"`come` 3ndo forma khassa.","explain_da":"`come → came`. `comed` makaynach."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach chefti lfilm? — La, machftouch. N3est bekri.","answers":["Did you see the film? — No, I didn't. I slept early.","Did you see the film? No, I didn't. I slept early.","Did you see the movie? — No, I didn't. I slept early.","Did you watch the film? — No, I didn't. I slept early."],"hint_en":"Did you ... the film? — No, I ... I ... early.","explain_da":"`Did you see…?` → `No, I didn't.` `sleep → slept`. `early` = bekri."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"On Saturday, I went to the souk. Then, I cooked lunch with my mother. Finally, we watched a film.","da":"Nhar ssebt, mchit l ssou9. Men ba3d, tiyebt lghda m3a mama. F l'akhir, chefna film.","pron":"on sa-teur-déy, aï wént tou the souk. thén, aï koukt leuntch with maï ma-theur. faï-na-li, wi wotcht a film"}],"reading":{"title_en":"My weekend in Chefchaouen","title_da":"Lwikand dyali f Chefchaouen","emoji":"💙","text_en":"Last weekend, I went to Chefchaouen with my friend Sarah. We took the bus from Casablanca on Friday evening. The trip was long, but we talked and slept a little. On Saturday morning, we got up early and had breakfast at a small café: bread, olive oil and mint tea. Then we walked in the old medina. The houses were blue and beautiful! Sarah took hundreds of photos. After that, we visited a small shop and I bought a blue scarf for my mother. At lunchtime, we ate a tagine with goat cheese. In the evening, we climbed to the Spanish Mosque and watched the sunset. It was amazing. On Sunday, we didn't do much. We drank coffee, read our books and came back to Casablanca at night. I didn't want to go home!","text_da":"Lwikand li fat, mchit l Chefchaouen m3a sa7bti Sarah. Khdina lkar men Casa nhar jjem3a f l3chiya. Rre7la kanet twila, walakin hderna w n3esna chwiya. Nhar ssebt f sbah, nedna bekri w fterna f wa7ed l9ehwa sghira: lkhobz, zit l3oud w atay b nne3na3. Men ba3d tmechchina f lmdina l9dima. Ddyour kanou zer9in w zwinin! Sarah khdat myat dyal ttsawer. Men ba3d hadchi, zorna wa7ed l7anout sghira w chrit chal zre9 l mama. F lwa9t dyal lghda, klina tajin b jben lme3za. F l3chiya, tle3na l jjame3 sbliouni w chefna ghroub chchems. Kan chi 7aja ra2i3a. Nhar l7ed, madernach bzzaf. Chrebna l9ehwa, 9rina lktouba dyalna w rje3na l Casa f lil. Mabghitch nrje3 l ddar!","glossary":[{"en":"trip","da":"rre7la / ssafar"},{"en":"got up early","da":"nad bekri"},{"en":"olive oil","da":"zit l3oud"},{"en":"walked","da":"tmechcha"},{"en":"hundreds of","da":"myat dyal"},{"en":"scarf","da":"chal (foulard)"},{"en":"goat cheese","da":"jben lme3za"},{"en":"climbed","da":"tle3"},{"en":"sunset","da":"ghroub chchems"},{"en":"came back","da":"rje3"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach mchaw l Chefchaouen?","options":["B lkar","B tomobil","B ttran","B ttiyara"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`We took the bus from Casablanca.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"They had breakfast at the hotel.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `had breakfast at a small café`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno chrat Nouha l mmha?","options":["Chal zre9","Tajin","Ktab","Jben"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I bought a blue scarf for my mother.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"On Sunday, they came back to Casablanca at night.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: `came back to Casablanca at night`."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Chno derti lwikand li fat?","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Tom kaysewwel Laila 3la lwikand dyalha. Sem3i mzyan: fin mchat Laila nhar ssebt? w chno dar Tom nhar l7ed?","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Hi Laila! What did you do last weekend?","da":"Ahlan Laila! Chno derti lwikand li fat?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"On Saturday, I went to my grandmother's house in Salé.","da":"Nhar ssebt, mchit l dar jeddati f Sla."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Oh nice. Did you take the train?","da":"Wah zwin. Wach khditi ttran?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"No, I didn't. My father took us in his car. We had lunch together and my grandmother made a big couscous.","da":"La. Bba ddana f tomobilo. Tgheddina m3a b3diyatna w jeddati 3emlat kesksou kbir."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Yummy! And what did you do on Sunday?","da":"Bnin! W nhar l7ed chno derti?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"I didn't do much. I cleaned my room, studied English and watched a film. And you?","da":"Madertch bzzaf. Ne9it biti, 9rit lingliziya w cheft film. W nta?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"I played football with Omar on Saturday morning. After that, we ate pizza.","da":"L3ebt lkora m3a Omar nhar ssebt f sbah. Men ba3d hadchi, klina lpizza."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Did you have a good time?","da":"Wach dewweztou wa9t zwin?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Yes, we did! But on Sunday I slept all day. I was so tired.","da":"Ah! Walakin nhar l7ed n3est nhar kamel. Kont 3iyan bzzaf."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin mchat Laila nhar ssebt?","options":["L dar jeddatha f Sla","L lb7er","L ssou9","L Chefchaouen"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I went to my grandmother's house in Salé.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila took the train to Salé.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `My father took us in his car.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I didn't do much.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 9alet Laila?","options":["Madertch bzzaf","Dert bzzaf dyal l7wayj","Khdemt bzzaf","Mabghitch ndir walou"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I didn't do much.` = madertch bzzaf. `much` = bzzaf."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno dar Tom nhar l7ed?","options":["N3es nhar kamel","L3eb lkora","Kla lpizza","9ra lingliziya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`On Sunday I slept all day.`"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"I worked all day yesterday.","da":"Lbare7 khdemt nhar kamel.","pron":"aï weurkt ol déy yès-teur-déy"},{"target_en":"We visited my aunt and played with the kids.","da":"Zorna khalti w l3ebna m3a drari.","pron":"wi vi-zi-tid maï ant and pléyd with the kidz"},{"target_en":"I went to the souk and bought some fish.","da":"Mchit l ssou9 w chrit chwiya dyal l7out.","pron":"aï wént tou the souk and bot som fich"},{"target_en":"She didn't come to the party.","da":"Majatch l l7efla.","pron":"chi di-dent keum tou the par-ti"},{"target_en":"Did you have a good weekend? — Yes, I did.","da":"Wach dewwezti wikand mzyan? — Ah.","pron":"did you hav a goud wik-énd? — yès, aï did"},{"target_en":"First, I had breakfast. Then, I went to work.","da":"Lowwel, ftert. Men ba3d, mchit l lkhedma.","pron":"feurst, aï had brék-fast. thén, aï wént tou weurk"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"7ki 3la lwikand dyalek","context_da":"Nhar ttnin. L'oustad Mr. Brown kaysewwel kol wa7ed f l9ism 3la lwikand dyalo. Jawbi b lmadi: `I went`, `I visited`, `I didn't…`. Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning, Nouha! Did you have a good weekend?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha! Wach dewwezti wikand mzyan?","expect_keywords":["yes","i did","no","i didn't","good","great"],"sample_en":"Yes, I did. It was great!"},{"bot_en":"What did you do on Saturday?","bot_da":"Chno derti nhar ssebt?","expect_keywords":["i went","i visited","i cooked","i watched","i played","i cleaned","i stayed","i had","i ate","went","visited"],"sample_en":"I went to the souk with my mother and we cooked lunch."},{"bot_en":"Did you go out on Sunday?","bot_da":"Wach khrejti nhar l7ed?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i did","i didn't","went","stayed"],"sample_en":"No, I didn't. I stayed at home and watched a film."},{"bot_en":"What did you eat?","bot_da":"Chno kliti?","expect_keywords":["i ate","i had","we ate","we had","couscous","tagine","fish","chicken","pizza"],"sample_en":"We ate couscous with vegetables."},{"bot_en":"Sounds delicious! Did you study English this weekend?","bot_da":"Bnin! Wach 9riti lingliziya had lwikand?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i did","i didn't","studied","a little"],"sample_en":"Yes, I did. I studied for one hour on Sunday."},{"bot_en":"Well done! Thank you, Nouha.","bot_da":"Mzyan! Choukran, Nouha.","expect_keywords":["thank","you're welcome","welcome","bye"],"sample_en":"Thank you, Mr. Brown!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Lwikand li fat (b lmadi)","prompt_da":"7ki 3la lwikand li fat f 6 wla 7 jomal. Sta3mli l'af3al f lmadi (`went`, `had`, `visited`, `watched`…), jomla wa7da b `didn't`, w ratbi l7kaya b `First`, `Then`, `After that`, `Finally`.","helper_en":["First, I ...","Then, I went to ...","After that, we ...","I didn't ...","Finally, ..."],"min_words":45,"keywords":["went","then"],"model_en":"Last weekend was busy but nice. On Saturday, I got up at eight. First, I cleaned the house with my sister. Then, we went to the souk and bought vegetables, fruit and a chicken. After that, I cooked a tagine for lunch and my cousins came to eat with us. In the evening, we drank tea and watched a film. On Sunday, I didn't go out. I slept until ten, called my friend Sarah and studied English for an hour. Finally, I made dinner for my family."}},{"id":"l17","order":17,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"🗺️","title_en":"Directions & places in town","title_da":"Ttri9 w lblayes f lmdina","goals_da":["Tsemmi lblayes dyal lmdina: `the bank`, `the pharmacy`, `the train station`…","Tsewli 3la ttri9: `Excuse me, where is the post office?` w `Is there a café near here?`","Tfehmi w t3tiw ttri9: `Turn left`, `Go straight on`, `It's next to the bank`","T9oli kifach katwsli w ch7al kaykhod ttri9: `by bus`, `on foot`, `It takes ten minutes`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Fin kayna lbanka? — lblayes f lmdina","body_da":"F had dars ghadi nt3ellmo kifach nsewlo 3la ttri9 f lmdina. 9bel kolchi, khassna n3erfo smiyat lblayes: `the bank` (lbanka), `the pharmacy` (sseydaliya), `the post office` (lbosta), `the train station` (lagar), `the bus stop` (blast tobis), `the hospital` (sbitar), `the supermarket` (ssoupermarchi), `the mosque` (jame3), `the café` (l9ehwa) w `the market` (ssou9).\n\nMelli kansewlo 3la blasa m3rofa f lmdina, kansta3mlo `the`: `Where is the bank?` — bhal f darija melli kan9oulo \"fin kayna **l**banka?\" (b l'alif w llam).\n\nBach tkouni mo2addaba, bdaï dima b `Excuse me` (= sme7 liya) 9bel ma tsewli chi wa7ed f zzen9a:\n\n- `Excuse me, where is the bank?` = Sme7 liya, fin kayna lbanka?\n- `Excuse me, where's the train station?` = Sme7 liya, fin kayn lagar?\n\nIla makontich 3arfa wach kayna chi blasa 9riba, sewli b `Is there a … near here?` (tfekkri `there is` men dars 10): `Is there a pharmacy near here?` = Wach kayna chi sseydaliya 9riba men hna? Ljawab: `Yes, there is.` wla `No, there isn't.`","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, where is the post office?","da":"Sme7 liya, fin kayna lbosta?","pron":"ik-skiouz mi, wér iz the post o-fis"},{"en":"Where's the bus stop, please?","da":"Fin kayna blast tobis, 3afak?","pron":"wérz the beus stop, pliz"},{"en":"Is there a bank near here?","da":"Wach kayna chi banka 9riba men hna?","pron":"iz thér a bank nir hir"},{"en":"Yes, there is. It's over there.","da":"Ah, kayna. Rah temma.","pron":"yès, thér iz. its o-veur thér"},{"en":"Sorry, I don't know. I'm not from here.","da":"Sme7 liya, ma3reftch. Ana machi men hna.","pron":"so-ri, aï dont no. aïm not from hir"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Dori 3la lisser! — l'amr (imperative) bach n3tiw ttri9","body_da":"Bach n3tiw ttri9 l chi wa7ed, kansta3mlo l'amr (`imperative`): l fi3l bo7do, bla `you`. Bhal f darija melli kan9oulo \"dori\", \"siri\", \"9et3i\". Lfar9: f lingliziya l'amr ma kaytbeddelch bin rrajel w lmra: `Turn left!` kat9al l rrajel, l lmra w l jama3a.\n\n- `Turn left.` = Dori 3la lisser.\n- `Turn right.` = Dori 3la limen.\n- `Go straight on.` = Siri nichan.\n- `Cross the street.` = 9et3i zzen9a.\n- `Take the first street on the right.` = Khoudi zzen9a l'oula 3la limen.\n- `Take the second street on the left.` = Khoudi zzen9a ttanya 3la lisser.\n- `Go past the bank.` = Douzi 3la lbanka.\n\nKanzido `at` bach n9oulo fin ndoro: `Turn left at the pharmacy.` = Dori 3la lisser 3nd sseydaliya. W bach nrebto lkhotowat kansta3mlo `then` (= men ba3d): `Go straight on, then turn right.`\n\nNnafy dyal l'amr b `Don't` + l fi3l (bhal \"ma ddorich\"): `Don't turn left, turn right!`","examples":[{"en":"Turn left at the mosque.","da":"Dori 3la lisser 3nd jame3.","pron":"teurn léft at the mosk"},{"en":"Go straight on for five minutes.","da":"Siri nichan khems d9ay9.","pron":"go stréyt on for faïv mi-nits"},{"en":"Cross the street and turn right.","da":"9et3i zzen9a w dori 3la limen.","pron":"kros the strit and teurn raït"},{"en":"Take the second street on the left.","da":"Khoudi zzen9a ttanya 3la lisser.","pron":"téyk the sé-keund strit on the léft"},{"en":"Don't take the first street, take the second one.","da":"Matakhdich zzen9a l'oula, khoudi ttanya.","pron":"dont téyk the feurst strit, téyk the sé-keund wan"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"It's next to… — fin kayna b ddebt?","body_da":"Melli kanwesfo fin kayna chi blasa, kansta3mlo had lkelmat (chi w7din t3ellemtihom f dars 10):\n\n- `next to` = 7da: `The bank is next to the pharmacy.`\n- `opposite` = 9balt / mwajha l: `The café is opposite the post office.`\n- `on the corner` = f lkonya (f l9ent): `The pharmacy is on the corner.`\n- `between … and …` = bin … w …: `The hospital is between the bank and the market.`\n- `behind` = mora: `The bus stop is behind the mosque.`\n- `in front of` = 9eddam: `The taxi is in front of the station.`\n- `on the left` / `on the right` = 3la lisser / 3la limen: `The supermarket is on your right.`\n\nRdi lbal: m3a `opposite` makanzidouch `of`: `opposite the bank` (machi \"opposite of\"). W melli kan9oulo blasa f chi zen9a: `It's on Hassan II Avenue.` / `It's in Derb Sultan.`","examples":[{"en":"The bank is next to the post office.","da":"Lbanka 7da lbosta.","pron":"the bank iz nékst tou the post o-fis"},{"en":"The café is opposite the mosque.","da":"L9ehwa 9balt jame3.","pron":"the ka-fé iz o-peu-zit the mosk"},{"en":"The pharmacy is on the corner, on your left.","da":"Sseydaliya f lkonya, 3la lisser dyalek.","pron":"the far-ma-si iz on the kor-neur, on your léft"},{"en":"The hospital is between the market and the school.","da":"Sbitar bin ssou9 w lmdrasa.","pron":"the hos-pi-teul iz bi-twin the mar-kit and the skoul"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"How do I get to…? — kifach nwsel? w ch7al kaykhod?","body_da":"Bach tsewli 3la ttri9 l chi blasa b3ida chwiya, 9oli `How do I get to the train station?` = Kifach nwsel l lagar? Had so2al mohim bzzaf f ssafar.\n\nLjawab kaykoun b l'amr (`Go straight on…`) wla b lwasila (= b ach ghadi tmchi):\n\n- `by bus` = b tobis, `by train` = b ttran, `by taxi` = b taxi, `by car` = b tomobil\n- `on foot` = 3la rejlik (rdi lbal: `on foot`, machi \"by foot\"!)\n- `You can take the bus.` = T9edri takhdi tobis. (`can` men dars 14)\n- `Take bus number 7.` = Khoudi tobis ra9m 7.\n\nBach tsewli 3la lwa9t: `How long does it take?` = Ch7al kaykhod (dyal lwa9t)? Ljawab: `It takes ten minutes.` = Kaykhod 3echra d9ay9. `It takes about an hour by train.` = Kaykhod ta9riban sa3a b ttran.\n\nW bach tsewli wach b3ida: `Is it far?` = Wach b3ida? — `No, it's near.` / `Yes, it's quite far.` (`quite` = chwiya, b jouj).","examples":[{"en":"How do I get to the hospital?","da":"Kifach nwsel l sbitar?","pron":"haw dou aï guét tou the hos-pi-teul"},{"en":"You can take the bus or a taxi.","da":"T9edri takhdi tobis wla taxi.","pron":"you kan téyk the beus or a tak-si"},{"en":"It takes ten minutes on foot.","da":"Kaykhod 3echra d9ay9 3la rejlik.","pron":"it téyks tén mi-nits on fout"},{"en":"I go to work by train every day.","da":"Kanmchi l lkhedma b ttran kol nhar.","pron":"aï go tou weurk baï tréyn év-ri déy"},{"en":"Is it far? — No, it's very near.","da":"Wach b3ida? — La, 9riba bzzaf.","pron":"iz it far? no, its vé-ri nir"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"bank","da":"lbanka","emoji":"🏦","pron":"bank","example_en":"The bank opens at nine.","example_da":"Lbanka kat7el f tes3oud."},{"en":"pharmacy","da":"sseydaliya (lfarmasyan)","emoji":"💊","pron":"far-ma-si","example_en":"Is there a pharmacy near here?","example_da":"Wach kayna chi sseydaliya 9riba men hna?"},{"en":"post office","da":"lbosta","emoji":"📮","pron":"post o-fis","example_en":"I need to go to the post office.","example_da":"Khassni nmchi l lbosta."},{"en":"train station","da":"lagar (dyal ttran)","emoji":"🚉","pron":"tréyn sté-cheun","example_en":"The train station is far from here.","example_da":"Lagar b3id men hna."},{"en":"bus stop","da":"blast tobis (lmo7atta)","emoji":"🚏","pron":"beus stop","example_en":"Wait at the bus stop.","example_da":"Tsennay f blast tobis."},{"en":"hospital","da":"sbitar","emoji":"🏥","pron":"hos-pi-teul","example_en":"My aunt works at the hospital.","example_da":"Khalti katkhdem f sbitar."},{"en":"supermarket","da":"ssoupermarchi (lmagaza lkbira)","emoji":"🛒","pron":"sou-peur-mar-kit","example_en":"We buy milk at the supermarket.","example_da":"Kanchriw l7lib men ssoupermarchi."},{"en":"mosque","da":"jame3","emoji":"🕌","pron":"mosk","example_en":"The mosque is on the corner.","example_da":"Jame3 f lkonya."},{"en":"café","da":"l9ehwa","emoji":"☕","pron":"ka-fé","example_en":"Let's meet at the café.","example_da":"Yallah ntla9aw f l9ehwa."},{"en":"market","da":"ssou9","emoji":"🧺","pron":"mar-kit","example_en":"The market is opposite the mosque.","example_da":"Ssou9 9balt jame3."},{"en":"street","da":"zzen9a","emoji":"🛣️","pron":"strit","example_en":"Take the second street on the left.","example_da":"Khoudi zzen9a ttanya 3la lisser."},{"en":"left","da":"lisser","emoji":"⬅️","pron":"léft","example_en":"Turn left at the bank.","example_da":"Dori 3la lisser 3nd lbanka."},{"en":"right","da":"limen","emoji":"➡️","pron":"raït","example_en":"The café is on your right.","example_da":"L9ehwa 3la limen dyalek."},{"en":"straight on","da":"nichan","emoji":"⬆️","pron":"stréyt on","example_en":"Go straight on for two minutes.","example_da":"Siri nichan jouj d9ay9."},{"en":"corner","da":"lkonya (l9ent)","emoji":"📐","pron":"kor-neur","example_en":"The pharmacy is on the corner.","example_da":"Sseydaliya f lkonya."},{"en":"far","da":"b3id / b3ida","emoji":"📏","pron":"far","example_en":"Is it far? No, it's near.","example_da":"Wach b3ida? La, 9riba."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Nouha katsewwel 3la lbosta f Rabat","context_da":"Nouha f Rabat l'awwal merra. Baghya tmchi l lbosta bach tsifet chi 7aja l khtha. Katsewwel wa7ed rrajel smiyto Karim f zzen9a.","lines":[{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Excuse me, where is the post office?","da":"Sme7 liya, fin kayna lbosta?"},{"speaker":"Karim","en":"The post office? Go straight on, then turn left at the bank.","da":"Lbosta? Siri nichan, men ba3d dori 3la lisser 3nd lbanka."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Turn left at the bank. OK. Is it far?","da":"Ndor 3la lisser 3nd lbanka. Wakha. Wach b3ida?"},{"speaker":"Karim","en":"No, it's not far. It takes five minutes on foot.","da":"La, machi b3ida. Kaykhod khems d9ay9 3la rejlik."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Great! And is there a pharmacy near here?","da":"Mzyan! W wach kayna chi sseydaliya 9riba men hna?"},{"speaker":"Karim","en":"Yes, there is. It's opposite the post office, on the corner.","da":"Ah, kayna. Rah 9balt lbosta, f lkonya."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Perfect. Thank you very much for your help!","da":"Mzyan bzzaf. Choukran bzzaf 3la lmosa3ada!"},{"speaker":"Karim","en":"You're welcome. Have a nice day!","da":"Bla jmil. Nhar zwin!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Melli chi wa7ed kay3tik ttri9 b lingliziya, 3awdi lkelmat lmohimma li 9al lik: `Turn left at the bank… OK!` — hakka kat2ekkdi b anna fhemti, w howa kayse77e7 lik ila ghlatti. W tfekkri: `on foot` (3la rejlik) walakin `by bus`, `by train`, `by taxi`, `by car`. Ila sewlek chi wa7ed 3la ttri9 w ma3reftihach, 9oli b kol basata: `Sorry, I don't know. I'm not from here.`"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"sseydaliya\" b lingliziya?","options":["pharmacy","bank","hospital","market"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`pharmacy` = sseydaliya. `bank` = lbanka. `hospital` = sbitar. `market` = ssou9."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Turn left.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Dori 3la lisser","Dori 3la limen","Siri nichan","9et3i zzen9a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Turn left` = dori 3la lisser. `Turn right` = dori 3la limen. `Go straight on` = siri nichan. `Cross the street` = 9et3i zzen9a."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lblasa b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"bank","da":"lbanka","emoji":"🏦"},{"en":"mosque","da":"jame3","emoji":"🕌"},{"en":"train station","da":"lagar","emoji":"🚉"},{"en":"bus stop","da":"blast tobis","emoji":"🚏"},{"en":"post office","da":"lbosta","emoji":"📮"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Excuse me, ___ is the bank?","options":["where","what","who"],"answer":"where","hint_da":"Fin = ?","explain_da":"`Where` = fin. `Excuse me, where is the bank?` = Sme7 liya, fin kayna lbanka? (`what` = chno, `who` = chkoun)"},{"type":"order","words":["and","straight","right.","Go","turn","on"],"answer":"Go straight on and turn right.","da":"Siri nichan w dori 3la limen."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Is there a pharmacy near here?","question_da":"Achmen jawab s7i7 3la had so2al?","options":["Yes, there is. It's next to the bank.","Yes, I am. It's next to the bank.","Yes, there are. It's next to the bank.","Yes, it does. It's next to the bank."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"So2al b `Is there…?` → ljawab b `Yes, there is.` wla `No, there isn't.` (`there is` = kayn / kayna, men dars 10). `there are` dyal ljam3."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It takes ten minutes on foot.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al kaykhod ttri9, w kifach?","options":["3echra d9ay9 3la rejlik","3echra d9ay9 b tobis","3echrin d9i9a b taxi","Jouj d9ay9 b tomobil"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`It takes ten minutes` = kaykhod 3echra d9ay9. `on foot` = 3la rejlik."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"The post office is ___ the hospital.","options":["opposite","under","between"],"answer":"opposite","hint_da":"9balt = ?","explain_da":"`opposite` = 9balt / mwajha. `between` khassha jouj 7wayj (`between the bank and the café`). `under` = t7t — makat9alch 3la blasa f zzen9a."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"In English we say \"by foot\".","statement_da":"F lingliziya kan9oulo `by foot`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"La! Kan9oulo `on foot` = 3la rejlik. `by` kanzidouha ghir m3a lwasa2il: `by bus`, `by train`, `by car`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Sme7 liya, fin kayn lagar?","answers":["Excuse me, where is the train station?","Excuse me, where's the train station?","Excuse me, where is the station?","Excuse me, where's the station?"],"hint_en":"Excuse me, where ... the ... station?","explain_da":"`Excuse me` = sme7 liya. `Where is the train station?` = fin kayn lagar?"},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Go ___ on and the mosque is on your right.","answers":["straight"],"hint_da":"Siri nichan! Lkelma li na9sa kat3ni \"nichan\".","explain_da":"`Go straight on` = siri nichan. Rdi lbal l lktaba: `straight` (s-t-r-a-i-g-h-t) — l7orouf `gh` ma kaytne9ouch."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Take the second street on the left.","da":"Khoudi zzen9a ttanya 3la lisser.","explain_da":"`Take` – `the` – `second` – `street` – `on` – `the` – `left`. `second` = ttani / ttanya."},{"type":"order","words":["get","hospital?","How","to","I","the","do"],"answer":"How do I get to the hospital?","da":"Kifach nwsel l sbitar?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Nouha katmchi men Casa l Rabat b ttran. Achmen jomla s7i7a?","options":["I go to Rabat by train.","I go to Rabat on train.","I go to Rabat with train.","I go to Rabat in train."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"M3a lwasa2il kansta3mlo `by`: `by train`, `by bus`, `by taxi`, `by car`. Ghir `on foot` hiya li mokhtalifa."},{"type":"translate","da":"Lbanka 7da sseydaliya, f lkonya.","answers":["The bank is next to the pharmacy, on the corner.","The bank is next to the pharmacy on the corner.","The bank is on the corner, next to the pharmacy.","The bank is on the corner next to the pharmacy."],"hint_en":"The bank is ... to the ..., on the ...","explain_da":"`next to` = 7da. `on the corner` = f lkonya."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Excuse me, how do I get to the bus stop?","da":"Sme7 liya, kifach nwsel l blast tobis?","pron":"ik-skiouz mi, haw dou aï guét tou the beus stop"}],"reading":{"title_en":"A day in Rabat","title_da":"Nhar f Rabat","emoji":"🚆","text_en":"Last Saturday, Nouha went to Rabat by train. The trip from Casablanca took one hour. At the train station, she asked a woman: \"Excuse me, how do I get to the medina?\" The woman said: \"Go straight on, then turn left at the big mosque. The medina is opposite the post office. It takes fifteen minutes on foot.\" Nouha walked slowly and looked at the shops. She stopped at a small café and had a mint tea. Then she asked a boy: \"Is there a pharmacy near here?\" He said: \"Yes, there is one on the corner, next to the bank.\" Nouha bought some medicine for her mother. In the afternoon, she took a taxi to the Kasbah of the Udayas. It was beautiful! At six o'clock, she went back to the station and took the train home.","text_da":"Ssebt li fat, Nouha mchat l Rabat b ttran. Ttri9 men Casa khdat sa3a. F lagar, sewlat wa7ed lmra: \"Sme7 liya, kifach nwsel l lmdina l9dima?\" Lmra 9alt liha: \"Siri nichan, men ba3d dori 3la lisser 3nd jame3 lkbir. Lmdina l9dima 9balt lbosta. Kaykhod khemstach d9i9a 3la rejlik.\" Nouha tmechat bechwiya w chafet l7wanet. W9fat f wa7ed l9ehwa sghira w cherbat atay. Men ba3d sewlat wa7ed lweld: \"Wach kayna chi sseydaliya 9riba men hna?\" 9al liha: \"Ah, kayna wa7da f lkonya, 7da lbanka.\" Nouha chrat chi dwa l mmha. F l3chiya, khdat taxi l 9asbat lwdaya. Kanet zwina bzzaf! F ssetta, rej3at l lagar w khdat ttran l ddar.","glossary":[{"en":"trip","da":"ttri9 / ssafar"},{"en":"asked","da":"sewlat (sewwel)"},{"en":"medina","da":"lmdina l9dima"},{"en":"walked","da":"tmechat (3la rejliha)"},{"en":"shops","da":"l7wanet"},{"en":"stopped","da":"w9fat"},{"en":"bought","da":"chrat"},{"en":"medicine","da":"ddwa"},{"en":"went back","da":"rej3at"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach mchat Nouha l Rabat?","options":["B ttran","B tobis","B taxi","B tomobil"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Nouha went to Rabat by train.` = mchat b ttran."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The medina is next to the post office.","statement_da":"Lmdina l9dima 7da lbosta.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `The medina is opposite the post office` = 9balt lbosta, machi 7daha."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al kaykhod ttri9 men lagar l lmdina l9dima 3la rejlik?","options":["15 d9i9a","5 d9ay9","Sa3a","30 d9i9a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`It takes fifteen minutes on foot.` = khemstach d9i9a."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin kayna sseydaliya?","options":["F lkonya, 7da lbanka","9balt lbosta","F lagar","7da l9ehwa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`There is one on the corner, next to the bank.`"}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Siya7 f Marrakech","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar. Rekkzi 3la: fin bgha ymchi Tom? Wach ghadi yakhod taxi? W ch7al kaykhod ttri9?","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Excuse me, how do I get to Jemaa el-Fna square?","da":"Sme7 liya, kifach nwsel l sa7at jame3 lefna?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Jemaa el-Fna? It's easy. Go straight on, then turn right at the pharmacy.","da":"Jame3 lefna? Sahla. Sir nichan, men ba3d dor 3la limen 3nd sseydaliya."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Turn right at the pharmacy. And then?","da":"Ndor 3la limen 3nd sseydaliya. W men ba3d?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Then take the first street on the left. The square is in front of you.","da":"Men ba3d khoud zzen9a l'oula 3la lisser. Ssa7a 9eddamek."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Is it far? Can I take a taxi?","da":"Wach b3ida? Wach n9der nakhod taxi?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"No, you don't need a taxi. It takes about ten minutes on foot.","da":"La, makhassekch taxi. Kaykhod ta9riban 3echra d9ay9 3la rejlik."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Perfect. Thank you so much!","da":"Mzyan bzzaf. Choukran bzzaf!"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"You're welcome. Enjoy Marrakech!","da":"Bla jmil. Tmette3 b Marrakech!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin bgha ymchi Tom?","options":["L sa7at jame3 lefna","L sseydaliya","L lagar","L lbanka"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`How do I get to Jemaa el-Fna square?`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Turn right at the pharmacy.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 9alt Amina?","options":["Dor 3la limen 3nd sseydaliya","Dor 3la lisser 3nd sseydaliya","Sir nichan 7ta l sseydaliya","9te3 zzen9a 3nd lbanka"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Turn right` = dor 3la limen. `at the pharmacy` = 3nd sseydaliya."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Tom takes a taxi to the square.","statement_da":"Tom ghadi yakhod taxi l ssa7a.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Amina 9alt: `you don't need a taxi` — ghadi ymchi 3la rejlih."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al kaykhod ttri9 3la rejlik?","options":["Ta9riban 10 d9ay9","Ta9riban 30 d9i9a","Sa3a","Jouj d9ay9"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`It takes about ten minutes on foot.` — `about` = ta9riban."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Excuse me, where is the bank?","da":"Sme7 liya, fin kayna lbanka?","pron":"ik-skiouz mi, wér iz the bank"},{"target_en":"Turn left at the pharmacy.","da":"Dori 3la lisser 3nd sseydaliya.","pron":"teurn léft at the far-ma-si"},{"target_en":"Go straight on, then turn right.","da":"Siri nichan, men ba3d dori 3la limen.","pron":"go stréyt on, then teurn raït"},{"target_en":"It's next to the post office.","da":"Rah 7da lbosta.","pron":"its nékst tou the post o-fis"},{"target_en":"How do I get to the train station?","da":"Kifach nwsel l lagar?","pron":"haw dou aï guét tou the tréyn sté-cheun"},{"target_en":"It takes ten minutes on foot.","da":"Kaykhod 3echra d9ay9 3la rejlik.","pron":"it téyks tén mi-nits on fout"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Siya7 kaysewlek 3la ttri9","context_da":"Nti f zzen9a f lmdina dyalek. Wa7ed ssiya7 kaysewlek 3la ttri9. Jawbih b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Excuse me! Is there a pharmacy near here?","bot_da":"Sme7 liya! Wach kayna chi sseydaliya 9riba men hna?","expect_keywords":["yes","there is","no","there isn't","pharmacy","next to","opposite","corner"],"sample_en":"Yes, there is. It's next to the bank."},{"bot_en":"Great! How do I get there?","bot_da":"Mzyan! Kifach nwsel liha?","expect_keywords":["go straight","straight on","turn left","turn right","take the","cross","go past"],"sample_en":"Go straight on and turn left at the mosque."},{"bot_en":"Is it far?","bot_da":"Wach b3ida?","expect_keywords":["no","not far","minutes","near","yes","far","on foot"],"sample_en":"No, it's not far. It takes five minutes on foot."},{"bot_en":"And where is the train station, please?","bot_da":"W fin kayn lagar, 3afak?","expect_keywords":["opposite","next to","on the corner","behind","near","straight","turn","bus","taxi","far"],"sample_en":"It's opposite the post office. You can take a taxi."},{"bot_en":"Thank you very much for your help!","bot_da":"Choukran bzzaf 3la lmosa3ada!","expect_keywords":["welcome","no problem","bye","goodbye","good luck","nice day","enjoy"],"sample_en":"You're welcome! Have a nice day."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ttri9 l darek","prompt_da":"Sa7btek Sarah ghadi tji 3ndek l ddar l'awwal merra. Ktbi liha message b lingliziya: kifach twsel men lagar (wla men blast tobis) l darek. Sta3mli `Go straight on`, `Turn left / right`, `next to`, `opposite`, w 9oli ch7al kaykhod ttri9 (`It takes … minutes`).","helper_en":["From the train station, go straight on ...","Turn left / right at the ...","My house is next to / opposite the ...","It takes ... minutes on foot.","You can also take a taxi."],"min_words":40,"keywords":["turn","straight","minutes"],"model_en":"Hi Sarah! Here is the way to my house. From the train station, go straight on for five minutes. Then turn left at the big mosque. Take the second street on the right. My house is opposite the pharmacy, next to a small café. It is a white door with the number 12. It takes about fifteen minutes on foot, or you can take a taxi for ten dirhams. Call me if you get lost! See you on Saturday."}},{"id":"l18","order":18,"level":"A2.1","emoji":"🩺","title_en":"Health & body: at the doctor","title_da":"Ss7a w ljism: 3nd tbib","goals_da":["Tsemmi l'a3da2 dyal ljism: `head`, `stomach`, `back`, `throat`, `tooth`…","T9oli chno kaydorrek: `I have a headache`, `My back hurts`, `I feel sick`","Tfehmi so2al tbib `What's the matter?` w tjawbi 3lih","T3tiw nasi7a b `should` / `shouldn't`, w tfehmi sseydali: `Take one tablet twice a day`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ljism dyalna — the body","body_da":"Bach thedri m3a tbib, khassek t3erfi smiyat l'a3da2 dyal ljism (`the body`):\n\n- `head` = rras\n- `stomach` = lkerch / lm3da\n- `back` = ddher\n- `throat` = l7el9\n- `tooth` = ssenna — ljam3 dyalha machi 3adi: `teeth` = ssnan (machi \"tooths\"!)\n- `arm` = ddra3\n- `leg` = rrjel\n- `eye` = l3in (ljam3: `eyes`)\n- `ear` = lwden (ljam3: `ears`)\n- `hand` = lyedd, `foot` = l9dem (ljam3 machi 3adi: `feet`)\n\nBhal f darija melli kan9oulo \"ras**i**\", \"kerch**i**\", f lingliziya kansta3mlo `my` 9bel l3odw: `my head`, `my stomach`, `my back`. W rdi lbal l lmofrad w ljam3: `my eye` (3in wa7da) / `my eyes` (bjouj).","examples":[{"en":"I have two eyes, two ears and one head.","da":"3ndi jouj 3inin, jouj wdnin w ras wa7ed.","pron":"aï hav tou aïz, tou irz and wan héd"},{"en":"My tooth hurts.","da":"Senti kaddorrni.","pron":"maï touth heurts"},{"en":"Wash your hands before you eat.","da":"Ghesli yeddik 9bel ma takli.","pron":"woch your handz bi-for you it"},{"en":"My arm is OK, but my leg hurts.","da":"Dra3i labas, walakin rejli kaddorrni.","pron":"maï arm iz o-kéy, beut maï lég heurts"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"I have a headache / My back hurts — chno kaydorrek?","body_da":"Kayn jouj tari9at bach t9oli ach kaydorrek:\n\n**1) `I have a …`** (3ndi …) m3a smiyat lmard:\n\n- `I have a headache.` = Rasi kaydorrni. (`head` + `ache` = wja3 rras)\n- `I have a stomach ache.` = Kerchi kaddorrni.\n- `I have a toothache.` = Senti kaddorrni.\n- `I have a sore throat.` = 7el9i kaydorrni. (`sore` = mdorr, mel-heb)\n- `I have a cold.` = 3ndi rrwa7.\n- `I have a fever.` = 3ndi sskhana.\n- `I have a cough.` = 3ndi lko77a.\n\n**2) `My … hurts.`** (… dyali kaydorrni) m3a l3odw dyal ljism: `My back hurts.` = Dehri kaydorrni. `My leg hurts.` = Rejli kaddorrni. Ila kan ljam3, bla `-s`: `My eyes hurt.` = 3iniya kaydorrouni.\n\nW bach t9oli kifach 7assa, kansta3mlo `I feel` + ssifa: `I feel sick.` = 7assa b rasi mrida. `I feel tired.` = 7assa b l3ya. `I feel better.` = 7assit b t7assn. `I feel dizzy.` = Rasi kaydour biya.\n\nBhal f darija: \"rasi kaydorrni\" t9edri t9oliha b jouj tari9at — `I have a headache` wla `My head hurts` — bjouj s7a7!","examples":[{"en":"I have a headache and a fever.","da":"Rasi kaydorrni w 3ndi sskhana.","pron":"aï hav a héd-éyk and a fi-veur"},{"en":"My back hurts a lot.","da":"Dehri kaydorrni bzzaf.","pron":"maï bak heurts a lot"},{"en":"I have a sore throat and a cough.","da":"7el9i kaydorrni w 3ndi lko77a.","pron":"aï hav a sor throt and a kof"},{"en":"I feel sick. I want to go home.","da":"7assa b rasi mrida. Bghit nmchi l ddar.","pron":"aï fil sik. aï wont tou go hom"},{"en":"My eyes hurt when I read.","da":"3iniya kaydorrouni melli kan9ra.","pron":"maï aïz heurt wén aï rid"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"3nd tbib: What's the matter?","body_da":"Melli katdekhli 3nd tbib (`the doctor`), kaysewlek:\n\n- `What's the matter?` = Malek? / Chno 3ndek? (so2al 3am 3la lmochkil)\n- `What's wrong?` = Chno wa9e3? / Malek? (nefs lma3na)\n- `How do you feel?` = Kifach 7assa?\n- `Where does it hurt?` = Fin kaydorrek?\n- `Do you have a fever?` = Wach 3ndek sskhana?\n\nW kay9oul lik:\n\n- `Open your mouth, please.` = 7elli fommek, 3afak.\n- `It's nothing serious.` = Ma kayn walou khatir. / `Don't worry.` = Matkhafich.\n- `You have a cold.` / `You have the flu.` = 3ndek rrwa7 / 3ndek lgrip.\n- `Take this medicine.` = Khoudi had ddwa.\n- `Get well soon!` = Allah ychafik! (7arfiyan: twelli bikhir 9rib)\n\nTfekkri: `What's the matter?` kat9al 7ta bra tbib, melli kanchoufo chi wa7ed m9elle9 wla mrid — bhal \"malek?\" f darija.","examples":[{"en":"What's the matter? You look tired.","da":"Malek? Bayna 3lik 3yyana.","pron":"wats the ma-teur? you louk taï-eurd"},{"en":"Where does it hurt? — Here, in my stomach.","da":"Fin kaydorrek? — Hna, f kerchi.","pron":"wér deuz it heurt? hir, in maï steu-meuk"},{"en":"Do you have a fever? — Yes, I think so.","da":"Wach 3ndek sskhana? — Ah, kandenn.","pron":"dou you hav a fi-veur? yès, aï think so"},{"en":"It's nothing serious. Get well soon!","da":"Ma kayn walou khatir. Allah ychafik!","pron":"its neu-thing si-ri-eus. guét wél soun"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"should / shouldn't — nasi7a (advice)","body_da":"Bach n3tiw nasi7a, kansta3mlo `should` (= khassek) w `shouldn't` (= makhasskich). Men ba3dhom kayji l fi3l f ssoura l'asliya (bla `to`, bla `-s`):\n\n- `You should rest.` = Khassek trta7i.\n- `You should drink a lot of water.` = Khassek tcherbi lma bzzaf.\n- `You should see a doctor.` = Khassek tchoufi tbib.\n- `You shouldn't eat sugar.` = Makhasskich takli sskar.\n- `You shouldn't smoke.` = Makhasskich tkmi.\n\n`should` ma kaytbeddelch m3a `he` / `she`: `She should rest.` (machi \"shoulds\"). Bhal `can` li chefna f dars 14.\n\nSo2al: `Should I take medicine?` = Wach khassni nakhod ddwa? — `Yes, you should.` / `No, you shouldn't.`\n\n`should` hiya nasi7a (khassek), machi amr 9asi. Tbib kay9oul `You should rest`, machi `Rest!`.","examples":[{"en":"You should stay in bed today.","da":"Khassek tb9ay f lfrach lyouma.","pron":"you choud stéy in béd tou-déy"},{"en":"You shouldn't drink cold water.","da":"Makhasskich tcherbi lma bared.","pron":"you choud-eunt drink kold wo-teur"},{"en":"He should go to the hospital.","da":"Khasso ymchi l sbitar.","pron":"hi choud go tou the hos-pi-teul"},{"en":"Should I take these tablets? — Yes, you should.","da":"Wach khassni nakhod had l7bob? — Ah, khassek.","pron":"choud aï téyk thiz tab-lits? yès, you choud"},{"en":"You shouldn't work when you're sick.","da":"Makhasskich tkhdmi melli nti mrida.","pron":"you choud-eunt weurk wén your sik"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"F sseydaliya: medicine, tablets, syrup","body_da":"Men ba3d tbib, kanmchiw l sseydaliya (`the pharmacy`). Lkelmat lmohimma:\n\n- `medicine` = ddwa (kelma 3amma)\n- `tablets` / `pills` = l7bob (7abba wa7da = `a tablet`)\n- `syrup` = ssirou (dwa sa2il, dyal lko77a)\n- `a prescription` = lwer9a dyal tbib\n- `twice a day` = jouj merrat f nhar; `three times a day` = tlata d lmerrat f nhar; `once a day` = merra f nhar (men dars 8)\n- `after meals` / `before meals` = men ba3d lmakla / 9bel lmakla\n\nSseydali (`the pharmacist`) kay9oul lik: `Take one tablet twice a day, after meals.` = Khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla.\n\nW nti t9edri tsewli: `Do you have something for a headache?` = Wach 3ndkom chi 7aja l wja3 rras? / `How often should I take it?` = Ch7al men merra khassni nakhdo?","examples":[{"en":"Do you have something for a cold?","da":"Wach 3ndkom chi 7aja l rrwa7?","pron":"dou you hav seum-thing for a kold"},{"en":"Take one tablet twice a day.","da":"Khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar.","pron":"téyk wan tab-lit twaïs a déy"},{"en":"This syrup is for your cough.","da":"Had ssirou dyal lko77a dyalek.","pron":"this si-reup iz for your kof"},{"en":"How often should I take it? — Three times a day, after meals.","da":"Ch7al men merra nakhdo? — Tlata d lmerrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla.","pron":"haw o-feun choud aï téyk it? thri taïmz a déy, af-teur milz"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"head","da":"rras","emoji":"🤕","pron":"héd","example_en":"My head hurts.","example_da":"Rasi kaydorrni."},{"en":"stomach","da":"lkerch (lm3da)","emoji":"🤢","pron":"steu-meuk","example_en":"I have a stomach ache.","example_da":"Kerchi kaddorrni."},{"en":"back","da":"ddher","emoji":"🧍‍♀️","pron":"bak","example_en":"My back hurts when I sit.","example_da":"Dehri kaydorrni melli kangles."},{"en":"throat","da":"l7el9","emoji":"😷","pron":"throt","example_en":"I have a sore throat.","example_da":"7el9i kaydorrni."},{"en":"tooth","da":"ssenna (ljam3: ssnan = `teeth`)","emoji":"🦷","pron":"touth","example_en":"I have a toothache.","example_da":"Senti kaddorrni."},{"en":"arm","da":"ddra3","emoji":"💪","pron":"arm","example_en":"My arm hurts.","example_da":"Dra3i kaydorrni."},{"en":"leg","da":"rrjel","emoji":"🦵","pron":"lég","example_en":"Her leg hurts.","example_da":"Rejlha kaddorrha."},{"en":"eye","da":"l3in (ljam3: 3inin = `eyes`)","emoji":"👁️","pron":"aï","example_en":"My eyes hurt.","example_da":"3iniya kaydorrouni."},{"en":"ear","da":"lwden (ljam3: wdnin = `ears`)","emoji":"👂","pron":"ir","example_en":"My ear hurts.","example_da":"Wedni kaddorrni."},{"en":"headache","da":"wja3 rras","emoji":"🤯","pron":"héd-éyk","example_en":"I have a terrible headache.","example_da":"Rasi kaydorrni bzzaf."},{"en":"cold","da":"rrwa7 (lberd)","emoji":"🤧","pron":"kold","example_en":"She has a cold.","example_da":"3ndha rrwa7."},{"en":"fever","da":"sskhana","emoji":"🌡️","pron":"fi-veur","example_en":"He has a fever.","example_da":"3ndo sskhana."},{"en":"doctor","da":"tbib / tbiba","emoji":"👩‍⚕️","pron":"dok-teur","example_en":"You should see a doctor.","example_da":"Khassek tchoufi tbib."},{"en":"medicine","da":"ddwa","emoji":"🧴","pron":"méd-sin","example_en":"Take this medicine after meals.","example_da":"Khoudi had ddwa men ba3d lmakla."},{"en":"tablet","da":"7abba (dyal ddwa)","emoji":"💊","pron":"tab-lit","example_en":"Take one tablet twice a day.","example_da":"Khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar."},{"en":"syrup","da":"ssirou (dwa sa2il)","emoji":"🥄","pron":"si-reup","example_en":"This syrup is for children.","example_da":"Had ssirou dyal ddrari."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"3nd tbiba","context_da":"Nouha mrida men lbare7. Mchat 3nd tbiba f Casa. Tbiba katsewwelha chno 3ndha w kat3tiha nasa2i7.","lines":[{"speaker":"Doctor","en":"Good morning, Nouha. What's the matter?","da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha. Malek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good morning, doctor. I have a sore throat and a headache.","da":"Sbah lkhir, a tbiba. 7el9i kaydorrni w rasi kaydorrni."},{"speaker":"Doctor","en":"I see. Do you have a fever?","da":"Fhemt. Wach 3ndek sskhana?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I think so. I feel very tired.","da":"Ah, kandenn. 7assa b l3ya bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Doctor","en":"Open your mouth, please… Yes, your throat is red. You have a cold.","da":"7elli fommek, 3afak… Ah, 7el9ek 7mer. 3ndek rrwa7."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Is it serious?","da":"Wach khatir?"},{"speaker":"Doctor","en":"No, don't worry. You should rest and drink a lot of water.","da":"La, matkhafich. Khassek trta7i w tcherbi lma bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Should I take any medicine?","da":"Wach khassni nakhod chi dwa?"},{"speaker":"Doctor","en":"Yes. Take these tablets twice a day, after meals. And you shouldn't drink cold drinks.","da":"Ah. Khoudi had l7bob jouj merrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla. W makhasskich tcherbi lmachroubat lbarda."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"OK. Thank you, doctor.","da":"Wakha. Choukran, a tbiba."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Rdi lbal l `-s` f `hurts`: `My back hurts` (wa7ed) walakin `My eyes hurt` (bzzaf). Lkelmat b `-ache` (wja3) kaymchiw m3a `I have a…`: `a headache`, `a toothache`, `a stomach ache`. Melli chi wa7ed mrid, 9oli lih `Get well soon!` (= Allah ychafik). W 3nd tbib, ila mafhemtich chi 7aja, matkhafich: 9oli `Can you repeat, please?` — t3ellemtiha f dars 2!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"rasi kaydorrni\" b lingliziya?","options":["I have a headache.","I have a cold.","My leg hurts.","I feel tired."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I have a headache` = rasi kaydorrni. `I have a cold` = 3ndi rrwa7. `My leg hurts` = rejli kaddorrni. `I feel tired` = 7assa b l3ya."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli l3odw dyal ljism b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"head","da":"rras","emoji":"🤕"},{"en":"stomach","da":"lkerch","emoji":"🤢"},{"en":"tooth","da":"ssenna","emoji":"🦷"},{"en":"leg","da":"rrjel","emoji":"🦵"},{"en":"eye","da":"l3in","emoji":"👁️"},{"en":"ear","da":"lwden","emoji":"👂"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"What's the matter?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kaysewwel tbib?","options":["Malek? Chno 3ndek?","Chno smiytek?","Fin kayn sbitar?","Ch7al f 3merk?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What's the matter?` = malek? / chno 3ndek? Tbib kaysewwelha f lbdaya."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ a sore throat.","options":["have","am","feel"],"answer":"have","hint_da":"7el9i kaydorrni = I ... a sore throat.","explain_da":"M3a smiyat lmard kansta3mlo `have`: `I have a sore throat`, `I have a cold`, `I have a fever`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"My eyes ___.","options":["hurt","hurts","hurting"],"answer":"hurt","hint_da":"`eyes` = jam3 (bjouj).","explain_da":"`My eyes` jam3 → bla `-s`: `My eyes hurt.` Lmofrad kayakhod `-s`: `My eye hurts.`"},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"You shouldn't eat sugar.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno hiya nnasi7a?","options":["Makhasskich takli sskar","Khassek takli sskar","Khassek tcherbi lma","Makhasskich tn3si"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`You shouldn't eat sugar` = makhasskich takli sskar. `shouldn't` = `should not` = makhasskich."},{"type":"order","words":["water.","should","a","You","of","drink","lot"],"answer":"You should drink a lot of water.","da":"Khassek tcherbi lma bzzaf."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Should I go to the doctor?","question_da":"Achmen jawab 9sir s7i7?","options":["Yes, you should.","Yes, you do.","Yes, you are.","Yes, you have."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"So2al b `Should I…?` → ljawab b `Yes, you should.` wla `No, you shouldn't.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"With \"he\" and \"she\" we say \"shoulds\": \"She shoulds rest.\"","statement_da":"M3a `he` w `she` kan9oulo `shoulds`: `She shoulds rest`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `should` ma kaytbeddelch: `She should rest.`, `He should rest.` — bhal `can`."},{"type":"translate","da":"3ndi rrwa7 w 7el9i kaydorrni.","answers":["I have a cold and a sore throat.","I've got a cold and a sore throat.","I have a cold and my throat hurts.","I have got a cold and a sore throat."],"hint_en":"I have a ... and a sore ...","explain_da":"`I have a cold` = 3ndi rrwa7. `a sore throat` = 7el9 kaydorr. Bjouj m3a `have`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Take one tablet twice a day.","da":"Khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar.","explain_da":"`Take` – `one` – `tablet` – `twice` – `a` – `day`. `twice` = jouj merrat."},{"type":"order","words":["medicine","meals.","Take","after","this"],"answer":"Take this medicine after meals.","da":"Khoudi had ddwa men ba3d lmakla."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I have a ___. My head hurts a lot.","answers":["headache","head ache"],"hint_da":"wja3 rras = head + ache","explain_da":"`headache` = `head` + `ache` (wja3). Kelma wa7da: `a headache`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Khassek trta7i w makhasskich tkhdmi lyouma.","answers":["You should rest and you shouldn't work today.","You should rest and shouldn't work today.","You should rest, and you shouldn't work today.","You should rest and you should not work today."],"hint_en":"You should ... and you shouldn't ... today.","explain_da":"`should` = khassek, `shouldn't` = makhasskich. Men ba3dhom l fi3l bla `to`: `should rest`, `shouldn't work`."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"How often should I take the syrup?","question_da":"Achmen jawab mnassb l had so2al f sseydaliya?","options":["Three times a day, after meals.","Three tablets, please.","In the pharmacy.","Because I have a cold."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`How often?` = ch7al men merra? → `three times a day` = tlata d lmerrat f nhar."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"I have a headache and I feel very tired.","da":"Rasi kaydorrni w 7assa b l3ya bzzaf.","pron":"aï hav a héd-éyk and aï fil vé-ri taï-eurd"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Omar's bad day","title_da":"Nhar khayb dyal Omar","emoji":"🤒","text_en":"Yesterday was a bad day for Omar. In the morning, he got up with a terrible headache and a sore throat. He didn't want to eat breakfast. \"What's the matter?\" his mother asked. \"I feel sick, Mum. My head hurts and I'm very cold,\" he said. His mother touched his head. \"You have a fever. You should go to the doctor.\" Omar went to the health centre near his house. The doctor looked at his throat and said: \"You have the flu. It's nothing serious, but you should stay in bed for three days. You shouldn't go to work and you shouldn't drink cold drinks.\" At the pharmacy, Omar bought some tablets and a syrup for his cough. The pharmacist said: \"Take one tablet three times a day, after meals.\" Today Omar feels a little better, but he is still tired. Get well soon, Omar!","text_da":"Lbare7 kan nhar khayb l Omar. F sbah, nad w rasso kaydorro bzzaf w 7el9o kaydorro. Mabghach yfter. \"Malek?\" sewlato mmo. \"7ass b rasi mrid, a mma. Rasi kaydorrni w fiya lberd bzzaf,\" 9al liha. Mmo 7attat yeddha 3la rasso. \"3ndek sskhana. Khassek tmchi 3nd tbib.\" Omar mcha l lmerkez ssi77i 9rib men daro. Tbib chaf 7el9o w 9al lih: \"3ndek lgrip. Ma kayn walou khatir, walakin khassek tb9a f lfrach tlat iyam. Makhassekch tmchi l lkhedma w makhassekch tcherb lmachroubat lbarda.\" F sseydaliya, Omar chra chi 7bob w sirou dyal lko77a. Sseydali 9al lih: \"Khoud 7abba wa7da tlata d lmerrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla.\" Lyouma Omar 7ass b rasso 7sen chwiya, walakin mazal 3yyan. Allah ychafik, a Omar!","glossary":[{"en":"got up","da":"nad (men nn3as)"},{"en":"terrible","da":"khayb bzzaf / 9wi"},{"en":"touched","da":"7attat yeddha 3la / 9asset"},{"en":"health centre","da":"lmerkez ssi77i"},{"en":"the flu","da":"lgrip"},{"en":"stay in bed","da":"b9a f lfrach"},{"en":"cough","da":"lko77a"},{"en":"pharmacist","da":"sseydali"},{"en":"still","da":"mazal"},{"en":"a little better","da":"7sen chwiya"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kan 3nd Omar f sbah?","options":["Wja3 rras w 7el9o kaydorro","Kerch kaddorro","Rejlo kaddorro","Wja3 ssnan"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`He got up with a terrible headache and a sore throat.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The doctor said Omar should go to work.","statement_da":"Tbib 9al l Omar khasso ymchi l lkhedma.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `You shouldn't go to work` = makhassekch tmchi l lkhedma."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men merra khasso yakhod l7abba?","options":["Tlata d lmerrat f nhar","Merra f nhar","Jouj merrat f nhar","Merra f ssimana"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Take one tablet three times a day, after meals.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach 7ass Omar lyouma?","options":["7sen chwiya, walakin mazal 3yyan","Mrid bzzaf, kter men lbare7","Labas tamaman","3ndo wja3 lkerch"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Today Omar feels a little better, but he is still tired.`"}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F sseydaliya","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar bin Laila w sseydali. Rekkzi 3la: chno kaydorr Laila? Chno 3taha sseydali? W ch7al men merra khassha takhdo?","lines":[{"speaker":"Pharmacist","en":"Good afternoon. Can I help you?","da":"Msa lkhir. Wach n9der n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, please. I have a cough and a sore throat. Do you have something for it?","da":"Ah, 3afak. 3ndi lko77a w 7el9i kaydorrni. Wach 3ndkom chi 7aja liha?"},{"speaker":"Pharmacist","en":"Do you have a fever?","da":"Wach 3ndek sskhana?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"No, I don't. But I feel very tired.","da":"La. Walakin 7assa b l3ya bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Pharmacist","en":"OK. This syrup is good for your cough. Take it three times a day, after meals.","da":"Wakha. Had ssirou mzyan l lko77a dyalek. Khoudih tlata d lmerrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Three times a day. And for my throat?","da":"Tlata d lmerrat f nhar. W l 7el9i?"},{"speaker":"Pharmacist","en":"These tablets. One tablet twice a day. And you should drink warm water with honey.","da":"Had l7bob. 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar. W khassek tcherbi lma dafi b l3sel."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Thank you. How much is it?","da":"Choukran. Ch7al ttaman?"},{"speaker":"Pharmacist","en":"Sixty-five dirhams, please. Get well soon!","da":"Khemsa w settin derhem, 3afak. Allah ychafik!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kaydorr Laila?","options":["Lko77a w l7el9","Rras w lkerch","Rrjel","Ddher"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I have a cough and a sore throat.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila has a fever.","statement_da":"Laila 3ndha sskhana.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `No, I don't.` — ma 3ndhach sskhana, walakin 3yyana."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Take it three times a day, after meals.","question_da":"Sem3i. Ch7al men merra, w fo9ach?","options":["Tlata d lmerrat f nhar, men ba3d lmakla","Jouj merrat f nhar, 9bel lmakla","Merra f nhar, f lil","Tlata d lmerrat f ssimana"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`three times a day` = tlata d lmerrat f nhar. `after meals` = men ba3d lmakla."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al khellsat Laila?","options":["65 derhem","56 derhem","75 derhem","25 derhem"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Sixty-five dirhams` = 65 derhem. (Rdi lbal: `sixty` = 60, `sixteen` = 16!)"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What's the matter?","da":"Malek?","pron":"wats the ma-teur"},{"target_en":"I have a headache.","da":"Rasi kaydorrni.","pron":"aï hav a héd-éyk"},{"target_en":"My stomach hurts.","da":"Kerchi kaddorrni.","pron":"maï steu-meuk heurts"},{"target_en":"I feel sick and tired.","da":"7assa b rasi mrida w 3yyana.","pron":"aï fil sik and taï-eurd"},{"target_en":"You should rest and drink water.","da":"Khassek trta7i w tcherbi lma.","pron":"you choud rést and drink wo-teur"},{"target_en":"Take one tablet twice a day.","da":"Khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar.","pron":"téyk wan tab-lit twaïs a déy"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"3nd tbib","context_da":"Nti mrida w mchiti 3nd tbib. Howa ghadi ysewlek. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning. What's the matter?","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir. Malek?","expect_keywords":["i have","hurts","hurt","i feel","headache","cold","throat","fever","stomach","sick","tired","cough"],"sample_en":"I have a headache and a sore throat."},{"bot_en":"I see. Do you have a fever?","bot_da":"Fhemt. Wach 3ndek sskhana?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i think","i don't","a little"],"sample_en":"Yes, I think so."},{"bot_en":"How do you feel today?","bot_da":"Kifach 7assa lyouma?","expect_keywords":["tired","sick","bad","not well","not good","terrible","weak","better","i feel"],"sample_en":"I feel very tired."},{"bot_en":"You have a cold. You should rest and drink water. Do you have any questions?","bot_da":"3ndek rrwa7. Khassek trta7i w tcherbi lma. Wach 3ndek chi so2al?","expect_keywords":["should i","medicine","tablets","tablet","how many","how often","no","thank","work"],"sample_en":"Should I take any medicine?"},{"bot_en":"Yes, take one tablet twice a day. Get well soon!","bot_da":"Ah, khoudi 7abba wa7da jouj merrat f nhar. Allah ychafik!","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","ok","okay","goodbye","bye","twice"],"sample_en":"Thank you, doctor. Goodbye!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Message l sa7btek lmrida","prompt_da":"Sa7btek Sarah mrida: 3ndha rrwa7 w sskhana. Ktbi liha message b lingliziya: sewliha kifach 7assa, 9oli liha `I'm sorry…`, 3tiha 3 nasa2i7 b `should` / `shouldn't`, w sali b `Get well soon!`.","helper_en":["Hi Sarah, how do you feel today?","I'm sorry you have a cold.","You should ...","You shouldn't ...","Get well soon!"],"min_words":40,"keywords":["should","soon"],"model_en":"Hi Sarah, how do you feel today? I'm sorry you have a cold and a fever. You should stay in bed and rest. You should drink a lot of warm water with lemon and honey. You shouldn't go to work tomorrow, and you shouldn't drink cold drinks. If you still feel sick on Monday, you should see a doctor. Do you need anything from the pharmacy? I can bring it to you. Get well soon! Nouha"}},{"id":"l19","order":19,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"🔮","title_en":"Plans: going to & will","title_da":"Lmokhattat: going to / will","goals_da":["Thedri 3la lmokhattat dyalek b `be going to`: `I'm going to visit my aunt.`","Tsta3mli `will` l 9arar f nefs lle7da, l 3ard dyal lmosa3ada w l lwa3d: `I'll help you.`","Ttwe99e3i lmosta9bal: `It will rain tomorrow.` / `It won't be cold.`","Tsewli w tjawbi: `What are you going to do this weekend?`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"be going to — lmokhattat (plans)","body_da":"Melli 3ndna mokhattat (`a plan`), chi 7aja 9errernaha 9bel, kansta3mlo `be going to` + l fi3l. Had l9a3ida sahla bzzaf 7it bhal darija b ddebt: \"**ghadi** n9ra\" = `I'm **going to** study`. L fi3l `go` = mcha, w `going` = ghadi!\n\nLbina: `am` / `is` / `are` + `going to` + l fi3l (kat3rfi `am/is/are` + `-ing` men dars 13):\n\n- `I'm going to visit my aunt.` = Ghadi nzour khalti.\n- `She's going to buy a new phone.` = Ghadi tchri portable jdid.\n- `We're going to travel to Agadir.` = Ghadi nsafro l Agadir.\n- `They're going to get married in July.` = Ghadi ytzewjo f yolyouz.\n\nNnafy: `not` men ba3d `am/is/are`: `I'm not going to work tomorrow.` = Ma ghadich nkhdem ghedda.\n\nSo2al: n9elbo `am/is/are` m3a lfa3il: `Are you going to stay at home?` = Wach ghadi tb9ay f ddar? — `Yes, I am.` / `No, I'm not.` W b `What`: `What are you going to do this weekend?` = Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?","examples":[{"en":"I'm going to visit my grandmother on Friday.","da":"Ghadi nzour jeddti nhar jjem3a.","pron":"aïm go-ing tou vi-zit maï grand-meu-theur on fraï-déy"},{"en":"He's going to study English in London.","da":"Ghadi y9ra lingliziya f London.","pron":"hiz go-ing tou steu-di in-glich in leun-deun"},{"en":"We're not going to go out tonight.","da":"Ma ghadich nkhorjo had lila.","pron":"wir not go-ing tou go awt tou-naït"},{"en":"Are you going to cook couscous on Friday?","da":"Wach ghadi ttiybi lkesksou nhar jjem3a?","pron":"ar you go-ing tou kouk kous-kous on fraï-déy"},{"en":"What are you going to do this weekend?","da":"Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?","pron":"wat ar you go-ing tou dou this wik-énd"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"will — 9arar f nefs lle7da, 3ard, w wa3d","body_da":"`will` + l fi3l kansta3mlouh melli kan9errro **f nefs lle7da**, machi 9bel. `will` ma kaytbeddelch m3a `he/she` (bhal `can` w `should`), w f lhadra kan9essrouh: `I'll`, `you'll`, `he'll`, `she'll`, `we'll`, `they'll`.\n\n- **9arar daba:** Ttilifoun kaysonni → `I'll get it!` = Ana njaweb! / F l9ehwa: `I'll have a mint tea, please.` = Ghadi nakhod atay, 3afak.\n- **3ard dyal lmosa3ada:** `I'll help you with the bags.` = Ghadi n3awnek thezzi l9fef. / `I'll carry it.` = Ana nhezzo.\n- **Wa3d:** `I'll call you tonight, I promise.` = Ghadi n3eyyet lik had lila, wa3d. / `I won't be late.` = Ma ghadich nt3ettel.\n\nNnafy: `will not` = `won't` (nte9ha: wont): `I won't tell anyone.` = Ma ghadich n9oul l 7ed.\n\nLfar9 m3a `going to`: `I'm going to call Sarah tonight.` (9errert 9bel = mokhattat) / Sarah 3eyytat daba w mafta7tich: `I'll call her later!` (9errert daba, f nefs lle7da).","examples":[{"en":"The phone is ringing. I'll get it!","da":"Ttilifoun kaysonni. Ana njaweb!","pron":"the fon iz rin-guing. aïl guét it"},{"en":"Don't worry, I'll help you.","da":"Matkhafich, ghadi n3awnek.","pron":"dont weu-ri, aïl hélp you"},{"en":"I'll call you tonight, I promise.","da":"Ghadi n3eyyet lik had lila, wa3d.","pron":"aïl kol you tou-naït, aï pro-mis"},{"en":"I won't be late.","da":"Ma ghadich nt3ettel.","pron":"aï wont bi léyt"},{"en":"It's hot in here. I'll open the window.","da":"Sskhana hna. Ghadi n7el cherjem.","pron":"its hot in hir. aïl o-peun the win-do"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"will — tawa99o3 (predictions): It will rain tomorrow","body_da":"Kansta3mlo `will` 7ta melli kan**twe99e3o** lmosta9bal (chno kandenno ghadi yw9e3), khossosan m3a `I think` (kandenn) w `I'm sure` (ana mt2ekkda):\n\n- `It will rain tomorrow.` = Ghadi ttih chta ghedda.\n- `I think Morocco will win the match.` = Kandenn lmeghrib ghadi yrbe7 lmatch.\n- `You'll love Marrakech!` = Ghadi t3jbek Marrakech!\n- `She'll be a great doctor.` = Ghadi tkoun tbiba kbira.\n\nSo2al: `Will it rain tomorrow?` = Wach ghadi ttih chta ghedda? — `Yes, it will.` / `No, it won't.`\n\nMelli kanchoufo chi 3alama 9eddamna daba, kansta3mlo `going to`: `Look at the clouds! It's going to rain.` = Chofi ss7ab! Ghadi ttih chta. (kanchoufo ss7ab daba, lmosta9bal bayn).\n\nMachi mochkil ila khlatti bin `will` w `going to` f ttawa99o3 — bjouj kayfehmouk. Lmohim: ma tsta3mlich `will` l mokhattat 9errertihom 9bel.","examples":[{"en":"I think it will be sunny tomorrow.","da":"Kandenn ghadi tkoun chems ghedda.","pron":"aï think it wil bi seu-ni tou-mo-ro"},{"en":"You'll love this restaurant!","da":"Ghadi y3jbek had rristora!","pron":"youl leuv this rés-teu-ront"},{"en":"Will you be at home tonight? — Yes, I will.","da":"Wach ghadi tkouni f ddar had lila? — Ah.","pron":"wil you bi at hom tou-naït? yès, aï wil"},{"en":"Look at the clouds! It's going to rain.","da":"Chofi ss7ab! Ghadi ttih chta.","pron":"louk at the klawdz. its go-ing tou réyn"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kelmat lwa9t dyal lmosta9bal","body_da":"Had lkelmat kaybeyno lwa9t f lmosta9bal. Kayjiw f l'akhir dyal ljomla (wla f lbdaya):\n\n- `tomorrow` = ghedda; `tomorrow morning` = ghedda f sbah\n- `tonight` = had lila / lyouma f lil\n- `this weekend` = had lweekend; `this summer` = had sseif\n- `next week` = ssimana jjaya; `next month` = chher jjay; `next year` = l3am jjay\n- `soon` = 9rib; `later` = men ba3d\n- `in two days` = men ba3d yomayn; `on Friday` = nhar jjem3a; `at 8 o'clock` = f tmenya\n\nRdi lbal: m3a `next` w `this` ma kanzidouch `on` wla `in`: `next week` (machi \"on next week\"), `this weekend`. Bhal darija: \"ssimana jjaya\" bla \"f\".\n\nSo2al lmohim dyal had dars: `What are you going to do this weekend?` — jawbi: `I'm going to…` wla `I don't know yet.` (= mazal ma3reftch) wla `Nothing special.` (= walou khass).","examples":[{"en":"I'm going to see the doctor tomorrow morning.","da":"Ghadi nchouf tbib ghedda f sbah.","pron":"aïm go-ing tou si the dok-teur tou-mo-ro mor-ning"},{"en":"They're going to get married next month.","da":"Ghadi ytzewjo chher jjay.","pron":"thér go-ing tou guét ma-rid nékst meunth"},{"en":"See you soon!","da":"Nchoufouk 9rib!","pron":"si you soun"},{"en":"What are you going to do tonight? — Nothing special.","da":"Chno ghadi tdiri had lila? — Walou khass.","pron":"wat ar you go-ing tou dou tou-naït? neu-thing spé-cheul"},{"en":"I'll finish this work in two days.","da":"Ghadi nkemmel had lkhedma men ba3d yomayn.","pron":"aïl fi-nich this weurk in tou déyz"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"tomorrow","da":"ghedda","emoji":"📅","pron":"tou-mo-ro","example_en":"See you tomorrow!","example_da":"Nchoufouk ghedda!"},{"en":"tonight","da":"had lila","emoji":"🌙","pron":"tou-naït","example_en":"I'll call you tonight.","example_da":"Ghadi n3eyyet lik had lila."},{"en":"this weekend","da":"had lweekend","emoji":"🎉","pron":"this wik-énd","example_en":"What are you going to do this weekend?","example_da":"Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?"},{"en":"next week","da":"ssimana jjaya","emoji":"📆","pron":"nékst wik","example_en":"I'm going to start a new job next week.","example_da":"Ghadi nbda khedma jdida ssimana jjaya."},{"en":"next month","da":"chher jjay","emoji":"🗓️","pron":"nékst meunth","example_en":"They're going to get married next month.","example_da":"Ghadi ytzewjo chher jjay."},{"en":"soon","da":"9rib","emoji":"⏳","pron":"soun","example_en":"I'll be home soon.","example_da":"Ghadi nkoun f ddar 9rib."},{"en":"plan","da":"mokhattat / bernamej","emoji":"📝","pron":"plan","example_en":"Do you have any plans for Sunday?","example_da":"Wach 3ndek chi bernamej l nhar l7edd?"},{"en":"visit","da":"zar (ghadi nzour)","emoji":"🏡","pron":"vi-zit","example_en":"We're going to visit my uncle.","example_da":"Ghadi nzouro 3emmi."},{"en":"travel","da":"safer","emoji":"✈️","pron":"tra-veul","example_en":"She's going to travel to Spain.","example_da":"Ghadi tsafer l Sbanya."},{"en":"stay","da":"b9a","emoji":"🏠","pron":"stéy","example_en":"I'm going to stay at home tonight.","example_da":"Ghadi nb9a f ddar had lila."},{"en":"rain","da":"chta (kattih)","emoji":"🌧️","pron":"réyn","example_en":"It will rain tomorrow.","example_da":"Ghadi ttih chta ghedda."},{"en":"help","da":"3awen","emoji":"🤲","pron":"hélp","example_en":"I'll help you with the bags.","example_da":"Ghadi n3awnek thezzi l9fef."},{"en":"call","da":"3eyyet (f ttilifoun)","emoji":"📞","pron":"kol","example_en":"Call me when you arrive.","example_da":"3eyyet liya melli twesli."},{"en":"promise","da":"wa3d / wa3ed","emoji":"🤞","pron":"pro-mis","example_en":"I promise I won't be late.","example_da":"Kanwa3dek ma ghadich nt3ettel."},{"en":"wedding","da":"l3ers","emoji":"💍","pron":"wé-ding","example_en":"The wedding is next Saturday.","example_da":"L3ers ssebt jjay."},{"en":"party","da":"7efla","emoji":"🎈","pron":"par-ti","example_en":"Are you going to come to the party?","example_da":"Wach ghadi tji l l7efla?"}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?","context_da":"Nhar lkhmis f l9ehwa. Sarah katsewwel Nouha 3la lmokhattat dyalha l lweekend.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hi Nouha! What are you going to do this weekend?","da":"Ahlan Nouha! Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm going to visit my family in Fes. My cousin's wedding is on Saturday.","da":"Ghadi nzour l3a2ila dyali f Fes. L3ers dyal bent khalti nhar ssebt."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Oh, nice! Are you going to take the train?","da":"Wah, zwin! Wach ghadi takhdi ttran?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, I'm not. I'm going to go by bus with my sister. It's cheaper.","da":"La. Ghadi nmchi b lkar m3a khti. Rkhes."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"What's the weather going to be like in Fes?","da":"Kifach ghadi ykoun ljow f Fes?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I think it will be hot. And you? What are your plans?","da":"Kandenn ghadi tkoun sskhana. W nti? Chno lbernamej dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nothing special. I'm going to stay at home and study. Oh no, it's late! I have a class at five.","da":"Walou khass. Ghadi nb9a f ddar w n9ra. Wah la, t3ettelt! 3ndi 7essa f lkhemsa."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Don't worry, I'll drive you there.","da":"Matkhafich, ghadi nwesslek b tomobil."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Thank you, Nouha! Have a great weekend, and bring me some sweets from Fes!","da":"Choukran, Nouha! Weekend sa3id, w jibi liya chi 7elwa men Fes!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I will, I promise!","da":"Ghadi njib, wa3d!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"`going to` = mokhattat 9errertih 9bel (bhal \"ghadi\" f darija). `will` = 9arar f nefs lle7da, 3ard wla wa3d. F lhadra ssari3a, l'ingliz kay9oulo `gonna` bdal `going to` (`I'm gonna go`) — fehmiha melli tsem3iha, walakin ma tktbihach. W tfekkri: men ba3d `will` w `going to`, l fi3l kayb9a bhal ma howa: `she will go`, `she's going to go` (bla `-s`, bla `-ing`)."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"ghedda\" b lingliziya?","options":["tomorrow","tonight","yesterday","soon"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`tomorrow` = ghedda. `tonight` = had lila. `yesterday` = lbare7. `soon` = 9rib."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I'm going to visit my aunt this weekend.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Ghadi nzour khalti had lweekend","Zert khalti lweekend li fat","Kanzour khalti kol weekend","Ghadi nzour jeddti ghedda"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm going to visit` = ghadi nzour (mosta9bal, mokhattat). `my aunt` = khalti / 3emmti. `this weekend` = had lweekend."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"She ___ going to buy a new phone.","options":["is","am","are"],"answer":"is","hint_da":"`She` → ?","explain_da":"M3a `she` kansta3mlo `is`: `She is going to…` / `She's going to…`"},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli kelmat lwa9t b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"tomorrow","da":"ghedda","emoji":"📅"},{"en":"tonight","da":"had lila","emoji":"🌙"},{"en":"next week","da":"ssimana jjaya","emoji":"📆"},{"en":"soon","da":"9rib","emoji":"⏳"},{"en":"this weekend","da":"had lweekend","emoji":"🎉"}]},{"type":"order","words":["going","tomorrow?","What","do","you","to","are"],"answer":"What are you going to do tomorrow?","da":"Chno ghadi tdiri ghedda?"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ttilifoun kaysonni daba. 9errerti f nefs lle7da bach tjawbi. Chno kat9oli?","options":["I'll get it!","I'm going to get it!","I will to get it!","I getting it!"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"9arar f nefs lle7da → `will`: `I'll get it!` = ana njaweb! `going to` dyal mokhattat 9errertih 9bel. `will to` w `I getting` ghalat."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Don't worry, I'll help you.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 9al lik?","options":["Matkhafich, ghadi n3awnek","Sme7 liya, ma ghadich n3awnek","3awnni, 3afak","Ghadi n3eyyet lik ghedda"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Don't worry` = matkhafich. `I'll help you` = ghadi n3awnek (3ard dyal lmosa3ada b `will`)."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Won't\" means \"will not\".","statement_da":"`won't` kat3ni `will not`.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `will not` → `won't` (nte9ha: wont). `I won't be late.` = ma ghadich nt3ettel."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Look at the clouds! It ___ rain.","options":["is going to","will to","going to"],"answer":"is going to","hint_da":"Kanchoufo ss7ab daba → ?","explain_da":"Melli kanchoufo chi 3alama daba, kansta3mlo `be going to`: `It is going to rain.` `will to` ghalat, w `going to` bo7dha bla `is` ghalat."},{"type":"translate","da":"Ghadi nsafer l Agadir ssimana jjaya.","answers":["I'm going to travel to Agadir next week.","I am going to travel to Agadir next week.","I'm going to go to Agadir next week.","I am going to go to Agadir next week."],"hint_en":"I'm going to ... to Agadir ... week.","explain_da":"Mokhattat → `I'm going to travel`. `next week` = ssimana jjaya (bla `in` wla `on`)."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"I'll call you tonight.","da":"Ghadi n3eyyet lik had lila.","explain_da":"`I'll` = `I will` (m9essra). `call` = 3eyyet. `tonight` = had lila."},{"type":"order","words":["stay","Are","to","home?","going","at","you"],"answer":"Are you going to stay at home?","da":"Wach ghadi tb9ay f ddar?"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"Are they going to come to the wedding?","question_da":"Achmen jawab 9sir s7i7?","options":["Yes, they are.","Yes, they is.","Yes, they going.","Yes, they do."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"So2al b `Are they going to…?` → ljawab 9sir b `are`: `Yes, they are.` / `No, they aren't.`"},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Don't worry, I ___ forget your birthday. I promise!","answers":["won't","will not","wont"],"hint_da":"Nnafy dyal `will` (ma ghadich nensa).","explain_da":"`I won't forget` = ma ghadich nensa. `won't` = `will not`. Wa3d → `will`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Ghadi ttih chta ghedda.","answers":["It will rain tomorrow.","It'll rain tomorrow.","It is going to rain tomorrow.","It's going to rain tomorrow."],"hint_en":"It ... rain tomorrow.","explain_da":"Tawa99o3 → `It will rain tomorrow.` (7ta `It's going to rain tomorrow.` s7i7a). `rain` = chta (kattih)."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"This weekend I'm going to visit my family in Fes.","da":"Had lweekend ghadi nzour l3a2ila dyali f Fes.","pron":"this wik-énd aïm go-ing tou vi-zit maï fa-mi-li in fés"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Nouha's summer plans","title_da":"Lmokhattat dyal Nouha l sseif","emoji":"☀️","text_en":"Summer is coming, and Nouha has a lot of plans. In July, she is going to visit her grandmother in Agadir with her sister. They are going to stay there for two weeks. \"We're going to swim every morning and eat fish every day!\" she says. Her grandmother is seventy-five, so Nouha is going to help her in the kitchen and in the garden. In August, Nouha is going to go to her cousin's wedding in Fes. She isn't going to buy a new dress; she is going to wear her blue caftan. After the wedding, she is going to start a new English course online. \"I think it will be difficult, but I'll study every evening,\" she says. \"And next year, I'll travel to London. I promise!\" What about the weather? Nouha is sure: \"It will be very hot in Agadir, but I won't stay inside!\"","text_da":"Sseif 9rib, w Nouha 3ndha bzzaf dyal lmokhattat. F yolyouz, ghadi tzour jeddtha f Agadir m3a khtha. Ghadi yb9aw temma jouj simanat. \"Ghadi n3oumo kol sbah w nakolo l7out kol nhar!\" kat9oul. Jeddtha 3ndha khemsa w seb3in 3am, dakchi 3lach Nouha ghadi t3awnha f lkouzina w f jjerda. F ghocht, Nouha ghadi tmchi l 3ers bent khalha f Fes. Ma ghadich tchri keswa jdida; ghadi tlbes l9eftan zzre9 dyalha. Men ba3d l3ers, ghadi tbda dawra jdida dyal lingliziya 3la l'internet. \"Kandenn ghadi tkoun s3iba, walakin ghadi n9ra kol 3chiya,\" kat9oul. \"W l3am jjay, ghadi nsafer l London. Wa3d!\" W ljow? Nouha mt2ekkda: \"Ghadi tkoun sskhana bzzaf f Agadir, walakin ma ghadich nb9a ldakhel!\"","glossary":[{"en":"is coming","da":"jay / 9rib"},{"en":"plans","da":"mokhattat"},{"en":"swim","da":"3am (kan3oum)"},{"en":"wedding","da":"l3ers"},{"en":"dress","da":"keswa"},{"en":"wear","da":"lbes"},{"en":"online","da":"3la l'internet"},{"en":"difficult","da":"s3ib / s3iba"},{"en":"inside","da":"ldakhel"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin ghadi tmchi Nouha f yolyouz?","options":["L Agadir, 3nd jeddtha","L Fes, l l3ers","L London","L Casa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`In July, she is going to visit her grandmother in Agadir.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha is going to buy a new dress for the wedding.","statement_da":"Nouha ghadi tchri keswa jdida l l3ers.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `She isn't going to buy a new dress` — ghadi tlbes l9eftan zzre9 dyalha."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno ghadi tdir Nouha men ba3d l3ers?","options":["Ghadi tbda dawra dyal lingliziya 3la l'internet","Ghadi tsafer l London","Ghadi tkhdem f Agadir","Ghadi tchri keswa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`After the wedding, she is going to start a new English course online.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kat9oul Nouha 3la ljow f Agadir?","options":["Ghadi tkoun sskhana bzzaf","Ghadi ttih chta","Ghadi ykoun lberd","Ma3arfach"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`It will be very hot in Agadir.`"}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Lmokhattat dyal lweekend","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i Omar w Laila. Rekkzi 3la: chno ghadi ydir Omar nhar ssebt? W chno ghadi tdir Laila nhar l7edd?","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Laila, what are you going to do this weekend?","da":"Laila, chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"On Saturday, I'm going to clean the house and cook for my parents. And you?","da":"Nhar ssebt, ghadi nne99i ddar w ntiyeb l waldiya. W nta?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I'm going to play football with my friends on Saturday morning. In the afternoon, I'm going to watch the match at a café.","da":"Ghadi nl3eb lkoura m3a s7abi ssebt f sbah. F l3chiya, ghadi ntferrej f lmatch f l9ehwa."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Who do you think will win?","da":"Chkoun kaddenn ghadi yrbe7?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Raja will win, I'm sure! And on Sunday? Any plans?","da":"Rraja ghadi trbe7, ana mt2ekked! W nhar l7edd? Chi bernamej?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Yes, I'm going to visit my grandmother in Mohammedia. She's not very well.","da":"Ah, ghadi nzour jeddti f lmo7ammadiya. Machi labas bzzaf."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I'm sorry to hear that. I'll drive you there if you want.","da":"Ana mt2essef. Ghadi nwesslek b tomobil ila bghiti."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Really? Thank you, Omar! I'll call you on Sunday morning.","da":"Bsse7? Choukran, Omar! Ghadi n3eyyet lik l7edd f sbah."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"OK. See you on Sunday!","da":"Wakha. Nchoufouk nhar l7edd!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno ghadi ydir Omar nhar ssebt f sbah?","options":["Ghadi yl3eb lkoura","Ghadi yne99i ddar","Ghadi yzour jeddto","Ghadi ytferrej f lmatch"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm going to play football with my friends on Saturday morning.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila is going to visit her grandmother on Saturday.","statement_da":"Laila ghadi tzour jeddtha nhar ssebt.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: nhar l7edd (`on Sunday`), machi ssebt."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I'll drive you there if you want.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 3red Omar 3la Laila?","options":["Ghadi ywesselha b tomobil","Ghadi y3eyyet liha","Ghadi yzour jeddtha bo7do","Ghadi ychri liha tomobil"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'll drive you there` = ghadi nwesslek b tomobil (3ard b `will`). `if you want` = ila bghiti."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chkoun kaddenn Omar ghadi yrbe7 lmatch?","options":["Rraja","Lwidad","Lmeghrib","Ma3arfch"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Raja will win, I'm sure!` — tawa99o3 b `will`."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What are you going to do this weekend?","da":"Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?","pron":"wat ar you go-ing tou dou this wik-énd"},{"target_en":"I'm going to visit my grandmother.","da":"Ghadi nzour jeddti.","pron":"aïm go-ing tou vi-zit maï grand-meu-theur"},{"target_en":"I'll help you with the bags.","da":"Ghadi n3awnek thezzi l9fef.","pron":"aïl hélp you with the bagz"},{"target_en":"It will be sunny tomorrow.","da":"Ghadi tkoun chems ghedda.","pron":"it wil bi seu-ni tou-mo-ro"},{"target_en":"I won't be late, I promise.","da":"Ma ghadich nt3ettel, wa3d.","pron":"aï wont bi léyt, aï pro-mis"},{"target_en":"See you next week!","da":"Nchoufouk ssimana jjaya!","pron":"si you nékst wik"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Sarah katsewlek 3la lmokhattat dyalek","context_da":"Sa7btek Sarah 3eyytat lik. Katsewlek 3la lweekend w 3la lmokhattat dyalek. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! What are you going to do this weekend?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Chno ghadi tdiri had lweekend?","expect_keywords":["going to","gonna","i'm going","i am going","visit","stay","nothing special","don't know"],"sample_en":"I'm going to visit my family."},{"bot_en":"Nice! Are you going to travel by train or by bus?","bot_da":"Zwin! Wach ghadi tsafri b ttran wla b lkar?","expect_keywords":["train","bus","car","taxi","going to","i'm not"],"sample_en":"I'm going to take the train."},{"bot_en":"What's the weather going to be like?","bot_da":"Kifach ghadi ykoun ljow?","expect_keywords":["sunny","hot","cold","rain","will","going to be","nice","windy","cloudy","i think"],"sample_en":"I think it will be sunny."},{"bot_en":"I need some help with my English homework tomorrow...","bot_da":"M7taja chi mosa3ada f lwajib dyal lingliziya ghedda…","expect_keywords":["i'll help","i will help","help you","don't worry","no problem","of course","sure"],"sample_en":"Don't worry, I'll help you tomorrow."},{"bot_en":"Thank you! Will you call me tonight?","bot_da":"Choukran! Wach ghadi t3eyti liya had lila?","expect_keywords":["yes","i will","i'll call","sure","of course","promise"],"sample_en":"Yes, I will. I promise!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Lmokhattat dyali","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal 3la lmokhattat dyalek l ssimana jjaya wla l had lweekend: chno ghadi tdiri, m3a men, w fo9ach. Sta3mli `going to` l lmokhattat, w zidi jomla wa7da 3la l'a9all b `will` (wa3d wla tawa99o3).","helper_en":["Next week I'm going to ...","On Saturday, my friend and I are going to ...","I'm not going to ...","I think it will be ...","I'll ..., I promise!"],"min_words":40,"keywords":["going to","will"],"model_en":"Next week I'm going to be very busy. On Monday, I'm going to start a new English course in the evening. On Wednesday, my sister and I are going to visit our aunt in Mohammedia. This weekend, we're going to go to a wedding in Fes. I'm not going to buy a new dress; I'm going to wear my caftan. I think the weather will be hot. I'll take lots of photos, I promise!"}},{"id":"l20","order":20,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"⚖️","title_en":"Comparatives & superlatives","title_da":"Lmo9arana: bigger, the biggest","goals_da":["T9arni bin jouj 7wayj: `Casablanca is bigger than Rabat.`","T9oli l'a7san wla l'akbar f majmou3a: `the biggest`, `the most expensive`","T7efdi lkelmat li makaytbb3ouch l9a3ida: `better`, `worse`, `further`","Tsta3mli `than` w `as … as`: `The bus is not as fast as the train.`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ssifat l9sira: bigger, the biggest","body_da":"Bach n9arno (`compare`) bin jouj 7wayj, kanzido `-er` l ssifa (`adjective` = lkelma li katwsef, bhal `big`, `small`) w men ba3dha `than` (= men):\n\n- `big` → `bigger than` (kber men): `Casablanca is bigger than Rabat.` = Casa kber men Rabat.\n- `small` → `smaller`, `cheap` → `cheaper` (rkhes), `old` → `older` (9dem), `young` → `younger` (sgher f l3mer), `tall` → `taller` (twel), `fast` → `faster` (sra3), `cold` → `colder` (bred)\n\nBach n9oulo l'akbar f majmou3a (`superlative`), kanzido `the … -est`:\n\n- `the biggest` (l'akbar / kber wa7ed): `Casablanca is the biggest city in Morocco.` = Casa hiya akbar mdina f lmeghrib.\n- `the cheapest`, `the oldest`, `the tallest`, `the fastest`\n\n**Lktaba:**\n\n- ssifa 9sira kattsali b 7arf wa7ed men ba3d 7arf 3illa (a, e, i, o, u) → kan3awdo l7arf l'akhir: `big` → `bigger` → `the biggest`, `hot` → `hotter` → `the hottest`, `thin` → `thinner`\n- kattsali b `-e` → kanzido ghir `-r` / `-st`: `nice` → `nicer` → `the nicest`, `large` → `larger`\n- kattsali b `-y` → `-y` katwelli `-i`: `easy` → `easier` → `the easiest`, `happy` → `happier`, `busy` → `busier`\n\nF darija 3ndna chi 7aja bhal hadi: kbir → **kber** men, rkhis → **rkhes** men, 9dim → **9dem** men. F lingliziya, l9a3ida wa7da l kolchi: `-er` + `than`.","examples":[{"en":"Casablanca is bigger than Rabat.","da":"Casa kber men Rabat.","pron":"ka-sa-blan-ka iz bi-geur than ra-bat"},{"en":"This bag is cheaper than that one.","da":"Had ssak rkhes men hadak.","pron":"this bag iz tchi-peur than that wan"},{"en":"Marrakech is hotter than Tangier in summer.","da":"Marrakech skhona kter men Tanja f sseif.","pron":"ma-ra-kéch iz ho-teur than tan-djir in seu-meur"},{"en":"This exercise is easier than the first one.","da":"Had ttamrin shel men l'awwal.","pron":"this ék-seur-saïz iz i-zi-eur than the feurst wan"},{"en":"My brother is the tallest in the family.","da":"Khouya howa twel wa7ed f l3a2ila.","pron":"maï breu-theur iz the to-list in the fa-mi-li"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Ssifat ttwila: more / the most","body_da":"Ila kanet ssifa twila (jouj ma9ati3 wla kter, bhal `expensive`: ik-spén-siv, 3ndha 3 ma9ati3), **ma** kanzidouch `-er`. Kanzido `more` 9belha:\n\n- `expensive` → `more expensive than` (ghla men): `The train is more expensive than the bus.`\n- `beautiful` → `more beautiful` (zwen men), `interesting` → `more interesting` (momti3 kter), `difficult` → `more difficult` (s3eb men), `important` → `more important` (mohim kter), `comfortable` → `more comfortable` (mrye7 kter)\n\nW l superlative: `the most` + ssifa:\n\n- `the most expensive` (l'aghla / ghla wa7ed): `This is the most expensive hotel in Agadir.`\n- `the most beautiful`, `the most interesting`, `the most difficult`\n\nNasi7a bach t3erfi: ssifa 9sira (`big`, `hot`, `old`) → `-er` / `-est`. Ssifa twila (`expensive`, `beautiful`) → `more` / `the most`. W ma tkhelltich bjouj: \"more bigger\" ghalat!","examples":[{"en":"The train is more expensive than the bus.","da":"Ttran ghla men lkar.","pron":"the tréyn iz mor ik-spén-siv than the beus"},{"en":"For me, Fes is more interesting than Casablanca.","da":"Bnnesba liya, Fes momti3a kter men Casa.","pron":"for mi, fés iz mor in-tris-ting than ka-sa-blan-ka"},{"en":"English is more difficult than Darija for me.","da":"Lingliziya s3eb men ddarija bnnesba liya.","pron":"in-glich iz mor di-fi-keult than da-ri-ja for mi"},{"en":"This is the most beautiful beach in Morocco.","da":"Hadi hiya a7san plaj f lmeghrib.","pron":"this iz the most biou-ti-foul bi-tch in mo-ro-ko"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Li makaytbb3ouch l9a3ida: better, worse, further","body_da":"Chi ssifat 9lal makaytbb3ouch l9a3ida — khassek t7efdihom b l9elb (bhal l'af3al li machi 3adiya f dars 16):\n\n- `good` (mzyan) → `better` (7sen) → `the best` (l'a7san / 7sen wa7ed)\n- `bad` (khayb) → `worse` (khyeb) → `the worst` (l'akhyeb)\n- `far` (b3id) → `further` (b3ed) → `the furthest` (l'ab3ad)\n- `much` / `many` (bzzaf) → `more` (kter) → `the most`\n- `little` (chwiya) → `less` (9ell) → `the least`\n\nMat9oulich \"gooder\" wla \"more good\"! `better` kat3rfiha déja men `I feel better` (dars 18).\n\n- `Mint tea is better than coffee.` = Atay 7sen men l9ehwa.\n- `My English is better now.` = Lingliziya dyali 7sen daba.\n- `This is the worst restaurant in town!` = Hada akhyeb rristora f lmdina!\n- `Agadir is further than Marrakech.` = Agadir b3ed men Marrakech.","examples":[{"en":"Mint tea is better than coffee.","da":"Atay 7sen men l9ehwa.","pron":"mint ti iz bé-teur than ko-fi"},{"en":"Couscous is the best dish in Morocco.","da":"Lkesksou howa a7san makla f lmeghrib.","pron":"kous-kous iz the bést dich in mo-ro-ko"},{"en":"The traffic in Casablanca is worse than in Rabat.","da":"Zz7am f Casa khyeb men Rabat.","pron":"the tra-fik in ka-sa-blan-ka iz weurs than in ra-bat"},{"en":"Monday is the worst day of the week!","da":"Ttnin howa akhyeb nhar f ssimana!","pron":"meun-déy iz the weurst déy ov the wik"},{"en":"Agadir is further from Casablanca than Marrakech.","da":"Agadir b3ed 3la Casa men Marrakech.","pron":"a-ga-dir iz feur-theur from ka-sa-blan-ka than ma-ra-kéch"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"than / as … as — kifach n9arno","body_da":"**`than`** (= men) kayji dima men ba3d lmo9aran: `bigger than`, `more expensive than`, `better than`. Rdi lbal l lktaba: `than` (b `a`), machi `then` (= men ba3d).\n\nMelli kan9arno m3a `me`, `him`, `her`: `She is taller than me.` = Hiya twel menni.\n\n**`as … as`** (= bhal / 9edd) melli jouj 7wayj metsawyin:\n\n- `Rabat is as beautiful as Casablanca.` = Rabat zwina bhal Casa.\n- `This bag is as cheap as that one.` = Had ssak rkhis bhal hadak.\n\n**`not as … as`** (= machi … bhal) melli l'awwal 9ell men ttani:\n\n- `The bus is not as fast as the train.` = Lkar machi sri3 bhal ttran. (ya3ni ttran sra3)\n- `Rabat is not as big as Casablanca.` = Rabat machi kbira bhal Casa.\n\nBach n9ewwiw lmo9arana: `much` (bzzaf) wla `a little` (chwiya) 9bel lmo9aran: `Marrakech is much hotter than Tangier.` = Marrakech skhona bzzaf kter men Tanja. / `This one is a little cheaper.` = Hada rkhes chwiya.\n\nSo2al: `Which is bigger, Casablanca or Rabat?` = Achmen wa7da kber, Casa wla Rabat?","examples":[{"en":"My sister is taller than me.","da":"Khti twel menni.","pron":"maï sis-teur iz to-leur than mi"},{"en":"Rabat is as beautiful as Casablanca.","da":"Rabat zwina bhal Casa.","pron":"ra-bat iz az biou-ti-foul az ka-sa-blan-ka"},{"en":"The bus is not as fast as the train.","da":"Lkar machi sri3 bhal ttran.","pron":"the beus iz not az fast az the tréyn"},{"en":"Marrakech is much hotter than Tangier.","da":"Marrakech skhona bzzaf kter men Tanja.","pron":"ma-ra-kéch iz meutch ho-teur than tan-djir"},{"en":"Which is cheaper, the bus or the train?","da":"Achmen wa7ed rkhes, lkar wla ttran?","pron":"witch iz tchi-peur, the beus or the tréyn"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"big","da":"kbir (`bigger` = kber men)","emoji":"🐘","pron":"big","example_en":"Casablanca is bigger than Fes.","example_da":"Casa kber men Fes."},{"en":"small","da":"sghir (`smaller` = sgher men)","emoji":"🐜","pron":"smol","example_en":"My flat is smaller than yours.","example_da":"Ddar dyali sgher men dyalek."},{"en":"tall","da":"twil (`taller` = twel men)","emoji":"🦒","pron":"tol","example_en":"Omar is taller than his father.","example_da":"Omar twel men bbah."},{"en":"cheap","da":"rkhis (`cheaper` = rkhes men)","emoji":"💸","pron":"tchip","example_en":"The bus is cheaper than the train.","example_da":"Lkar rkhes men ttran."},{"en":"expensive","da":"ghali (`more expensive` = ghla men)","emoji":"💎","pron":"ik-spén-siv","example_en":"This hotel is the most expensive in town.","example_da":"Had lotil howa l'aghla f lmdina."},{"en":"hot","da":"skhon (`hotter` = skhon kter)","emoji":"🔥","pron":"hot","example_en":"July is hotter than May.","example_da":"Yolyouz skhon kter men may."},{"en":"cold","da":"bared (`colder` = bred men)","emoji":"❄️","pron":"kold","example_en":"Ifrane is the coldest city in Morocco.","example_da":"Ifran hiya abred mdina f lmeghrib."},{"en":"old","da":"9dim / kbir f l3mer (`older` = 9dem, kber men)","emoji":"🏛️","pron":"old","example_en":"Fes is older than Casablanca.","example_da":"Fes 9dem men Casa."},{"en":"young","da":"sghir f l3mer (`younger` = sgher men)","emoji":"👶","pron":"yeung","example_en":"My sister is younger than me.","example_da":"Khti sgher menni."},{"en":"easy","da":"sahl (`easier` = shel men)","emoji":"👍","pron":"i-zi","example_en":"This lesson is easier than lesson 19.","example_da":"Had dars shel men dars 19."},{"en":"difficult","da":"s3ib (`more difficult` = s3eb men)","emoji":"🧗‍♀️","pron":"di-fi-keult","example_en":"Grammar is more difficult than vocabulary.","example_da":"L9awa3id s3eb men lkelmat."},{"en":"beautiful","da":"zwin (`more beautiful` = zwen men)","emoji":"🌸","pron":"biou-ti-foul","example_en":"Chefchaouen is the most beautiful town in Morocco.","example_da":"Chefchawen hiya a7san mdina f lmeghrib."},{"en":"interesting","da":"momti3, fih lfa2ida (`more interesting` = momti3 kter)","emoji":"🤔","pron":"in-tris-ting","example_en":"History is more interesting than maths for me.","example_da":"Ttarikh momti3 kter men l7sab bnnesba liya."},{"en":"fast","da":"sri3 (`faster` = sra3 men)","emoji":"🚄","pron":"fast","example_en":"A taxi is faster than a bus.","example_da":"Taxi sra3 men tobis."},{"en":"slow","da":"bti2, m3ettel (`slower` = m3ettel kter)","emoji":"🐢","pron":"slo","example_en":"The old bus is slower than the new one.","example_da":"Lkar l9dim m3ettel kter men jjdid."},{"en":"far","da":"b3id (`further` = b3ed men)","emoji":"📏","pron":"far","example_en":"Agadir is further than Marrakech.","example_da":"Agadir b3ed men Marrakech."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Agadir wla Marrakech?","context_da":"Nouha w sa7bha Omar kaykhettto l 3otla dyal sseif. Kay9arno bin Agadir w Marrakech.","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Where are we going to go this summer? Agadir or Marrakech?","da":"Fin ghadi nmchiw had sseif? Agadir wla Marrakech?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I think Agadir is more beautiful. It has the beach and the sea.","da":"Kandenn Agadir zwina kter. Fiha lplaj w lb7er."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"But Marrakech is more interesting. The medina is older and bigger.","da":"Walakin Marrakech momti3a kter. Lmdina l9dima dyalha 9dem w kber."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, but Marrakech is much hotter than Agadir in summer!","da":"Ah, walakin Marrakech skhona bzzaf kter men Agadir f sseif!"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"That's true. Is Agadir more expensive?","da":"Hadchi s7i7. Wach Agadir ghla?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"The hotels are a little more expensive, but the fish is cheaper and fresher.","da":"Lotilat ghla chwiya, walakin l7out rkhes w tri kter."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"And which city is further from Casablanca?","da":"W achmen mdina b3ed 3la Casa?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Agadir. It takes about seven hours by bus. The train to Marrakech is faster.","da":"Agadir. Kaykhod ta9riban seb3 swaye3 b lkar. Ttran l Marrakech sra3."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"OK, you win! Agadir is the best choice for the summer.","da":"Wakha, rbe7ti! Agadir hiya a7san khtiyar l sseif."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Great! It's the nicest city in Morocco!","da":"Mzyan! Hiya a7san mdina f lmeghrib!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Tlata d l'aghlat li kaydirouhom bzzaf — tjennbihom: 1) \"more bigger\" ✗ → `bigger` ✓ (ya `-er` ya `more`, machi bjouj). 2) \"then\" ✗ → `than` ✓ (`then` = men ba3d). 3) \"gooder\" ✗ → `better` ✓. W tfekkri: l superlative kayakhod dima `the`: `the best`, `the biggest`. Melli kat9arni, ma t3eyyi rassek: b `-er than` w `the -est` t9edri t9oli l'aghlabiya dyal lmo9aranat!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno howa lmo9aran (`comparative`) dyal `big`?","options":["bigger","biger","more big","biggest"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`big` → `bigger` (kan3awdo l `g`: b-i-g-g-e-r). `biggest` howa l superlative. `more big` ghalat."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Casablanca is ___ than Rabat.","options":["bigger","biggest","more big"],"answer":"bigger","hint_da":"Casa kber men Rabat.","explain_da":"M3a `than` kansta3mlo lmo9aran: `bigger than`. `the biggest` kayji bla `than`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"The train is faster than the bus.","question_da":"Sem3i w khtari lma3na.","options":["Ttran sra3 men lkar","Lkar sra3 men ttran","Ttran w lkar bjouj sra3 bhal bhal","Ttran ghla men lkar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`faster than` = sra3 men. Lli 9bel `than` howa li sra3: `The train is faster than the bus` = ttran sra3."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lmo9aran b lingliziya m3a lma3na dyalo b darija.","pairs":[{"en":"bigger","da":"kber (men)","emoji":"🐘"},{"en":"cheaper","da":"rkhes (men)","emoji":"💸"},{"en":"better","da":"7sen (men)","emoji":"😊"},{"en":"worse","da":"khyeb (men)","emoji":"👎"},{"en":"more expensive","da":"ghla (men)","emoji":"💎"},{"en":"further","da":"b3ed (men)","emoji":"📏"}]},{"type":"order","words":["than","Marrakech","Tangier.","hotter","is"],"answer":"Marrakech is hotter than Tangier.","da":"Marrakech skhona kter men Tanja."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ljomla ss7i7a:","options":["This is the most expensive hotel in Agadir.","This is the expensivest hotel in Agadir.","This is the more expensive hotel in Agadir.","This is the most expensiver hotel in Agadir."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`expensive` ssifa twila → `the most expensive`. Ma kanzidouch `-er` wla `-est` l ssifat ttwila."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"My sister is younger than me.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 9alt?","options":["Khti sgher menni f l3mer","Khti kber menni f l3mer","Khti twel menni","Khti 9ser menni"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`younger than me` = sgher menni f l3mer. `young` = sghir f l3mer, `old` = kbir f l3mer."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Couscous is the ___ dish in Morocco.","options":["most famous","famousest","more famous"],"answer":"most famous","hint_da":"`famous` = mchhour (ssifa twila). L superlative b `the`…","explain_da":"`famous` twila → `the most famous` (l'akter chohra). `more famous` kayji m3a `than`, machi m3a `the`."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"More better\" is correct English.","statement_da":"`More better` s7i7a f lingliziya.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `better` howa déja lmo9aran dyal `good`. Kan9oulo `better than`, bla `more`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Atay 7sen men l9ehwa.","answers":["Tea is better than coffee.","Mint tea is better than coffee.","Tea's better than coffee.","The tea is better than the coffee."],"hint_en":"Tea is ... than coffee.","explain_da":"`good` → `better than` = 7sen men. Machi \"gooder\"!"},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"The bus is not as fast as the train.","da":"Lkar machi sri3 bhal ttran.","explain_da":"`not as fast as` = machi sri3 bhal. `as … as` kat9arn bin jouj 7wayj metsawyin, w `not as … as` melli l'awwal 9ell."},{"type":"order","words":["the","shop.","cheapest","This","in","is","the","phone"],"answer":"This phone is the cheapest in the shop.","da":"Had lportable howa rkhes wa7ed f l7anout."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Today is ___ than yesterday. (hot)","answers":["hotter"],"hint_da":"`hot` kattsali b 7arf wa7ed men ba3d 7arf 3illa → kan3awdo l7arf l'akhir.","explain_da":"`hot` → `hotter` (b jouj `t`). Bhal `big` → `bigger`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Lkelma `worse` hiya lmo9aran dyal:","options":["bad","good","far","big"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`bad` → `worse` → `the worst`. `good` → `better`. `far` → `further`. `big` → `bigger`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Had lkhedma s3eb men lkhedma l9dima dyali.","answers":["This job is more difficult than my old job.","This job is harder than my old job.","This work is more difficult than my old work.","This job is more difficult than my old one."],"hint_en":"This job is more ... than my old job.","explain_da":"`difficult` ssifa twila → `more difficult than`. (`harder` 7ta hiya s7i7a: `hard` = s3ib, 9sira → `-er`.)"},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Marrakech is hotter than Casablanca, but Agadir is the most beautiful.","da":"Marrakech skhona kter men Casa, walakin Agadir hiya a7san wa7da.","pron":"ma-ra-kéch iz ho-teur than ka-sa-blan-ka, beut a-ga-dir iz the most biou-ti-foul"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Three cities","title_da":"Tlata d lmdon","emoji":"🏙️","text_en":"Morocco has many beautiful cities, but which one is the best? Casablanca is the biggest city in the country. It is bigger than Rabat and more modern than Fes. Life in Casablanca is faster and more expensive than in other cities, and the traffic is the worst in Morocco! Marrakech is smaller than Casablanca, but it is more popular with tourists. It is also much hotter: in summer, it is one of the hottest cities in the country. The medina of Marrakech is older and more interesting than the new city. Agadir is further south. It is not as old as Marrakech, because an earthquake destroyed the old city in 1960. But Agadir has the best beach and the freshest fish. For many Moroccans, Agadir is the most relaxing city in Morocco. And for Nouha? \"Casablanca is my home, but Agadir is the most beautiful!\"","text_da":"Lmeghrib fih bzzaf dyal lmdon zwinin, walakin achmen wa7da hiya l'a7san? Casa hiya akbar mdina f lblad. Kber men Rabat w 3asriya kter men Fes. L7ayat f Casa sri3a kter w ghalya kter men lmdon l'okhra, w zz7am dyal ttomobilat howa l'akhyeb f lmeghrib! Marrakech sgher men Casa, walakin ssiya7 kaybghiwha kter. W hiya skhona bzzaf kter: f sseif, hiya men askhen lmdon f lblad. Lmdina l9dima dyal Marrakech 9dem w momti3a kter men lmdina jjdida. Agadir b3ida kter f jjanoub. Machi 9dima bhal Marrakech, 7it zelzal heddem lmdina l9dima f 1960. Walakin Agadir 3ndha a7san plaj w tra l7out. Bnnesba l bzzaf dyal lmgharba, Agadir hiya l'akter mdina mrye7a f lmeghrib. W Nouha? \"Casa hiya dari, walakin Agadir hiya a7san wa7da!\"","glossary":[{"en":"country","da":"lblad"},{"en":"modern","da":"3asri / 3asriya"},{"en":"traffic","da":"zz7am (dyal ttomobilat)"},{"en":"popular","da":"m7boub / nnas kaybghiwh"},{"en":"tourists","da":"ssiya7"},{"en":"south","da":"jjanoub"},{"en":"earthquake","da":"zelzal"},{"en":"destroyed","da":"heddem"},{"en":"fresh","da":"tri / triya"},{"en":"relaxing","da":"mrye7 / kayrye7"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen mdina hiya l'akbar f lmeghrib?","options":["Casablanca","Marrakech","Agadir","Rabat"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Casablanca is the biggest city in the country.`"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Marrakech is bigger than Casablanca.","statement_da":"Marrakech kber men Casa.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `Marrakech is smaller than Casablanca.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach Agadir machi 9dima bhal Marrakech?","options":["7it zelzal heddem lmdina l9dima f 1960","7it hiya f jjanoub","7it 3ndha lplaj","7it ssiya7 kaybghiwha"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`An earthquake destroyed the old city in 1960.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno kat9oul Nouha 3la Agadir?","options":["Hiya a7san wa7da (zwina kter men kolchi)","Hiya l'akbar","Hiya l'aghla","Zz7am dyalha khayb"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Agadir is the most beautiful!` = a7san wa7da / zwina kter men kolchi."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Achmen portable?","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sarah baghya tchri portable. Sem3i: achmen portable rkhes? W achmen wa7ed khtarat f l'akhir, w 3lach?","lines":[{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good morning! Can I help you?","da":"Sbah lkhir! Wach n9der n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Yes, please. I'm looking for a phone. Which one is better, the black one or the white one?","da":"Ah, 3afak. Kan9elleb 3la portable. Achmen wa7ed 7sen, lk7el wla lbyed?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"The black one is newer and has a bigger screen. But the white one is cheaper.","da":"Lk7el jdid kter w 3ndo chacha kber. Walakin lbyed rkhes."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"How much is the black one?","da":"Ch7al lk7el?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"It's three thousand dirhams. The white one is two thousand.","da":"Tlat alaf derhem. Lbyed b alfayn."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hmm, the black one is much more expensive. Is the camera better?","da":"Hmm, lk7el ghla bzzaf. Wach lkamira 7sen?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, it's the best camera in the shop. But the white phone is lighter and easier to use.","da":"Ah, hiya a7san kamira f l7anout. Walakin lportable lbyed khfif kter w shel f l'isti3mal."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I think the white one is better for me. I'll take it.","da":"Kandenn lbyed 7sen liya. Ghadi nakhdo."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good choice! It's the most popular phone this year.","da":"Khtiyar mzyan! Howa lportable li kaytchra kter had l3am."}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen portable rkhes?","options":["Lbyed","Lk7el","Bjouj nefs ttaman","Ma9alch"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`The white one is cheaper.` — lbyed b 2000 derhem, lk7el b 3000."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The black phone has a smaller screen.","statement_da":"Lportable lk7el 3ndo chacha sgher.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: `The black one… has a bigger screen.` = chacha kber."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"It's the best camera in the shop.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno 9al Omar 3la lkamira?","options":["Hiya a7san kamira f l7anout","Hiya akhyeb kamira f l7anout","Hiya aghla kamira f l7anout","Hiya kamira 9dima"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`the best` = l'a7san (superlative dyal `good`)."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"F l'akhir, achmen portable khtarat Sarah, w 3lach?","options":["Lbyed, 7it 7sen liha w rkhes","Lk7el, 7it 3ndo a7san kamira","Bjouj","7ta wa7ed, mchat bla ma tchri"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I think the white one is better for me. I'll take it.`"}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Casablanca is bigger than Rabat.","da":"Casa kber men Rabat.","pron":"ka-sa-blan-ka iz bi-geur than ra-bat"},{"target_en":"This bag is cheaper than that one.","da":"Had ssak rkhes men hadak.","pron":"this bag iz tchi-peur than that wan"},{"target_en":"Marrakech is the hottest city in summer.","da":"Marrakech hiya askhen mdina f sseif.","pron":"ma-ra-kéch iz the ho-tist si-ti in seu-meur"},{"target_en":"This exercise is easier than the first one.","da":"Had ttamrin shel men l'awwal.","pron":"this ék-seur-saïz iz i-zi-eur than the feurst wan"},{"target_en":"Mint tea is the best drink in the world.","da":"Atay howa a7san mechroub f l3alam.","pron":"mint ti iz the bést drink in the weurld"},{"target_en":"The bus is not as fast as the train.","da":"Lkar machi sri3 bhal ttran.","pron":"the beus iz not az fast az the tréyn"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Sarah katsewlek 3la lmdon dyal lmeghrib","context_da":"Sa7btek Sarah baghya t3ref lmeghrib kter. Katsewlek w nti kat9arni liha. Jawbi b sot 3ali w wade7! Ila ma3reftich, chofi ljawab lmo9tara7 w 3awdih.","turns":[{"bot_en":"Nouha, which city is bigger, Casablanca or Rabat?","bot_da":"Nouha, achmen mdina kber, Casa wla Rabat?","expect_keywords":["casablanca","casa","bigger"],"sample_en":"Casablanca is bigger than Rabat."},{"bot_en":"And which city is hotter in summer, Marrakech or Tangier?","bot_da":"W achmen mdina skhona kter f sseif, Marrakech wla Tanja?","expect_keywords":["marrakech","marrakesh","hotter"],"sample_en":"Marrakech is much hotter than Tangier."},{"bot_en":"Is the train more expensive than the bus?","bot_da":"Wach ttran ghla men lkar?","expect_keywords":["yes","more expensive","no","cheaper","but","faster","it is"],"sample_en":"Yes, it's more expensive, but it's faster."},{"bot_en":"What's the best food in Morocco, in your opinion?","bot_da":"Chno hiya a7san makla f lmeghrib, f ra2yek?","expect_keywords":["couscous","tagine","tajine","the best","best","pastilla","harira","is the"],"sample_en":"Couscous is the best food in Morocco!"},{"bot_en":"Last question: is English easier than Darija for you?","bot_da":"Akhir so2al: wach lingliziya shel men ddarija bnnesba lik?","expect_keywords":["easier","more difficult","harder","no","yes","as easy as","difficult","interesting"],"sample_en":"No! Darija is easier for me, but English is more interesting."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"9arni bin jouj mdon","prompt_da":"Ktbi 5 wla 6 jomal kat9arni fihom bin jouj mdon f lmeghrib (matalan Casa w Marrakech): lkobr, ljow, ttaman, lmakla, nnas. Sta3mli `-er than`, `more … than`, w `the …est` / `the most …`. W 9oli achmen wa7da hiya `the best` bnnesba lik, w 3lach.","helper_en":["... is bigger than ...","... is more beautiful than ...","The food in ... is cheaper.","... is the hottest city in summer.","I think ... is the best city because ..."],"min_words":40,"keywords":["than","more","best"],"model_en":"I live in Casablanca, but I love Marrakech. Casablanca is bigger and more modern than Marrakech. It has more jobs, but life is more expensive and the traffic is worse. Marrakech is smaller, hotter and more beautiful. The medina is older and more interesting than the centre of Casablanca. The food in Marrakech is cheaper, and the people are friendlier. For me, Casablanca is the best city for work, but Marrakech is the best city for holidays!"}},{"id":"l21","order":21,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"💼","title_en":"Jobs & work","title_da":"Lkhedma","goals_da":["Tsewli w tjawbi 3la `What do you do?` w t9oli fin w kifach katkhdmi","Tsta3mli `have to`, `don't have to`, `must` w `mustn't` bach thedri 3la lwajibat dyal lkhedma","Tjawbi 3la l'as2ila dyal `job interview` (lmo9abala dyal lkhedma)","T3erfi lkelmat dyal `CV`: `experience`, `skills`, `diploma`, `full-time`, `part-time`, `salary`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"What do you do? — Chno katkhdmi?","body_da":"Bach tsewli chi wa7ed 3la khedmto, l'ingliz kay9oulo `What do you do?` — 7arfiyan \"chno katdir?\", walakin lma3na: chno katkhdem? Kayn 7ta `What's your job?`, nefs lma3na.\n\nLjawab: `I'm a` + lkhedma. Dima m3a `a` wla `an` (bhal dars 6): `I'm a nurse.`, `I'm an engineer.` — machi \"I'm nurse\".\n\nBach t9oli fin w kifach katkhdmi:\n\n- `I work in` + lblassa: `I work in a hospital.` = kankhdem f sbitar.\n- `I work for` + cherika wla chkhss: `I work for a big company.` = kankhdem 3nd cherika kbira.\n- `I work as` + lkhedma: `I work as a cashier.` = kankhdem kaysiya.\n\nW ila makatkhdmich daba: `I'm unemployed.` = makhddamach, wla `I'm looking for a job.` = kan9elleb 3la khedma. `I'm self-employed.` = kankhdem l rassi.\n\n**Nasi7a:** `What do you do?` (lkhedma) machi bhal `What are you doing?` (chno katdiri daba — dars 13). Farra9i binathom!","examples":[{"en":"What do you do?","da":"Chno katkhdmi?","pron":"wat dou you dou"},{"en":"I'm a nurse. I work in a hospital in Rabat.","da":"Ana fermliya. Kankhdem f sbitar f Rabat.","pron":"aïm a neurs. aï weurk in a hos-pi-teul in ra-bat"},{"en":"My brother works for a big company.","da":"Khouya kaykhdem 3nd wa7ed cherika kbira.","pron":"maï bra-theur weurks for a big keum-pa-ni"},{"en":"She works as a cashier in a shop.","da":"Hiya katkhdem kaysiya f wa7ed l7anout.","pron":"chi weurks az a ka-chir in a chop"},{"en":"I'm looking for a job.","da":"Kan9elleb 3la khedma.","pron":"aïm lou-king for a djob"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"have to / don't have to — khassni / machi daroori","body_da":"`have to` + lfi3l = khass + lfi3l: 7aja wajiba, lazem tdiriha (l9anoun, lkhedma, lmoudir…).\n\n- `I have to work on Saturday.` = khassni nkhdem nhar ssebt.\n- M3a `he/she/it`: `has to` → `She has to wear a uniform.` = khassha tlbes lebsa dyal lkhedma.\n- So2al: `Do you have to…?` / `Does she have to…?` → `Yes, I do.` / `No, she doesn't.`\n- Lmadi (dars 16): `had to` → `Yesterday I had to stay late.` = lbare7 kan khassni nb9a 7ta l m3ettel.\n\nNnafi: `don't have to` / `doesn't have to` = **machi daroori** — 3ndek lkhtiyar, ila ma dertihach 3adi.\n\n- `We don't have to work on Sundays.` = makhassnach nkhdmo nhar l7edd (3ndna rra7a).\n- `He doesn't have to wear a suit.` = machi daroori ylbes kostim.\n\nBhal f darija: \"khassni\" = `I have to`, \"machi daroori\" = `I don't have to`. Redi lbal: `don't have to` **machi** mamnou3! Mamnou3 ghadi nchoufouh f l9ism jjay m3a `mustn't`.","examples":[{"en":"I have to get up at six every day.","da":"Khassni nfi9 m3a ssetta kol nhar.","pron":"aï hav tou guèt eup at siks év-ri déy"},{"en":"She has to speak English at work.","da":"Khassha thder b lingliziya f lkhedma.","pron":"chi haz tou spik in-glich at weurk"},{"en":"We don't have to work on Sundays.","da":"Makhassnach nkhdmo nhar l7edd — machi daroori.","pron":"wi dont hav tou weurk on seun-déyz"},{"en":"Do you have to wear a uniform?","da":"Wach khassek tlebsi lebsa dyal lkhedma?","pron":"dou you hav tou wér a you-ni-form"},{"en":"Yesterday I had to finish a report.","da":"Lbare7 kan khassni nkemmel wa7ed tta9rir.","pron":"yès-teur-déy aï had tou fi-nich a ri-port"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"must / mustn't — lazem / mamnou3","body_da":"`must` = lazem — 9awiya chwiya kter men `have to`, kat9al f l9awanin, l'ichharat w l'awamir. `must` ma katbeddelch: `I must`, `she must` (bla `-s`), w men ba3dha lfi3l direct, bla `to`: `You must wear a helmet.` (machi \"must to wear\").\n\n`mustn't` (= `must not`) = **mamnou3**: `You mustn't smoke here.` = mamnou3 tkemmi hna.\n\nLfar9 lmohimm:\n\n- `You don't have to come.` = machi daroori tji (ila bghiti tji, mer7ba; ila la, 3adi).\n- `You mustn't come.` = mamnou3 tji!\n\nF lhadra l3adiya, l'ingliz kaysta3mlo `have to` kter men `must`. `must` kat9rayha bzzaf f lwra9 w l'ichharat: `Visitors must sign here.`","examples":[{"en":"You must be on time.","da":"Lazem tkouni f lwa9t.","pron":"you meust bi on taïm"},{"en":"Employees must wear a badge.","da":"Lkhddama lazem ylebso lbita9a dyal lkhedma.","pron":"èm-ploï-iz meust wér a badj"},{"en":"You mustn't use your phone in the meeting.","da":"Mamnou3 tsta3mli ttilifoun dyalek f l'ijtima3.","pron":"you meus-ent youz your fon in the mi-ting"},{"en":"You don't have to wear a suit, but you mustn't wear jeans.","da":"Machi daroori tlebsi kostim, walakin mamnou3 tlebsi ddjin.","pron":"you dont hav tou wér a sout, beut you meus-ent wér djinz"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lmo9abala dyal lkhedma — the job interview","body_da":"F `job interview` (lmo9abala dyal lkhedma), kaynin as2ila kaytsewlo dima. Wejjdi ljawab dyalek men 9bel!\n\n- `Tell me about yourself.` = hder liya 3la rassek. → smiytek, l3mer, mnin nti, chno 9riti, fin khdemti: `My name is Nouha, I'm 28. I studied tourism and I worked as a receptionist for two years.`\n- `Why do you want this job?` = 3lach bghiti had lkhedma? → `Because I like working with people.` / `Because I want to learn new things.`\n- `What are your strengths?` = chno hiya no9at l9owwa dyalek? → `I'm organized, I'm patient and I work well in a team.`\n- `Do you have experience?` = wach 3ndek tajriba? → `Yes, I have three years of experience as a receptionist.` / `No, but I learn fast.`\n\nLkelmat dyal `CV`: `experience` = ttajriba, `skills` = lmaharat (chno kat3rfi ddiri), `diploma` = ddiplom / chhada, `full-time` = b lwa9t kaml, `part-time` = b nos lwa9t, `salary` = chhriya.\n\nRedi lbal: 3la lkhedma li fatet, sta3mli lmadi (dars 16): `I worked`, `I studied`. 3la daba: `I work`, `I'm working`.","examples":[{"en":"Tell me about yourself.","da":"Hder liya 3la rassek.","pron":"tèl mi a-bawt your-sèlf"},{"en":"Why do you want this job?","da":"3lach bghiti had lkhedma?","pron":"waï dou you wont this djob"},{"en":"I have three years of experience as a receptionist.","da":"3ndi tlata dyal ssnin dyal ttajriba f l'isti9bal.","pron":"aï hav thri yirz ov ik-spi-ri-èns az a ri-sèp-cheu-nist"},{"en":"My strengths? I'm organized and I work well in a team.","da":"No9at l9owwa dyali? Ana mnaddma w kankhdem mzyan m3a lmajmou3a.","pron":"maï strèngths? aïm or-ga-naïzd and aï weurk wèl in a tim"},{"en":"Is it a full-time or a part-time job?","da":"Wach hadi khedma b lwa9t kaml wla b nos lwa9t?","pron":"iz it a foul-taïm or a part-taïm djob"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"job","da":"khedma","emoji":"💼","pron":"djob","example_en":"I'm looking for a new job.","example_da":"Kan9elleb 3la khedma jdida."},{"en":"office","da":"lbiro / lmekteb","emoji":"🏢","pron":"o-fis","example_en":"I work in an office in Casablanca.","example_da":"Kankhdem f biro f Casa."},{"en":"factory","da":"lma3mel","emoji":"🏭","pron":"fak-teu-ri","example_en":"My father worked in a factory.","example_da":"Bba kan khddam f lma3mel."},{"en":"shop","da":"7anout","emoji":"🏪","pron":"chop","example_en":"She works in a shop.","example_da":"Hiya katkhdem f 7anout."},{"en":"hospital","da":"sbitar","emoji":"🏥","pron":"hos-pi-teul","example_en":"Nurses work in a hospital.","example_da":"Lfermliyat kaykhdmo f sbitar."},{"en":"boss","da":"lmoudir / lpatron","emoji":"👔","pron":"bos","example_en":"My boss is very kind.","example_da":"Lmoudir dyali dérif bzzaf."},{"en":"colleague","da":"zmil f lkhedma","emoji":"👩‍💼","pron":"ko-lig","example_en":"My colleagues are friendly.","example_da":"Zmlani f lkhedma dérifin."},{"en":"experience","da":"ttajriba","emoji":"📋","pron":"ik-spi-ri-èns","example_en":"I have two years of experience.","example_da":"3ndi 3amayn dyal ttajriba."},{"en":"skills","da":"lmaharat (chno kat3rfi ddiri)","emoji":"🛠️","pron":"skilz","example_en":"Computer skills are important.","example_da":"Lmaharat dyal lpc mohimmin."},{"en":"diploma","da":"ddiplom / chhada","emoji":"🎓","pron":"di-plo-ma","example_en":"I have a diploma in accounting.","example_da":"3ndi diplom f lmo7asaba."},{"en":"full-time","da":"b lwa9t kaml","emoji":"🕘","pron":"foul-taïm","example_en":"It's a full-time job.","example_da":"Hadi khedma b lwa9t kaml."},{"en":"part-time","da":"b nos lwa9t","emoji":"🕒","pron":"part-taïm","example_en":"She works part-time in a café.","example_da":"Hiya katkhdem b nos lwa9t f 9ehwa."},{"en":"salary","da":"chhriya / l'oujra","emoji":"💰","pron":"sa-la-ri","example_en":"The salary is 5,000 dirhams a month.","example_da":"Chhriya hiya 5000 derhem f chhar."},{"en":"interview","da":"lmo9abala","emoji":"🗣️","pron":"in-teur-vyou","example_en":"I have a job interview tomorrow.","example_da":"3ndi mo9abala dyal khedma ghedda."},{"en":"uniform","da":"lebsa dyal lkhedma","emoji":"👕","pron":"you-ni-form","example_en":"I have to wear a uniform.","example_da":"Khassni nlbes lebsa dyal lkhedma."},{"en":"meeting","da":"l'ijtima3","emoji":"👥","pron":"mi-ting","example_en":"We have a meeting at ten.","example_da":"3ndna ijtima3 m3a l3echra."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Mo9abala dyal khedma f lotil","context_da":"Nouha 3ndha mo9abala dyal khedma f l'isti9bal dyal wa7ed lotil f Marrakech. Lmoudir, ssi Brown, kaysewwelha.","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Good morning, Nouha. Please, sit down. Tell me about yourself.","da":"Sbah lkhir, Nouha. Glsi 3afak. Hder liya 3la rassek."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you. I'm 28 years old and I'm from Casablanca. I studied tourism for two years.","da":"Choukran. 3ndi 28 3am w ana men Casa. 9rit ssiya7a 3amayn."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Do you have experience?","da":"Wach 3ndek chi tajriba?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes. I worked as a receptionist in a small hotel for three years.","da":"Ah. Khdemt f l'isti9bal dyal wa7ed lotil sghir tlata dyal ssnin."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Why do you want this job?","da":"3lach bghiti had lkhedma?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Because I like working with people, and I want to use my English.","da":"7it kan3jebni nkhdem m3a nnas, w bghit nsta3mel lingliziya dyali."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"What are your strengths?","da":"Chno hiya no9at l9owwa dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"I'm organized and patient. I'm never late.","da":"Ana mnaddma w sbbara. 3emmerni makant3ettel."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Great. You have to work some weekends. Is that OK?","da":"Mzyan. Khassek tkhdmi chi iyam dyal ssebt w l7edd. Wach hadchi wakha?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, no problem. When can I start?","da":"Ah, machi mochkil. Fo9ach n9der nbda?"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"F lmo9abala, l'ingliz kaybghiw ljawab l9sir w lwade7. Ma t9olich ghir `yes` wla `no` — zidi jomla: `Yes, I have two years of experience.` W ila mafhemtich so2al, 9oli b kol thi9a: `Sorry, could you repeat the question, please?` — hadchi 3adi w kaybyen annaki mo2addaba."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach tsewli chi wa7ed 3la khedmto?","options":["What do you do?","How do you do?","What are you doing?","Where do you go?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What do you do?` = chno katkhdem? `What are you doing?` = chno katdir daba (dars 13). `How do you do?` = ta7iya rasmiya 9dima, machi so2al 3la lkhedma."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lblassa dyal lkhedma m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"office","da":"lbiro","emoji":"🏢"},{"en":"factory","da":"lma3mel","emoji":"🏭"},{"en":"hospital","da":"sbitar","emoji":"🏥"},{"en":"shop","da":"7anout","emoji":"🏪"},{"en":"school","da":"lmedrasa","emoji":"🏫"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I work in a hospital.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fin katkhdem had lmra?","options":["F sbitar","F lma3mel","F 7anout","F lmedrasa"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I work in a hospital.` = kankhdem f sbitar. `in` + lblassa."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"She ___ as a cashier in a shop.","options":["works","work","working"],"answer":"works","hint_da":"Hiya → fekkri f dars 8: `he/she` + `-s`.","explain_da":"`She works` — m3a `he/she/it` kanzido `-s` l lfi3l f l7adir lbassit."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ to get up at six every day.","options":["have","has","must"],"answer":"have","hint_da":"Khassni nfi9… ana = `I`.","explain_da":"`I have to` = khassni. `has to` ghir m3a `he/she/it`. `must` ma kayjich m3a `to`."},{"type":"order","words":["I","work","in","an","office","in","Rabat."],"answer":"I work in an office in Rabat.","da":"Kankhdem f biro f Rabat.","explain_da":"`I work in` + lblassa. `office` kaybda b 7arf motaharrik (vowel) → `an office`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari ljomla s7i7a:","options":["She must wear a uniform.","She must to wear a uniform.","She musts wear a uniform.","She must wears a uniform."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`must` ma kaytbeddelch w ma kayjich men ba3do `to`: `she must wear`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"You don't have to work on Sunday.","question_da":"Sem3i mzyan. Chno lma3na?","options":["Machi daroori tkhdmi nhar l7edd","Mamnou3 tkhdmi nhar l7edd","Khassek tkhdmi nhar l7edd","Lazem tkhdmi nhar l7edd"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`don't have to` = machi daroori. `mustn't` = mamnou3. Farra9i binathom!"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"You mustn't smoke here\" means you can smoke if you want.","statement_da":"`You mustn't smoke here` kat3ni t9edri tkemmi ila bghiti.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `mustn't` = mamnou3. Li kat3ni \"ila bghiti\" hiya `don't have to`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Khassha thder b lingliziya f lkhedma.","answers":["She has to speak English at work.","She must speak English at work.","She needs to speak English at work."],"hint_en":"She ... to speak ... at ...","explain_da":"`She has to` = khassha. M3a `she` kan9oulo `has to`, machi `have to`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Do you have experience?","da":"Wach 3ndek tajriba?","explain_da":"Sem3i: `Do` – `you` – `have` – `experience`. `experience` = ttajriba."},{"type":"order","words":["Why","do","you","want","this","job?"],"answer":"Why do you want this job?","da":"3lach bghiti had lkhedma?","explain_da":"So2al b `Why` + `do` + `you` + lfi3l: `Why do you want…?`"},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"What are your strengths?","question_da":"Nti f lmo9abala. Achmen jawab mnassb l had so2al?","options":["I'm organized and I work well in a team.","I'm 28 years old.","The salary is 5,000 dirhams.","I live in Casablanca."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`strengths` = no9at l9owwa. Ljawab: ssifat dyalek lmzyanin f lkhedma: `organized`, `patient`, `I work well in a team`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"She works ___ in a café, only in the mornings.","answers":["part-time","part time","parttime"],"hint_da":"B nos lwa9t = …","explain_da":"`part-time` = b nos lwa9t. `full-time` = b lwa9t kaml."},{"type":"translate","da":"Ana fermliya. Kankhdem f sbitar f Casablanca.","answers":["I am a nurse. I work in a hospital in Casablanca.","I'm a nurse. I work in a hospital in Casablanca.","I'm a nurse and I work in a hospital in Casablanca.","I am a nurse and I work in a hospital in Casablanca."],"hint_en":"I ... a nurse. I ... in a ... in ...","explain_da":"Lkhedma dima m3a `a`/`an`: `a nurse`. `in a hospital` = f sbitar."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"I'm organized and patient, and I have three years of experience.","da":"Ana mnaddma w sbbara, w 3ndi tlata dyal ssnin dyal ttajriba.","pron":"aïm or-ga-naïzd and péy-chènt, and aï hav thri yirz ov ik-spi-ri-èns"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Two jobs, two lives","title_da":"Jouj khedmat, jouj 7ayawat","emoji":"👷‍♂️","text_en":"Omar is 30 years old and he lives in Tangier. He works in a big car factory. He has to start work at seven o'clock in the morning, so he gets up at half past five. He must wear a uniform, a helmet and special shoes, because the factory can be dangerous. Omar works full-time, from Monday to Friday. He doesn't have to work at the weekend. He likes his colleagues, but the work is hard and the salary is not very high.\n\nHis sister Laila is a teacher. She works part-time in a primary school in Tetouan. She has to prepare her lessons at home, but she doesn't have to wear a uniform. Her students are small children, so she must be patient. Laila loves her job. Next month, she has an interview for a full-time job in a bigger school. She is a little nervous, but she has a diploma and five years of experience.","text_da":"Omar 3ndo 30 3am w kayskon f Tanja. Kaykhdem f wa7ed lma3mel kbir dyal ttomobilat. Khasso ybda lkhedma m3a ssb3a dyal sbah, 3la hadak kayfi9 m3a lkhemsa w nos. Lazem ylbes lebsa dyal lkhedma, lkask w sbbat khass, 7it lma3mel y9der ykoun khatir. Omar kaykhdem b lwa9t kaml, men ttnin 7ta l jem3a. Makhassouch ykhdem f ssebt w l7edd. Kay3jbouh zmlano, walakin lkhedma s3iba w chhriya machi 3alya bzzaf.\n\nKhto Laila oustada. Katkhdem b nos lwa9t f wa7ed lmedrasa ibtida2iya f Titwan. Khassha twejjed ddorous dyalha f ddar, walakin makhasshach tlbes lebsa dyal lkhedma. Ttlamed dyalha drari sghar, 3la hadak lazem tkoun sbbara. Laila kat3chi9 khdemtha. Chhar jjay, 3ndha mo9abala l khedma b lwa9t kaml f medrasa kber. Hiya mkhel3a chwiya, walakin 3ndha ddiplom w khemsa dyal ssnin dyal ttajriba.","glossary":[{"en":"factory","da":"lma3mel"},{"en":"helmet","da":"lkask"},{"en":"dangerous","da":"khatir"},{"en":"colleagues","da":"zmlan f lkhedma"},{"en":"salary","da":"chhriya"},{"en":"primary school","da":"lmedrasa l'ibtida2iya"},{"en":"to prepare","da":"twejjed"},{"en":"patient","da":"sbbar / sbbara"},{"en":"nervous","da":"mkhel3 / mkhel3a chwiya"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach khass Omar ybda lkhedma?","options":["M3a ssb3a dyal sbah","M3a lkhemsa w nos","M3a ttmenya","M3a ssetta"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"He has to start work at seven o'clock.\" Kayfi9 m3a lkhemsa w nos, walakin kaybda lkhedma m3a ssb3a."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar has to work at the weekend.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"He doesn't have to work at the weekend.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach lazem Laila tkoun sbbara?","options":["7it ttlamed dyalha drari sghar","7it lkhedma f lma3mel khatira","7it chhriya 9lila","7it katkhdem f ssebt w l7edd"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Her students are small children, so she must be patient.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Laila has a diploma and five years of experience.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"she has a diploma and five years of experience.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Khedma jdida","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar. Rekkzi 3la: fin kaykhdem Omar daba? w chno khasso ydir f lkhedma?","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hi, Omar! I heard you have a new job. What do you do now?","da":"Ahlan, Omar! Sme3t belli 3ndek khedma jdida. Chno katkhdem daba?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Hi, Sarah! Yes, I'm a waiter. I work in a restaurant in Agadir.","da":"Ahlan, Sarah! Ah, ana serbay. Kankhdem f restaurant f Agadir."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nice! Is it full-time?","da":"Zwin! Wach b lwa9t kaml?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"No, it's part-time. I work from six to eleven in the evening.","da":"La, b nos lwa9t. Kankhdem men ssetta 7ta l 7dach f lil."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Do you have to wear a uniform?","da":"Wach khassek tlbes lebsa dyal lkhedma?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, a white shirt and black trousers. And I mustn't use my phone at work.","da":"Ah, 9amija byda w serwal k7el. W mamnou3 nsta3mel ttilifoun dyali f lkhedma."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"What about the salary?","da":"W chhriya?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"It's not bad: 3,000 dirhams a month, plus tips. My boss is nice, but I have to work every Saturday.","da":"Machi khayba: 3000 derhem f chhar, zayd lbakhchich. Lmoudir dyali dérif, walakin khassni nkhdem kol sebt."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Well, good luck with the new job!","da":"Yallah, bttawfi9 f lkhedma jdida!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khedmet Omar daba?","options":["Serbay f restaurant","Fermli f sbitar","Oustad f medrasa","Khddam f ma3mel"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm a waiter. I work in a restaurant in Agadir.\" `waiter` = serbay."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar works full-time.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"No, it's part-time.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I mustn't use my phone at work.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat3ni had ljomla?","options":["Mamnou3 nsta3mel ttilifoun f lkhedma","Machi daroori nsta3mel ttilifoun f lkhedma","Khassni nsta3mel ttilifoun f lkhedma","N9der nsta3mel ttilifoun f lkhedma"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`mustn't` = mamnou3."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al chhriya dyal Omar?","options":["3000 derhem f chhar","5000 derhem f chhar","2000 derhem f chhar","6000 derhem f chhar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"3,000 dirhams a month, plus tips.\" `tips` = lbakhchich."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"What do you do?","da":"Chno katkhdem?","pron":"wat dou you dou"},{"target_en":"I'm a teacher. I work in a school.","da":"Ana oustada. Kankhdem f medrasa.","pron":"aïm a ti-tcheur. aï weurk in a skoul"},{"target_en":"I have to work on Saturday.","da":"Khassni nkhdem nhar ssebt.","pron":"aï hav tou weurk on sa-teur-déy"},{"target_en":"You mustn't be late.","da":"Mamnou3 tt3ettli.","pron":"you meus-ent bi léyt"},{"target_en":"Tell me about yourself.","da":"Hder liya 3la rassek.","pron":"tèl mi a-bawt your-sèlf"},{"target_en":"I have two years of experience.","da":"3ndi 3amayn dyal ttajriba.","pron":"aï hav tou yirz ov ik-spi-ri-èns"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Mo9abala dyal khedma","context_da":"Nti f mo9abala l khedma f l'isti9bal dyal wa7ed lotil f Marrakech. Lmoudir ghadi ysewlek. Jawbi b jomal kamlin, machi ghir `yes` wla `no`!","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good morning. Please sit down. Tell me about yourself.","bot_da":"Sbah lkhir. Glsi 3afak. Hder liya 3la rassek.","expect_keywords":["my name","i'm","i am","years old","from","i live","i studied"],"sample_en":"My name is Nouha. I'm from Casablanca and I studied tourism."},{"bot_en":"Do you have any experience?","bot_da":"Wach 3ndek chi tajriba?","expect_keywords":["yes","experience","i worked","years","no, but"],"sample_en":"Yes, I worked as a receptionist for two years."},{"bot_en":"Why do you want this job?","bot_da":"3lach bghiti had lkhedma?","expect_keywords":["because","i like","i love","i want","people","english"],"sample_en":"Because I like working with people and I want to use my English."},{"bot_en":"What are your strengths?","bot_da":"Chno hiya no9at l9owwa dyalek?","expect_keywords":["organized","organised","patient","hard","team","friendly","never late","i'm","i am"],"sample_en":"I'm organized and patient, and I work well in a team."},{"bot_en":"You have to work some Saturdays. Is that OK for you?","bot_da":"Khassek tkhdmi chi iyam dyal ssebt. Wach hadchi wakha?","expect_keywords":["yes","no problem","ok","okay","fine","of course","sure"],"sample_en":"Yes, no problem."},{"bot_en":"Great. Do you have any questions for me?","bot_da":"Mzyan. Wach 3ndek chi so2al liya?","expect_keywords":["salary","when","start","full-time","part-time","hours","what time","no, thank you","yes"],"sample_en":"Yes. Is it a full-time job? And when can I start?"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Khedmti wla lkhedma li kanbghi","prompt_da":"Ktbi 50 kelma 3la khedma (dyalek wla li katbghi tkhdmiha): chno katkhdmi (wla chno bghiti tkhdmi), fin, chno khassek tdiri f had lkhedma (`have to`), chno machi daroori (`don't have to`), w chno mamnou3 (`mustn't`). Zidi 3lach kat3jbek.","helper_en":["I'm a ... / I want to be a ...","I work in a ...","I have to ...","I don't have to ...","I mustn't ..."],"min_words":50,"keywords":["work","have to"],"model_en":"I'm a receptionist. I work in a small hotel in Casablanca. I work full-time, from Monday to Friday. I have to speak with tourists in English, so my English is very important. I have to wear a uniform and I must be polite and patient. I don't have to work at night, but I have to work some Saturdays. I mustn't use my phone at the reception desk. I like my job because I meet new people every day, and my colleagues are very friendly."}},{"id":"l22","order":22,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"✈️","title_en":"Travel: at the airport & the hotel","title_da":"Ssafar: lmatar w lotil","goals_da":["T7ejzi bit wla tikiya b `I'd like to book…`","Tfehmi lkelmat dyal lmatar: `check-in`, `boarding pass`, `gate`, `luggage`, `delayed`","Tsewli b 'adab f lotil: `Could I have…?`, `Is breakfast included?`, `What time is check-out?`","Tchekiwi mochkil f lotil: `The Wi-Fi doesn't work`, `There's no hot water`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"I'd like to… — bghit… b 'adab","body_da":"`would like` = bghit, walakin b 'adab kter men `want`. `I would like` kat9esser dima w katwelli `I'd like`.\n\nKaynin jouj tari9at:\n\n- `I'd like` + ism: `I'd like a ticket to London.` = bghit tikiya l London.\n- `I'd like to` + fi3l: `I'd like to book a room.` = bghit n7jez bit.\n\nSo2al: `Would you like…?` = wach bghiti…? Ljawab: `Yes, please.` / `No, thank you.`\n\nKatkhdem m3a ga3 nnas: `She'd like`, `We'd like`, `They'd like` — nefs lforma, bla `-s`.\n\nF darija kan9oulo \"bghit\" f kolchi, walakin f lingliziya `I want a room` kat'ban 9ass7a chwiya m3a nnas li makat3rfihomch. F lotil, f lmatar, f restaurant → dima `I'd like`. (Chefti `I'd like` 9bel f dars 9, f l9ehwa — hna nefs chi, walakin f ssafar.)","examples":[{"en":"I'd like to book a room for two nights.","da":"Bghit n7jez bit l jouj lyali.","pron":"aïd laïk tou bouk a roum for tou naïts"},{"en":"I'd like a ticket to Madrid, please.","da":"Bghit tikiya l Madrid, 3afak.","pron":"aïd laïk a ti-kit tou ma-drid, pliz"},{"en":"Would you like a single or a double room?","da":"Wach bghiti bit l wa7ed wla bit l jouj?","pron":"woud you laïk a sin-gueul or a deu-beul roum"},{"en":"We'd like to check in, please.","da":"Bghina nsejjlo lwsoul dyalna, 3afak.","pron":"wid laïk tou tchèk in, pliz"},{"en":"I'd like to pay by card.","da":"Bghit nkhelles b lkart.","pron":"aïd laïk tou péy baï kard"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"F lmatar — at the airport","body_da":"F lmatar kaynin mara7il, w kol wa7da 3ndha lkelmat dyalha:\n\n- `check-in desk`: lbiro fin kat3ti lbagaj w kat'akhdi `boarding pass` (lwer9a li kadkhli biha l ttiyara). Kay9oulo lik: `Passport, please.` → `Here's my passport.` = hak lpasspor dyali.\n- `Window or aisle?` = blassa 7da cherjem (`window seat`) wla 7da lmemcha (`aisle seat`)? Redi lbal: `aisle` kat9ra \"aïl\" — l `s` ma kat9rach!\n- `security` = lmora9aba. `passport control` = lmora9aba dyal lpasspor.\n- `gate` = lbab fin katrekbi ttiyara: `Gate 12`. `boarding` = rrkoub.\n- `flight` = rri7la / ttiyara: `Is the flight on time?` = wach ttiyara f lwa9t? `The flight is delayed.` = ttiyara mt3ettla.\n\n`luggage` (wla `baggage`) = lbagaj — ism ma kayt3eddch, bhal `water`: `my luggage is heavy` (machi \"luggages\"). Bach t3eddi: `one bag`, `two suitcases`. `hand luggage` = ssak sghir li kaydkhol m3ak f ttiyara.","examples":[{"en":"Here's my passport and my ticket.","da":"Hak lpasspor dyali w ttikiya dyali.","pron":"hirz maï pas-port and maï ti-kit"},{"en":"Would you like a window seat or an aisle seat?","da":"Wach bghiti blassa 7da cherjem wla 7da lmemcha?","pron":"woud you laïk a win-do sit or an aïl sit"},{"en":"Your flight leaves from gate 12.","da":"Ttiyara dyalek ghadi tkhrej men lbab 12.","pron":"your flaït livz from guéyt twèlv"},{"en":"The flight to Paris is delayed.","da":"Ttiyara dyal Paris mt3ettla.","pron":"the flaït tou pa-ris iz di-léyd"},{"en":"How many bags do you have?","da":"Ch7al men chanta 3ndek?","pron":"haw mé-ni bagz dou you hav"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"F lotil — at the hotel","body_da":"Melli katwesli l lotil, kat9oli: `Hello, I have a reservation.` = 3ndi 7ajz, wla `I'd like to check in.`\n\n- `check in` = kat'akhdi ssarout melli katwesli. `check out` = katkhelsi w katkhelli lbit melli katmchi. So2al mohimm: `What time is check-out?` (3adatan m3a l7dach wla ttnach).\n- Nnaw3 dyal lbit: `single room` = bit l wa7ed, `double room` = bit l jouj (nmousiya kbira), `twin room` = bit b jouj nmousiyat.\n- `Is breakfast included?` = wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?\n- `key` / `key card` = ssarout / lkart dyal lbit. `floor` = ttab9a: `Your room is on the third floor.` (l'ar9am ttartibiya men dars 11: `first`, `second`, `third`).\n\nBach ttelbi chi 7aja b 'adab: `Could I have…, please?` → `Could I have the Wi-Fi password, please?`, `Could I have another towel?`. `Could I have` 'adab kter men `Can I have` (dars 9 w 14).","examples":[{"en":"Hello, I have a reservation. My name is Nouha Alami.","da":"Salam, 3ndi 7ajz. Smiyti Nouha Alami.","pron":"hé-lo, aï hav a ré-zeur-véy-cheun. maï néym iz nou-ha a-la-mi"},{"en":"Is breakfast included?","da":"Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?","pron":"iz brèk-feust in-klou-did"},{"en":"What time is check-out?","da":"Fo9ach khassni nkhelli lbit?","pron":"wat taïm iz tchèk-awt"},{"en":"Could I have the Wi-Fi password, please?","da":"Wach ymken t3tini lkod dyal lWi-Fi, 3afak?","pron":"koud aï hav the waï-faï pass-weurd, pliz"},{"en":"Your room is on the second floor. Here's your key.","da":"Lbit dyalek f ttab9a ttanya. Hak ssarout dyalek.","pron":"your roum iz on the sé-keund flor. hirz your ki"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lmachakil f lotil — problems","body_da":"Ila kan chi mochkil, bdaï dima b 'adab: `Excuse me, there's a problem with my room.` Men ba3d 9oli chno lmochkil:\n\n- `The Wi-Fi doesn't work.` = lWi-Fi makhddamch. (`doesn't work` = nnafi dyal l7adir lbassit, dars 8.) `The air conditioning doesn't work.` = lklimatizasyon makhddamach.\n- `There's no hot water.` = makaynch lma skhoun. `There are no towels.` = makaynch lfwat. (`There's no` / `There are no` = dars 10.)\n- `The room is too noisy.` = lbit fih ssda3 bzzaf. `It's too cold.` (`too` = bzzaf, kter men lma39oul — dars 12.)\n\nMen ba3d, tlbi l7ell: `Could you send someone to fix it?` = wach ymken tsift chi wa7ed ysle7ha? wla `Could I change rooms?` = wach n9der nbeddel lbit?\n\nLmowaddaf ghadi yjawbek: `I'm sorry about that. I'll send someone right away.` = sme7 liya, ghadi nsift chi wa7ed daba daba. (`I'll` = 9arar f lwa9t, dars 19.)","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, the Wi-Fi in my room doesn't work.","da":"Sme7 liya, lWi-Fi f lbit dyali makhddamch.","pron":"ik-skiouz mi, the waï-faï in maï roum deu-zent weurk"},{"en":"There's no hot water in the bathroom.","da":"Makaynch lma skhoun f ddouch.","pron":"thérz no hot wo-teur in the bath-roum"},{"en":"The room is too noisy. Could I change rooms?","da":"Lbit fih ssda3 bzzaf. Wach n9der nbeddel lbit?","pron":"the roum iz tou noï-zi. koud aï tchéyndj roumz"},{"en":"I'm sorry about that. I'll send someone right away.","da":"Sme7 liya 3la hadchi. Ghadi nsift chi wa7ed daba daba.","pron":"aïm so-ri a-bawt that. aïl sènd seum-wan raït a-wéy"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"airport","da":"lmatar","emoji":"✈️","pron":"ér-port","example_en":"We're at the airport.","example_da":"7na f lmatar."},{"en":"flight","da":"rri7la (ttiyara)","emoji":"🛫","pron":"flaït","example_en":"My flight is at 9 a.m.","example_da":"Rri7la dyali m3a tts3oud dyal sbah."},{"en":"ticket","da":"ttikiya / lbiyi","emoji":"🎫","pron":"ti-kit","example_en":"I'd like a ticket to Madrid.","example_da":"Bghit tikiya l Madrid."},{"en":"passport","da":"lpasspor","emoji":"🛂","pron":"pas-port","example_en":"Here's my passport.","example_da":"Hak lpasspor dyali."},{"en":"boarding pass","da":"lwer9a dyal rrkoub f ttiyara","emoji":"🎟️","pron":"bor-ding pass","example_en":"Here's your boarding pass.","example_da":"Hak lwer9a dyal rrkoub dyalek."},{"en":"gate","da":"lbab dyal rrkoub","emoji":"🚪","pron":"guéyt","example_en":"Go to gate 7.","example_da":"Siri l lbab 7."},{"en":"luggage","da":"lbagaj / chwanet","emoji":"🧳","pron":"leu-guidj","example_en":"My luggage is very heavy.","example_da":"Lbagaj dyali t9il bzzaf."},{"en":"delayed","da":"mt3ettel / mt3ettla","emoji":"⏳","pron":"di-léyd","example_en":"The flight is delayed.","example_da":"Ttiyara mt3ettla."},{"en":"reservation","da":"l7ajz","emoji":"📅","pron":"ré-zeur-véy-cheun","example_en":"I have a reservation for tonight.","example_da":"3ndi 7ajz l had llila."},{"en":"single room","da":"bit l wa7ed","emoji":"🛏️","pron":"sin-gueul roum","example_en":"I'd like a single room.","example_da":"Bghit bit l wa7ed."},{"en":"double room","da":"bit l jouj","emoji":"🛌","pron":"deu-beul roum","example_en":"A double room for two nights, please.","example_da":"Bit l jouj l jouj lyali, 3afak."},{"en":"key","da":"ssarout","emoji":"🔑","pron":"ki","example_en":"Here's your key.","example_da":"Hak ssarout dyalek."},{"en":"breakfast included","da":"lftor dakhel f ttaman","emoji":"🥐","pron":"brèk-feust in-klou-did","example_en":"Is breakfast included?","example_da":"Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?"},{"en":"to check in","da":"tsejjli lwsoul (f lotil wla f lmatar)","emoji":"🛎️","pron":"tou tchèk in","example_en":"We can check in at 2 p.m.","example_da":"N9dro nsejjlo lwsoul m3a jjouj dyal l3chiya."},{"en":"to check out","da":"tkhelsi w tkhelli lbit","emoji":"🧾","pron":"tou tchèk awt","example_en":"Check-out is at 11 a.m.","example_da":"Lkhrouj men lbit m3a l7dach dyal sbah."},{"en":"to book","da":"t7ejzi","emoji":"📲","pron":"tou bouk","example_en":"I'd like to book a room.","example_da":"Bghit n7jez bit."}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"F l'isti9bal dyal lotil","context_da":"Nouha weslat l wa7ed lotil f London. Kathder m3a Tom, li khddam f l'isti9bal.","lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Good evening! Welcome to the Park Hotel. How can I help you?","da":"Msa lkhir! Mer7ba bik f Park Hotel. Kifach n9der n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good evening. I have a reservation. My name is Nouha Alami.","da":"Msa lkhir. 3ndi 7ajz. Smiyti Nouha Alami."},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Let me check… Yes, a single room for three nights. Could I see your passport, please?","da":"Khellini nchouf… Ah, bit l wa7ed l tlata dyal lyali. Wach ymken nchouf lpasspor dyalek, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Of course. Here you are. Is breakfast included?","da":"Wakha. Hak. Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Yes, it is. Breakfast is from seven to ten in the restaurant on the ground floor.","da":"Ah. Lftor men ssb3a 7ta l l3echra f restaurant f ttab9a l'ardiya."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Great. And what time is check-out?","da":"Mzyan. W fo9ach khassni nkhelli lbit?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Check-out is at eleven. Here's your key card. Your room is 305, on the third floor.","da":"Lkhrouj m3a l7dach. Hak lkart dyal lbit. Lbit dyalek howa 305, f ttab9a ttalta."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you. Could I have the Wi-Fi password, please?","da":"Choukran. Wach ymken t3tini lkod dyal lWi-Fi, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Tom","en":"Sure, it's on this card. The lift is on your left. Enjoy your stay!","da":"Wakha, rah mektoub f had lkart. L'assanseur 3la lissr dyalek. Tmetta3i b l'i9ama dyalek!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Thank you very much!","da":"Choukran bzzaf!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"F lmatar w f lotil, kolchi kaymchi b 'adab. Bdaï dima b `Excuse me` wla `Hello`, w sta3mli `Could I…?` / `I'd like…` 3la 9bel `I want`. W ila chi 7aja makhddamach, ma t3eyytich — 9oli b hdou2: `Excuse me, there's a problem with my room.` Hakka ghadi y3awnouk dghya. W 7di lpasspor dyalek dima m3ak — kaytlbouh f kol blassa!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli lkelma dyal ssafar m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"passport","da":"lpasspor","emoji":"🛂"},{"en":"luggage","da":"lbagaj","emoji":"🧳"},{"en":"gate","da":"lbab dyal rrkoub","emoji":"🚪"},{"en":"ticket","da":"ttikiya","emoji":"🎫"},{"en":"key","da":"ssarout","emoji":"🔑"}]},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"The flight is delayed.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno w9e3 l ttiyara?","options":["T3ettlat","Khrjat f lwa9t","Tlghat","Weslat"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`delayed` = mt3ettla. `on time` = f lwa9t. `cancelled` = tlghat."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach t9oli \"bghit\" b 'adab f lotil?","options":["I'd like","I want","I have","I need"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'd like` = `I would like` = bghit (b 'adab). `I want` kat'ban 9ass7a chwiya m3a nnas li makat3rfihomch."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I'd like ___ book a double room, please.","options":["to","for","at"],"answer":"to","hint_da":"`I'd like` + ? + fi3l (`book`).","explain_da":"`I'd like to` + fi3l: `I'd like to book`. `I'd like` + ism direct: `I'd like a room`."},{"type":"order","words":["Is","breakfast","included","in","the","price?"],"answer":"Is breakfast included in the price?","da":"Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?","explain_da":"`Is` + `breakfast` + `included` — so2al b `to be`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Your room is on the third floor.","question_da":"Sem3i. Fin lbit?","options":["F ttab9a ttalta","F ttab9a ttanya","F ttab9a l'oula","F ttab9a rrab3a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`third` = ttalt / ttalta (3). `second` = ttani, `first` = l'ewwel, `fourth` = rrabe3 — dars 11."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"There ___ no hot water in my room.","options":["is","are","have"],"answer":"is","hint_da":"`water` ma kayt3eddch → mofrad.","explain_da":"`There is no hot water` — `water` ism ma kayt3eddch, 3la hadak `is`. `There are no towels` m3a ljam3."},{"type":"mcq","question_en":"What time is check-out?","question_da":"Achmen jawab mnassb l had so2al?","options":["At eleven in the morning.","Breakfast is included.","It's on the second floor.","Two nights, please."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`What time…?` kaysewwel 3la lwa9t → `At eleven`."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"Luggage\" is a countable noun, so you can say \"three luggages\".","statement_da":"`luggage` kayt3edd, 3la hadak n9dro n9oulo `three luggages`.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! `luggage` ma kayt3eddch (bhal `water`). Kan9oulo `my luggage` wla `three bags` / `three suitcases`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"Could I have the Wi-Fi password, please?","da":"Wach ymken t3tini lkod dyal lWi-Fi, 3afak?","explain_da":"`Could I have…?` = talab b 'adab. `password` = lkod ssirri."},{"type":"translate","da":"Bghit n7jez bit l wa7ed l jouj lyali.","answers":["I'd like to book a single room for two nights.","I would like to book a single room for two nights.","I'd like to reserve a single room for two nights.","I would like to reserve a single room for two nights."],"hint_en":"I'd like to ... a ... room for ... nights.","explain_da":"`book` = 7jez. `single room` = bit l wa7ed. `for two nights` = l jouj lyali."},{"type":"order","words":["Excuse","me,","the","Wi-Fi","doesn't","work."],"answer":"Excuse me, the Wi-Fi doesn't work.","da":"Sme7 liya, lWi-Fi makhddamch.","explain_da":"Bdaï b `Excuse me`, men ba3d lmochkil: `the Wi-Fi doesn't work`."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Nti f lmatar. Lmowaddaf kay9oul: `Window or aisle?` — 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["3la lblassa fin bghiti tglsi f ttiyara","3la lbagaj dyalek","3la lpasspor dyalek","3la lwa9t dyal rri7la"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`window seat` = blassa 7da cherjem, `aisle seat` = blassa 7da lmemcha. `aisle` kat9ra \"aïl\" — l `s` ma kat9rach!"},{"type":"translate","da":"Sme7 liya, makaynch lma skhoun f lbit dyali.","answers":["Excuse me, there is no hot water in my room.","Excuse me, there's no hot water in my room.","Sorry, there is no hot water in my room.","Sorry, there's no hot water in my room."],"hint_en":"Excuse me, there ... no ... water in my room.","explain_da":"`There's no hot water` = makaynch lma skhoun. Mochkil → bdaï b `Excuse me`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Hello, I have a reservation for two nights. Is breakfast included?","da":"Salam, 3ndi 7ajz l jouj lyali. Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?","pron":"hé-lo, aï hav a ré-zeur-véy-cheun for tou naïts. iz brèk-feust in-klou-did"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Amina's trip to Istanbul","title_da":"Ssafar dyal Amina l Istanbul","emoji":"🕌","text_en":"Last month, Amina travelled to Istanbul for the first time. She booked her flight and her hotel online, two months before the trip. At Casablanca airport, she went to the check-in desk, showed her passport and got her boarding pass. She asked for a window seat because she wanted to see the sea. The flight was delayed for one hour, so she drank a coffee and read a book. In Istanbul, she took a taxi to the hotel. She had a reservation for a single room for four nights, with breakfast included. The room was small but clean, and it was on the fifth floor, with a beautiful view of the city. On the first night, the Wi-Fi didn't work, so she went to the reception and asked politely for help. The receptionist was very kind and fixed the problem in ten minutes. Amina says it was the best trip of her life.","text_da":"Chhar li fat, Amina saffrat l Istanbul l'awwal merra. 7ejzat rri7la dyalha w lotil dyalha 3la l'internet, jouj chhour 9bel ssafar. F lmatar dyal Casa, mchat l lbiro dyal ttasjil, werrat lpasspor dyalha w khdat lwer9a dyal rrkoub. Tlbat blassa 7da cherjem 7it bghat tchouf lb7er. Ttiyara t3ettlat b sa3a, 3la hadak chrbat 9ehwa w 9rat ktab. F Istanbul, khdat taxi l lotil. Kan 3ndha 7ajz dyal bit l wa7ed l rb3a dyal lyali, w lftor dakhel f ttaman. Lbit kan sghir walakin n9i, w kan f ttab9a lkhamsa, b mandar zwin 3la lmdina. F llila l'oula, lWi-Fi makhdemch, 3la hadak mchat l l'isti9bal w tlbat lmosa3ada b 'adab. Lmowaddaf dyal l'isti9bal kan dérif bzzaf w sle7 lmochkil f 3echra d d9ay9. Amina kat9oul belli kanet a7san ri7la f 7yatha.","glossary":[{"en":"travelled","da":"saffrat"},{"en":"online","da":"3la l'internet"},{"en":"showed","da":"werrat"},{"en":"clean","da":"n9i"},{"en":"view","da":"lmandar"},{"en":"politely","da":"b 'adab"},{"en":"fixed","da":"sle7"},{"en":"trip","da":"rri7la / ssafar"},{"en":"for the first time","da":"l'awwal merra"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach 7ejzat Amina rri7la w lotil?","options":["Jouj chhour 9bel ssafar","Nhar ssafar","F lmatar","Simana 9bel ssafar"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"She booked her flight and her hotel online, two months before the trip.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The flight was on time.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"The flight was delayed for one hour.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach tlbat Amina blassa 7da cherjem?","options":["7it bghat tchouf lb7er","7it bghat tn3es","7it kanet khayfa","7it bghat t9ra ktab"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"She asked for a window seat because she wanted to see the sea.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"The receptionist fixed the Wi-Fi problem in ten minutes.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"The receptionist was very kind and fixed the problem in ten minutes.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"F lbiro dyal ttasjil f lmatar","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i l7iwar f lmatar. Rekkzi 3la: ch7al men chanta 3nd Omar? w men achmen bab ghadi yrkeb?","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Good morning. Where are you flying to today?","da":"Sbah lkhir. L fin ghadi tsafer lyouma?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good morning. To London. Here's my passport and my ticket.","da":"Sbah lkhir. L London. Hak lpasspor dyali w ttikiya dyali."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Thank you. How many bags do you have?","da":"Choukran. Ch7al men chanta 3ndek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Two. One big suitcase and one small bag for hand luggage.","da":"Jouj. Wa7ed chanta kbira w wa7ed ssak sghir ndkhlo m3aya f ttiyara."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"OK. Would you like a window seat or an aisle seat?","da":"Wakha. Wach bghiti blassa 7da cherjem wla 7da lmemcha?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"An aisle seat, please. Is the flight on time?","da":"7da lmemcha, 3afak. Wach ttiyara f lwa9t?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"I'm afraid it's delayed by thirty minutes. Here's your boarding pass. Your gate is B4, and boarding starts at 10:20.","da":"M3a l'asaf mt3ettla b tlatin d9i9a. Hak lwer9a dyal rrkoub dyalek. Lbab dyalek howa B4, w rrkoub kaybda m3a l3echra w 3echrin."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Thank you. Where is gate B4?","da":"Choukran. Fin lbab B4?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Go through security, then turn right. It's at the end. Have a good flight!","da":"Douz men lmora9aba, 3ad dor 3la limen. Rah f l'akhir. Ri7la sa3ida!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"L fin ghadi ysafer Omar?","options":["L London","L Paris","L Madrid","L Istanbul"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"To London.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Ch7al men chanta 3ndo?","options":["Jouj","Wa7da","Tlata","Walou"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Two. One big suitcase and one small bag.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I'm afraid it's delayed by thirty minutes.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat9oul lmowaddafa?","options":["Ttiyara mt3ettla b tlatin d9i9a","Ttiyara f lwa9t","Ttiyara khrjat","Ttiyara mt3ettla b sa3a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I'm afraid…` = m3a l'asaf (machi \"khayfa\"!). `delayed by thirty minutes` = mt3ettla b 30 d9i9a."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar wants a window seat.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"An aisle seat, please.\""}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"I'd like to book a room, please.","da":"Bghit n7jez bit, 3afak.","pron":"aïd laïk tou bouk a roum, pliz"},{"target_en":"Here's my passport.","da":"Hak lpasspor dyali.","pron":"hirz maï pas-port"},{"target_en":"Is breakfast included?","da":"Wach lftor dakhel f ttaman?","pron":"iz brèk-feust in-klou-did"},{"target_en":"What time is check-out?","da":"Fo9ach khassni nkhelli lbit?","pron":"wat taïm iz tchèk-awt"},{"target_en":"Could I have another towel, please?","da":"Wach ymken t3tini fouta khra, 3afak?","pron":"koud aï hav a-neu-theur ta-weul, pliz"},{"target_en":"The flight is delayed.","da":"Ttiyara mt3ettla.","pron":"the flaït iz di-léyd"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"F l'isti9bal dyal lotil","context_da":"Weslti l wa7ed lotil f Agadir. Lmowaddaf dyal l'isti9bal ghadi yhder m3ak. Jawbi b 'adab, w f l'akhir chekiwi mochkil f lbit!","turns":[{"bot_en":"Good evening! Welcome. How can I help you?","bot_da":"Msa lkhir! Mer7ba. Kifach n9der n3awnek?","expect_keywords":["reservation","booked","i'd like","i would like","a room","check in","my name"],"sample_en":"Good evening. I have a reservation. My name is Nouha."},{"bot_en":"Let me see… Yes. A single room for two nights. Could I see your passport, please?","bot_da":"Khellini nchouf… Ah. Bit l wa7ed l jouj lyali. Wach ymken nchouf lpasspor dyalek, 3afak?","expect_keywords":["here","of course","sure","yes","passport"],"sample_en":"Of course. Here you are."},{"bot_en":"Thank you. Do you have any questions?","bot_da":"Choukran. Wach 3ndek chi so2al?","expect_keywords":["breakfast","included","check-out","check out","what time","wi-fi","wifi","password","could i"],"sample_en":"Yes. Is breakfast included? And what time is check-out?"},{"bot_en":"Breakfast is included, from seven to ten, and check-out is at eleven. Here's your key.","bot_da":"Lftor dakhel f ttaman, men ssb3a 7ta l l3echra, w lkhrouj m3a l7dach. Hak ssarout dyalek.","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","great","ok","okay","perfect"],"sample_en":"Great, thank you."},{"bot_en":"Is everything OK with your room?","bot_da":"Wach kolchi mzyan f lbit dyalek?","expect_keywords":["doesn't work","no hot water","problem","too noisy","too cold","wi-fi","wifi","excuse me","there's no","there is no"],"sample_en":"Excuse me, there's a problem. The Wi-Fi doesn't work."},{"bot_en":"I'm very sorry about that. I'll send someone right away.","bot_da":"Sme7 liya bzzaf 3la hadchi. Ghadi nsift chi wa7ed daba daba.","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","ok","okay","no problem"],"sample_en":"Thank you very much."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ssafar dyali","prompt_da":"Ktbi 50 kelma 3la wa7ed ssafar (7a9i9i wla khayali): fin mchiti w m3a men, kifach daz lmatar (`check-in`, `flight`), kifach kan lotil (`room`, `breakfast`), w wach kan chi mochkil. Sta3mli lmadi (`went`, `was`, `booked`) w lkelmat dyal had dars.","helper_en":["Last year, I went to ...","I booked a ... room for ... nights.","At the airport, ...","The hotel was ...","There was a problem: ..."],"min_words":50,"keywords":["hotel","room"],"model_en":"Last summer, I went to Istanbul with my sister. We booked our flight and a double room for five nights online. At the airport, we checked in and got our boarding passes. The flight was delayed by one hour, but it was OK. The hotel was small and clean, and breakfast was included. On the first day, there was a problem: the air conditioning in our room didn't work. We went to the reception and the receptionist changed our room. The new room was bigger and quieter. It was a wonderful trip!"}},{"id":"l23","order":23,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"📱","title_en":"Phone calls, messages & emails","title_da":"Ttilifoun, lmessajat w l'emails","goals_da":["Tjawbi 3la ttilifoun w t9eddmi rassek: `Hello, this is Nouha`","Ttelbi chi wa7ed f ttilifoun: `Can I speak to…?`, `Hold on, please`, `Can I take a message?`","Tsewli b 'adab b `Could you tell me…?` w `Do you know…?`","Tktbi `message` wla `email` 9sir: `Hi…` / `Dear…`, `I'm writing to…`, `Best regards`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"F ttilifoun — kifach njawbo w n9eddmo rassna","body_da":"F ttilifoun, lingliziya kattbeddel chwiya. Bach t9oli chkoun nti, **ma t9olich** `I'm Nouha` — 9oli: `Hello, this is Nouha.` wla `It's Nouha.` (`this is` hna = ana / hadi).\n\nBach tsewli chkoun kay3eyyet: `Who's calling, please?` = chkoun m3aya, 3afak?\n\nBach ttelbi chi wa7ed:\n\n- `Can I speak to Sarah, please?` = wach ymken nhder m3a Sarah?\n- `Could I speak to Mr. Brown, please?` — `Could` 'adab kter (f lkhedma, m3a nnas li makat3rfihomch).\n\nLjawab:\n\n- `Speaking.` = ana hiya / ana howa (7arfiyan: \"kanhder\"). Kat9al melli nti bnefsek li kaytleb lik.\n- `Hold on, please.` / `Just a moment, please.` = tsenna chwiya, 3afak.\n- `I'll put you through.` = ghadi nwesslek (lih / liha).\n- `Sorry, she's not here right now.` = sme7 liya, hiya makaynach daba. `He's in a meeting.` = rah f ijtima3.\n\nBhal f darija: \"Allo, chkoun m3aya?\" → `Hello, who's calling?`","examples":[{"en":"Hello, this is Nouha. Can I speak to Sarah, please?","da":"Allo, ana Nouha. Wach ymken nhder m3a Sarah, 3afak?","pron":"hé-lo, this iz nou-ha. kan aï spik tou sé-ra, pliz"},{"en":"Speaking!","da":"Ana hiya! (ana li kanhder)","pron":"spi-king"},{"en":"Hold on, please. I'll put you through.","da":"Tsenna chwiya, 3afak. Ghadi nwesslek.","pron":"hold on, pliz. aïl pout you throu"},{"en":"Who's calling, please?","da":"Chkoun m3aya, 3afak?","pron":"houz ko-ling, pliz"},{"en":"Sorry, she's not here right now.","da":"Sme7 liya, hiya makaynach daba.","pron":"so-ri, chiz not hir raït naw"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Khelli message, 3awdi 3eyyti, wla… nnemra ghalta!","body_da":"Ila chkhss makaynch:\n\n- Li jaweb kay9oul: `Can I take a message?` = wach bghiti tkhelli `message`?\n- Nti kat9oli: `Can I leave a message?` = wach n9der nkhelli `message`? wla `Could you ask her to call me back?` = wach ymken t9oul liha t3awed t3eyyet liya?\n- Wla: `No, thank you. I'll call back later.` = la, choukran, ghadi n3awed n3eyyet men ba3d. (`call back` = 3awed 3eyyet.)\n\nIla ghlti f nnemra: `Sorry, I think you have the wrong number.` wla b 9sar: `Sorry, wrong number.`\n\nLmachakil f lkhett:\n\n- `Sorry, I can't hear you.` = sme7 liya, ma kansme3kch.\n- `The line is bad.` = rrizo khayb.\n- `Could you speak up, please?` = wach ymken t3elli sotek? / `Could you repeat that, please?` (dars 2).\n\nBach tsaliw: `Thanks for calling. Bye!` = choukran 3la l'ittisal. Bslama!","examples":[{"en":"She's not here. Can I take a message?","da":"Hiya makaynach. Wach bghiti tkhelli message?","pron":"chiz not hir. kan aï téyk a mè-sidj"},{"en":"No, thank you. I'll call back later.","da":"La, choukran. Ghadi n3awed n3eyyet men ba3d.","pron":"no, thank you. aïl kol bak léy-teur"},{"en":"Could you ask him to call me back?","da":"Wach ymken t9oul lih y3awed y3eyyet liya?","pron":"koud you ask him tou kol mi bak"},{"en":"Sorry, I think you have the wrong number.","da":"Sme7 liya, kandenn ghlti f nnemra.","pron":"so-ri, aï think you hav the rong neum-beur"},{"en":"Sorry, I can't hear you. The line is bad.","da":"Sme7 liya, ma kansme3kch. Rrizo khayb.","pron":"so-ri, aï kant hir you. the laïn iz bad"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Could you tell me…? / Do you know…? — so2al b 'adab","body_da":"Bach tsewli chi wa7ed makat3rfihch b 'adab, l'ingliz kaydiro so2al dakhel so2al:\n\n- `Where is the bank?` → `Could you tell me where the bank is?` = wach ymken t9oul liya fin kayna lbanka?\n- `Where is the bank?` → `Do you know where the bank is?` = wach kat3ref fin kayna lbanka?\n\n**Redi lbal l ttartib:** men ba3d `Could you tell me…` / `Do you know…`, lfi3l kaymchi l **l'akhir**, bhal jomla 3adiya, machi bhal so2al: `where the bank is` (machi \"where is the bank\").\n\nM3a l7adir lbassit, `do` / `does` kaytmse7: `What time does the shop open?` → `Do you know what time the shop opens?` (lfi3l kayakhod `-s`).\n\nSo2al dyal `wach` (`yes` / `no`) → kanzido `if`: `Is Sarah there?` → `Could you tell me if Sarah is there?`\n\nF darija 3ndna nefs lfikra: \"Wach t9der t9oul liya fin kayna lbanka?\" — sahla 3lik!","examples":[{"en":"Could you tell me where the bank is?","da":"Wach ymken t9oul liya fin kayna lbanka?","pron":"koud you tèl mi wér the bank iz"},{"en":"Do you know what time the shop opens?","da":"Wach kat3ref fo9ach kay7el l7anout?","pron":"dou you no wat taïm the chop o-peunz"},{"en":"Could you tell me when she'll be back?","da":"Wach ymken t9oul liya fo9ach ghadi trje3?","pron":"koud you tèl mi wèn chil bi bak"},{"en":"Do you know if Mr. Brown is in the office today?","da":"Wach kat3ref wach ssi Brown kayn f lbiro lyouma?","pron":"dou you no if mis-teur brawn iz in the o-fis tou-déy"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Kifach tktbi message wla email 9sir","body_da":"`email` wla `message` 9sir 3ndo 4 ajza2:\n\n**1. Tta7iya:** m3a s7ab: `Hi Sarah,` / `Hello Omar,`. Rasmi (lkhedma, l'idara): `Dear Mr. Brown,` / `Dear Ms. Alami,`. Ila makat3rfich smiyt chkhss: `Dear Sir or Madam,`.\n\n**2. 3lach katktbi:** rasmi: `I'm writing to ask about…` = kanktb lik bach nsewwel 3la…, `I'm writing to confirm…` = bach n'akked… M3a s7ab: `Just a quick message to say…` = ghir `message` 9sir bach n9oul… W bach tchekri: `Thank you for your email / your help.`\n\n**3. Ttalab:** `Could you send me…?` = wach ymken tsift liya…? / `Could you tell me if…?`\n\n**4. Lkhtam:** rasmi: `Best regards,` / `Kind regards,` + smiytek. M3a s7ab: `See you soon!` / `Take care!` / `Love,` (ghir m3a l3a2ila w s7ab 9rab bzzaf).\n\nF lmessajat m3a s7ab, kaynin ikhtisarat: `thx` = `thanks`, `pls` = `please`, `u` = `you`, `CU` = `see you`, `ASAP` = `as soon as possible` (f a9rab wa9t), `btw` = `by the way` (bilmonassaba). **Ma tsta3mlihomch f `email` rasmi!**","examples":[{"en":"Dear Mr. Brown, I'm writing to ask about the English course.","da":"Ssi Brown lmo7taram, kanktb lik bach nsewwel 3la dawra dyal lingliziya.","pron":"dir mis-teur brawn, aïm raï-ting tou ask a-bawt the in-glich kors"},{"en":"Thank you for your help. Best regards, Nouha","da":"Choukran 3la lmosa3ada dyalek. M3a a7san tta7iyat, Nouha","pron":"thank you for your hèlp. bèst ri-gardz, nou-ha"},{"en":"Hi Sarah, just a quick message to say thank you for yesterday. See you soon!","da":"Ahlan Sarah, ghir message 9sir bach n9oul lik choukran 3la lbare7. Nchoufouk 9rib!","pron":"haï sé-ra, djeust a kwik mè-sidj tou séy thank you for yès-teur-déy. si you soun"},{"en":"Could you send me the address, please?","da":"Wach ymken tsift liya l3onwan, 3afak?","pron":"koud you sènd mi the a-drès, pliz"},{"en":"Thx! CU tomorrow :)","da":"Choukran! Nchoufouk ghedda :) (ghir m3a s7ab)","pron":"thanks! si you tou-mo-ro"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"phone call","da":"mokalama (f ttilifoun)","emoji":"📞","pron":"fon kol","example_en":"I have to make a phone call.","example_da":"Khassni ndir mokalama."},{"en":"to call","da":"t3eyyti (f ttilifoun)","emoji":"📲","pron":"tou kol","example_en":"Call me tomorrow.","example_da":"3eyyet liya ghedda."},{"en":"to call back","da":"t3awdi t3eyyti","emoji":"🔁","pron":"tou kol bak","example_en":"I'll call back later.","example_da":"Ghadi n3awed n3eyyet men ba3d."},{"en":"message","da":"message / risala","emoji":"💬","pron":"mè-sidj","example_en":"Can I take a message?","example_da":"Wach bghiti tkhelli message?"},{"en":"text message","da":"SMS / message mektoub","emoji":"✉️","pron":"tèkst mè-sidj","example_en":"Send me a text message.","example_da":"Sift liya SMS."},{"en":"to hold on","da":"ttsennay chwiya (f lkhett)","emoji":"⏸️","pron":"tou hold on","example_en":"Hold on, please.","example_da":"Tsenna chwiya, 3afak."},{"en":"wrong number","da":"nnemra ghalta","emoji":"❌","pron":"rong neum-beur","example_en":"Sorry, wrong number.","example_da":"Sme7 liya, nnemra ghalta."},{"en":"line","da":"lkhett / rrizo","emoji":"📶","pron":"laïn","example_en":"The line is bad.","example_da":"Rrizo khayb."},{"en":"busy","da":"mechghoul (lkhett wla chkhss)","emoji":"🔴","pron":"bi-zi","example_en":"The line is busy.","example_da":"Lkhett mechghoul."},{"en":"to speak to","da":"thedri m3a","emoji":"🗣️","pron":"tou spik tou","example_en":"Can I speak to Sarah?","example_da":"Wach ymken nhder m3a Sarah?"},{"en":"email","da":"email","emoji":"📧","pron":"i-méyl","example_en":"Send me an email.","example_da":"Sift liya email."},{"en":"to send","da":"tsifti","emoji":"📤","pron":"tou sènd","example_en":"Could you send me the photo?","example_da":"Wach ymken tsift liya ttaswira?"},{"en":"to reply","da":"tjawbi (3la message wla email)","emoji":"↩️","pron":"tou ri-plaï","example_en":"Please reply before Friday.","example_da":"3afak jawbi 9bel ljem3a."},{"en":"Dear…","da":"(bdaya dyal email rasmi) … lmo7taram / lmo7tarama","emoji":"📝","pron":"dir","example_en":"Dear Mr. Brown,","example_da":"Ssi Brown lmo7taram,"},{"en":"Best regards","da":"m3a a7san tta7iyat (khtam dyal email rasmi)","emoji":"🙏","pron":"bèst ri-gardz","example_en":"Best regards, Nouha","example_da":"M3a a7san tta7iyat, Nouha"},{"en":"See you soon","da":"nchoufouk 9rib (khtam m3a s7ab)","emoji":"👋","pron":"si you soun","example_en":"Bye! See you soon!","example_da":"Bslama! Nchoufouk 9rib!"}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Mokalama l lmedrasa dyal lloghat","context_da":"Nouha kat3eyyet l lmedrasa dyal lloghat bach thder m3a l'oustad dyalha, ssi Brown. Laila, lmowaddafa dyal l'isti9bal, hiya li jawbat.","lines":[{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Good morning, Atlas Language School. Laila speaking. How can I help you?","da":"Sbah lkhir, Atlas Language School. Laila m3ak. Kifach n9der n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Good morning. This is Nouha Alami. Could I speak to Mr. Brown, please?","da":"Sbah lkhir. Ana Nouha Alami. Wach ymken nhder m3a ssi Brown, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"I'm sorry, he's in a meeting right now. Can I take a message?","da":"Sme7 liya, rah f ijtima3 daba. Wach bghiti tkhelli message?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, please. Could you ask him to call me back? It's about the exam on Friday.","da":"Ah, 3afak. Wach ymken t9oli lih y3awed y3eyyet liya? Lmawdou3 howa l'imti7an dyal ljem3a."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Of course. Could you give me your phone number, please?","da":"Wakha. Wach ymken t3tini nnemra dyalek, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, it's 06 61 23 45 78.","da":"Ah, hiya 06 61 23 45 78."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Sorry, I didn't hear the last part. Could you repeat that, please?","da":"Sme7 liya, masme3tch l'akhir. Wach ymken t3awdi, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Sure. 06 61 23 45 78.","da":"Wakha. 06 61 23 45 78."},{"speaker":"Laila","en":"Thank you, Nouha. He'll call you back this afternoon.","da":"Choukran, Nouha. Ghadi y3awed y3eyyet lik had l3chiya."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Great, thank you very much. Goodbye!","da":"Mzyan, choukran bzzaf. Bslama!"}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"F ttilifoun ma kanchoufouch lwjeh, 3la hadak l'adab kaybyen f lkelmat: `please`, `Could you…?`, `Thanks for calling`. W ila ma fhemtich, 9oli bla 7chouma: `Sorry, could you speak more slowly, please?` — 7ta l'ingliz kay9oulouha! W f lmessajat m3a s7ab, `thx`, `pls`, `CU` 3adi, walakin f `email` rasmi ktbi lkelmat kamlin: `Thank you`, `please`."}],"exercises":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"F ttilifoun, kifach t9oli \"ana Nouha\"?","options":["Hello, this is Nouha.","Hello, I'm Nouha here.","Hello, here Nouha.","Hello, me Nouha."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"F ttilifoun kan9oulo `This is Nouha` wla `It's Nouha`, machi `I'm Nouha`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Sorry, she's in a meeting right now.","question_da":"Sem3i. 3lach Sarah ma t9derch thder daba?","options":["7it hiya f ijtima3","7it hiya f ssafar","7it nnemra ghalta","7it rrizo khayb"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`She's in a meeting right now.` = hiya f ijtima3 daba. `right now` = daba daba."},{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli ljomla dyal ttilifoun m3a lma3na dyalha.","pairs":[{"en":"Speaking.","da":"Ana hiya (ana li kanhder)","emoji":"🗣️"},{"en":"Hold on, please.","da":"Tsenna chwiya, 3afak","emoji":"⏸️"},{"en":"Wrong number.","da":"Nnemra ghalta","emoji":"❌"},{"en":"Can I take a message?","da":"Wach bghiti tkhelli message?","emoji":"💬"},{"en":"I'll put you through.","da":"Ghadi nwesslek (lih / liha)","emoji":"🔀"}]},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Can I ___ to Sarah, please?","options":["speak","say","tell"],"answer":"speak","hint_da":"Nhder m3a = `speak to`.","explain_da":"`speak to` + chkhss. `say` w `tell` ma kaymchiwch hna."},{"type":"order","words":["Could","you","ask","her","to","call","me","back?"],"answer":"Could you ask her to call me back?","da":"Wach ymken t9oul liha t3awed t3eyyet liya?","explain_da":"`Could you ask` + chkhss + `to` + fi3l. `call me back` = 3awed 3eyyet liya."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Sorry, I think you have the wrong number.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno lmochkil?","options":["Ghlti f nnemra","Lkhett khayb","Hiya f ijtima3","Makaynch chi mochkil"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`wrong number` = nnemra ghalta. `I think` = kandenn."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Khtari so2al b 'adab s7i7:","options":["Could you tell me where the bank is?","Could you tell me where is the bank?","Could you tell me where the bank?","Could you tell me where does the bank is?"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"Men ba3d `Could you tell me…`, lfi3l kaymchi l l'akhir: `where the bank is` — bhal jomla 3adiya, machi so2al."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Do you know what time the shop ___?","options":["opens","open","does open"],"answer":"opens","hint_da":"So2al indirect: bla `does`, w lfi3l m3a `the shop` (= `it`).","explain_da":"F so2al indirect makaynch `does`: `what time the shop opens` — lfi3l kayakhod `-s` 7it `the shop` = `it`."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"You can write \"Dear Sir or Madam\" when you don't know the name of the person.","statement_da":"T9edri tktbi `Dear Sir or Madam` melli makat3rfich smiyt chkhss.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7! `Dear Sir or Madam` = bdaya rasmiya melli makat3rfich l'ism. Ila kat3rfih: `Dear Mr. Brown`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"I'll call back later.","da":"Ghadi n3awed n3eyyet men ba3d.","explain_da":"`I'll` = `I will` (9arar daba, dars 19). `call back` = 3awed 3eyyet. `later` = men ba3d."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach ymken nhder m3a ssi Brown, 3afak?","answers":["Could I speak to Mr. Brown, please?","Can I speak to Mr. Brown, please?","May I speak to Mr. Brown, please?","Could I speak with Mr. Brown, please?","Can I speak with Mr. Brown, please?"],"hint_en":"Could I ... to Mr. Brown, ...?","explain_da":"`Could I speak to…?` = b 'adab kter men `Can I…?`. Bjouj s7a7."},{"type":"order","words":["Do","you","know","where","the","station","is?"],"answer":"Do you know where the station is?","da":"Wach kat3ref fin kayna lma7atta?","explain_da":"So2al indirect: `Do you know` + `where` + `the station` + `is` — lfi3l f l'akhir."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Nti katktbi `email` rasmi l lmoudir dyal cherika. Kifach tkemmlih?","options":["Best regards, Nouha","CU! Nouha","Love, Nouha","Bye bye, Nouha"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"F `email` rasmi: `Best regards` wla `Kind regards`. `CU`, `Love` ghir m3a s7ab w l3a2ila."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"Thank you ___ your email.","answers":["for"],"hint_da":"Choukran 3la… = `Thank you` + ?","explain_da":"`Thank you for` + ism: `Thank you for your email`, `Thank you for your help`."},{"type":"translate","da":"Kanktb lik bach nsewwel 3la dawra dyal lingliziya.","answers":["I am writing to ask about the English course.","I'm writing to ask about the English course.","I am writing to ask you about the English course.","I'm writing to ask you about the English course."],"hint_en":"I'm ... to ask about the ... course.","explain_da":"`I'm writing to…` = kanktb lik bach… — bdaya rasmiya dyal `email`."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"Hello, this is Nouha. Could I speak to Sarah, please?","da":"Allo, ana Nouha. Wach ymken nhder m3a Sarah, 3afak?","pron":"hé-lo, this iz nou-ha. koud aï spik tou sé-ra, pliz"}],"reading":{"title_en":"An email from the school","title_da":"Email men lmedrasa","emoji":"📧","text_en":"Dear Ms. Alami,\n\nThank you for your email about our English course. I'm writing to confirm your place in the evening class. The course starts on Monday, 3 March, at 6 p.m. and finishes at 8 p.m. The lessons are on Mondays and Wednesdays, in room 4 on the second floor. You don't have to buy a book, because we give you all the materials on the first day. Could you send me a copy of your ID card before Friday, please? We need it for your student card.\n\nIf you have any questions, you can call the school between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m., or you can send me a message on WhatsApp. If I'm not in the office, my colleague Laila can take a message and I'll call you back.\n\nI look forward to meeting you.\n\nBest regards,\nDavid Brown\nDirector, Atlas Language School","text_da":"Ssayida Alami lmo7tarama,\n\nChoukran 3la l'email dyalek 3la dawra dyal lingliziya dyalna. Kanktb lik bach n'akked lblassa dyalek f l9ism dyal l3chiya. Ddawra katbda nhar ttnin 3 mars, m3a ssetta dyal l3chiya, w katsali m3a ttmenya. Ddorous nhar ttnin w nhar larb3, f l9a3a 4 f ttab9a ttanya. Makhasskch tchri ktab, 7it kan3tiwk ga3 lwata2i9 f l'awwal nhar. Wach ymken tsifti liya noskha dyal lkart lwataniya dyalek 9bel ljem3a, 3afak? Khassna-ha l lkart dyal ttalib dyalek.\n\nIla 3ndek chi so2al, t9edri t3eyyti l lmedrasa bin tts3oud dyal sbah w lkhemsa dyal l3chiya, wla tsifti liya message f WhatsApp. Ila makontch f lbiro, zmilti Laila t9der takhod lmessage w ana n3awed n3eyyet lik.\n\nMetchewwe9 bach ntla9a bik.\n\nM3a a7san tta7iyat,\nDavid Brown\nLmoudir, Atlas Language School","glossary":[{"en":"to confirm","da":"t'akked"},{"en":"place","da":"blassa"},{"en":"materials","da":"lwata2i9 w lktouba dyal ddars"},{"en":"a copy","da":"noskha"},{"en":"ID card","da":"lkart lwataniya"},{"en":"colleague","da":"zmil / zmila f lkhedma"},{"en":"I look forward to meeting you","da":"metchewwe9 bach ntla9a bik"},{"en":"director","da":"lmoudir"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"3lach kayktb ssi Brown had `email`?","options":["Bach y'akked lblassa dyal Nouha f ddawra","Bach ylghi ddawra","Bach ytleb lflous","Bach y3eyyet l Nouha"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I'm writing to confirm your place in the evening class.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Nouha has to buy a book for the course.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"You don't have to buy a book, because we give you all the materials.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno khass Nouha tsift 9bel ljem3a?","options":["Noskha dyal lkart lwataniya","Noskha dyal ddiplom","Taswira","Lflous dyal ddawra"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Could you send me a copy of your ID card before Friday, please?\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"If Mr. Brown is not in the office, Laila can take a message.","answer":true,"explain_da":"S7i7: \"my colleague Laila can take a message and I'll call you back.\""}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Mokalama l cherika dyal ssafar","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"Sem3i lmokalama. Rekkzi 3la: m3a men bgha yhder Omar? w fo9ach ghadi yrje3 dak chkhss?","lines":[{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Good afternoon, Sahara Travel. How can I help you?","da":"Msa lkhir, Sahara Travel. Kifach n9der n3awnek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Good afternoon. This is Omar Idrissi. Could I speak to Mr. Brown, please?","da":"Msa lkhir. Ana Omar Idrissi. Wach ymken nhder m3a ssi Brown, 3afak?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"I'm sorry, Mr. Brown isn't in the office this afternoon.","da":"Sme7 liya, ssi Brown makaynch f lbiro had l3chiya."},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Oh. Could you tell me when he'll be back?","da":"Ah. Wach ymken t9oli liya fo9ach ghadi yrje3?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"He'll be back tomorrow morning at nine. Would you like to leave a message?","da":"Ghadi yrje3 ghedda f sbah m3a tts3oud. Wach bghiti tkhelli message?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, please. It's about my ticket to Istanbul. Could you ask him to call me back?","da":"Ah, 3afak. Lmawdou3 howa ttikiya dyali l Istanbul. Wach ymken t9oli lih y3awed y3eyyet liya?"},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Of course. What's your number?","da":"Wakha. Chno hiya nnemra dyalek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"It's 06 12 34 56 78.","da":"Hiya 06 12 34 56 78."},{"speaker":"Amina","en":"Thank you, Mr. Idrissi. I'll give him the message. Goodbye!","da":"Choukran, ssi Idrissi. Ghadi n3ti lih lmessage. Bslama!"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"M3a men bgha yhder Omar?","options":["M3a ssi Brown","M3a Amina","M3a lmoudir dyal lotil","M3a Laila"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"Could I speak to Mr. Brown, please?\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach ghadi yrje3 ssi Brown?","options":["Ghedda f sbah m3a tts3oud","Had l3chiya","Ghedda f l3chiya","Men ba3d sa3a"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"He'll be back tomorrow morning at nine.\""},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Would you like to leave a message?","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat9tare7 Amina?","options":["Ykhelli message","Y3awed y3eyyet","Yji l lbiro","Ysift email"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`leave a message` = khelli `message`. `Would you like to…?` = wach bghiti…?"},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Omar is calling about a hotel reservation.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"It's about my ticket to Istanbul.\""}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Hello, this is Nouha.","da":"Allo, ana Nouha.","pron":"hé-lo, this iz nou-ha"},{"target_en":"Can I speak to Omar, please?","da":"Wach ymken nhder m3a Omar, 3afak?","pron":"kan aï spik tou o-mar, pliz"},{"target_en":"Hold on, please.","da":"Tsenna chwiya, 3afak.","pron":"hold on, pliz"},{"target_en":"Can I take a message?","da":"Wach bghiti tkhelli message?","pron":"kan aï téyk a mè-sidj"},{"target_en":"Sorry, wrong number.","da":"Sme7 liya, nnemra ghalta.","pron":"so-ri, rong neum-beur"},{"target_en":"Could you tell me where the station is?","da":"Wach ymken t9oul liya fin kayna lma7atta?","pron":"koud you tèl mi wér the stéy-cheun iz"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Mokalama: kat9elbi 3la Sarah","context_da":"Kat3eyyti l ddar dyal Sarah, sa7btek. Khoha Tom howa li jaweb. Sarah makaynach — khelli `message`!","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hello?","bot_da":"Allo?","expect_keywords":["hello","this is","it's","speak to","sarah","is sarah"],"sample_en":"Hello, this is Nouha. Can I speak to Sarah, please?"},{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha. This is Tom, Sarah's brother. Sorry, she's not here right now. Can I take a message?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha. Ana Tom, khou Sarah. Sme7 liya, hiya makaynach daba. Wach bghiti tkhelli `message`?","expect_keywords":["yes","please","tell her","ask her","call me back","message"],"sample_en":"Yes, please. Could you ask her to call me back?"},{"bot_en":"Of course. Could you tell me what it's about?","bot_da":"Wakha. Wach ymken t9oli liya 3la ach lmawdou3?","expect_keywords":["about","it's about","tomorrow","class","meeting","party","homework"],"sample_en":"It's about our English class tomorrow."},{"bot_en":"OK. And what's your phone number?","bot_da":"Wakha. W chno hiya nnemra dyalek?","expect_keywords":["it's","my number","zero","0","six","06"],"sample_en":"It's 06 61 23 45 78."},{"bot_en":"Sorry, the line is bad. Could you repeat that, please?","bot_da":"Sme7 liya, rrizo khayb. Wach ymken t3awdi, 3afak?","expect_keywords":["sure","of course","yes","zero","0","six","06","it's"],"sample_en":"Sure. 06 61 23 45 78."},{"bot_en":"Got it, thanks. I'll give her the message. Bye!","bot_da":"Wakha, choukran. Ghadi n3ti liha lmessage. Bslama!","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","bye","goodbye","see you"],"sample_en":"Thank you, Tom. Goodbye!"}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Email 9sir l l'oustad","prompt_da":"Ktbi `email` 9sir (50 kelma) l ssi Brown, l'oustad dyalek: 9oli lih belli ma ghadich tjiy l l7issa dyal nhar larb3 (3lach?), sewlih b 'adab 3la lwajib (`homework`) wla 3la l'imti7an, w chekrih. Bdaï b `Dear Mr. Brown,` w kemmli b `Best regards,`.","helper_en":["Dear Mr. Brown,","I'm writing to tell you that ...","Could you tell me ...?","Thank you for ...","Best regards,"],"min_words":50,"keywords":["dear","regards"],"model_en":"Dear Mr. Brown,\n\nI'm writing to tell you that I can't come to the class on Wednesday, because I have a job interview in Rabat. I'm sorry about that. Could you tell me what the homework is for next week? And do you know if the exam is on Friday or on Monday? Thank you for your help and for your patience with my English.\n\nBest regards,\nNouha Alami"}},{"id":"l24","order":24,"level":"A2.2","emoji":"🏆","title_en":"Have you ever…? Present perfect & big review","title_da":"Wach 3emrek…? Lmoraja3a lkbira","goals_da":["Thedri 3la ttajarib dyal 7yatek b `have/has` + `past participle`: `I have been to Spain`","Tsewli w tjawbi 3la `Have you ever…?` b `Yes, I have` / `No, never`","Tferr9i bin `been` w `gone`, w bin `present perfect` w `past simple`","T3awdi l'ahamm no9at dyal A1 w A2: `to be`, `present simple`, `past simple`, `going to`, `comparatives`"],"sections":[{"type":"explain","title_da":"Present perfect — ttajarib dyal l7ayat","body_da":"Melli kanhedro 3la 7aja derniha f 7yatna **bla ma n9oulo fo9ach**, kansta3mlo `present perfect`: `have` / `has` + `past participle` (ttasrif ttalet dyal lfi3l).\n\n- L'af3al l3adiya: `past participle` = nefs lforma dyal lmadi b `-ed`: `visited`, `tried`, `worked`.\n- L'af3al li machi 3adiya (7fedihom!): `be → been`, `see → seen`, `eat → eaten`, `go → gone`, `meet → met`, `do → done`, `have → had`, `drink → drunk`, `read → read`, `write → written`, `take → taken`.\n\nL'amtila: `I have visited Fes.` = zert Fes (f 7yati, chi merra — fo9ach? machi mohimm). `She has eaten sushi.` = hiya sb9 liha klat sushi.\n\nL'ikhtisar: `I've`, `you've`, `we've`, `they've` / `he's`, `she's` (hna `'s` = `has`!).\n\nNnafi: `haven't` / `hasn't`: `I haven't seen that film.` = ma cheftch dak lfilm (7ta daba).\n\nF darija kan9oulo \"sb9 liya…\" wla \"3emmerni ma…\": `I have tried couscous with fish.` = sb9 liya klit lkesksou b l7out.","examples":[{"en":"I have visited Fes three times.","da":"Zert Fes tlata dyal lmerrat (f 7yati).","pron":"aï hav vi-zi-tid fès thri taïmz"},{"en":"She has eaten Japanese food.","da":"Hiya sb9 liha klat lmakla lyabaniya.","pron":"chi haz i-teun dja-pa-niz foud"},{"en":"We've seen that film twice.","da":"Chefna dak lfilm jouj merrat.","pron":"wiv sin that film twaïs"},{"en":"I haven't met his wife.","da":"Ma tla9itch mrato (7ta daba).","pron":"aï ha-veunt mèt hiz waïf"},{"en":"They've never tried camel meat.","da":"3emmerhom ma jerrbo l7em jjmel.","pron":"théyv né-veur traïd ka-meul mit"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Have you ever…? — Wach 3emrek…?","body_da":"`ever` = chi merra f 7yatek (kayji f so2al): `Have you ever been to Spain?` = wach 3emrek mchiti l Spanya?\n\nLjawab l9sir:\n\n- `Yes, I have.` = ah, sb9 liya.\n- `No, I haven't.` = la, 3emmerni.\n- `No, never.` = la, 3emmerni (walou).\n\n`never` = 3emmer… ma. Hiya b rassha nafiya, 3la hadak **ma kanzidouch** `not`: `I have never been to Spain.` (machi \"I haven't never\").\n\nM3a `he/she`: `Has she ever…?` → `Yes, she has.` / `No, she hasn't.`\n\n`been to` = mchit l (w rje3t): `I've been to Spain.` Dima m3a `to`: `been to Spain`, `been to the cinema`.\n\nBhal f darija: \"Wach 3emrek…?\" → \"3emmerni!\" wla \"Ah, sb9 liya.\" Sahla, yak?","examples":[{"en":"Have you ever been to Spain?","da":"Wach 3emrek mchiti l Spanya?","pron":"hav you é-veur bin tou spéyn"},{"en":"Yes, I have. I went there in 2019.","da":"Ah, mchit. Mchit ltemma f 2019.","pron":"yès, aï hav. aï wènt thér in tou-thaw-zeund-naïn-tin"},{"en":"No, I haven't. I've never been abroad.","da":"La, 3emmerni. 3emmerni ma kherjt men lmeghrib.","pron":"no, aï ha-veunt. aïv né-veur bin a-brod"},{"en":"Has your brother ever eaten snails?","da":"Wach 3emmer khouk kla lbebbouch?","pron":"haz your bra-theur é-veur i-teun snéylz"},{"en":"Have you ever met a famous person?","da":"Wach 3emrek tla9iti chi chkhss mechhour?","pron":"hav you é-veur mèt a féy-meuss peur-seun"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"been wla gone? Present perfect wla past simple?","body_da":"**`been` wla `gone`?**\n\n- `She has been to London.` = mchat l London w rej3at (ttajriba).\n- `She has gone to London.` = mchat l London w **mazal temma** (makaynach daba).\n\n**`present perfect` wla `past simple`?**\n\n- `present perfect` = ttajriba, **bla wa9t m7edded**: `I have visited Fes.` (fo9ach? ma mohimch).\n- `past simple` (dars 15-16) = m3a **wa9t m7edded**: `I visited Fes last year.`, `in 2020`, `yesterday`, `two days ago`, `when I was a child`.\n\nF lhadra, 3adatan kanbdaw b `present perfect` w kankemmlo b `past simple`:\n\n`Have you ever been to Marrakech?` → `Yes, I have. I went there last summer. It was great!`\n\n**L9a3ida ddahabiya:** ila kayna `yesterday`, `last…`, `…ago`, `in 2015`, `when…` → `past simple`, **3emmerk** ma tsta3mli `present perfect`!","examples":[{"en":"Omar has gone to the market. He'll be back at six.","da":"Omar mcha l ssou9 (mazal temma). Ghadi yrje3 m3a ssetta.","pron":"o-mar haz gon tou the mar-kit. hil bi bak at siks"},{"en":"Omar has been to the market. Look, he bought vegetables.","da":"Omar kan mcha l ssou9 (w rje3). Chofi, chra lkhodra.","pron":"o-mar haz bin tou the mar-kit. louk, hi bot vèdj-teu-beulz"},{"en":"I've been to Tangier twice. The last time was in 2022.","da":"Mchit l Tanja jouj merrat. L'akhir merra kanet f 2022.","pron":"aïv bin tou tan-djir twaïs. the last taïm woz in tou-thaw-zeund-twèn-ti-tou"},{"en":"Have you ever tried snails? — Yes, I tried them in Jemaa el-Fna last year.","da":"Wach 3emrek jerrbti lbebbouch? — Ah, jerrebthom f Jam3 lfna l3am li fat.","pron":"hav you é-veur traïd snéylz — yès, aï traïd thèm in dja-ma èl-fna last yir"}]},{"type":"explain","title_da":"Lmoraja3a lkbira — men dars 1 7ta dars 23","body_da":"Mabrouk, Nouha! Hada l'akhir dars. Nchoufo l'ahamm no9at f jomla wa7da kol wa7da:\n\n- `to be` (dars 3): `am / is / are` → `I'm a nurse.`, `She isn't here.`, `Are you ready?`\n- `present simple` (dars 7-8): l3adat w l7a9ayi9 → `I work`, `she works`, `Do you…?`, `Does she…?`, `don't / doesn't`.\n- `present continuous` (dars 13): daba → `I'm studying now.`\n- `past simple` (dars 15-16): lmadi m7edded → `was / were`, `went`, `didn't go`, `Did you go?`\n- Lmosta9bal (dars 19): `going to` l lmokhattat → `I'm going to travel.` / `will` l l9arar w lwa3d → `I'll help you.`\n- Lmo9arana (dars 20): `bigger than`, `more expensive than`, `the best`.\n- `have to / must` (dars 21), `I'd like` (dars 22), `Could you tell me…?` (dars 23).\n- `present perfect` (dars 24): ttajarib → `Have you ever…?`\n\n**L7ila:** sewli rassek **fo9ach?** → daba (`continuous`), dima (`simple`), lbare7 (`past`), ghedda (`going to` / `will`), f 7yati bla wa9t (`present perfect`).","examples":[{"en":"I usually work in Casablanca, but today I'm working in Rabat.","da":"3adatan kankhdem f Casa, walakin lyouma kankhdem f Rabat.","pron":"aï you-jou-a-li weurk in ka-sa-blan-ka, beut tou-déy aïm weur-king in ra-bat"},{"en":"Last year I went to Agadir. Next year I'm going to visit Spain.","da":"L3am li fat mchit l Agadir. L3am jjay ghadi nzour Spanya.","pron":"last yir aï wènt tou a-ga-dir. nèkst yir aïm go-ing tou vi-zit spéyn"},{"en":"Marrakech is hotter than Tangier, but Tangier is the most beautiful city for me.","da":"Marrakech skhouna kter men Tanja, walakin Tanja hiya azwa9 mdina 3ndi.","pron":"ma-ra-kèch iz ho-teur than tan-djir, beut tan-djir iz the most byou-ti-foul si-ti for mi"},{"en":"I have learned a lot of English this year!","da":"T3ellemt bzzaf dyal lingliziya had l3am!","pron":"aï hav leurnd a lot ov in-glich this yir"}]},{"type":"vocab","title_da":"Lkelmat dyal dars","items":[{"en":"been","da":"mchit l… / knt (ttasrif ttalet dyal `be`)","emoji":"✈️","pron":"bin","example_en":"I've been to Fes.","example_da":"Mchit l Fes (chi merra f 7yati)."},{"en":"seen","da":"cheft (ttasrif ttalet dyal `see`)","emoji":"👀","pron":"sin","example_en":"Have you seen this film?","example_da":"Wach chefti had lfilm?"},{"en":"eaten","da":"klit (ttasrif ttalet dyal `eat`)","emoji":"🍽️","pron":"i-teun","example_en":"I've never eaten sushi.","example_da":"3emmerni ma klit sushi."},{"en":"tried","da":"jerrebt (ttasrif ttalet dyal `try`)","emoji":"🧪","pron":"traïd","example_en":"Have you ever tried snails?","example_da":"Wach 3emrek jerrbti lbebbouch?"},{"en":"met","da":"tla9it (ttasrif ttalet dyal `meet`)","emoji":"🤝","pron":"mèt","example_en":"I've met a famous singer.","example_da":"Tla9it wa7ed lmoghanni mechhour."},{"en":"visited","da":"zert (ttasrif ttalet dyal `visit`)","emoji":"🕌","pron":"vi-zi-tid","example_en":"She has visited Chefchaouen.","example_da":"Hiya zaret Chefchaouen."},{"en":"gone","da":"mcha w mazal temma (ttasrif ttalet dyal `go`)","emoji":"🚶","pron":"gon","example_en":"He has gone to work.","example_da":"Mcha l lkhedma (mazal temma)."},{"en":"ever","da":"chi merra f 7yatek (f so2al)","emoji":"❓","pron":"é-veur","example_en":"Have you ever been to Egypt?","example_da":"Wach 3emrek mchiti l Masr?"},{"en":"never","da":"3emmer… ma","emoji":"🚫","pron":"né-veur","example_en":"I've never been abroad.","example_da":"3emmerni ma kherjt men lmeghrib."},{"en":"abroad","da":"f lkharij / berra men lblad","emoji":"🌍","pron":"a-brod","example_en":"My cousin lives abroad.","example_da":"Weld 3emmi kayskon f lkharij."},{"en":"twice","da":"jouj merrat","emoji":"2️⃣","pron":"twaïs","example_en":"I've seen it twice.","example_da":"Chefto jouj merrat."},{"en":"famous","da":"mechhour / mechhoura","emoji":"⭐","pron":"féy-meuss","example_en":"Have you ever met a famous person?","example_da":"Wach 3emrek tla9iti chi chkhss mechhour?"},{"en":"snails","da":"lbebbouch","emoji":"🐌","pron":"snéylz","example_en":"Have you ever eaten snails?","example_da":"Wach 3emrek kliti lbebbouch?"},{"en":"camel","da":"jjmel","emoji":"🐪","pron":"ka-meul","example_en":"I have seen a camel in Merzouga.","example_da":"Cheft jjmel f Merzouga."},{"en":"the mountains","da":"jjbel","emoji":"🏔️","pron":"the mawn-teunz","example_en":"We've been to the Atlas Mountains.","example_da":"Mchina l jbal l'Atlas."},{"en":"a foreign country","da":"blad berraniya","emoji":"🗺️","pron":"a fo-rin keun-tri","example_en":"Have you ever visited a foreign country?","example_da":"Wach 3emrek zerti chi blad berraniya?"}]},{"type":"dialogue","title_da":"Wach 3emrek…? — Nouha w Sarah f l9ehwa","context_da":"Nouha w Sarah galsin f l9ehwa, kaythedro 3la ssafar w ttajarib dyalhom.","lines":[{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nouha, have you ever been abroad?","da":"Nouha, wach 3emrek mchiti l lkharij?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Yes, I have. I've been to Spain twice.","da":"Ah, mchit. Mchit l Spanya jouj merrat."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Really? When did you go?","da":"Bss7? Fo9ach mchiti?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"The first time was in 2018, with my family. We visited Madrid and Seville.","da":"L'awwal merra kanet f 2018, m3a l3a2ila dyali. Zerna Madrid w Seville."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Nice! Have you ever eaten paella?","da":"Zwin! Wach 3emrek kliti lpaella?"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"No, I haven't. I've never tried it. And you? Have you ever eaten couscous?","da":"La, 3emmerni. 3emmerni ma jerrebtha. W nti? Wach 3emrek kliti lkesksou?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Of course! I ate couscous last Friday at my neighbour's house. It was delicious.","da":"Bitta3b! Klit lkesksou ljem3a li fatet 3nd jjara dyali. Kan bnin."},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Have you ever been to the Sahara?","da":"Wach 3emrek mchiti l ssa7ra?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Not yet, but I'm going to go to Merzouga next month!","da":"Mazal, walakin ghadi nmchi l Merzouga chhar jjay!"},{"speaker":"Nouha","en":"Wow! You're going to love it. The desert is the most beautiful place in Morocco.","da":"Waw! Ghadi t3jbek bzzaf. Ssa7ra hiya azwa9 blassa f lmeghrib."}]},{"type":"tip","title_da":"Nasi7a","body_da":"Melli katsewli `Have you ever…?`, ljawab l9sir kafi: `Yes, I have.` / `No, never.` W men ba3d, ila bghiti tzidi ttafasil (fo9ach? fin? m3a men?) — dowzi l lmadi lbassit: `I went there in 2019.` Hadi hiya l9a3ida ddahabiya: ttajriba → `present perfect`; lwa9t m7edded → `past simple`. W mabrouk, Nouha — hada l'akhir dars! Mchiti men `Hello` 7ta l `Have you ever…?`. 3awdi ddorous li s3ab 3lik, w kemmli ttari9!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"match","instruction_da":"Wessli ttasrif ttalet (past participle) m3a lma3na dyalo.","pairs":[{"en":"been (to)","da":"mchit (l)","emoji":"✈️"},{"en":"seen","da":"cheft","emoji":"👀"},{"en":"eaten","da":"klit","emoji":"🍽️"},{"en":"met","da":"tla9it","emoji":"🤝"},{"en":"tried","da":"jerrebt","emoji":"🧪"}]},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno howa ttasrif ttalet (past participle) dyal `eat`?","options":["eaten","ate","eated","eating"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`eat – ate – eaten`. `ate` = lmadi lbassit (dars 16). `eaten` = ttasrif ttalet, kaymchi m3a `have/has`."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"Have you ever been to Spain?","question_da":"Sem3i. 3la ach kaysewwel?","options":["Wach 3emrek mchiti l Spanya","Wach ghadi tmchi l Spanya","Wach nti men Spanya","Wach kat3jbek Spanya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`Have you ever been to…?` = wach 3emrek mchiti l…? `ever` = chi merra f 7yatek."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"I ___ never eaten sushi.","options":["have","has","am"],"answer":"have","hint_da":"ana + ? + `never` + `eaten`","explain_da":"`I have never eaten` — m3a `I` kan9oulo `have`. `has` ghir m3a `he/she/it`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"She ___ visited Chefchaouen three times.","options":["has","have","is"],"answer":"has","hint_da":"Hiya → ?","explain_da":"`She has visited` — m3a `he/she/it` → `has`."},{"type":"order","words":["Have","you","ever","met","a","famous","person?"],"answer":"Have you ever met a famous person?","da":"Wach 3emrek tla9iti chi chkhss mechhour?","explain_da":"So2al: `Have` + `you` + `ever` + ttasrif ttalet (`met`)."},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Omar makaynch f ddar daba, rah f Rabat. Chno n9oulo?","options":["Omar has gone to Rabat.","Omar has been to Rabat.","Omar is been to Rabat.","Omar has go to Rabat."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`has gone` = mcha w mazal temma. `has been` = mcha w rje3."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"No, I haven't. I've never been abroad.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kat9oul had lmra?","options":["3emmerha ma kherjat men lblad","Mchat l lkharij bzzaf","Ghadi tmchi l lkharij","Hiya f lkharij daba"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I've never been abroad` = 3emmerni ma kherjt men lblad. `abroad` = lkharij."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"\"I have visited Fes last year\" is correct English.","statement_da":"Ljomla `I have visited Fes last year` s7i7a.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet! M3a lwa9t m7edded (`last year`) kansta3mlo lmadi lbassit: `I visited Fes last year.`"},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Lmoraja3a (dars 8): khtari ljomla s7i7a.","options":["She doesn't like coffee.","She don't like coffee.","She doesn't likes coffee.","She not like coffee."],"answer":0,"explain_da":"M3a `she` → `doesn't` + lfi3l bla `-s`: `doesn't like`."},{"type":"dictation","say_en":"I've never tried camel meat.","da":"3emmerni ma jerrebt l7em jjmel.","explain_da":"`I've` = `I have`. `never` = 3emmer… ma. `tried` = jerrebt."},{"type":"translate","da":"Wach 3emrek kliti lbebbouch?","answers":["Have you ever eaten snails?","Have you ever tried snails?"],"hint_en":"Have you ... eaten ...?","explain_da":"`Have you ever eaten…?` = wach 3emrek kliti…? `snails` = lbebbouch."},{"type":"order","words":["She","has","been","to","London","twice."],"answer":"She has been to London twice.","da":"Hiya mchat l London jouj merrat.","explain_da":"`has been to` + lblassa + `twice` (jouj merrat). `been` dima m3a `to`."},{"type":"fill","sentence_en":"A: Have you ever been to Fes? B: Yes, I ___. I went there in 2020.","answers":["have"],"hint_da":"Ljawab l9sir: `Yes, I` …","explain_da":"Ljawab l9sir: `Yes, I have.` Men ba3d, m3a lwa9t m7edded (`in 2020`) → `went` (lmadi lbassit)."},{"type":"translate","da":"Ghedda ghadi nzour khti f Rabat. Hiya kber menni.","answers":["Tomorrow I'm going to visit my sister in Rabat. She's older than me.","Tomorrow I am going to visit my sister in Rabat. She is older than me.","Tomorrow I'm going to visit my sister in Rabat. She is older than me.","Tomorrow I am going to visit my sister in Rabat. She's older than me."],"hint_en":"Tomorrow I'm ... to visit my ... in Rabat. She's ... than me.","explain_da":"Moraja3a: `going to` (dars 19) l lmokhattat, `older than` (dars 20) l lmo9arana."},{"type":"speak","target_en":"I've been to Spain twice, but I've never been to England.","da":"Mchit l Spanya jouj merrat, walakin 3emmerni ma mchit l Ingiltira.","pron":"aïv bin tou spéyn twaïs, beut aïv né-veur bin tou in-gleund"}],"reading":{"title_en":"Amina's interesting life","title_da":"L7ayat lmohimma dyal Amina","emoji":"🌍","text_en":"My name is Amina and I'm 35 years old. I have had a very interesting life. I was born in a small village near Ouarzazate, but I moved to Marrakech in 2010. I have worked as a nurse, a tour guide and, today, an English teacher. I have travelled a lot: I've been to France, Turkey and Egypt, and I've visited twelve Moroccan cities. I've never been to America, but I'm going to go next year, because my sister lives in New York. I've eaten strange food in my life: snails in Jemaa el-Fna and raw fish in Istanbul. But I've never tried camel meat! I've met many kind people, and I've learned three languages. Last month, I started my fourth: Spanish. It's harder than English, but it's more useful for my job. My advice? Life is short. Try new things, visit new places and never stop learning.","text_da":"Smiyti Amina w 3ndi 35 3am. 3echt 7ayat mohimma bzzaf. Tzadit f wa7ed ddouwar sghir 7da Werzazat, walakin nta9elt l Marrakech f 2010. Khdemt fermliya, w morchida siya7iya, w lyouma oustada dyal lingliziya. Saffert bzzaf: mchit l Fransa, Torkya w Masr, w zert tnach mdina meghribiya. 3emmerni ma mchit l Amrika, walakin ghadi nmchi l3am jjay, 7it khti kateskon f New York. Klit makla ghriba f 7yati: lbebbouch f Jam3 lfna w l7out khder f Istanbul. Walakin 3emmerni ma jerrebt l7em jjmel! Tla9it bzzaf dyal nnas dérifin, w t3ellemt tlata dyal lloghat. Chhar li fat, bdit rrab3a: l'isbaniya. S3iba kter men lingliziya, walakin nafi3a kter l khdemti. Nnasi7a dyali? L7ayat 9sira. Jerrbi 7wayj jdad, zouri blayes jdad w 3emmrek ma t7ebsi tt3ellem.","glossary":[{"en":"interesting","da":"mohimm / fih lfayda"},{"en":"I was born","da":"tzadit"},{"en":"village","da":"ddouwar"},{"en":"tour guide","da":"morchid / morchida siya7iya"},{"en":"travelled","da":"saffert"},{"en":"raw fish","da":"l7out khder (machi mtiyeb)"},{"en":"languages","da":"lloghat"},{"en":"useful","da":"nafi3 / nafi3a"},{"en":"advice","da":"nasi7a"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fin tzadet Amina?","options":["F douwar sghir 7da Werzazat","F Marrakech","F New York","F Istanbul"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I was born in a small village near Ouarzazate.\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Amina has been to America.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"I've never been to America, but I'm going to go next year.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Chno 3emmerha ma jerrbat Amina?","options":["L7em jjmel","Lbebbouch","L7out khder","Lmakla ttorkiya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"But I've never tried camel meat!\""},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Amina thinks Spanish is easier than English.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"It's harder than English.\" `harder` = s3eb kter."}]},"listening":{"title_da":"Wach 3emrek…? — lo3ba f l9ism","emoji":"🎧","pre_da":"F l'akhir 7issa, l'oustad kaysewwel ttlamed 3la ttajarib dyalhom. Sem3i w rekkzi 3la: l fin mcha Omar f lkharij? w chno 3emmro ma dar?","lines":[{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"OK, Omar, it's your turn. Have you ever been abroad?","da":"Wakha, Omar, nnoba dyalek. Wach 3emrek mchiti l lkharij?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, I have. I've been to Turkey.","da":"Ah, mchit. Mchit l Torkya."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"When did you go there?","da":"Fo9ach mchiti ltemma?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"I went to Istanbul two years ago, with my brother. We stayed for a week.","da":"Mchit l Istanbul hadi 3amayn, m3a khouya. B9ina simana."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Did you like it?","da":"Wach 3jbatek?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, it was fantastic. The food was delicious, but the city was more expensive than Casablanca.","da":"Ah, kanet ra2i3a. Lmakla kanet bnina, walakin lmdina kanet ghalya kter men Casa."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Have you ever tried Turkish coffee?","da":"Wach 3emrek jerrbti l9ehwa ttorkiya?"},{"speaker":"Omar","en":"Yes, I have, many times. But I've never eaten Turkish sweets. I don't like sugar.","da":"Ah, jerrebtha, bzzaf dyal lmerrat. Walakin 3emmerni ma klit l7elwa ttorkiya. Ma kanbghich sskkar."},{"speaker":"Mr. Brown","en":"Interesting! Thank you, Omar. Now, Laila, have you ever met a famous person?","da":"Mohimm! Choukran, Omar. Daba, Laila, wach 3emrek tla9iti chi chkhss mechhour?"}],"questions":[{"type":"mcq","question_da":"L fin mcha Omar f lkharij?","options":["L Torkya","L Spanya","L Fransa","L Masr"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I've been to Turkey.\""},{"type":"mcq","question_da":"Fo9ach mcha l Istanbul?","options":["Hadi 3amayn","L3am li fat","Hadi simana","F 2010"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"\"I went to Istanbul two years ago.\" `two years ago` = hadi 3amayn."},{"type":"listen_mcq","say_en":"I've never eaten Turkish sweets.","question_da":"Sem3i. Chno kay9oul Omar?","options":["3emmro ma kla l7elwa ttorkiya","Kla l7elwa ttorkiya bzzaf","Ghadi yakol l7elwa ttorkiya","Kat3jbo l7elwa ttorkiya"],"answer":0,"explain_da":"`I've never eaten` = 3emmerni ma klit. `sweets` = l7elwa."},{"type":"truefalse","statement_en":"Istanbul was cheaper than Casablanca.","answer":false,"explain_da":"Ghalet: \"the city was more expensive than Casablanca.\" `cheaper` = rkhes."}]},"speaking":{"pronunciation":[{"target_en":"Have you ever been to Spain?","da":"Wach 3emrek mchiti l Spanya?","pron":"hav you é-veur bin tou spéyn"},{"target_en":"Yes, I have. I went there in 2019.","da":"Ah, mchit. Mchit ltemma f 2019.","pron":"yès, aï hav. aï wènt thér in tou-thaw-zeund-naïn-tin"},{"target_en":"No, I haven't. Never.","da":"La, 3emmerni. Walou.","pron":"no, aï ha-veunt. né-veur"},{"target_en":"I've eaten couscous many times.","da":"Klit lkesksou bzzaf dyal lmerrat.","pron":"aïv i-teun kous-kous mé-ni taïmz"},{"target_en":"She has gone to the market.","da":"Hiya mchat l ssou9 (mazal temma).","pron":"chi haz gon tou the mar-kit"},{"target_en":"I have learned a lot this year!","da":"T3ellemt bzzaf had l3am!","pron":"aï hav leurnd a lot this yir"}],"roleplay":{"title_da":"Wach 3emrek…? — lo3ba dyal ttajarib","context_da":"Sarah katsewlek 3la ttajarib dyal 7yatek. Jawbi b `Yes, I have` / `No, I haven't`, w zidi ttafasil b lmadi lbassit!","turns":[{"bot_en":"Hi Nouha! Have you ever been abroad?","bot_da":"Ahlan Nouha! Wach 3emrek mchiti l lkharij?","expect_keywords":["yes, i have","no, i haven't","i have","i haven't","never","i've been","been to"],"sample_en":"Yes, I have. I've been to Spain."},{"bot_en":"Interesting! Have you ever eaten food from another country?","bot_da":"Mohimm! Wach 3emrek kliti makla dyal blad khra?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i have","haven't","never","eaten","tried","pizza","sushi"],"sample_en":"Yes, I have. I've eaten pizza and sushi."},{"bot_en":"And when did you eat it?","bot_da":"W fo9ach klitiha?","expect_keywords":["last","ago","in 20","when i","yesterday","ate","tried"],"sample_en":"I ate sushi last year, in Casablanca."},{"bot_en":"Have you ever met a famous person?","bot_da":"Wach 3emrek tla9iti chi chkhss mechhour?","expect_keywords":["yes","no","i have","haven't","never","met"],"sample_en":"No, I haven't. I've never met a famous person."},{"bot_en":"What are you going to do after this course?","bot_da":"Chno ghadi tdiri men ba3d had ddawra?","expect_keywords":["going to","i'll","i will","travel","work","study","practise","practice","speak"],"sample_en":"I'm going to practise English every day and travel to London."},{"bot_en":"Great! You have learned a lot. Congratulations, Nouha!","bot_da":"Mzyan! T3ellemti bzzaf. Mabrouk, Nouha!","expect_keywords":["thank","thanks","happy","glad","bye"],"sample_en":"Thank you so much, Sarah! I'm very happy."}]}},"writing":{"title_da":"Ttajarib dyali — l'akhir ktaba","prompt_da":"Ktbi 60 kelma 3la ttajarib dyal 7yatek: fin mchiti (`I've been to…`), chno kliti wla jerrbti (`I've tried…`), chkoun tla9iti, w chno 3emmrek ma derti (`I've never…`). Zidi jomla b lmadi lbassit (fo9ach?) w jomla 3la lmosta9bal (`I'm going to…`). Hadi hiya lmoraja3a lkbira dyalek!","helper_en":["I've been to ...","I've never ...","I went there in ...","I've tried ...","Next year, I'm going to ..."],"min_words":60,"keywords":["never","been"],"model_en":"I'm Nouha and I've had many good experiences in my life. I've been to Spain twice, with my family. The first time was in 2018, and we visited Madrid. I've visited many cities in Morocco, but I've never been to the Sahara. I've eaten pizza, sushi and Turkish food, and I've tried snails in Marrakech. I've never met a famous person, but I've met many kind people in my English class. Next year, I'm going to travel to London and speak English every day. I think it will be the best trip of my life!"}}],"placement":[{"level":"A1.1","type":"mcq","question_da":"Kifach kan9oulo \"choukran\" b lingliziya?","options":["Thank you","Please","Sorry","Hello"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"I ___ Nouha.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["am","is","are","be"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"What's your name?","question_da":"Achmen jawab s7i7?","options":["My name is Sara.","I'm fine, thanks.","I'm twenty.","Yes, please."],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.1","type":"mcq","question_da":"Achmen kelma kat3ni \"ktab\"?","options":["book","table","car","door"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"She ___ to work every day.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["goes","go","going","is go"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"___ you like coffee?","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["Do","Does","Are","Is"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"There ___ two chairs in the room.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["are","is","am","be"],"answer":0},{"level":"A1.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"What time is it? (7:30)","question_da":"Khtari ljawab s7i7.","options":["It's half past seven.","It's seven and half.","It's thirty seven.","It's seven past half."],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"Look! She ___ a book now.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["is reading","reads","read","reading"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"I ___ to Marrakech last year.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["went","go","goed","going"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"___ you swim?","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["Can","Do","Are","Is"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.1","type":"mcq","question_en":"They ___ at home yesterday.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["were","was","are","be"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"Casablanca is ___ than Rabat.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["bigger","more big","biggest","big"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"Tomorrow I ___ visit my grandmother.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["am going to","go to","going","goes to"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"Have you ever ___ to London?","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["been","be","went","go"],"answer":0},{"level":"A2.2","type":"mcq","question_en":"You ___ wear a seatbelt. It's the law.","question_da":"Khtari lkelma s7i7a.","options":["must","can","should not","might"],"answer":0}]};
